at existed in which countries?", "answer": "Sweden, Finland, and Norway", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "The Pantanal is a mid-size pickup truck made by the Brazilian off-road vehicle manufacturer Troller Ve\u00edculos Especiais S/A, a manufacturer of off-road vehicles in which country, from 2006 to 2008?", "answer": "Brazil", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Where is the there a small medevial castle", "answer": "Scotland", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What is the name of this policy of favoring members of a disadvantaged group who suffer or have suffered from discrimination within a culture of which Black Economic Empowerment is a form? ", "answer": "Affirmative action", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "The 32nd TCA Awards were hosted by a  Mexican actor best known for his roles as Fernando Mendiola in what?", "answer": "La Fea Mas Bella", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Are the documentaries Welcome to Durham, USA and The Agronomist both about Durham, North Carolina?", "answer": "no", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Which member of the band Bad Seeds was older, Anita Lane or Nick Cave?", "answer": "Nick Cave", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which close friend of George Washington, Alexander Hamilton, and Thomas Jefferson, did a scion of the Huger family of South Carolina attempt to rescue?", "answer": "Gilbert du Motier, Marquis de Lafayette", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "John Severin was an American comics artist who had a 45 year stint with the magazine Cracked that was founded in what year?", "answer": "1958", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Rags Ragland died how many years after starring in Meet the People?", "answer": "II", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Do filmmakers Chris Carter and Theo van Gogh share the same nationality?", "answer": "no", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "What genre is The Warriors Gate?", "answer": "action", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Brutti di notte is a parody of the film starring which actress?", "answe