st Bollywood film to be shot in Afghanistan,the title character was based on matka, king Ratan Khatri, Matka\" gambling or satta\" is a form of lottery which originally involved betting on the opening and closing rates of cotton transmitted from where?", "answer": "New York Cotton Exchange", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What American composer who died in 1978 was associated with an American Opera Company located in Jackson, Mississippi?", "answer": "William Grant Still", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What occupation was shared by both John Frankenheimer and Tiffanie DeBartolo?", "answer": "director", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "What is the population of the largest city in Iraq, who's 1956\u201357 Iraq FA Cup Championship was open to teams from the capital?", "answer": "8,765,000", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What wrestling promotion was formed by the current NEVER Openweight Champion?", "answer": "Pro Wrestling Fujiwara Group", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which mine in California, lasting from 1873 to 1883, became one of the most noted mercury producers in the world?", "answer": "Sulphur Bank Mine", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Name the mother of Edward Stafford, 4th Baron Stafford, who was the daughter of the English nobleman and politician Edward Stanley, 3rd Earl of Derby?", "answer": "Mary Stanley", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which author was born first, Lorraine Hansberry or Sandra Gulland?", "answer": "Lorraine Vivian Hansberry", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "What is the Kaurna name of the river that runs along Mount Torrens in South Australia?", "answer": "Ngangkiparri", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What does the L stand for in Patriot Games star Samuel L. Jackson's name?", "answer": "Leroy", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which movie was co-written by the person who directed \"Blood\"?", "answer": "The Awakening", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Are Kelly Jones and Martha Reeves both singers?", "answer": "yes", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Which professional American football team based in Ohio did Ivan \"John\" Jurkovic play for?", "answer": "Cleveland Browns", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Who is the oldest of the Van Dyke family?", "answer": "Dick Van Dyke", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Choi Min-sik, is a South Korean actor, he also starred alongside Scarlett Johansson in Lucy, an English-language French science fiction action film written and directed by who?", "answer": "Luc Besson", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Snow White is a Disney media franchise based on a German fairy tale by who?", "answer": "Brothers Grimm", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What connection does the private liberal arts college known for its distinctive curriculum centered on reading and discussing the Great Books of Western Civilization have to] EnVISIONing Annapolis? ", "answer": "Important contributors and co-sponsors", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "The Prancing Horse was used by which top Italian fighter ace?", "answer": "Count Francesco Baracca", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What Bible college located in Louisville, Kentucky, was attended by Paul R. House who served for a time as president of the Evangelical Theological Society?", "answer": "Southern Baptist Theological Seminary", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Joan Jett & the Blackhearts covered a song by the first westerner to achieve pop start status in Japan.  When was that song first recorded?", "answer": "1975", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "This Federation of Indian Airlines member is owned by what Indian business conglomerate?", "answer": "Wadia Group", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "MindGamers is a 2015 Austrian science fiction film directed by who, the film stars Antonia Campbell-Hughes, a Northern Irish actress and former fashion designer, best known for appearing in Jack Dee's sitcom \"Lead Balloon\"?", "answer": "Andrew Goth", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "When was Jordan Mintz whictleblowing publicized?", "answer": "October 2001", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Who played the onscreen husband of a variety show banjo player?", "answer": "banjo player and former member of the television variety show \"Hee Haw\" gang having played the role of Ida Lee Nagger, the ironing, nagging wife of Laverne Nagger (Gordie Tapp).", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "The motorway reffered to as the Mid Wirral Motorway is located in a suburb known for which buildings?", "answer": "Joseph Groome Towers", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What suicide attack was located inside the Forward Operating Base Chapman? ", "answer": "Camp Chapman attack", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What principal dancer in the Bolshoi ballet, born in 1988, is a student of Valery Lagunov?", "answer": "Vladislav Lantratov", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "what was the birth year of the fifth governor of a British colony in north America that existed from 1632 to 1776?", "answer": "1626", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What is a semi-professional football club in Hyde, Greater Manchester, England?", "answer": "Hyde United Football Club", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "The pop singer in the lead role in \"Tere Bin Laden\" received how many Lux Style Awards?", "answer": "five", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What's Golden was included in an open world racing video game that was developed by Playground Games and published by who?", "answer": "Microsoft Studios", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which  province in the north of the island of Ireland did Queen Medb of Connacht  made his invasion", "answer": "Ulster", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Jeremy Brock is the writer and director of this 2011 drama that was adapted from him and what other female?", "answer": "Rosemary Sutcliff", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Gabe Turner has collaborated with the actor and film director who won his first Academy Award in which 1995 crime thriller?", "answer": "The Usual Suspects", "type": "bridg