e Alba", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "How many people were killed by a van bomb by the man Inga Bejer Engh prosecuted in a high profile 2012 trial?", "answer": "eight", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "The Jargon Society has published books by the founder and primary theorist of what group of poets?", "answer": "Objectivist", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Restoration literature is the English literature written during the historical period commonly referred to as the English Restoration (1660\u20131689), which corresponds to the last years of the direct Stuart reign, it saw Locke's \"Treatises of Government\", the founding of the Royal Society, the experiments and holy meditations of Robert William Boyle, was an Anglo-Irish natural philosopher, chemist, physicist and inventor born in Lismore, County Waterford, in which location?", "answer": "Ireland", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "John Martin & Co. is responsible for the pageant that has been known as what since 1996?", "answer": "Credit Union Christmas Pageant", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Who directed Revolver, the 2005 crime thriller starring the English actor Jason Statham?", "answer": "Guy Ritchie", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What sport does Pieter Nys and Fortuna Sittard have in common?", "answer": "football", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What British comedy film starred Robin Weaver?", "answer": "The Inbetweeners 2", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Whitney Williams has a chair on the board of a non-profit with Ben Affleck and what other company?", "answer": "williamsworks", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which painter created the 'Beguiling of Merlin' and was closely associated with the later part of the Pre-Raphaelite movement? ", "answer": "Edward Burne-Jones", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Nikolaas Tinbergen shared the 1973 Nobel in Medicine with the zoologist who was of what nationality?", "answer": "Austrian", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "In what conference is the University that had a coach born on September 9th, 1960?", "answer": "the Big 12 Conference", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Oliver Boot had a role in the Moliere-based film that was first performed in what year?", "answer": "1664", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": " \"Your Love Had Taken Me That High\" is a song recorded by a singer that received a string of Country Music Association awards for duets with who?", "answer": "Loretta Lynn", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "How far north from Salzburg is the Austrian village that shares a name with a controversial German Pilsner or pale lager?", "answer": "33 km", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "The Grinch is a fictional character created by an author that died in what year?", "answer": "1991", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Were Nikos Koundouros and Curtis Hanson both film directors?", "answer": "yes", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Qwirkle and Evo, are which type of entertainment?", "answer": "game", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "What Emmy Award winner worked on Miles from Home?", "answer": "Gary Sinise", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Who replaced the Peabody Award winner, made famous for his NPR flagship program, in 2004?", "answer": "Ren\u00e9e Montagne", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What show is an American-Canadian drama starring Scott Lowell playing Ted Schmidt?", "answer": "Queer as Folk", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "\"HMS \"Sussex\" was an 80-gun third-rate ship, of the line of the English Royal Navy, for which sovereign state on the island of Great Britain from the 10th century\u2014when it emerged from various Anglo-Saxon kingdoms\u2014until 1707, when it united with Scotland to form the Kingdom of Great Britain?", "answer": "Kingdom of England", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Arthur bell as an amateur cricketer player for what league known for employing professional players.", "answer": "Lancashire League", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "In what year was the woman whose former chief of staff was Rachel Noerdlinger born?", "answer": "1954", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "In regards to the album that had, according to Dave Grohl, his favourite song he has ever written, when was it released?", "answer": "April 12, 2011", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "True Williams was the first to illustrate which title character of a Mark Twain novel?", "answer": "Thomas \"Tom\" Sawyer", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "KKWQ-FM is a local radio station covering which area, that is a coextensive with Angle Township?", "answer": "The Northwest Angle", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Who worked for both the Security Service and the Secret Intelligence Service, and began writing novels under his pen name, Audre Lorde or John le Carr\u00e9?", "answer": "David John Moore Cornwell", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "When did the British/Irish digital television channel, which features Spliced, first launch?", "answer": "22 July 2002", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "The Oxus cobra contains what kind of ions for their venom to be active? ", "answer": "magnesium", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "The team Kevin Goldthwaite last played for play their home games at Providence Park since what year?", "answer": "2011", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Are Naser Mestarihi and Justin Sane both singer-songwriters?", "answer": "yes", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Abeliophyllum and Brillantaisia, are types of what?", "answer": "plants", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Which 2004 Nickelodeon show was created by Sue Rose and starred Molly Hagan? ", "answer": "Unfabulous", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": " Charles Runnington was born in a country in southern what?", "answer": "England", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Chris Vance, is an English actor, and is the second actor after which English actor, and a former model and competitive diver, to play Frank Martin?", "answer": "Jason Statham", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "In which school was the fictiona