id Connell", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What is the connection between F\u00e9lix du Temple de la Croix and Early flying machines?", "answer": "aircraft of any sort", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which topic in the Dear America series took place in New York City?", "answer": "Triangle Shirtwaist Factory fire", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Who is best known for writing and directing science fiction films such as \"Cube\", \"Cypher\", \"Nothing\", and \"Splice\", Vincenzo Natali or Leigh Jason?", "answer": "Vincenzo Natali", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "What country does Florida Board of Regents and State University System of Florida have in common?", "answer": "United States", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Tadesse Meskela is the General Manager of the Oromia Coffee Farmers Cooperative Union an was featured in a documentary film released in what year?", "answer": "2006", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Where was the Hockey League which drafted Niclas Bergfors based?", "answer": "Newark, New Jersey", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "In which year did the team that Jonathan Spector joined in 2006 move to its new home ?", "answer": "2016", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Ivano Bonetti (born 1 August 1964 in Brescia) is an Italian football manager and former midfielder, he appeared for the English club, Grimsby Town Football Club is a professional football club based in the town of Cleethorpes, Lincolnshire, England, that competes in what?", "answer": "League Two", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which person included in the label 300 Entertainment has a debut single \"Trap Queen?\"", "answer": "Fetty Wap", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Whitechapel is a series that depicted a killer who was copying the actions of which unidentified serial killer?", "answer": "Jack the Ripper", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What star of the 1994 film Krantiveer was born January 1, 1951?", "answer": "Nana Patekar", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Who publi