y Cecily von Ziegesar, that the character Eric van der Woodsen appears in?", "answer": "Gossip Girl", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "In what year did Frederick Chesson meet the author of \"Incidents in the Life of a Slave Girl\"?", "answer": "1858", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "NBA Access with Ahmad Rashad, an American sportscaster (mostly with NBC Sports) and former professional football player, is an American television program which initially aired on Saturday afternoons on which channel?", "answer": "ABC", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which album came after \"The Dutchess\"?", "answer": "\"Double Dutchess\"", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Who died at an earlier date, H. P. Lovecraft or Timothy Leary?", "answer": "Howard Phillips Lovecraft", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "In which American space drama film did Clint Eastwood star with the actor who played Bret Maverick in the 1950s western comedy series \"Maverick\"?", "answer": "Space Cowboys", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which director did sound engineer Joseph Geisinger work with to be nominated for an Academy Award?", "answer": "Sam Raimi", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What's the difference between Texas Monthly nd Lucky?", "answer": "first published in 2000", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Moscow Water Dog and Bavarian Mountain Hound, are a breed of what?", "answer": "dog", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "What actor in the Calendar Girl Murders was born in March?", "answer": "Sharon Stone", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Sandy Fox was a voice actress in King of the Hill, what else do they have in common?", "answer": "American", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Comedian Frank Gorshin was a member of The Kopykats, a group of comedians on which television variety show in 1972?", "answer": "The ABC Comedy Hour", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "The short story from The Wind\u2019s Twelve Quarters that won the Hugo Award in 1974 was published in what year?", "answer": "197