il explores the life of what Irish priest who raped, molested and abused at least 25 children in what state?", "answer": "California", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "When was the Australian radio and television presenter who was part of the host for 1 vs. 100 born? ", "answer": "29 October 1964", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Baseball All-Star Bo Jackson and Craig Erickson were both drafted twice in the NFL Draft. What team do they have in common?", "answer": "Tampa Bay Buccaneers", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What song recorded by Barbadian recording artist Rihanna was written by Corey Chorus?", "answer": "\"Cheers (Drink to That)\"", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What was the nickname of the Brazilian heiress that signed the Lei Aurea?", "answer": "\"the Redemptress\"", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Katherine Bailess acted in what series that was originally title Bounce?", "answer": "Hit the Floor", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Kurt Julian Weillwas a German composer, active from the 1920s in his native country, and in his later years in the United States, with Brecht, he developed productions such as his best-known work, the Threepenny Opera is a \"play with music\" by Bertolt Brecht and who, adapted from John Gay's 18th-century English ballad opera, \"The Beggar's Opera\"?", "answer": "Elisabeth Hauptmann", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What cast member of \"All That\" is known for playing a talk show host on the recurring SNL sketch \"What Up with That?\"?", "answer": "Kenan Thompson", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Ubaydallah ibn Abdallah ibn Tahir was the last major Tahirid to hold high office in what dynasty?", "answer": "Tahirid dynasty", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Are Robert Florey and Geoff Murphy both in the film-making profession?", "answer": "yes", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Consider the eccentric Knoxville businessman with whom George Roby Dempster often staged politcal battles. In what year were they born?", "a