r action film?", "answer": "Transformers", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": " The garden city movement is a method of urban planning in which self-contained communities are surrounded by \"greenbelts\", containing proportionate areas of residences, industry, and agriculture, the idea was initiated in 1898 by Sir Ebenezer Howard, (29 January 1850 \u2013 1 May 1928), the English founder of the garden city movement, is known for his publication, in which year?", "answer": "1898", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What is the name of the sixth studio album by American rapper Future which contains the song titled Selfish?", "answer": "Hndrxx", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "The star of the film that includes the song \"Man on the Edge\" on its soundtrack was born in what year?", "answer": "1944", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "By how many days per decade has the melt season lengthened in the shallowest of the world's major oceans?", "answer": "5 days per decade", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which film did Cliff Potts, and the actor who was nominated for the Academy Award for Best Supporting Actor for \"Coming Home\", both appear in? ", "answer": "\"Silent Running\"", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What is the name of the 40th president who was in office when the Job Partnership Act of 1982 was passed?", "answer": "Ronald Reagan", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What position does Bob Diaco hold with the football team hat has the most wins and the highest winning percentage of any program over the last 50 years?", "answer": "defensive coordinator", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "The 2005 Florida Atlantic University Owls football team represented Florida Atlantic University in the 2005 NCAA Division I-A football season, the team was coached by Howard Leslie Schnellenberger, an retired football coach, of which nationality, with long service at both the professional and college levels?", "answer": "American", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What was the name of 