ual Thoroughbred horse race in 1950?", "answer": "Comic Court", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What did the king of England, Scotland and Ireland create in 1652?", "answer": "The I'Anson Baronetcy of Bassetbury", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Joseph Morgan is best known for his roll in what CW show that eventually spun off into \"The Originals\"?", "answer": "The Vampire Diaries", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Pieter 'Piet' Klijnveld, was a Dutch accountant who started a practice that after several mergers would grow into which professional service company and one of the Big Four auditors, along with Deloitte, Ernst & Young (EY), and PricewaterhouseCoopers (PwC)?", "answer": "KPMG", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Between the Lapageria and Satureja genus, which is the national flower of Chile?", "answer": "Lapageria", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "What project did the namesake of 2752 Wu Chien-Shiung work on?", "answer": "the Manhattan Project", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "The last champion of the FFB Open was an English professional snooker player from where?", "answer": "Leicester", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What animated car character was voiced by Paul Newman?", "answer": "Doc Hudson", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Cache is a city in Comanche County, Oklahoma, it is the location of Star House, the home of the Comanche chief Quanah Parker, was a Comanche war leader of the Quahadi (\"Antelope\") band of which people?", "answer": "Comanche", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Are musicians Paul Cotton and Cedric Bixler-Zavala both members of a band?", "answer": "yes", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "What team did Boom Boom captain in 2016?", "answer": "Peshawar Zalmi", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Rishabh Shukla, is an Indian film and television actor and a voice-dubbing artist, who speaks Hindi as his mother tongue language, as a Hindi dubbing actor he is most known as the voice of which fictional character and the main antago