": "Take Off", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": " Sheila Mullen is a Scottish painter whose works are in the permanents collection of the senior patrilineal descendant of who?", "answer": "James, Duke of Monmouth", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which city that publishes the Marathi daily newspaper 'Loksatta' is titled \"The City of Gates\"?", "answer": "Aurangabad", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What was the name of the 2009 book about the US Coast Guard's most daring rescue about a T2 tanker, originating in the Coast Guard Station of Chatham, which had broken in two during a storm and inspired a 2016 film?", "answer": "The Finest Hours", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "How many times has the driver, who won the Nation's Cup with Petter Solberg, in the 2014 Race of Champions, won  the 24 Hours of Le Mans ?", "answer": "nine", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "George Juskalian took part in the invasion of what area during WWII?", "answer": "French North Africa", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Run Fatboy Run is a 2007 British-American comedy film directed by an actor who graduated from where?", "answer": "Northwestern University", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What is the third track on the Rolling Stones album that was the first to feature the same track listings in both its UK and US versions?", "answer": "\"In Another Land\"", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Buddymoon was written in part by a German actor who appeared in a number of TV shows was named one of The Hollywood Reporter's top 25 digital stars in what year?", "answer": "2015", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Did the authors Isaac Asimov and Jean Giono write their fictions in a similar setting?", "answer": "no", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Which Chinese professional tennis play lost in the first round of the 2013 ASB Classic to Jamie Hampton?", "answer": "Zheng Jie", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What nationality was the player acquired by the Milwaukee Bucks from the Charlotte Bobc