hern Soul movement?", "answer": "Blackpool Mecca", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What is the name of the 1972 film based on Nicholas Monsarrat's novel and stars Colin Blakely?", "answer": "Something to Hide", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Mile 81 contained an excerpt from what Stephen King novel that was published November 8, 2011?", "answer": "11/22/63", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Who directed the black comedy film for which Jacques Mathou was best known? ", "answer": "Jean-Pierre Jeunet and Marc", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "The lead vocalist of rock band Drug Restaurant is also a member of the cast of a South Korean variety show that airs on what network?", "answer": "KBS2", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "That's My Mommy, released in which year, is an one reel animated \"Tom and Jerry\" short directed and produced by William Hanna and Joseph Barbera?", "answer": "1955", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which film became a defining film of the French New Wave movement and is the first series of five films in which Jean-Pierre Leaud stars? ", "answer": "The 400 Blows", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Has Alek Keshishian been the writer for more films than Mark Krikorian?", "answer": "yes", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "What is Chinese name for the science fiction prequel to an American neo-noir science fiction film directed by Denis Villeneuve?", "answer": "2048: No Escape or 2048: Nowhere to Escape", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "The inner urban neighbourhood Eureka Tower is in had a population of what in 2011?", "answer": "11,235", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "A Seattle Illustrator and editorial cartoonist, who was the first illustrator to show a public market that overlooks the Elliot Bay waterfront, was the son of what other cartoonist?", "answer": "John Hager", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Are Roy Rowland and V\u00edctor Erice both film directors?", "answer": "yes", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Are the magazines, M