 Padre", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "What are the accounting companies that make up the \"Big Four\" excluding Ernst & Young?", "answer": "PricewaterhouseCoopers, Deloitte Touche Tohmatsu", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What nationality is the man whom Vladimir Kozlov won the WWE Tag Team Championship with?", "answer": "Canadian", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Who was the coach for the team that won the 2004 Sugar Bowl?", "answer": "Nick Saban", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which is from farther west, The Commuters or Amplifier?", "answer": "The Commuters", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "The Northumbrian Dialect was spoken in a kingdom whose name reflects what approximate southern limit to the kingdom's territory?", "answer": "the Humber estuary", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "The Capital District, also known as the Capital Region, refers to the metropolitan area surrounding Albany, the capital of the U.S. state of New York, in the 21st century, the Capital District has emerged as a major anchor, of which marketing name for the eastern part of the U.S. state of New York, encompassing the Capital District and the Hudson Valley?", "answer": "Tech Valley", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which was founded first, Pomona College or Brown University?", "answer": "Brown University", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Who did the man who played Mick Carter in EastEnders play in Human Traffic?", "answer": "Moff", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Where was the owner of FAME Studios inducted in 1985 after having Ray Whitley single What Kind of Fool recorded at his studio?", "answer": "Alabama Music Hall of Fame", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What television series was an adaptation of a novel and had a character played by an actress who is also known for her roles on \"ER\" and \"Desparate Housewives\"?", "answer": "\"Pretty Little Liars\"", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "This character in the historical drama legal thriller film \"Bridge o