ptop\"", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "During the Great Depression, which U.S. President dedicated Timberline Lodge in Clackamas County, Oregon?", "answer": "President Franklin D. Roosevelt", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What HBO original series featured an actor who also starred in the 2016 film \"The Pass\"?", "answer": "\"Looking\"", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Wayne B. Sappleton was a star at an institution founded in what year?", "answer": "1870", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "No One Would Tell is based on the true story of Jamie Fuller, who murdered his girlfriend in a city in Essex County, Massachusetts, with a population of what?", "answer": "39,502", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Where is the birthplace of \"Babe\" Hardy?", "answer": "Harlem", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Johnny Mathis Sings included a song that started out as the instrumental title track to a film directed by whom?", "answer": "Blake Edwards", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Both Teide National Park and Garajonay National Park belongs to which country?", "answer": "Spain", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "George Rochberg's Symphony No. 5 was first performed in 1986 under the direction of what Hungarian-born orchestral and operatic conductor?", "answer": "Georg Solti", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "The Tama Maru No. 2 was damaged by what World War II American naval scout plane and dive bomber that was manufactured by Douglas Aircraft?", "answer": "Douglas SBD Dauntless", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which  American actor was real life brother of Joey Lawrence, Matthew Lawrence ", "answer": "Andrew James Lawrence", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "At what frequency the news magazine published in which Ursula Gauthier was reporter in China?", "answer": "weekly", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "In what year was the book published that first talks about biopower?", "answer": "1976", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What episode of South Park was created using 