rook, South Australia?", "answer": "Adelaide Hills Council", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which United States Secretary of War under Franklin Pierce was elected President under the Provisional Confederate States Constitution?", "answer": "Jefferson Davis", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Who released the singles \"I Hope You Dance\" and \"Call Me Crazy\"?", "answer": "Lee Ann Womack", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What is the birthday of the woman Romy Ruyssen fought in the first Invicta Fighting Championships?", "answer": "March 31, 1981", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Of the cities Abdiel V\u00e1zquez has lived in, which one was the capital of Nuevo Leon?", "answer": "Monterrey", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What are the masks that Bill Johnson's character in the 1986 horror film made of?", "answer": "human skin", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Are Miles Kane and The Libertines from England?", "answer": "yes", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "To whom did J. Walter Duncan sell the USFL team who played home games at Giants Stadium in 1983?", "answer": "Donald Trump", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What genre is the Dumb and Dumber Moive?", "answer": "gross-out humor", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What is the population of the small town with an Air Force Base 7 mi northeast of Sacramento, California?", "answer": "743", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which Magnolia actor was also a United States Navy Combat veteran in World War II?", "answer": "Jason Robards", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What sitcom aired on NBC and Yahoo had a character named Michelle Slater (played by American actress Lauren Stamile)?", "answer": "Community", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Are Veronica and Ulex both in the flowering plant family?", "answer": "yes", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "What state is Ruxton Park and Pikes Peak located in?", "answer": "Colorado", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "The satellite Bianca is named after the sister of Kath