 many research areas of computing science who held the Schlumberger Centennial Chair in Computer Sciences at the University of Texas at Austin from 1984 until his retirement in 1999, he was a professor of mathematics (1962\u20131984), at which university of technology located in Eindhoven, Netherlands?", "answer": "Eindhoven University of Technology", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Where was the rock band whose song released in June 2001 that topped the Adult 40 for 23 weeks from?", "answer": "Los Angeles, California", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "July 31, 1912 this Nobel Prize winner in Economic Sciences founded EdChoice?", "answer": "Milton Friedman", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What year was the band who released Signs of Light formed?", "answer": "2009", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What type of game are both Total Overdoes and Chili Con Carnage?", "answer": "third-person shooter", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Who is the president of organization that Forrest Griffin vs. Stephan Bonnar was thought to be one of the greatest fights in history?", "answer": "Dana White", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which ReDRagon member was born on March 1, 1987 ?", "answer": "Kyle O'Reilly", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which American black comedy film did Peter Berg directed ", "answer": "Very Bad Things", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What film with actor Barry Keoghan was selected to compete for the Palme d'Or?", "answer": "Killing of a Sacred Deer", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What day of the week did a Finnish children's TV show shown from 1961 to 1968 about brids also known as psittacines of the roughly 393 species in 92 genera that make up the order Psittaciformes?", "answer": "Sunday", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Jim Bambra has contributed to which single-player role-playing gamebooks?", "answer": "Fighting Fantasy", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Who has more citizenship, Ferenc Moln\u00e1r or Orhan Pamuk?", "answer": "Ferenc Moln