bsite Heeb?", "answer": "America's Civil War", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Who has received more medals, Andrei Okounkov or Valery Goppa?", "answer": "Andrei Yuryevich Okounkov", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "The Irish Mob existing since the early 19th century is said to have murdered which Lebanese American bookmaker from South Boston? ", "answer": "Louis R. Litif", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "The republican senator who got re-elected in the 996 United States Senate election in Oklahoma was born on which day ?", "answer": "November 17, 1934", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Born in 1976, what German-American actress was part of the voice cast in The Galapagos Affair: Satan Came to Eden?", "answer": "Diane Kruger", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What is the nationality of the author of \"Play Dirty\"?", "answer": "American", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Who was formed first,The Used orBlessid Union of Souls ?", "answer": "Blessid Union of Souls", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "What is a Japanese anime series and the sixth \"Pretty Cure\" installment by Izumi Todo, Otra Pel\u00edcula de Huevos y un Pollo or Fresh Pretty Cure! ?", "answer": "Fresh Pretty Cure!", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Jo Seung-woo, is a South Korean actor, he is best known for his leading roles in Inside Men, released in which year, is a South Korean neo noir political crime action film written and directed by Woo Min-ho based on Yoon Tae-ho's webtoon \"The Insiders\"?", "answer": "2015", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What was the pro-slavery group called that Silas Soule clashed with?", "answer": "\"Border Ruffians\"", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Guy Walters competed against which former professional boxer that is a two-weight world champion?", "answer": "Virgil Hill", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Who directed the Indian crime action film which  Ram Sampath composed song for ", "answer": "Rahul Dholakia", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Mark of the Gorilla is 1950 Jungle Jim film that starred an actor best known for playing which character ?", "answer": "Tarzan", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Are Anthony Himbs and David Hewlett both Canadian?", "answer": "no", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "What Richie Valen cover did Selena sing?", "answer": "\"La Bamba\"", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "] Moose Pond is located in a town with a population of what at the 2010 census?", "answer": "391", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Who is Harry's nemesis in the Half-Blood Prince?", "answer": "Lord Voldemort", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "In Norway, Pinnekj\u00f8tt, Stick Meat, is a main course dinner dish of lamb or mutton, this dish is largely associated with the celebration of Christmas, served with pur\u00e9ed swede and potatoes, beer and Akvavit, is a flavoured spirit, that has been produced since the 15th century, principally produced in which country?", "answer": "Scandinavia", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Godspeed, was under Captain Bartholomew Gosnold, an English lawyer, explorer, and privateer who was instrumental in founding of which organization?", "answer": "Virginia Company of London", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Are James Merrill and James Joyce both American poets?", "answer": "no", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Which opera had more acts: Madama Butterfly (original) or Rigoletto?", "answer": "Rigoletto", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Who was the director of the 1968 Metrocolor Cold War era suspense and espionage film that had its screenplay written by the novelist who wrote under the pseudonym Ian Stuart?", "answer": "John Sturges", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Nayo Wallace portrayed the character of Sarabi in a musical directed by who ?", "answer": "Julie Taymor", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Katie Aselton and Toni Collette star alongside American comedian, who describes herself as \u201calt-cabaret provocateur?\u201d", "answer": "Bridget Everett", "type