n American film editor who has worked with the director for over forty years, edit all the films? ", "answer": "Martin Scorsese", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which brand belongs to the elder brother of the owners of Adidas ?", "answer": "Puma", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Rosa Rio providedsilent film soundtrack accompaniment for which English comic actor?", "answer": "Charlie Chaplin", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What was expanded by the US bicameral legislature by the Federal-Aid Highway Act of 1968?", "answer": "Interstate Highway System", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Frodingham TMD is a depot located to the east of a railway station that serves what town?", "answer": "Scunthorpe in North Lincolnshire, England", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Who ran for the Michigan gubernatorial election in 2006 and was a CEO?", "answer": "Dick DeVos", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What is the name of the leguminous tree that creates the flavor Imli for the digestive tablet Hajmola?", "answer": "Tamarind", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which actor starred in Dr. Cabbie and \"The Big Bang Theory\"?", "answer": "Kunal Nayyar", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "The Mega Powers were a tag team in the World Wrestling Federation (WWF) and World Championship Wrestling (WCW), the Mega Powers consisted of Hulk Hogan, and \"Macho Man\" Randy Savage with who, that was an American professional wrestling manager and occasional professional wrestler?", "answer": "Miss Elizabeth", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Who was an English Lawyer and statesman and also has close links with Patrick Barnewall?", "answer": "Thomas Cromwell", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What adult fiction book by Kat Spears in based on a play 1897 by Edmond Rostand?", "answer": "Sway", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "ANCAP is a state-owned company involved in the production of a basic ingredient of concrete which was patented in what year?", "answer": "1824", "type": "bridge"}, {"question":