vania has been served by whom since 2003?", "answer": "Tim Murphy", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "The Missouri Rhineland is a geographical area located mostly in a valley that is how long?", "answer": "2300 mi", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Kindada Jones' is the daughter of composer Quincy Jones and what 1970 Golden Globe Winner for Best Actress in a Television Drama? ", "answer": "Peggy Lipton", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "The 34th Annual Tony Awards were co-hosted by the actor who was a combat veteran in which war?", "answer": "World War II", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which baroque composer wrote for the King's Theatre in Haymarket?", "answer": "George Frideric Handel", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What film studio made both The Island at the Top of the World and The Love Bug?", "answer": "Walt Disney Productions", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "What position did the Diyawadana Nilame of the Temple of Sacred Tooth Relic hold from 1900 - 1964?", "answer": "Ceylonese legislator", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What began in 1653 and was lead by the Lord protector of the Commonwealth of England, Scotland, and Ireland?", "answer": "The Protectorate", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Letters from a Porcupine was a documentary about a rock band formed where?", "answer": "Los Angeles, California", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "The Torbreck Home Units were the first high-rise and mix-use residential development in Queensland, Australia, one of these heritage-listed home units are located at which capital of and most populous city in the Australian state of Queensland, and the third most populous city in Australia?", "answer": "Brisbane", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Terttu Nevalainen, is a Finnish linguist and the current Chair of English Philology at which organization, Nevalainen works on the History of English, English is a West Germanic language that originated from Anglo-Frisian dialects brought to Britain in the mid 5th to 7th c