ican television drama series in which Michael Gladis played a role as Paul Kinsey?", "answer": "thirteen", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "The song \"Smile\" from 1st Round was composed by an actor of what nationality?", "answer": "English", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Turbulence or turbulent flow can be characterized by which branch of  mathematics?", "answer": "Chaos theory", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Segugio Italiano and Swedish Vallhund, are breeds of what animal?", "answer": "dog", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Are both Peng Shuai and Daniel Nestor professional sports players?", "answer": "yes", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Rugby union at the 1979 South Pacific Games was held in Fiji at the newly renovated National Stadium in which southeast coastal city on the island of Viti Levu?", "answer": "Suva", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What song did a Jamaican singer, songwriter, supermodel, record producer, and actress release in 1983?", "answer": "Living My Life", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Joseph E. \"Jeb\" Bradley (born October 20, 1952) is an American politician and member of the Republican Party who currently serves as the Majority Leader of the New Hampshire Senate, the New Hampshire Senate has been meeting since when?", "answer": "1784", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Are the band \"Soda Stereo\" and \"Alanis Morissette\" from the same country?", "answer": "no", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "When was the magazine with which Matsuko Deluxe began his work established? ", "answer": "November 1994", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "IN what city were stations WAAM-TV and WJZ-TV located?", "answer": "Baltimore", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What club does Curt Schilling hold the highest strikeout-to-walk ratio of any of its members?", "answer": "the 3,000-strikeout club", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": " Der B\u00e4renh\u00e4uter was influenced by the German composer who created which opera?", "answer": "\"Hansel 