ot\u00e1", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "The Finer Things was written by which rock and blues English musician?", "answer": "Stephen Lawrence \"Steve\" Winwood", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Are Great Dane and Westphalian Dachsbracke both breeds of dog", "answer": "yes", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Are 919 Third Avenue and the Morgan Stanley Building located in the same area of New York?", "answer": "yes", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Shadow Warriors was a British comedy power metal band, formed in late which year, by Ian Samuel \"Sam\" Totman, an English-New Zealand musician, best known as the guitarist and the main songwriter for the power metal band DragonForce?", "answer": "2000", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which National Basketball Association team in Phoenix, Arizona did Kyle Robert Macy play for? ", "answer": "The Phoenix Suns", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What is the nationality of the chef and restaurateur featured in Restaurant: Impossible?", "answer": "English", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "The Honda XL350R is a dual-sport motorcycle made by Honda in 1984\u20131985, both \"Cycle\" and which motorcycling magazine in the United States, ranked it as one of the ten best motorcycles of 1985?", "answer": "Cycle World", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Clive Lloyd was replaced as captain for one match during 1983-84 by which Antiguan?", "answer": "Sir Isaac Vivian Alexander Richards", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Are Joe Elliott and Paul Meany both keyboardists?", "answer": "no", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Does Darlingia or Laurus have more species?", "answer": "Laurus", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "What member of Garin i Giperboloidy was born on June 24, 1963?", "answer": "Yuri Dmitriyevich Kasparyan", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "In what city did the 2009 NASCAR Nationwide Series champion win the 2010 Irwin Tools Night Race?", "answer": "Bristol, Tennessee", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Who founded the Honest Conpnay along with Brian Lee", "answer": "Jessica Alba", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What song by Jessi Colter did Erika Jo sing?", "answer": "\"I'm Not Lisa\"", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "When did Sherry Thomas receive the Romance Writers of America RITA Award for Best Historical Romance?", "answer": "2011", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What is the birthyear of the last born player to cross the Old Firm divide twice?", "answer": "1979", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": " WAXM is a Country-formatted broadcast radio station that serves The Eastern Kentucky Coalfield and what other area?", "answer": "Southwest Virginia", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Who co-directed the eight-episode Danish television mini-series that the American paranormal hospital drama, All Souls, was based on?", "answer": "Lars von Trier and Morten Arnfred", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Patrick Galbraith and Ilie N\u0103stase are famous for playing what sport?", "answer": "tennis", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "What is the name of the satirical program on Comedy Central that stars an American comedian, television host, and actor who also appeared in the 2005 American romantic comedy \"Bewitched\"?", "answer": "The Colbert Report", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Ghostbusters II starred which Canadian-American actor and comedian?", "answer": "Frederick Allan \"Rick\" Moranis", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "The song \"Partyman\" by which artist appears in the Batman movie as Joker defaces the exhibits in Gotham City?", "answer": "Prince", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Are I Lombardi alla prima crociata and Giasone both operas?", "answer": "yes", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "\"Alvin for President\" is a song by which American animated fictional musical group?", "answer": "Alvin and the Chipmunks", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What is the name of the album by the wife of saxophonist Jim Tomlinson which includes four songs with lyrics written by Kazuo Ishiguro?", "answer": "Breakfast on the Morning Tram", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Under Cover is the ninth studio album by heavy metal vocalist Ozzy Osbourne, additional songs on this album which are not featured include which song written and performed, by John Lennon from his 1980 album \"Double Fantasy\"?", "answer": "Woman", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Were Robert Wise and Stuart Gillard both actors in films in the 20th century?", "answer": "no", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "The singer who released the 1986 album Girls Like Me was born in what year?", "answer": "1958", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "The Concerns of a Citizen was written by which Republican party politician?", "answer": "George Wilcken Romney", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Are both Elizabeth Jane Howard and Patrick White from the same country?", "answer": "no", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Emdadul Haque Milon is an archer from a country with what capital?", "answer": "Dhaka", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Is the Caribbean the homeland of both Jean Rhys and Adolfo Bioy Casares?", "answer": "no", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "The 2015 Segunda Divisi\u00f3n play-offs took place in June 2015 and has determined the third team which will be promoted to which season that started on 21 August 2015 and concluded on 15 May 2016?", "answer": "2015\u201316 La Liga", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Chioma Ubogagu plays for what professional women's soccer team based in Orlando?", "answer": "Orlando Pride", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What race in china allows speeds up to 260 km/h on 6.2km of streets?", "answer": "Guia Race of Macau", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "When was the Nothing More album that had the song \"Go to War\" released?", "answer": "September 15, 2017", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Auguste Laurent discovered what aromatic organic compound with the molecular formula CHOH?", "answer": "Phenol", "type": "bridge"}, {"question"