cated in Caithness, Scotland, and west of John o' Groats?", "answer": "Castle of Mey", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Were both Swann v. Charlotte-Mecklenburg Board of Education and Abington School District v. Schempp based on racial questions?", "answer": "no", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "What raid project will include five new underground stations under St Kilda Road?", "answer": "Melbourne Metro Rail Project", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "The 2017 British GT Championship will be the 25th British GT Championship, a sports car championship promoted by the St\u00e9phane Ratel Organisation (SRO), it will occur at which motor racing track in the village of Little Budworth, Cheshire, England?", "answer": "Oulton Park Circuit", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which American bassist and founding member of Return to Forever also founded the band Animal Logic?", "answer": "Stanley Clarke", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What is the name of this video game franchise, focusing on multi colored birds, created by a Finnish developer, publisher, distributor of video games and entertainment company headquartered in Espoo, Finland?", "answer": "Angry Birds", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Who developed the television series of which the fifteenth episode of the second season was \"Wrath of the Villains: Mad Grey Dawn\"?", "answer": "Bruno Heller", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Cornelis Gerrit \"Kees\" van der Staaij, is a Dutch politician of the Reformed Political Party, he has been an MP since 19 May 1998 and focuses on matters including Kingdom relations of which location, commonly known as the Netherlands, is a sovereign state and constitutional monarchy with the large majority of its territory in western Europe and several small islands in the Caribbean Sea, in the West Indies islands (Leeward Islands / Lesser Antilles)?", "answer": "Kingdom of the Netherlands", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What  capitol city is the  Jordan banking and financial sci