e for what American motorcycle manufacturer that was founded in Milwaukee, Wisconsin?", "answer": "Harley-Davidson, Inc.", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Are New York Woman and New Idea, from Australia, both weekly publications?", "answer": "no", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Does Jet or Real Simple come out more times in a year?", "answer": "Jet", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Are James Glickenhaus and Eric Red both automotive entrepreneurs?", "answer": "no", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Between Brad Anderson and Bernard Vorhaus, who had more diverse work experiences?", "answer": "Brad Anderson", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Where was the man who won the gold medal in the competitions held from September 20 to October 1, 1991, in Cairo, Egypt born?", "answer": "Windhoek", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Who wrote and directed \"Tiger and Crane Fist\", a parody of a martial arts film, which usually contain numerous martial arts fights?", "answer": "Steve Oedekerk", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which movie starring Peter Capaldi is set to release on 10 November 2017?", "answer": "Paddington 2", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Where is the institute formerly directed by food technologist Vishweshwaraiah Prakash located?", "answer": "foothills of the Chamundi Hills", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Tom Who is the editor of the Nature Photonics where American physicist Tom Baehr-Jones has been published in?", "answer": "Oliver Graydon", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Robert Covington, and injured 76er during the 2016-17 season, attanded which college basketball program?", "answer": "Tennessee State University", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What is the name of this singer who released several albums with her country music singer daughter that worked with Mark Selby?", "answer": "Naomi", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "In 1924  E. C. Rhodes became Reader at a university founded in what year?", "answer": "1895", "type": "bridge