e two roles of the writer of Father to a Sister of Thought?", "answer": "lead singer and guitarist", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What type of soprano was Emma Matthews famous for?", "answer": "lyric soprano is a type of operatic soprano voice", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "How many council members serve alongside Jim Strickland?", "answer": "thirteen", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "The Broadmeadows railway station is situated on the boundary of Elizabeth North and a suburb that was formed as part of a merger in what year?", "answer": "1993", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "An American country music singer known for his flashy Nudie and Manuel suits and blond pompadour recorded an album with which American entertainer in 1974?", "answer": "Dolly Parton", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Who was the employer of the cartoonist who drew \"Little Nemo\"?", "answer": "William Randolph Hearst", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "808 peaked at number eight on what?", "answer": "Billboard\" Hot 100", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Roy Nielsen and Max Manus both were a resistance fighter/member of what World War?", "answer": "World War II", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Before Chop Socky Chooks what episode did Mike Kubat receive a Leo Award for?", "answer": "\"Spindly Tam Kanushu\"", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Ramakrishna Pillai, (1878\u20131916) was a nationalist writer, journalist, editor, and political activist, Karl Marx (1912) are among his most noted works in Malayalam, the first ever biography of Karl Marx in any Indian language, which languages spoken in India belong to several language families, the major ones being the Indo-Aryan languages spoken by 75% of Indians and the Dravidian languages spoken by what percentage, of Indians?", "answer": "20%", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "When did the American retired professional basketball player born who won NBA Sixth Man of the Year Award with Manu Gin\u00f3bili and Jason Terry?", "answer": "Novem