ortland Press Herald", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which took place longer in 1945, Battle of Luzon or Operation Undertone?", "answer": "Battle of Luzon", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "What did a niece of Cissy Houston became a United Nations Global Ambassador for?", "answer": "the Food and Agriculture Organization", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "A historic neighborhood in the Kentucky city originally called Lebanon was added to the U.S. National Register of Historic Places on which date?", "answer": "June 7, 1978", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "The actress who stars in the 1999 film \"Universal Soldier: The Return\" has her own show on which network?", "answer": "ESPN", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "In which city did Michel Hugo become a professor?", "answer": "Paradise, Nevada", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What game featured In the Streets to Africa?", "answer": "action-adventure video game", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "When did Reinhold Niebuhr write \"Moral Man and Immoral Society\" and argue Christian Realism?", "answer": "the twentieth century", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "The first televised speech in the House of Commons of the United Kingdom was made by a politician that was assassinated by what group?", "answer": "Provisional Irish Republican Army", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which politician was once a Lieutenant Governor of Kentucky and a mayor in Louisville?", "answer": "Jerry Edwin Abramson", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Confrontation Camp is an American rap rock group consisting of many members, including which American DJ and turntablist?", "answer": "DJ Lord", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What postmaster was the indirect namesake of Urge Overkill's second EP?", "answer": "Sylvester Stull", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "How many people are employed by the laboratory across from McKenzie, Maryland?", "answer": "some 1,000", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "On what team did Taylor Griffin's younger b