orthern German?", "answer": "Laurids Rudebeck", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What film was the song for which Sukhwinder Singh won the Best Male Playback Award?", "answer": "Dil Se", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "She's Leaving Home was from the album released on what date?", "answer": "26 May 1967", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Among India's oldest universities founded in 1918, Osmania University is in which city?", "answer": "Hyderabad", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What year was the university Steve Cole is a professor at founded?", "answer": "1885", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Who magazine is based in Milan, Italy Donna Moderna or Parents?", "answer": "Donna Moderna", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Vishwavir Ahuja is the CEO of what scheduled commercial bank that is headquartered in Maharashtra, India?", "answer": "RBL Bank Limited", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "2015 Idlib offensive refers to a series of rebel operations and is mentioned in the English-language weekly magazine-format newspaper edited where?", "answer": "London", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which style of minimalist furniture and housewares from Denmark associated was Hans J. Wegner, one of the leading figures of its movement ", "answer": "Danish modern", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What is the nickname of the radio presenter who has a show on an FM band radio station in Sydney Australia with a target market of people aged 39-54?", "answer": "\"The Love God\"", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Who directed the film where the actor who played Gandalf played Cogsworth?", "answer": "Bill Condon", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Clive Dunn is the cousin of which English actress and dancer?", "answer": "Gretchen Franklin", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which Stephen King novel did the name of the band Ad Sluijter contributed to come from? ", "answer": "The Eyes of the Dragon", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "My Life as a Fake is a 2003 novel by Australian writer Peter Carey based on the Ern Malley hoax of 1943, in which two poets created a fictitious poet, Ern Malley, and submitted poems in his name to which Australian literary and artistic avant-garde movement of the 1940s, and name of this magazine?", "answer": "Angry Penguins", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "In what year was the 76th Guards Air Assault Division involved in the January Events?", "answer": "1991", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which magazine, Nintendo Power or Armchair General, was produced by Weider History Group?", "answer": "Armchair General", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "An American twin-engine attack helicopter that was developed for the United States Marine Corps as part of the H-1 upgrade program is also called what when based on the ICAO phonetic alphabet pronunciation of it's variant letter? ", "answer": "Zulu Cobra", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What is the name of the musician who wrote \"That's the Way God Planned It\" and released an album called \"Everybody Likes Some Kind of Music\"?", "answer": "Billy Preston", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Christine Ebersole appeared on Broadway in what musical, based on a 1975 documentary?", "answer": "Grey Gardens", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Syed Ali Raza Usama and Dionciel Armstrong, have which occupation in common?", "answer": "Film Director", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "What nationality was the character portrayed by Richard Heinrich Ludwig M\u00fcnch in \"Patton\" (1970)?", "answer": "German", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Martha Ellen Reeves got her masters at a university located in which US state ?", "answer": "Missouri", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Cydista and Pachystegia, are related to what?", "answer": "shrubs", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Texas v. White and United States v. Curtiss-Wright Export Corp. were argued in what court?", "answer": "The Supreme Court", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "What railway routes connecting two major cities in the North West of England are included in the City Line?", "answer": "Liverpool\u2013Manchester lines", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "For what NBC sketch comedy is the creator of 30 Rock best known?", "answer": "\"Saturday Night Live\"", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "When did Denmark lose control of Frederiknagore?", "answer": "until 1845, when their alliance with a defeated France led to the colony being ceded to the British East Indian company.", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Does Sansha contain more islands than Xingning, Guangdong?", "answer": "yes", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Did the bands Twenty One Pilots and Catherine Wheel both perform on tour?", "answer": "yes", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "In which year was this American actor, director, writer, producer, dancer and musician born who directed the film \"One, Two, Many?\"", "answer": "1965", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What cultural region in County Galway, Ireland, is where Irish writer of thrillers and television screenplays, Manning O'Brine, was born?", "answer": "Connemara", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "When was the General of American Civil War born who established Camp Smith?", "answer": "September 21, 1825", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What type of music did the pianist who wrote the original music score to The Incredible Shrinking Woman find early success with?", "answer": "innovative electronic music", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Who was the son of the ruling king of the second largest city in Afghanistan", "answer": "Vasudeva of Kabul", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "The team captains the British game show Insert Name Here are Richard Osman and another comedian who was born in what year?", "answer": "1983", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which five other actors hosted the 30th Tony Awards in 1976 alongside the actor nominated for an Academy Award for Best Supporting Actor for his performance in Roman Holiday?", "answer": "Richard Burto