ies, Worsleya or Gordonia?", "answer": "Gordonia", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "One of the most successful Hindi playback singers, worked with three other singers on the remix of what?", "answer": "Bachna Ae Hasseeno", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "In 2007 Rand Hummel  was named Director of THE WILDS of New England located in what county?", "answer": "Hillsborough County", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which mathematician contributed most to the decidability of various algebraic groups, Anatoly Maltsev or Semyon Aranovich Gershgorin?", "answer": "Anatoly Ivanovich Maltsev", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "What is the name of the lowest road in Great Britain, that crosses through the village and civil parish in the Fens of England?", "answer": "A1101 road", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Operation Y and Shurik's Other Adventures was a film starring which actor, director, and scriptwriter?", "answer": "Yevgeny Alexandrovich Morgunov", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What is the given name of the founder of the activist group that protested the trial of Geert Wilders?", "answer": "Stephen Christopher Yaxley-Lennon", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Who has more occupations related to movies, Walter Lang or Scott Derrickson?", "answer": "Scott Derrickson", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Which character created by Brian K. Vaughan and Adrian Alphona has control of a vehicle in the form of a large frog?", "answer": "Chase Stein", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Born January 21, 1963 this professional basketball player was named \"Sixth Man of The Year\" in the 1991-92 season, ", "answer": "Detlef Schrempf", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What British Politician, who was the Prime Minister of the Unted Kingdom, was the person who forced a resignation from PAtrick Mercer?", "answer": "David Cameron", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Live at the Sex Machine included a track sampled by the group of what nationality in \"Smack My Bitch Up\"?", "a