lications?", "answer": "no", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "What is the name of this 2008 American superhero film based on the Marvel Comics character of the same name, in which Jeff Bridges earned an Academy Award nomination for his role in the film?", "answer": "Iron Man", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What is the nationality of the man who founded Fly Eye Records?", "answer": "Scottish", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Are Panzhou and Shunde District in the same country?", "answer": "yes", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "\"Candy\" is the debut single of an singer that starred with Diane Keaton in a 2007 romantic comedy directed by who?", "answer": "Michael Lehmann", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which 1917 British silent drama film stars the professional boxer with the nickname \"The Mighty Atom\"?", "answer": "A Pit Boy's Romance", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Outside The Nine is the official fan club of a metal band from what state?", "answer": "Iowa", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Who was born first Kevin Reynolds or Jan Bucquoy?", "answer": "Jan Bucquoy", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Who was president of The King's College and directed a film with John Sullivan?", "answer": "Dinesh D'Souza", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which country's former capital hosts the Simba Sports Club?", "answer": "Tanzania", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "How To Pick Up Girls is the 1978 made for TV movie filmed on location in which city, starring Desi Arnaz Jr., an American actor and musician and the son of Lucille Ball?", "answer": "New York City", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "John Ratzenberger's \"Made in America\" has visited a variety of factories, including a company that since 1984 has been a wholly owned subsidiary of who?", "answer": "Hallmark Cards", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Under what union did the king who created Duchy of Holstein serve?", "answer": "the Kalmar Union", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "The O'Reilly Fact