ctor who has received six Laurence Olivier Awards, and a Golden Globe award, and has received how many Oscar nominations?", "answer": "two", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which Hesitation Wounds band member toured with Bruce Springsteen's band in 2009?", "answer": "Jay Weinberg", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "which American writer does Jean Graham  research on", "answer": "Amy Tan", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "The One-Million-Liter Test Sphere \u2014 also known as the Test Sphere, the Horton Test Sphere, the Cloud Study Chamber, Building 527, and the \u201cEight Ball\u201d (or \u201c8-ball\u201d) \u2014 is a decommissioned biological warfare (BW) chamber and testing facility located on which United States Army Medical Command installation located in Frederick, Maryland?", "answer": "Fort Detrick", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What 1992 Circle-Vision 360\u00b0 film presented at three Disney parks around the world opened it's attraction on April 2, 2007 in the Tomorrowland section? ", "answer": "The Timekeeper", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What is is a United States federal statute enacted by the 111th United States Congress and signed into law by President Barack Obama, who at the time the Deputy White House Chief of Staff for Implementation for U.S. President Barack Obama made this one of her major projects?", "answer": "The Patient Protection and Affordable Care Act", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "How old was Kipling when he wrote The Ballad of the \"Clampherdown\"", "answer": "December 1865", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Are both Ride a Wild Pony and A Goofy Movie produced by Walt Disney affiliated companies?", "answer": "yes", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "What airline does the airline alliance Oneworld share their terminal with at the The Heathrow Airport?", "answer": "Virgin Atlantic", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What brothers are known for How Six Made Their Way in the World and Grimms' Fairy Tales?", "answer": "Jacob and