kle who played collegiately at what university?", "answer": "Oklahoma", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Dressed to Kill Tour was by Cher in support of what album?", "answer": "Closer to the Truth", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What date did the television series first air in which \"Shareholder Meeting\" is an episode?", "answer": "March 24, 2005", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "No Exit and Cup-A-Jo Productions have what in common?", "answer": "theatre", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What type of living organisms are represented by the genus Mandragora, whose members are known as mandrakes, and Physostegia or the lionshearts native to North America?", "answer": "plants", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "The Jackson 5, a popular American family music group formed in 1964 but in which year did the younger band member Michael Jackson pursue a solo career while still part of the group?", "answer": "1971", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Are The Badgemand and Finger Eleven both from Canada?", "answer": "no", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "In what War did the father of Princess Christina Margarethe of Hesse die?", "answer": "World War II", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Jack Scrimshaw debuted at the match held at what stadium in Westcourt, Cairns?", "answer": "Cazaly's Stadium", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Are Adam Gontier and Coko of the same nationality?", "answer": "no", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Did both Kanni and Bloodhound originate in the same continent?", "answer": "no", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Who is Scott Weiland associated with?", "answer": "Stone Temple Pilots", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "The Wrecking Crew, released in December, 1968, and starring Dean Martin, an American singer, actor, comedian, and film producer, Martin was nicknamed what, for his seemingly effortless charisma and self-assurance?", "answer": "King of Cool", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Singer Crystal Gayle\u2019s single, \"Hello I