": "Analytics", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What deathcore band is from Knoxville, Tennessee that Misery Chastain toured with?", "answer": "Whitechapel", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which professional basketball player won a NBA championship and spoke positively on the book \"the 21 irrefutable laws of leadership\"?", "answer": "Harrison Barnes", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": " Where is a multi-use indoor arena, that was opened byan English ice dancer who won a gold medal at the 1984 Winter Olympics, located at?", "answer": "National Ice Centre", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which hierarcchiologist believed It states that the selection of a candidate for a position is based on the candidate's performance in their current role, rather than on abilities relevant to the intended role?", "answer": "Laurence J. Peter", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Who is a two-time winner of the Pulitzer Prize and the National Book Award and a recipient of the Presidential Medal of Freedom, Antonin Artaud or David McCullough? ", "answer": "David Gaub McCullough", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Lawrence Turman, currently the director of the peter Stark Program at the University of Southern California produced an American adventure crime-thriller film starring Joseph Mazzello as who? ", "answer": "Roarke", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Tangled in Reins is the second album by a rock band that is based in Norwalk, Connecticut, and was formed in what year?", "answer": "1990", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What character does Deborah Joy Winans play in the American television drama series, created by Craig Wright?", "answer": "Charity", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Who owns the hotel whose replica statue of liberty featured on the Statue of Liberty Forever stamp ?", "answer": "MGM Resorts International.", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "From which French philosopher's work did John Maus derive the title of the album whose positive response caused him to grow more widely accepted as an outsider artist?", "answer": "Alain Badiou", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "On which channel did a television series air in 2015 that starred the main vocalist of the South Korean girl group Apink?", "answer": "KBS2", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Lauryn Hill was a member of which hip hop group?", "answer": "Fugees", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "San Jacinto Day is the celebration of the Battle of San Jacinto in what year?", "answer": "1836", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "The Pass Christian School District is a public school district, based in which city in Harrison County, Mississippi, United States?", "answer": "Pass Christian", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "The re-release of \"Panda\" by Desiigner and \"The Life of Pablo\" by Kanye West were both released in what month?", "answer": "February", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Who directed a 2015 Indian Tamil action comedy film with music from an Indian musical duo based in Chennai, Tamil Nadu?", "answer": "Sundar C.", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Who created and served as the executive producer of the show in which Jonathan turner reprised in 2015?", "answer": "Michael Jacobs", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What is the name of the metalcore band from Orange County, CA who album was produced by David Bendeth?", "answer": "Of Mice & Men", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Eye for an Eye is a 1996 American psychological thriller film starring an American actor who currently stars in what HBO sci-fi drama series?", "answer": "Westworld", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Cliff Bennett and the Rebel Rousers are a 1960s British rhythm and blues, soul and beat group who had two Top 10 hits, one being, Got to Get You into My Life, a song by who, first released in 1966 on the album \"Revolver\"?", "answer": "Beatles", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Da'Sean Butler was drafted 42nd overall by the Miami Heat in an NBA draft held at what venue?", "answer": "Theatre at Madison 