d Hello Sleepwalkers have the same number of band members?", "answer": "yes", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Ron Baxter is a former basketball forward for a team that currently competes in what conference?", "answer": "the Big 12", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Nikos Sofis attended which multi-campus private business school with headquarters in Switzerland?", "answer": "EU Business School", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Donald Molosi won an award for his performance as the first President of what country in \"Blue, Black and White\"?", "answer": "Botswana", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Mario Parga appeared in which San Jose-based guitar magazine?", "answer": "Guitar Player", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Who is a member of more bands, Geoff Rickly or Denis B\u00e9langer?", "answer": "Geoffrey William \"Geoff\" Rickly", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "The term \"\u02bb ula-\u02bb ai-h\u0101wane\" is a Hawaiian phrase translating to \"red [bird] that eats \"h\u0101wane\", it was only ever reported from the forested mountains of  Kohala, Hawaii, Kohala, is the name of the northwest portion of the island of Hawai\u02bb i, in which location?", "answer": "Hawaiian Archipelago", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "When did the original location of The History of Ranching mural eventually close?", "answer": "2001", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Who was the brother of 16th century poet group the Wilton Circle's leader?", "answer": "Philip Sidney", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "The cover art for EA Sports UFC 2 features Ronda Rousey and a boxer born in what year?", "answer": "1988", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Are \"Woman's World\" and \"The Delineator\" both American women's magazines?", "answer": "yes", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Who has more work to be known for, Bill Melendez or Garry Marshall?", "answer": "Garry Kent Marshall", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Who has the most series Momina Duraid or Hiroshi Inagaki?", "answe