r": "Chase Manhattan Corporation", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "The December 1992 nor'easter produced record high tides and snowfall across which country's northeastern region, along the Maryland coast, the storm was less severe than the Perfect Storm in the previous year, 1991, also known as The No-Name Storm (especially in the years immediately after it took place) and the Halloween Gale, was a nor'easter that absorbed Hurricane Grace and ultimately evolved back into a small unnamed hurricane late in its life cycle?", "answer": "United States", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which corporation produces this brand that first appeared in 1928 in the United States and whose concept car released in 1995 could fit two passengers and had a space for a laptop on a small table?", "answer": "Chrysler Corporation", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which private, nonsectarian institution has a famous artist featured in major museum solo shows?", "answer": "Pratt Institute", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "At 1972 Prague Skate event, the ladie's title was won by a woman born in what year?", "answer": "1956", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Gina Philips will have a cameo appearance in the 2017 film written and directed by whom?", "answer": "Victor Salva", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Lionel Friedberg and Ralph Staub, have which mutual occupations?", "answer": "director, writer and producer", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": " The Guelphic Legion was a paramilitary unit maintained at the expense of a king whose reign was ended by what?", "answer": "the Unification of Germany", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What is George Miller connection to Mad Max 2", "answer": "Created by director George Miller", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "X.com was an online bank that later became the company that supports what feature?", "answer": "online money transfers", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "The 2004 Philadelphia Eagles season ended with an off-season pickup of the player with what nickname?", "answer": "The Freak", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Castra of Izb\u0103\u0219e\u0219ti was made in this province that was the largest territorial and administrative unit of the empire's territorial possessions outside of Italy until what year", "answer": "293 AD", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Bassist of the band who released Voivod was originally in a band based where? ", "answer": "San Rafael, California", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "How many novels has the author of Sheikh's Castaway written?", "answer": "almost 40", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "In a Front-engine, rear-wheel-drive layout what type of engine is a heat engine where the combustion of a fuel occurs with an oxidizer (usually air) in a combustion chamber that is an integral part of the working fluid flow circuit?", "answer": "An internal combustion engine", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What Austrian Formula One Team advisor works with a company headquartered in Fuschl am See, Austria?", "answer": "Helmut Marko", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Rebecca Akufo-Addo is the current First Lady of Ghana and gets her title by being what relationship to the president?", "answer": "wife", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "K\u00fcbra Kegan was born in the capital of what republic?", "answer": "Turkey", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Where do the bands KMFDM and Empire of the Sun originate from ? ", "answer": "KMFDM (originally Kein Mehrheit F\u00fcr Die Mitleid, loosely translated by the band as \"no pity for the majority\") is an industrial band led by German", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "What is the number one hit released by the rapper also known for his The Streets Made Me album?", "answer": "Slow Motion", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Luzzasco Luzzaschi and Carlo Gesualdo were both composers during which time period?", "answer": "Italian Renaissance", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "In 2015, Baker Mayfield won the Oklahoma starting quarterback position over which future Atlanta Falcons quarterback?", "answer": "Trevor Knight", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Who was born first, Winston Churchill or Edith Hamilton?", "answer": "Edith Hamilton", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "What type of group does Umphrey's McGee and Iron Maiden have in common?", "answer": "band", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What is the name of the Austro-Hungarian general and historian from the province straddling the southern border of the Habsburg Monarchy?", "answer": "Emil Vojnovi\u0107 von Belobreska", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "John Edward Avery, Jr. played for what team that only played one season in 2001", "answer": "XFL", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "In what year was Yuk Young-soo's husband born?", "answer": "1917", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Of which West Germanic language was Craig Seymour a professor at the University of Massachusetts Dartmouth?", "answer": "English", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "when did the Tower Of Terror lose its status as the fastest roller coaster in the world?", "answer": "On opening, it claimed the records of fastest roller coaster in the world, previously shared by and Tower of Terror.", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which group features more members who play an instrument, Moonbabies or Massive Attack?", "answer": "Moonbabies", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Did both Battle of Chancellorsville and Battle of Pusan Perimeter take place on the same continent?", "answer": "no", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Are University of Virginia and King Mongkut's University of Technology Thonburi both institutions of higher learning?", "answer": "yes", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Who co- founded one of the stores that bought out some of the Focus DIY chain?", "answer": "Richard Block and David Quayle", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "PSR B1919+21 is a pulsar with a period of 1.3373 seconds and a pulse width of 0.04 seconds, it was discovered by which Northern Ir