iga trophy in the season that started on 29 August 1998 and finished on 20 June 1999?", "answer": "F\u00fatbol Club Barcelona", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Czes\u0142aw Mi\u0142osz, writter of the 1953 nonfiction \"The Captive Mind\" was professor of Slavic Languages and Literatures at which American University? ", "answer": "University of California, Berkeley", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "what do It's a Small World and Son of Flubber have in common?", "answer": "Walt Disney", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "What year was the original proposer of the dS/CFT correspondence of string theory born?", "answer": "1955", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Where was the author of A Yellow Raft in Blue Water the first Chair of the Native American Studies program?", "answer": "Dartmouth", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "K'ak'upakal was ruler at a pre-columbian city that is located in Tinum Municipality, in what Mexican state?", "answer": "Yucat\u00e1n State", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "The Australian cricket team toured Sri Lanka from 6 August to 20 September 2011, four uncapped players had been named in the Australian Test squad, including Shaun Edward Marsh, an Australian cricketer who plays for the Western Warriors in Australian domestic cricket and has represented Australia at Test, One Day International and Twenty20 International levels, and nicknamed SOS, an acronym of what ?", "answer": "Son of Swampy", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Peng Shuai and Peter Fleming are/were both what?", "answer": "tennis player", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Bertram Mackennal was a sculptor most famous for designing coins and what else featuring King George V of England?", "answer": "stamps", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Are W. B. Yeats and Richard Wilbur of the same nationality?", "answer": "no", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Which Superbowl featured Jack Maitland and was the first to be played on artificial turf?", "answer": "Super Bowl V", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Jon Fratelli and Morten Harket, have which occupation in common?", "answer": "musician", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Both Alexander Sumarokov and Mikhail Lomonosov inaugurated classicism in what?", "answer": "Russian literature", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "\"Purple Rain-Union\" is the sixth episode of the fourth season of the animated comedy series \"Bob's Burgers\", it aired on Fox in the United States on which date, the title of the episode is a reference to the song, film, and album \"Purple Rain\" by Prince?", "answer": "December 1, 2013", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "In what City was the Realpha car based on?", "answer": "Surbiton, Surrey, England", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which feature film directed by Elissa Down casted Rhys Wakefield as Thomas Mollison?", "answer": "The Black Balloon", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What baseball player won the 1987 National League Cy Young Award, Steve Bedrosian or Alek Keshishian?", "answer": "Stephen Wayne Bedrosian", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "The Capitol version of Desolation Boulevard includes what single that was written and produced by Nicky Chinn and Mike Chapman?", "answer": "The Ballroom Blitz", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Who founded the University where Rick Potts received his bachelor's degree?", "answer": "Baptist Minister Russell Conwell", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "The Rome Sand Plains are located 5 mi west of the center of a city located in what congressional district?", "answer": "New York's 22nd congressional district", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "The person who wrote dialogues and lyrics for the Telugu version for Sampoorna Ramayanam received the Sahitya Akademi Award in what year? ", "answer": "1987", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "When was the German former ski jumper who led after the first day at \"FIS Ski Flying World Championships 2002\" born? ", "answer": "9 November 1974", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Blackl