inger", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Of the two plants, Bloomeria and Luculia, which is found in the broader area of land?", "answer": "Luculia", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Who was the coach for two time UFC heavy weight champion with victories over Brock Lesnar and Junior dos Santos?", "answer": "Larry Jamill Kelly", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What is Sacha Baron Cohen's role in Ali G Indahouse?", "answer": "written and performed by comedian", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Was the documentary 500 Years Later released first or was it the documentary Here Is Always Somewhere Else?", "answer": "500 Years Later", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "The title of the TV series Bae Doona is presently in is a play on what word?", "answer": "sensate", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What actor that was born in January 22, 1975 appeared in the film Out in fifty?", "answer": "Balthazar Getty", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What position or purpose does Jean Paul Leroux and M\u00eda Maestro have in common?", "answer": "role", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Rhine Gold is the 2nd album by Copenhagen's Choir of Young Believers. Who is the band leader?", "answer": "Jannis Noya Makrigiannis", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Council Rock was a meeting ground for New York Native Americans, who sometimes had this term used for them incorrectly?", "answer": "Metoac", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Famous lobster Big Jake's health began deteriorating on arrival to what Boston airport?", "answer": "Logan International Airport", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What non-profit organization did one of the builders of the UC1 Freya co-found?", "answer": "Copenhagen Suborbitals", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What 2016 biographical film features the directorial debut of Garth Davis, featuring the Ajay Kapoor actor from Neighbors?", "answer": "Lion", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What is a common ingredient for both a Mimosa cocktail and a Bronx cocktail?", "answer": "orange juice", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Which country was Dora Luz's work in The Three Caballeros premiered in? ", "answer": "Mexico", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Who is Mary, Crown Princess of Denmark's mother-in-law?", "answer": "Queen Margrethe II", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which covered song, whose original version was released in 1969, was featured in Nina Hagen in Ekstasy?", "answer": "Spirit in the Sky", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "\"Movin'\" is a song by Swedish-Congolese singer-songwriter Mohombi, it is the lead singer from his second studio album, \"Universe\", it features Birdman, KMC and \"Movin'\" is a song by Swedish-Congolese singer-songwriter Mohombi, it is the lead singer from his second studio album, \"Universe\", it features Birdman, KMC and Brandon Caskey, an American rapper, from which organization?", "answer": "Cash Money Records", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which actress from Love Rain was also known by the mononym Yoona?", "answer": "Im Yoon-ah", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "The Queen Paola Foundation was started by the whife of which Belgian monarch?", "answer": "King Albert II", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What was the population in 2010 of the town in Maine that all of State Road 206 (SR 206) is located in?", "answer": "1,527", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "The 1955 Scottish League Cup Final was played on 22 October 1955, at Hampden Park, a football stadium in the Mount Florida area of Glasgow, in which country?", "answer": "Scotland", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Crystal arthropathy is a class of joint disorder (called \"arthropathy\"), which acid is characterized by accumulation of tiny crystals in one or more joints. Polarizing microscopy and application of other crystallographic techniques have improved identification of different microcrystals including monosodium urate, what is the heterocyclic compound of carbon, nitrogen, oxygen, and hydrogen with the formula CHNO?"