abinet of a New Jersey governor whose term ended in what year?", "answer": "2018", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Jules Flandrin was a contemporary of what famous French painter known for work associated with Fauvism and Expressionism?", "answer": "Georges Rouault", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What director directed The Prestige, and the 2005 superhero film based on the DC comic book character Batman?", "answer": "Christopher Nolan", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "The city where WKYI-CD is located is the historical and nominal seat of what county?", "answer": "Jefferson County", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "How many costumers do this company have that is a \"global e-learning player\" along with Element K?", "answer": "10,000", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Cell or Kaiser Chiefs, which band was formed first? ", "answer": "Cell", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Marcia Gardner is an Australian screenwriter who has worked on such shows as which Australian television series that premiered on ABC TV on 1 February 2013 at 8:30 pm, and the series stars Craig McLachlan in the lead role of Doctor Lucien Blake?", "answer": "The Doctor Blake Mysteries", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "which Amtrak's flagship service along the Northeast Corridor is  currently the only services in the country", "answer": "Acela Express", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Upwords and Ghettopoly, are both forms of what?", "answer": "board game", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "What do Yangchun and Zaoyang have in common?", "answer": "county-level city", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Kevin Zegers starred in the 2008 crime thriller written and directed by whom?", "answer": "Kari Skogland", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "When was the director of \"Just Married\" born? ", "answer": "July 23, 1968", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "In which country is The Swatch Group and Tourbillion shops mainly based?", "answer": "Switzerland", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": " \"I 