yed by played by Matthew Settle?", "answer": "Ronald Speirs", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": " I Never Knew That About Britain was a TV show with a reporter who has written and appeared in a number of television and radio programmes about what?", "answer": "British history", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Who produced both DC Nation and Beware the Batman?", "answer": "Warner Bros", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Who created a miniseries based on the mathematician Theodore John Kaczynski?", "answer": "Andrew Sodroski", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "The word Consigliere was popularized by a novel written by which author ?", "answer": "Mario Puzo", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Are both Ohio State University and University of Delaware a land-grant institute?", "answer": "yes", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "What is the nickname of the American rapper of Korean descent who is in the trio of Thirsty Fish?", "answer": "Jonathan Park", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which  English actress, author and columnist starred as second wife in Land of the Pharaohs", "answer": "Dame Joan Henrietta Collins", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "5 Magazine featured which professional footballer?", "answer": "Riyad Karim Mahrez", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "what did the maker of Boston Beer Company inherited from his father ", "answer": "brewery on King Street", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "The Winter Line was a series of German and Italian military fortifications in Italy, constructed during World War II by Organisation Todt and commanded by Albert Kesselring,  was a German \"Luftwaffe Generalfeldmarschall\" during which event?", "answer": "World War II", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which is an electropunk band, Mindless Self Indulgence or The Life and Times?", "answer": "Mindless Self Indulgence", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Which player of the NFL football team located in New York was the eleventh draft of the 1980 NFL Draft? ", "answer": "James Zachery", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "In 2009 High and Mighty was sold to a mailorder group headquartered in what city?", "answer": "Manchester, England", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "When was the American actor born who acted as Carl Grimes in \"Judge, Jury, Executioner\"?", "answer": "June 27, 1999", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Author Kurt Vonnegut, who is most famous for his novel Slaughterhouse-Five, created Granfalloon, which is defined as a \"false karass\" in the fictional religion of what?", "answer": "Bokononism", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "From which country came a dance used to convert slaves from a continent that borders the Mediterranean Sea?", "answer": "Guatemala", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "When was the athlete  who won the women's 2013 CrossFit Games born? ", "answer": "14 March 1982", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What was the 2010 Census population of the town located south of the Merrill Shell Bank Light?", "answer": "4,613", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Suite francaise is by what French composer and pianist who is also known for Trois mouvements perpetuels?", "answer": "Francis Jean Marcel Poulenc", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Archermining camp was situated 2 miles southeast of an unincorporated town that had a population of what in the 2010 census?", "answer": "2,478", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "When was the election that the lawyer born on February 29, 1916 lost in New York?", "answer": "November 6, 1962", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Uksuum Cauyai: Drums of Winter, also referred to only as \"Drums of Winter,\" released in which year, is an ethnographic documentary on the culture of the Yup'ik people in Emmonak, a village on the shore of the Bering Sea?", "answer": "1988", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which fighter from WEC 38 is known as the \"busiest\" fighter in the UFC?", "answer": "Donald Cerrone", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "the Ohio Collaborative is a task force created by an American politician who cannot stand for reelection due to what?", "answer": "term limits", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Who holds a World Land Speed Record and named Daniel Jubb \"one of the world's leading rocket scientists\"?", "answer": "Andy Green", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "The Japanese action role-playing game, Rise of Mana, was developed for Sony Interactive Entertainment's PlayStation Vita and what other devices?", "answer": "iOS, Android", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "George Boscawen, 9th Viscount Falmouth is a former officer in which regiment of the British Army ?", "answer": "the Guards Division, Foot Guards regiments", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Friedrich Klose (1862\u20131942) was a German composer, his opera \"Ilsebill\" (1903) is inspired by the music of Richard Wagner and which leading German composer of the late Romantic and early modern eras? ", "answer": "Richard Georg Strauss", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Timothy Gerard Grunhard was  was the offensive line coach for the Kansas Jayhawks representing what university?", "answer": "University of Kansas", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which city was Matthew Wilson, a retired professional Australian road racing cyclist, born in?", "answer": "1 October 1977 in Melbourne, Victoria", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "The Clausius\u2013Clapeyron relation was named after a German physicist and mathematician who is considered one of the central founders of what area of science?", "answer": "the science of thermodynamics", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which neo-soul singer had a debut album entitled There's Nothing Like This?", "answer": "Omar", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Fake Problems and Monoral, play which mutual genre?", "answer": "rock", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Which is taller The Steinway Tower or 126 Madison Avenue building, as planned?", "answer": "The Steinway Tower", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "What is the name of this series of mass executions during World War II, which, along with Sambor Ghetto, was anenexed to the Ukranian SSR?", "answer": "NKVD prisoner massacres", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "\"The Real Slim Shady\" is a song taken from the eighth studio album \"The Marshall Mathers LP 2\" (2013)  of what hip hop recording artist?", "answer": "Eminem", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Emilio Leciguyena was executed by supporters of which Spanish general?", "answer": "Francisco Franco Bahamonde", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Between Haberlea and Aeonium, which genus has more species?", "answer": "Aeonium", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Where is the chain of bookstores located that claims to be the largest independent new and used bookstore in the world and has #1 best-selling small press title of 2013, 2014, and 2015 \"The Do-It-Yourself Guide to Fighting the Big Motherf*ckin' Sad\"?", "answer": "Portland, Oregon", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "The Chamber of Horrors is a 1929 British silent horror film based from one of the attractions in London owned by whom?", "answer": "Madame Tussauds", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What is the stage name of the singer who qualified to perform in the final round of Lithuania in the Eurovision Song Contest 2015, along with  Monika Linkyt\u0117 and Vaidas Baumila?", "answer": "Mia", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What comic strip, created by Robert Crumb, did Manuel \"Manny\" Perez work on later in his career?", "answer": "Fritz the Cat", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Donnette Thayer is a vocalist, guitarist, and songwriter most active in the 1980s and early 1990s indie rock scenes of Northern California, he later formed Hex with Steve Kilbey of The Church, an Australian psychedelic rock band formed in Sydney in which year?", "answer": "1980", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "In what 2013 period drama did Micheal Fassbender win an Empire Award for best supporting actor?", "answer": "12 Years a Slave", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Who sang in more bands, Michael Crafter or Vincent Walker?", "answer": "Michael Crafter", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Between Augusto Roa Bastos and David Mamet, who is a film director?", "answer": "David Alan Mamet", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "What Design Engineer who works at Ride Centerline LLC designed a roller coaster that operates at Six Flags Magic Mountain in Valencia, California?", "answer": "Alan Schilke", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Hollywood Casino is owned by the company based in what Pennsylvania town?", "answer": "Wyomissing", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "In the scandal that received the most attention among food safety incidents, what was the food adulterated with?", "answer": "melamine", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which traditional event that began on 26 December did the Pakistani cricket team replace with a tour of South Africa during the 2012-13 cricket season?", "answer": "Boxing Day Test", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Who did NFL Street 2 feature on their cover had played college football at the University of Miami?", "answer": "Jeremy Charles Shockey", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Who is older, Michael Howard or Clark Johnson?", "answer": "Clark Johnson", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "What precious metal did both McIntyre Mines and the Kemess Mine dig for?", "answer": "gold", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "From which University did the star of the film For Christ's Sake graduate ?", "answer": "San Francisco State University", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which was founded first, the University of Virginia or the University of Nebraska system's first college?", "answer": "The University of Virginia", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "what does Corey I. Sanders and Excalibur Hotel and Casino have in common?", "answer": "MGM Resorts", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Are Lee Gi-kwang and Chad Kroeger from the same country?", "answer": "no", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "What is the capital of the British overseas territory belonging to the Leeward Islands where the Anitlles coqui is found?", "answer": "The Valley", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What paper was presented that includes comediennes that were also TV hosts?", "answer": "The Unkosher Comediennes", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "The 2000 Molson Indy Vancouver was a Championship Auto Racing Teams (CART) motor race held on which date, at Concord Pacific Place in Vancouver, British Columbia, Canada, Paul Anthony Tracy, a Canadian former professional auto racing driver, won the race by less than half a second over his teammate?", "answer": "September 3, 2000", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Q: Who is noted for being the only Eurasian person to be commemorated in Japan's Shinto shrine that is located in Chiyoda, Tokya, Japan?", "answer": "Ry\u014d Kurusu", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What unit was directed by Shiro Ishii and based at the Pingfang district of Harbin?", "answer": "Unit 731", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Henry of Almain was the song of one of the wealthiest men in Europe who joined what?", "answer": "the Barons' Crusade", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Glentham is situated on the road that passes through what three English counties?", "answer": "South Yorkshire, Nottinghamshire and Lincolnshire", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which American former professional basketball player who played for the Bulls, that was featured in NBA Jam 2001?", "answer": "Scottie Pippen", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What is the population of the largest town on Kaua' i?", "answer": "10,699", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Firebird is a retelling of the ballet by which Russian composer?", "answer": "Igor Stravinsky", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "The Talented Mr. Ripley is a 1999 film about what fictional character in a series of crime novels by American novelist Patricia Highsmith, as well as several film adaptations?", "answer": "Tom Ripley", "type": "bridge"}, {"