rgotten Dreams or Call Me Lucky?", "answer": "Cave of Forgotten Dreams", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "What medication, used as chemotherapy and to suppress the immune system, is used as treatment for Autoimmune encephalitis?", "answer": "Cyclophosphamide", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Yoo Ah-in (born Uhm Hong-sik on October 6, 1986) is a South Korean film and television actor, Yoo Ah-in is best known for his leading roles in the coming-of-age film Punch, a South Korean coming-of-age film directed by Lee Han, made in which year, about the budding mentor-mentee relationship forged between a rebellious high school student from a poor household (Yoo Ah-in) and his meddlesome homeroom teacher who moves in next door?", "answer": "2011", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which one has the most species, Titanopsis or Spathiphyllum?", "answer": "Spathiphyllum", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "What is the name of the American action comedy film, that has a 2013 sequel?", "answer": "Red", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "At what hospital did the younger brother of Joey Dunlop die?", "answer": "a Coleraine hospital", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What genre of music do both Doc Hammer and 6 Interpretations have in common?", "answer": "rock", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What contest Did Peter Nalitch known for \"Lost and Forgotten\" place 11th in?", "answer": "Eurovision Song Contest 2010", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "The company that Corexit is an indirect subsidiary of is headquartered in what city?", "answer": "St. Paul, Minnesota", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What county was Josh Gates born in?", "answer": "Essex County", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which of Worldviews Entertainment's films was based on a novel by Tom Rob Smith?", "answer": "Child 44", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "The 1998 American horror film produced and directed by Gus Van Sant was a remake of a film that had an actress win what Golden Globe Award?", "answer": "Best Supporting Actress", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which writer contributing to the comedy film \"Meet Wally Sparks\" is also a stand-up comedian?", "answer": "Rodney Dangerfield", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which band's debut album is named after a hockey played nicknamed \"The Great One\"?", "answer": "Electro Quarterstaff", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "The estranged husband of Francesca von Habsburg was born in what year?", "answer": "1961", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Are Lucia di Lammermoor and The Bartered Bride both comic operas?", "answer": "no", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "What team did Pekka Markkanen's first son play for in addition to the Chicago Bulls?", "answer": "Minnesota Timberwolves", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What two occupations do  Alberto Cavalcanti and Oscar Apfel have in common?", "answer": "film director and producer", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Who created Creature comforts and how many academy awards did he win? ", "answer": "Park has been nominated for an Academy Award a total of six times, and won four with \"Creature Comforts\"", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What Alabama governor ran against Fob James in 1998?", "answer": "Don Siegelman", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What 1948 Heisman Trophy winner and American football player played college football on the same team as quarterback Gilbert Johnson?", "answer": "Doak Walker", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Make Me... is a song for the album that was released on what record imprint?", "answer": "RCA Records", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Who directed the film that  starried Mara Wilson and Trevor Coppola?", "answer": "Danny DeVito", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which of the following is related to the east Asian Chaenomeles: Wulfenia or Pseudocydonia?", "answer": "Pseudocydonia", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "What Canadian Director of Military Operations and Intelligence also served as a senior staff officer in the C