er": "Kvass", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Paul Dean played as lead guitarist for a rock band formed where?", "answer": "Calgary, Alberta", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What is the name of Matthias Egger's university in German?", "answer": "Universit\u00e4t Bern", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What position did American financial services director John Hailer recently retire from in an asset management group related to a large French corporate and investment bank?", "answer": "President and Chief Executive Officer", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "When was the amusement zone founded at which the mummified body of Elmer McCurdy was positively identified in 1976, founded ?", "answer": "1902", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What is the nationality of an author who gave an introduction in the novel Sweets and Other Stories?", "answer": "American", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "The Irton Cross lies chronologically between the Gosforth cross and an Anglo-Saxon cross which probably dates from the 7th or early 8th century, featuring reliefs and inscriptions in what alphabet?", "answer": "runic alphabet", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "On which river is this city that has N'Dolo Airport situated?", "answer": "Congo River", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "In which division does this American professional basketball franchise, based in Wisconsin and founded in 1968, compete, whose former members include Ruben Patterson?", "answer": "Eastern Conference Central Division", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which genus is part of the mallow family; Ferraria or Abelmoschus?", "answer": "Abelmoschus", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "The daughter of John Aniston appeared in which 1998 motion picture alongside Paul Rudd?", "answer": "The Object of My Affection", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Khorol or Khorlo, is a multi-trick tile-based game played in Mongolia, Inner Mongolia, and Tuva, usually on Lunar New Year's, the Mongolian Lunar New Year, is commonly known as what?", "answer": "Tsagaan Sar", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "he Columbus Blue Jackets play in a league that has how many teams ?", "answer": "31 teams", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What is the first name the founders of Hotel Baxter and Ted's Montana Grill have in common?", "answer": "George", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Agent Hannah Wells in the ABC political drama stared in the film adaptation of who's debut novel published in 2011? ", "answer": "Veronica Roth", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "St. Ignatius, located on Flathead Indian Reservation, is listed in what register?", "answer": "National Register of Historic Places", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "How many languages could Syria possibly speak?", "answer": "22", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "were Black Stone Cherry and Gene Loves Jezebel both british bands?", "answer": "no", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Which one is located in Northern California Iron Mountain Mine or Spring Creek Dam?", "answer": "Iron Mountain Mine", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Was Halma or Battle Sheep introduced first?", "answer": "Halma", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Did both Eduardo Montes-Bradley and Frank Borzage direct films?", "answer": "yes", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "The Editor is a 2014 Canadian horror comedy-mystery film by who, and starring Paz de la Huerta, is an American actress and model?", "answer": "Astron-6", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Lake Tana and Lake Sary-Chelek, are natural lakes?", "answer": "yes", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Between Elle and That's Life, which magazine has a wider audience?", "answer": "Elle", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Papa, is a 2012 South Korean comedy-drama film written and directed by Han Ji-seung, Park Yong-woo stars as a talent manager who persuades his step-daughter from a contract marriage, played by which South Korean actress and model, she is best known for starring in the television series \"Reply 1994\" (2013)?", "answer": "Go Ara", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which director was born first, Joe D'Amato or Alan Mak?", "answer": "Joe D'Amato", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "The 2007 Firestone Indy 400 included a massive pile-up on lap 144 that ended the race for the four-time IndyCar champion of what nationality?", "answer": "Scottish", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Eleven Eleven is the studio album by the folk-rock musician of what nationality?", "answer": "American", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "John Lennon was apart of which band that wrote \"Rain\"?", "answer": "the Beatles", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What is the capacity of the stadium that Stadium railway station, Perth will serve?", "answer": "60,000", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Henry M. \"Hank\" Ferris is a former head football coach for which public doctoral research university (R3) located in the Upper Montclair section of Montclair, at the intersection of the Great Notch area of Little Falls, and the Montclair Heights section of Clifton, in the U.S. state of New Jersey?", "answer": "Montclair State University", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Anna Hamilton Phelan was nominated for an Oscar for the depiction of what naturalist's life?", "answer": "Dian Fossey", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": " Bardufoss Airportis a primary airport situated at Bardufoss in M\u00e5lselv, Norway, Norwegian Air Shuttle operates three daily flights with Boeing 737s to where?", "answer": "Oslo", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "The Wife stars the actress of what nationality?", "answer": "American", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which group of plants contains more species, Verticordia or Ericaceae?", "answer": "Ericaceae", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "432 Park Avenue and One Vanderbilt, are skyscrapers in which city?", "answer": "New York City", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "In what city was Nickelodeon Splat City located?", "answer": "Santa Clara, California", "type": "bridg