ilm written and directed by the man labelled \"the first popular Surrealist\"?", "answer": "Blue Velvet", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What son of Queen Mary died on the August 1942 Dunbeath Air Crash?", "answer": "Prince George, Duke of Kent", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "When was the  English former professional footballer which Spaniard Antonio L\u00f3pez replaced as a coach born", "answer": "10 June 1966", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "When did the former U.S. Secretary of Homeland Security assume the office of White House Chief of Staff?", "answer": "July 31, 2017", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Gaius Cassius Longinus, was a Roman senator, a leading instigator of the plot to kill Julius Caesar, and the brother in-law of Marcus Junius Brutus, he commanded troops with Brutus during the Battle of Philippi against the combined forces of which Roman politician and general who played a critical role in the transformation of the Roman Republic from an oligarchy into the autocratic Roman Empire?", "answer": "Mark Antony", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "the aborignal group who traditionally lived in the area contiguaous with Coffs Harbour, New South Wales speak what language?", "answer": "Gumbaynggir language", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Thomas Rickman is an American film director and screenwriter known for a biographical film which tells the story of what country music singer? ", "answer": "Loretta Lynn", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What actor who served as the First Lady of the United States from 1981 to 1989, starred in a film n which a voice claiming to be that of God preempts all radio programs for days all over the world?", "answer": "Nancy Davis Reagan", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which university is located outside of the United States, University of Central Florida or Ain Shams University?", "answer": "University of Central Florida", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Coton de Tulear and Australian Silky Terrier, is a breed of what?", "answer": "dog", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Gandalf is a fictional character played by English stage and screen actor, Ian McKellen, in what two J.R.R. Tolkien novels turned films?", "answer": "\"The Hobbit\" and \"The Lord of the Rings\"", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "\"Verna\" is the twelfth episode of the fourth season of the American television comedy series \"30 Rock\", and the 70th overall episode of the series, which former SNL cast member guest stars as the title character of this episode, an American actress and comedian best known for her work on \"Saturday Night Live\", where she was a repertory player from 1986\u201391?", "answer": "Janet Vivian \"Jan\" Hooks", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Mewtwo, is a fictional creature from Nintendo and Game Freak's \"Pok\u00e9mon\" media franchise, in English, Jay Goede voiced Mewtwo in Pok\u00e9mon Live!, it was a musical stage show that toured in which country, on September 22, 2000 to January 19, 2001?", "answer": "United States", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What occupation did Christina Stead and William S. Burroughs share?", "answer": "writer", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Who is a Spanish professional footballer who plays for and captains both Real Madrid and the Spain national team, who has a Finnish footballer nicknamed \"Sergio\" because his style of play was similar?  ", "answer": "Sergio Ramos Garc\u00eda", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Who is the other lyricist for the Hindi movie Don, besides Lalji Pandey? ", "answer": "Indeewar", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "The jukebox musical Dream Lover: The Bobby Darin Musical is based on an original concept and stage play by which Australian writer, reporter and entertainer and Melbourne radio 3AW commentator?", "answer": "John-Michael Howson", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Karan Kapoor is the grandson of which Shakespearean actor-manager?", "answer": "Geoffrey Kendal", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Franklin Seaver Pratt (November 1, 1829 \u2013 January 11, 1894), also known as Franklyn or Frank S. Pratt, was an American settler, businessman, public servant and diplomat of the Kingdom of Hawaii, he married who, that was a great grandniece of Kamehameha I, being a great granddaughter of Kalokuokamaile, the older brother of Kamehameha I, founder of the Kingdom of Hawaii?", "answer": "Elizabeth Kekaikuihala Keka\u02bbaniauokalani Kalaninuiohilaukapu La\u02bbanui Pratt", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Ivan Tors and David Gordon Green, are in the film industry?", "answer": "yes", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "On their first releases which of Variety and Autoweek appeared more regularly ? ", "answer": "Variety", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "The 1921 Louisville Brecks season was their inaugural season in the which organization,  Louisville, Kentucky had two professional American football teams in this league?", "answer": "National Football League", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which member of the Epiphany Philosophers was also a Welsh Anglican bishop ?", "answer": "Rowan Williams", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Who was born first, Irwin Shaw or John Dunning?", "answer": "Irwin Shaw", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Are Editors and Empire of the Sun both English?", "answer": "no", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Do Archive and Blue Peter come from the same country?", "answer": "no", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Which teammate did Ali Ashfaq play with who was nicknamed the Sikkimese Sniper?", "answer": "Bhaichung Bhutia", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Jenny Lewis discography is the lead singer of what American indie rock band based in Los Angeles", "answer": "Rilo Kiley", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "The Dormition of St. Mary Cathedral, Bera is a church in the fortress that dates back to which century?", "answer": "13th century", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "The OFAB-100-120 is a bomb that can be carried on what twin-engine jetcraft?", "answer": "Sukhoi Su-25", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Good Ventures was founded, in part, by which co-founder of Facebook?", "answer": "Dustin Aaron Moskovitz", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "On which record label did the band who released the single Feel It Still release their eighth full-length album Woodstock?", "answer": "Atlantic Records", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Who produced the album that included a re-recording of \"Lithium\"?", "answer": "Butch Vig", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "The Marshall Library of Economics is located in a collegiate public research university, located where?", "answer": "Cambridge, England", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Humanitarian protections in war are denied to certain combatants under what treaty?", "answer": "Geneva Convention", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Does the Suwannee Canal or the Ohio and Erie Canal connect to other canal systems in Pennsylvania?", "answer": "Ohio and Erie Canal", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "What year was the firstprofessional golf  tournament sponsored by the producers of Noilly Pratt held?", "answer": "1961", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Cowie Water is south of which ruined fortress in Scotland?", "answer": "Cowie Castle", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What triggered both the 2016 Minneapolis shooting and the unlikely outcome of the 2016 US presidential election?", "answer": "larger rise of Islamophobia", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Are Real Simple and Bust both names of women's interest and lifestyle magazines?", "answer": "yes", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "In what year was the man who introduced the Healthcare Quality Improvement Act of 1986 born?", "answer": "1949", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which rock band was formed first,  The Rockfords or Radio Iodine?", "answer": "Radio Iodine", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "What is the area of the town that Church of St. Anne is located in (in Acres)?", "answer": "887", "type": "bridg