 of low-cost carriers (LCCs)?", "answer": "Jeju Air", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What is the capitol of the region located in central East Afganistan, and represented by the Cricket team Band-e-Amir Region?", "answer": "Maidan Shar", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Hotel Lester-Lester Cafe, also known as the Dodge House-Long Branch, is a historic building located in Mason City, Iowa, in which country, it was built as a two-story building a block away from the passenger and freight depots of the Chicago and North Western Railroad and the Chicago Great Western Railway?", "answer": "United States", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Who governs the size classification of Caldwell County Railroad?", "answer": "Surface Transportation Board", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Who had a longer life, Giacomo Gentilomo or Claude Sautet?", "answer": "Giacomo Gentilomo", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Who was the coach of Karl-Anthony Towns Jr., a Dominican-American professional basketball player for the Minnesota Timberwolves of the National Basketball Association ?", "answer": "Graham Betchart", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Who renounced his American citizenship and wrote a play with a cat named \"Carbucketty\"?", "answer": "T. S. Eliot", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Where is the club located that Silvan Hefti played for?", "answer": "St. Gallen", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Who wrote the novel which Katherine Langford played a role in the movie that based on the book?", "answer": "Jay Asher", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Kim Ki-duk's most widely known feature came out in which year ?", "answer": "2003", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Annenberg Community Beach House was built by the creator of which media company?", "answer": "Hearst Communications", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Who has recieved a MacArthure Fellowship, Colson Whitehead or John Kenneth Galbraith?", "answer": "Colson Whitehead", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "In what year did Beatrix Potter publish the children's book the inspired the name of Tiggwinkles animal charity?", "answer": "1905", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": " The End is an EP by an English heavy metal band which was only available at dates with the  final show was February 4, 2017, in their home city of what?", "answer": "Birmingham", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What year did Lilakoi Moon star in a crime-thriller?", "answer": "1994", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Bounce is currently hosted by what former Australian football player born in 1979", "answer": "Cameron Mooney", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Who's roles include Danny Tanner on the ABC sitcom \"Full House\" and was in a 2004 American teen comedy film starring Mary-Kate Olsen, Ashley Olsen and Eugene Levy.?", "answer": "Robert Lane \"Bob\" Saget", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "While T\u00e2b is a board game, what type of game is Time's Up!?", "answer": "charades-based party game", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "What is the name of the 2017 movie, which is also the name of the navel by Dave Evers was the last performance by Bill Paxton?", "answer": "The Circle", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Are both London LeGrand and Michael Locher Swiss musicians?", "answer": "no", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Which Cardiff City footballer played during the 2009 Houphou\u00ebt-Boigny stampede?", "answer": "Sol Bamba", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "When was the  American actress who hosted 16th People's Choice Awards born? ", "answer": "August 22, 1939", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which American film director is known for the sexploitation film genre, Wes Anderson or Doris Wishman?", "answer": "Doris Wishman", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Are both Hippophae and Pelargonium genera of sea buckthorns?", "answer": "no", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Where does the latest champion of the Scottish Open live?", "answer": "London", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Miro Kosta Str