ated in which city?", "answer": "New York City", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What is the centerpiece of a former monastery complex of the Canons Regular of the Lateran, opposite of the chief diplomatic mission of the United Kingdom in Lithuania that represents the British Overseas Territories in Lithuania ?", "answer": "St. Peter and St. Paul's Church", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Did Brett Anderson or Michael Monroe release the most solo albums?", "answer": "Brett Lewis Anderson", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Does Dean Silvers or Anja Salomonowitz have more titles in the entertainment industry?", "answer": "Dean Silvers", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "What Hindi singer originally sang the song \"Har Kisi Ko\"? ", "answer": "Manhar Udhas", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What cable and satellite television channel was founded in 1992 and showed the premier episode of The Tex Avery Show?", "answer": "Cartoon Network", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What was the position in the Wehrmacht of the deputy head of the counter-espionage bureau in the Abwehr who worked with Otto Armster?", "answer": "general", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Nine Black Alps and Big Data are both bands?", "answer": "yes", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "The 601 is equipped with which American all-weather, carrier-capable tactical airborne early warning (AEW) aircraft?", "answer": "Northrop Grumman E-2C Hawkeye", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What prize was the translator of the song \"My Boy\" awarded? ", "answer": "the Gold Badge", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What year was the actress portraying Buffy Summers born?", "answer": "1977", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "When was the director and co-writer of Ratatouille born?", "answer": "September 24, 1957", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Consider the band that wrote Uncle Tom's Cabin. In what year were they form?", "answer": "1984", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "On the Riviera was choreographed by the man known as what?", "answer": "the Father of Theatrical Jazz Dance", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which actress that was a member of South Korean girl group is co-staring in Unexpected Love?", "answer": "Krystal Jung", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Thermopsis rhombifolia could be found in the Great Plains, where do Great Plains could be found in the United States?", "answer": "west of the Mississippi River", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "In what country is the company headquartered where Walter van de Vijver was the head of exploration and production until 2004?", "answer": "the Netherlands", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "who is a Professor of Chemical and Biological Engineering at the University of Wisconsin-Madison known is leadership of industrial R&D organizations at both Dow Chemical Company and n American multinational conglomerate corporation incorporated in New York and headquartered in Boston, Massachusetts ?", "answer": "William F. Banholzer", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What kind of group does Trym Torson and Emperor have in common?", "answer": "band", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which actress stared in The Rippling Blossom and Curse of the Royal Harem?", "answer": "Myolie Wu", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "The 2010 Brit Awards were hosted by Peter Kay and a television presenter best known for what telethons?", "answer": "\"Red Nose Day\"", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Who directed the film that had all the same stars as That One night?", "answer": "James Wong", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Revolutions of Time...The Journey features recordings made for which eighteenth studio album by American outlaw country singer Willie Nelson?", "answer": "Red Headed Stranger", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Die by the drop is second album released on March 30 2010 by a Rock supergroup . In which City and state was this rock supergroup formed in 2009 ?", "answer": "Nashville, Tennessee", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "A low 