on": "Which King of the United Kingdom received birthday homours in 1936 and abdicated in the same year?", "answer": "Edward VIII", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Who was born first Andrzej Munk or Franklin Adreon?", "answer": "Franklin \"Pete\" Adreon", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Harriet Guild graduated from which academic medical teaching and research arm of the university with the same name?", "answer": "Johns Hopkins School of Medicine", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What occupation did both Carole Penny Marshall and Doug Langway perform?", "answer": "director", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Simmias of Thebes appears as a main discussion partner in a dialogue from the man who founded what?", "answer": "the Academy in Athens", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Rocket Rods opened on the infrastructure of what Disneyland attraction that operated from 1967 to 1995?", "answer": "PeopleMover", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Who were the lyrics in the Broadway musical where Lena Hall played Nicola by?", "answer": "Cyndi Lauper", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Who was born in an earlier year, Arantxa S\u00e1nchez Vicario or Mark Edmondson?", "answer": "Mark Edmondson", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "What Luftwaffe general who was responsible for the murder of the male civilians of a Greek village was later convicted for war crimes?", "answer": "Kurt Student", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What is the  action hack and slash video game based on a  Marvel Studios film directed by Kenneth Branagh, written by Ashley Edward Miller & Zack Stentz and Don Payne, and stars Chris Hemsworth?", "answer": "Thor: God of Thunder", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What is the name of this Austrian-born British molecular biologist and recipient of the 1962 Nobel Prize for Chemistry after whom S. Samar Hasnain's professorship is named?", "answer": "Max Perutz", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Joi Harris was killed while filming a motorcycle stunt, doubling as \"Domino\" on the set of which film intended to be the twelfth installment in the \"X-Men\" film series?", "answer": "Deadpool 2", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Who is part of both New Order and The Other Two?", "answer": "Stephen Paul David Morris", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Who is affiliated with more bands, Ronnie James Dio or Luca Prodan?", "answer": "Ronnie James Dio", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "What 2005 French Psychological thriller stars Belgian actress Marie Kremer?", "answer": "Cach\u00e9", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which American botanist and inventor, born into slavery in Missouri, was sculpted into a monument by Tina Allen?", "answer": "George Washington Carver", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Tim Colceri, is an American actor and comedian, he is most known for his role in the Stanley Kubrick film \"Full Metal Jacket\", released in which year, where he played the door gunner who uttered the much-quoted lines \"Get some!\", adopted as the byline for the 2008 movie \"Tropic Thunder\")?", "answer": "1987", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Has Lin-Manuel Miranda or The Barefoot Executive received more awards?", "answer": "Lin-Manuel Miranda", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Song of Scheherazade is a 1947 American musical film directed by Walter Reisch which features what Canadian-American actress, dancer, and singer?", "answer": "Yvonne De Carlo", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Thomas William Baxter played on the left wing for which Northern Irish, intermediate football club who are based in Ballyskeagh, County Down and play in the NIFL Premier Intermediate League?", "answer": "Lisburn Distillery Football Club", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which is cultivated across more continents, Clintonia or Washingtonia? ", "answer": "Washingtonia", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "What T.V. show did the episode Colonel Homer air on?", "answer": "The Simpsons", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "The event that caused the destruction of America's \"Black Wall Street\" in 1921 resulted in how many deaths according the American Red Cross?", "answer": "300", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What was the battle cited as at which John Brown commanded forces during the Kansas campaign and took place on June 2, 1856?", "answer": "Bleeding Kansas", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Ocean's 11 stars an American entertainer who starred in his own weekly comedy series playing a talk show host, and who appeared on television as early as what year?", "answer": "1948", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "In the 1981 Volvo Masters who beat the winner of the 1975 Wimbledon men's double that partnered with Sandy Mayer?", "answer": "Ivan Lendl", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which of these two men worked as a professor at New York University, Frankie Kazarian or Paul Boghossian?", "answer": "Paul Boghossian", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "What is the name of this fifth episode of The Simpsons tenth season, in which Leary and Brian Grazer appeared as guest stars as themselves?", "answer": "When You Dish Upon a Star", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Voyage of the Little Mermaid is a live show attraction at a theme park that opened in which year ?", "answer": "1989", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "The Monster by Eminem was a top-selling single globally in 2013-14 including New Zealand, and featured which guest singer?", "answer": "Rihanna", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "In 2008 City Theatre Dublin ran productions of a play by who?", "answer": "Oscar Wilde", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Who was born first, Jim Crace or Cid Corman?", "answer": "Cid (Sidney) Corman", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "What film did Timothy Bjorklund create in 2004?", "answer": "Teacher's Pet is a 2004 American animated musical", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Portishead and The Replacements, are which type of musical organization?", "answer": "band", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Who edited the essays of the man who received the Nobel Prize in literature in 1946?", "answer": "Theodore Ziolkowski.", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What was the original title of the opera in which Placido Domingo first appeared in 1961?  ", "answer": "\"Violetta\"", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which mountain is Earth's highest peak, Ghent Kangri, or Mount Everest?", "answer": "Mount Everest", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "At which university did the father of Damien Wilkins play shooting guard/small forward collegiately?", "answer": "University of Tennessee at Chattanooga", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Who was an American former professional baseball left fielder, Andrea Martin or Chuck Essegian?", "answer": "Charles Abraham \"Chuck\" Essegian", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Which single from Portishead's second studio album was #25 in the UK charts at the time if it's release?", "answer": "Over", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "is a British Sikh centenarian marathon runner of Punjabi Indian descent.", "answer": "Fauja Singh", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Aleksei Balabanov and Jean Vigo, have which occupation in common?", "answer": "film director", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "What English actor and musician starred in a movie with Harrison Ford in 1983?", "answer": "Kenneth George Baker", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which band was formed first, Navarone or Balance and Composure?", "answer": "Balance and Composure", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Flula Borg, who was one of the writers for the film \"Buddymoon\", is currently living in what city?", "answer": "Los Angeles", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which hospital shares its grounds with the Washington Hospital Center, Howard University Hospital or Children's National Medical Center?", "answer": "Children\u2019s National Medical Center", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "What is the first book in the prequel series to the four books referred to also as the Predator Cities Quartet by Philip Reeve?", "answer": "Fever Crumb", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Francis Ponge and Theodore Roethke, have which occupation in common?", "answer": "poet", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Are both The California Reich and Andrew and Jeremy Get Married based in the US?", "answer": "no", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "What cycling team from Russia was in the 2015 Danmark Rundt?", "answer": "Tinkoff", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What channel does Southern at Heart and Damaris Phillips have in common?", "answer": "Food Network", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What 2010 championship did the driver, who finished second in the 2017 Mexico City ePrix, win?", "answer": "British Formula 3 Championship", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What is the name of the television adaptor of the historical novel by Ken Follett published in 1989?", "answer": "Sergio Mimica-Gezzan", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Jeff Beck was a guitarist for the English rock band formed in London in what year?", "answer": "1963", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Was Lev Kuleshov and Lo Wei work in the same country?", "answer": "no", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Which film director, Cheick Oumar Sissoko or Michel Boisrond, also held a career in politics?", "answer": "Cheick Oumar Sissoko", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Which university uses English as the language of instruction, University of A Coru\u00f1a or German University in Cairo?", "answer": "German University in Cairo", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Lars Nieuwpoort formerly played for which Dutch club, founded in 2001?", "answer": "Almere City Football Club", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "American Beauty: Original Motion Picture Score was composed bu what American composer born in 1955", "answer": "Thomas Newman", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Mastermind and Small World, are what form of entertainment?", "answer": "game", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "The Amazing Race Canada 3 compete for a grand prize that includes the opportunity to fly anywhere for a year on this airlines founded in what year?", "answer": "1937", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Michiyo Yasuda worked for which Koganei-based animation studio?", "answer": "Studio Ghibli", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Mount Roberts' peak in located within a property that encompasses how many acres?", "answer": "5500", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "When was the American actor and comedian who starred in \"The Shaggy Dog\" born? ", "answer": "June 13, 1953", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What was the venue of the NHL draft that last featured 10 U.S.-trained players in the first round before 2010?", "answer": "Nationwide Arena", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Lincoln County, Kansas has a county seat of a city with a population of what as of 2010?", "answer": "1,297", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What type of profession does Utpala Sen and Hemanta Mukherjee have in common?", "answer": "singer", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Horatio was present on the battlefield when Hamlet's father defeated the prince who delivers the final lines of the play that represent a hopeful future for which country?", "answer": "Denmark", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which ABC talk show host appeared in the documentary Manny?", "answer": "Jimmy Kimmel", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What company did producers of A.I. Artificial Intelligence co-found in 1981", "answer": "Amblin Entertainment", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Are Anda, Heilongjiang and Beibei District both in the Chongqing municipality?", "answer": "no", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Kathy Jordan and Jack Sock, share which occupation?", "answer": "tennis player", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "What member of blues rock band from Athens, Alabama helped found Single Lock Records?", "answer": "Ben Tanner", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Bass Player and Lindy's Sports, are a type of which publication?", "answer": "magazine", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "What country of origin does Nickelodeon Animation Studio and The Loud Househave in common?", "answer": "American", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "The River Dee flows through Wales and what village in England?", "answer": "Farndon is a village", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Jurij Slatkonja was a choirmaster for which State of the Holy Roman Empire?", "answer": "Duchy of Carniola", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which was created first, Solarquest or The Great Train Robbery?", "answer": "The Great Train Robbery", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Beaconsfield Supply Store was the birthplace of the supermarkets founded in what year?", "answer": "1930", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Where was Riverdance, whose music was created by M\u00e1irt\u00edn O'Connor, first performed in 1995?", "answer": "Dublin", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Who hosted \"The Toast of the Town\" and also featured guest performer Sandy Stewart?", "answer": "Ed Sullivan", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which magazine has been published in more countries, More or My Weekly?", "answer": "More", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Ivar the Boneless was the brother of which 9th century Viking chieftain?", "answer": "Ubba", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Pennsylvania Route 436 has a southern terminus at the route that is a spur of what other US route?", "answer": "US 19", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "In which county is the city in which Jovita Id\u00e1r was born ?", "answer": "Webb County,", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Who was Anil Mohile's partner married to?", "answer": "Anuradha Paudwal", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "The Oregon Trail is a 2009 iOS and DSiware version of a computer game that was designed to teach school children about the realities of pioneer life in what century?", "answer": "19th-century", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Osechi-ry\u014dri, are traditional food,started in the Heian Period (794-1185), sometimes used to celebrate which annual festival with its own customs?", "answer": "Japanese New Year", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "How far is Medesano located from the capital of  the Emilia-Romagna region of Italy?", "answer": "100 km", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "How many people was this American contract killer and serial killer, who was the subject of the movie The Iceman, convicted of killing?", "answer": "five", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Manning Field at John L. Guidry Stadium was named for the family headed by the quarterback who played in the NFL for how many seasons?", "answer": "16", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Are Clerodendrum and Bergenia from the same family?", "answer": "no", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Noble Henry Willingham, Jr and the founder of the Chun Kuk Do school of fighting appeared together in which TV series?", "answer": "Walker, Texas Ranger", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Where was the drivers' world champion of 1995 born?", "answer": "Lanark", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "As of May 2017, Anthony Joshua is ranked as the world's best heavyweight by the Transnational Boxing Rankings Board and BoxRec, the second British boxer, after which British professional boxer, to win both a gold medal at the Olympics and a world title by a major professional sanctioning body, as well as being the first British heavyweight to do so?", "answer": "James Frederick DeGale", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Pinocchio and The Devil and Max Devlin were both produced by what entity?", "answer": "Walt Disney Productions", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Iron City is now produced in a brewery that was once used to produce beer from company that was founded in what year?", "answer": "1839", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Bridge Plaza in Brooklyn is bordered on the west by the bridge that has a length of what?", "answer": "6855 ft", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Are Agon and Medina both games for exactly two players?", "answer": "no", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Do Melville Shavelson and Jason Reitman have different nationalities?", "answer": "yes", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "In the twelfth season of \"The Simpsons\" who represented an American pioneer nurseryman who introduced apple trees to large parts of Pennsylvania, Ontario, Ohio, Indiana, and Illinois, as well as the northern counties of present-day West Virginia?", "answer": "Lisa", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Dan Bejar and Stacey McClean, are both artists, what is their occupation?", "answer": "singer", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Which NBA team did the 1999 NBA Draftee that is one of only two players to have won  EuroLeague title, an NBA championship, and an Olympic gold medal play for?", "answer": "San Antonio Spurs", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Where is the 181st Infantry Brigade's headquarters in Rock Island Arsenal located in the U.S?", "answer": "Illinois", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Svetlana Andreyevna Ivanova starred in which film about the 2008 South Ossetia war ?", "answer": "August Eighth", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "\"Born Rich\" and \"Innocence\" are what type of films?", "answer": "documentary film", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Which of these names is a genus of plant that consists of grass species:  Poa or Gymnocladus?", "answer": "Poa", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Which Manson Family member, nicknamed \"Blue,\" appeared in The Family Jams album?", "answer": "Sandra Collins Good", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Whale watching in New Zealand is predominantly centered around the areas of Kaikoura and the Hauraki Gulf, the Hauraki Gulf Marine Park (just outside Auckland city) is also a significant whale watching area with a resident population including which toothed whale belonging to the oceanic dolphin family, of which it is the largest member?", "answer": "Orca", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "I've Got My Own Hell to Raise by Bettye LaVette was released September 27, 2005, the album comprises covers of songs written by other female artists including which American singer-songwriter and author, and is the eldest daughter of country music icon Johnny Cash and his first wife, Vivian Liberto Cash Distin?", "answer": "Rosanne Cash", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which President of the United States planned to trade and build skyscrapers in German in 2000?", "answer": "Donald Trump", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "NBA Jam Extreme is a 1996 basketball arcade game by Acclaim Entertainment based on the 1996\u201397 NBA season, \"Extreme\" also features which longtime American sports broadcaster, and honored for his work as a member of the Basketball Hall of Fame?", "answer": "Marv Albert", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "University of Pittsburgh and Northwestern University, are both which type of universities?", "answer": "research", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "The radio series \"Hollywood PLayhouse\" was sponsored by Jergens Lotion and a company founded in what year?", "answer": "1870", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Who is the director of a film which featured the winner of FX's inaugural MMA competition?", "answer": "James Z. Feng", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which Floyd County university does Linda C. Gugin teach Emeritus of Political Science?", "answer": "Indiana University Southeast", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Do both Rongcheng, Shandong and Dongsheng District border the Yellow Sea?", "answer": "no", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Which animated film was released first, Khan Kluay or A Town Called Panic?", "answer": "Khan Kluay", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Who has more experience singing in bands, Jacob Hoggard or King Diamond?", "answer": "King Diamond", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Did Tampa Bay Rays acquired any veteran players from Red Sox?", "answer": "veteran stars Wade Boggs", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Where is the Disney-Pixar film co-directed by the first woman to win the Academy Award for Best Animated Feature set?", "answer": "the Scottish Highlands", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Of the two presidents who served during the heyday of the \"Kansas City Star,\" which one did NOT use nuclear weapons in war?", "answer": "Dwight D. Eisenhower", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Who was the grandson of King George V, and had a school built in honor of him in Oundle, Northamptonshire?", "answer": "Prince William of Gloucester", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "When will the election be held that includes democrat Jay Gonzalez as a candidate?", "answer": "November 6, 2018", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Robert Walser and Ira Levin are both a?", "answer": "writer", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Which of the following is a progressive magazine that comes out quarterly: Jewish Currents or Card Player?", "answer": "Jewish Currents", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Who was the author of the novel which was the basis for the 2011 film of the same nae which starred the actress whose screen debut was in the television film \"Replacing Dad\"?", "answer": "Kaui Hart", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Pandaemonium, 1660-1886: The Coming of the Machine as Seen by Contemporary Observers is a book of contemporary observations of the coming, development and impact of the Industrial Revolution in the United Kingdom, collected by documentary film-maker Humphrey Jenningsm and published posthumously in 1985 by Icon Books, the book takes its title from the first excerpt within it, the section in Book I of \"Paradise Lost\" (1660) in which English poet, polemicist, man of letters, and civil servant for the Commonwealth of England under Oliver Cromwell, describes the building of Pandaemonium, the capital city of Hell?", "answer": "John Milton", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Tracy Chevalier and Dashiell Hammett, have which shared nationality?", "answer": "American", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Who distributed the short film \"Turbo Charged Prelude\"?", "answer": "Universal Pictures", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Captain China stars the actor known for playing whom in \"The Wolf Man\"?", "answer": "Larry Talbot", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What is the name of the woman who shot Selena Quintanilla in the back and killed her at the Days Inn motel in Corpus, Christi?", "answer": "Yolanda Sald\u00edvar (born September 19, 1960) is an American woman who was convicted of the murder of Tejano singer, Selena Quintanilla-P\u00e9rez", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which film did Jennifer Tilly star in 12 years before the release of The Making of Plus One?", "answer": "Bride of Chucky", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which band has more members, The Kooks or Grant Lee Buffalo?", "answer": "The Kooks", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Ian Cognito is a British stand-up comedian who has been compared to a Jewish-American stand-up comedian who was convicted in an obcenity trial in what year?", "answer": "1964", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Freddy Mveng plays for which Swiss football club based in Lausanne?", "answer": "FC Lausanne-Sport", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What distinction does the representative who drew national media attention to the death of Aiyana Jones hold?", "answer": "Dean of the House of Representatives", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "The second President of Egypt led the Free Officers Movement along with what other man?", "answer": "Muhammad Naguib", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Who is older, Diederik Boer or Jasper Cillessen?", "answer": "Diederik Boer", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Are Yeo Hoon-min and John Kay both singers ?", "answer": "yes", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "A foam weapon, a padded mock weapon used for simulated handheld combat, is used in a North American medieval combat sport, begun in 1977 with the creation of what?", "answer": "Dagorhir", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "