 {"question": "What princely family did the family in which the station motto for the RAF Mount Batten branch from?", "answer": "Battenberg family", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Are Tim Burstall and James Bridges both screenwriter, film director, producer?", "answer": "yes", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Jay Clark Buckey, Jr., is an American physician and astronaut who flew aboard one space shuttle mission (STS-90) as a Payload Specialist, Buckey withdrew from the race when which former Governor, from New Hampshire, entered the race? ", "answer": "Jeanne Shaheen", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What nationality was the person The Rape of Lucretia was written for ?", "answer": "English", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which tennis player is younger, Sun Tiantian or Anna Kournikova?", "answer": "Sun Tiantian", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Who was born in Barry, Wales and was involved in the E-borders programme?", "answer": "Damian Green", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Venkatesan Guruswami is a computer scientist at what private research university in Pittsburgh, Pennsylvania", "answer": "Carnegie Mellon University", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Edgar Howard Wright, is an English director, screenwriter, producer, and actor, and is known for Hot Fuzz, released in which year, an action comedy film directed by Edgar Wright?", "answer": "2007", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Where did the player who is ahead of Ray Rice in the Raven's list of all-time leading rushers play his college football ?", "answer": "Tennessee", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Six Days, Seven Nights was directed by a man who owns what production company?", "answer": "The Montecito Picture Company", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What year was the first entry in the series in which Xanthe Huynh was cast as Haru Okumura released?", "answer": "1996", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Are Poly-1 and Mattel Aquarius both home computers?", "answer": "yes", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "The Cheakamus Valley basalts are part of what southwestern British Columbia formation?", "answer": "Cascade Volcanoes", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What is the nickname of the monarch to whom Francis Nethersole was secretary?", "answer": "The Winter Queen", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Mark Fuller presided over the case of the governor who was the last of what faith to hold the post in Alabama?", "answer": "Roman Catholic", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which band was formed first Short Stack or This Picture?", "answer": "This Picture", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "\"Calling All Girls\" is a song written by a musician of which nationality ?", "answer": "English", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "The home of the first US Secretary of the Treasury is preserved at what memorial?", "answer": "Hamilton Grange National Memorial", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "One Night in Istanbul stars a British actor and recording artist who is best known for his portrayal of Jonah Kirby on what BBC One drama?", "answer": "Waterloo Road", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What is the year of the event which occured first, Carnival! was produced, or Gower Champion was born?", "answer": "1919", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Autzen Stadium is located north of which public flagship research university in Eugene city?", "answer": "University of Oregon", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which park is located in the Canary Islands in Spain, Caba\u00f1eros National Park or Garajonay National Park?", "answer": "Garajonay National Park", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "What is the story line of the movie Chicken Little?", "answer": "a chicken who believes the world is coming to an end", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What character from Pearls Before Swine came from the superfamily Muroidea?", "answer": "Rat", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "She attended college in the United States at Hampshire College, and held a role in an epic space opera. Who wrote and directed this film?", "answer": "Rian Johnson", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Who was the creator of Ripred the rat, and author of bestselling trilogy of chronicles including \"Mockingjay\"?", "answer": "Suzanne Collins", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What is the name of the main antagonist, son of Lady Capulet's brother and who was slain in a duel by Romeo Montague?", "answer": "Tybalt", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Barry Sonnenfeld and Patricio Guzm\u00e1n, both are some form of director?", "answer": "yes", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Franz Burri, was a supporter of Nazi Germany from an early age and frequently visited the country during the 1930s, his hopes for a career in the SS were dashed when Reinhard Heydrich deemed him unsuitable, Heydrich was a high-ranking German Nazi official during World War II, and a main architect of which event?", "answer": "Holocaust", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which 1997 children's-fantasy-comedy film stars a former child actress who now focuses on a career writing?", "answer": "A Simple Wish", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "In what year was the movie Dragon Fist starring Nora Miao released?", "answer": "1979", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which president signed this act that led to Choctaw tribe of Native Americans being forced to move out of Choctaw County by federal troops in 1830?", "answer": "President Andrew Jackson", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What was the 2016 album recorded by the lead vocalist from the band who recorded the single \"Fallen Angels\"?", "answer": "The Shadow Side", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Are McCall's and MODE both focused on plus-size consumers?", "answer": "no", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "The label that has remixed the singer whose debut single was \"Before Your Love/A Moment Like This\" was established in what year?", "answer": "1989", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "George Batchelor founded and edited what specific scientific journal that publishes original work encompassing the field of fluid mechanics?  ", "answer": "Journal of Fluid Mechanics", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Sun Zhe and Yao Ming both play what sport?", "answer": "Basketball", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What other format was the Greatest Hits released on besides the analog sound storage medium known as LP?", "answer": "cassette", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What is the rebranded name of the racing series now that was won in 2016 by the Prema Powerteam?", "answer": "FIA Formula 2 Championship", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Who was a presidential nominee and praised Rober Pape's \"Dying to Win\"?", "answer": "Ron Paul", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "This ferrocement building originally built by Martin Maurer is located in a hamlet with a population of what at the 2010 census?", "answer": "4,472", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Two years after the Coupe de France Final where Olympique de Marseille defeats AS Monaco, what honor did the man with the most goals that match receive?", "answer": "European Footballer of the Year", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What band did Red Triangle work with that was from Derby, Derbyshire, England?", "answer": "The Struts", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What is the name of the opera created by a composer of Italian and French opera in the early classical period?", "answer": "Il re pastore", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which top-selling luxury automobile was the body of Robert Donati found in?", "answer": "Cadillac", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "When was the studio behind Guardians of the Galaxy Vol 2 bought by The Walt Disney Company?", "answer": "August 2015", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Wistful, an American racehorse, won at which Louisville, Kentucky Grade 1 stakes race?", "answer": "The Kentucky Oaks", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "When did the younger sister of Tanushree Dutta appear in a Kannada comedy film directed by Pon Kumaran?", "answer":