rist?", "answer": "Che Guevara", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Back to the moon is the first book by an author born on which day ?", "answer": "February 19, 1943", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Acorus and Clivia, are which specific genus?", "answer": "monocot flowering plants", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Omar Metwally played \"Dr. Fahim Nasir\" in a movie directed by who?", "answer": "Jaume Collet-Serra", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Are Schwantesia and Cleome both flowering plants?", "answer": "no", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Which episode of this season of \"The Simpsons\"' that had two hold-over episodes from the previous season was written by Ken Keeler, Dan Greaney, and David S. Cohen?", "answer": "Treehouse of Horror VII", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Who were the directors of the 1997 documentary film which starred the actress best known for her long-running TV variety show, \"The Carol Burnett Show\"?", "answer": "Chris Hegedus and D. A. Pennebaker", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Syed Noor and Paul Sloane, have which occupation in common?", "answer": "film director", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Who wrote the movie Brigitte Nielsen starred in in 1986?", "answer": "Sylvester Stallone", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What is the same of the city that  is the second largest city municipality in Italy and appeared in The 2010 Giro d'Italia?", "answer": "Verona", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What live series did the American comedian, who was replaced by Andrew Lawrence in \"Stand Up for the Week,\" write and perform in?", "answer": "\"Saturday Night Live\"", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Who was the director of the 2008 English-language science fiction action film in which a French former kickboxer and K-1 fighter starred?", "answer": "Mathieu Kassovitz", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which of the two, Vanderbilt University or Wake Forest University is nonprofit?", "answer": "Wake Forest University", "type