y from?", "answer": "4,397", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "In which town was the writer of the song You Take Me for Granted born ?", "answer": "Vienna, Missouri", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Giuseppe \"Oscar\" Damiani is the agent of a French-born Gabonese professional footballer how is known for his speed, and clocked how many metres in 3.7 seconds?", "answer": "30 metres", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Tunnel Vision is a single from an album, when was the album released?", "answer": "March 31, 2017", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "The hotel and casino in Winchester, Nevada where the 37th Daytime Emmy Awards were held, has how many hotel rooms?", "answer": "2,956 hotel rooms", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Tim McCarty is an American football coach and former player, from 1999 to 2003 McCarty was the head football coach at which four-year private Christian liberal arts college in Hillsboro, Kansas, United States?", "answer": "Tabor College", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Where is the band who released Steroids from?", "answer": "Sacramento, California", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Who has performed more roles in the film industry, Max Neufeld or Benedek Fliegauf?", "answer": "Max Neufeld", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "What is the middle name of the tennis player who lost to Pete Sampras in the 1994 Lipton Championships-Men's Singles?", "answer": "Kirk", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "The Chief Product Officer of the company who acquired FreeCharge for $400 million also works for which social media application?", "answer": "Facebook Inc.", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "In what country does the Franz Beckenbauer Cup take place?", "answer": "Germany", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Non-Stop Mix Best is by a pair of producers who are of what heritage?", "answer": "Belgian", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "SuperFresh is a supermarket brand owned by Key Food Stores Co-op, Inc. is a cooperative of independently owned supermarkets, fo