Stanford Jr.?", "answer": "the Farm", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What was the name of the other movie that Gammino dubbed, other than the one that was originally titled \"Licence Revoked\"?", "answer": "The Living Daylights", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "In which region of the US did Marie Weaver earn her B.A.?", "answer": "New England", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Lakdi-ka-pul railway station is in which major city in the southern Indian state of Telangana?", "answer": "Hyderabad", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "In the Safran Companies release of Over Her Dead Body who dies on the day of her wedding?", "answer": "The film is about Kate (Eva Longoria), who dies on the day of her wedding to fianc\u00e9 Henry (Paul Rudd)", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Were Capturing the Friedmans and Bomb Harvest both documentaries?", "answer": "yes", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Which game dates back to at least the Roman Empire: Nine Men's Morris, or Icehouse pieces?", "answer": "Nine Men's Morris", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Universal Press Syndicate merged with what company featuring a writer born December 8, 1961", "answer": "Uclick", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Kickapoo Site 7 is located in the Kansas county that had a population of what in 2010?", "answer": "9,984", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which creator of \"Absolutely Fabulous\" has also won three BAFTAs?", "answer": "Jennifer Saunders", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Yingtan and Chifeng, are in which country?", "answer": "People's Republic of China", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Which one was an American poet, Frank O'Connor or Edwin Arlington Robinson?", "answer": "Edwin Arlington Robinson", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Which of these Asian directors was behind the science fiction adventure film \"Snowpiercer\", Bong Joon-ho or Vincent Kok?", "answer": "Bong", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "In 2006, Marty Stratton was responsible for the overall development of what first-person shooter video game developed by id Software?", "answer": "Rage", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which mixed martial artist and current UFC Middleweight Champion stars in the film My Name Is Lenny?", "answer": "Michael Bisping", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What is the CPVI of the district Maureen Reed announced her running for in 2010 but later withdrew? ", "answer": "R + 12", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Are both Ted Sharks and Kevin Reynolds from the same country?", "answer": "no", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "The Bag Man is was inspired by a work from what Swiss Jungian psycologist and scholar?", "answer": "Marie-Louise von Franz", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Who as one of the seven crew members killed in the Space Shuttle \"Challenger\" disaster, who's death lead to the cancellation of the Teacher in Space Project ?", "answer": "Sharon Christa McAuliffe", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What tier of English football is the club that Tommy Rooney played with in 2004-2005?", "answer": "fifth", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Keith Raniere's company encourages what?", "answer": "a path of personal and professional development.", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": " \"Ms. Jackson\", a song by American alternative hip hop duo OutKast, was the second single from, \"Stankonia\", recorded in the duo's recording facility located in what Georgia city?", "answer": "Atlanta", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Cressida Dick, currently the Commissioner of Police of the Metropolis, operates as the head of what?", "answer": "London's Metropolitan Police Service", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Sean May played with Rashad McCants, and another American professional basketball player to win the NCAA Championship for which university?", "answer": "North Carolina Tar Heels", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Thamesville, Ontario is located between Chatham and which city with a population of 383,822 people and is at the confluence o