hat American professional wrestler who started his professional wrestling career in 1999 with Ultimate Pro Wrestling?", "answer": "John Felix Anthony Cena", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "When was the host of Inkigayo who is also a member of Got7 born?", "answer": "September 22, 1994", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which came out first, \"Hollywood Chinese\" or \"The Truth According to Wikipedia\"?", "answer": "Hollywood Chinese", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "The County seat of Grant County, Kansas has a population of what?", "answer": "6,161", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Rivers of My Fathers\" is a song by a soul and jazz poet whose own term for himself was what?", "answer": "bluesologist", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which games were held in Seoul, South Korea the year Eriko Asai won a gold medal? ", "answer": "1986 Asian Games", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Dani Stevenson released a single used in the film starring the actor who played what role in \"XXX\"?", "answer": "Xander Cage", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Who lived longer, Bo Widerberg or Petar B. Vasilev?", "answer": "Petar B. Vasilev", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "\u00dana Palliser sang over the credits of a BBC drama series set in what year?", "answer": "1943", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Seedley railway station is a disused station located in the Seedley area of Pendleton, is an inner city area of Salford in Greater Manchester, in which country?", "answer": "England", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Who produced the album containing lyrics about Ian Curtis's failing marriage?", "answer": "Martin Hannett", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What type of communication medium does Lip Service and Ruta Gedmintas have in common?", "answer": "television", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Did James Cruze and Raoul Walsh act and direct in silent films? ", "answer": "yes", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "The English electronic band that Peter Gordeno has toured with since 1998 was formed where?", "answer": "Basildon, Essex", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What song written by Leonard McNally with music composed by James Hook was the favorite song of the King of the United Kingdom of Great Britain and Ireland?", "answer": "The Lass of Richmond Hill", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "By what nickname was the father of George Frederick of Brandenburg-Ansbach known ? ", "answer": "George the Pious", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Sunday Times Fast Track 100 is sponsored by the group founded by whom?", "answer": "Sir Richard Branson and Nik Powell", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What sport do Ruslan Zhiganshin and Elena Ilinykh compete in?", "answer": "ice dancer", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Whose novel about a time traveler attempting to prevent John F Kennedy's assassination, was adapted into a miniseries Executive Produced by J.J. Abrams?", "answer": "Stephen King", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Who was the third Vice President of the United States, whose character sings the \"Your Obedient Servant\" song from Act 2 of the musical \"Hamilton\"?", "answer": "Aaron Burr", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Were Dorothy Arzner and James Foley from the same directorial eras?", "answer": "no", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "A band formed in 2005 by Jamie Laurie had what hit song that peaked at #3 on the Billboard Modern Rock Tracks?", "answer": "Handlebars", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What country did the explorers that the film Glory & Honor was based on originate from?", "answer": "United States", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Walter Lang and Fred Savage both shared what profession?", "answer": "director", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Buried in the crypt of the Christ Episcopal Church is the owner of a  2-story, five-bay, rectangular frame residence whose roof is pierced by what?", "answer": "two large central chimneys", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "The Widower is a British television miniseries that portrays the life and crimes of convicted murderer Malcolm Webster,  an Englishman convicted of the murder of who? ", "answer": "his first wife", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Mike Gibbons was an American boxer who claimed the Middleweight Champion of the World status following what Polish American professional boxer's murder?", "answer": "Stanley Ketchel", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What was the debut film of the female star from the sitcom series Off the Rack?", "answer": "\"Divorce American Style\"", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Barefoot is a romantic comedy-drama film starring an actor known for playing Ben Covington in what television series?", "answer": "Felicity", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "David Buchan, was a Scottish naval officer and Arctic explorer, the Arctic consists of the Arctic Ocean, adjacent seas, and parts of which U.S. state, Northern Canada, Finland, Greenland (Denmark), Iceland, Norway, Russia and Sweden?", "answer": "Alaska", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Ian Young wrote Continuum that was a magazine publsuhed by a group that denied the existence of what?", "answer": "HIV/AIDS", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "The Queen's Medical Center was founded in 1859 by the fourth monarch of Hawaii and what Queen?", "answer": "Emma", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What album's cover art was done by the artist best known for \"The Adventures of Vasco Pyjama\" and the \"Curly Flats\" series?", "answer": "Wangaratta Wahine", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which Fear and Jane's Addiction band member worked on You Oughta Know? ", "answer": "Flea", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What is this digestif made with dozens of herbs and spices and high percentage alcohol from the company headquartered in Germany that the American businessman and philanthropist Sidney E. Frank sponsored?", "answer": "J\u00e4germeister", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What star of the 1997 Danish film Credo had her breakthrough role in the 1986 Danish film \"Early Spring\"?", "answer": "Sofie Gr\u00e5b\u00f8l", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Adam Shore and Denis B\u00e9langer, have which occupation in commojn?", "answer": "vocalist", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Which Supreme Court case addressed more Amendments of the US Constitution, District of Columbia v. Heller or Gibbons v. Ogden?", "answer": "District of Columbia v. Heller", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "The murderer in the investigation the documentary The Witness covers was sentenced to what official punishment?", "answer": "life imprisonment", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Both the San Francisco Giants and the San Francisco 49ers played in what famous stadium?", "answer": "Candlestick Park", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which movie came out first Dragonslayer or Freaky Friday ?", "answer": "Freaky Friday", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Heavy young Heathens composed the music for which MTV show that debuted on January 3, 2013 ?", "answer": "Buckwild", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which game did the author of the e-book \"How to Win at the Sport of Business\" play for charity at Intel Extreme Masters Season X \u2013 San Jose?", "answer": "League of Legends", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Who was born first, Johnette Napolitano or Lux Interior?", "answer": "Lux Interior", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "How many years after the death of George I was the Order of Saints George and Constantine instituted?", "answer": "It was instituted in January 1936", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What is the film in which Lily James plays Debora best known for?", "answer": "its choreography", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What Emperor is the establisher of the Order of Saint Anastasia the great-great-granddaughter of?", "answer": "Alexander II", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What is the name of the musical that is based on the 2000 film with the music is by Elton John, stars the actor known for the 2016 film Spider-Man in the title role?", "answer": "Billy Elliot the Musical", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Who, Seth Savoy or Christopher Guest, is a Cajun American film director and screenwriter raised in Little Rock, Arkansas?", "answer": "Seth Savoy", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "which movie is an adoption of the first published erotic novel anonymously in Vienna, Austria in 1906?", "answer": "Sensational Janine", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Is it true that both Ann Beattie and James Merrill received a Pulitzer Prize for Poetry?", "answer": "no", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "What television show features a character who is a working-class man who hunts supernatural creatures portrayed by Jim Beaver and a protagonist portrayed by Jensen Ackles?", "answer": "Supernatural", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "OSA Archivum, abbreviated as OSA, short for Open Society Archives at the Central European University, is an archival repository and laboratory that aims to explore new ways of assessing, contextualizing, presenting, and making use of archival documents both in a professional and a consciously activist way, it was founded in 1995, by which Hungarian-American investor, business magnate, philanthropist, and author?", "answer": "George Soros", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "The actor who plays hotelier Paul Rusesabagina in Hotel Rwanda was born in what year?", "answer": "1964", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What is the nationality for novelists Elizabeth Jane Howard and Jim Crace? English", "answer": "English", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Who was born first, Sarah Cracknell or Brendon Urie?", "answer": "Sarah Cracknell", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Planter's Punch and modern Bumbo both contain what type of rum? Dark Rum", "answer": "dark rum", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "What is the home city of the team that Idriz Naser Voca plays for?", "answer": "Lucerne", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "The director of the film \"Muriel\" also directed a film from a screen play by who?", "answer": "Alain Robbe-Grillet", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "When did the boy band that Dong Young-bae is a member of debut?", "answer": "August 19, 2006", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Edizioni Piemme is an Italian book publisher with specialisms in religion, and in fiction for children and young adults, among its best known publications are the works of who, author of \"The Kite Runner\"?", "answer": "Khaled Hosseini", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Who portrays the character that adopted Henry Mills in the series Once Upon a Time ?", "answer": "Lana Parrilla,", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Christian Nicholas Stadil owns what sports brand that is based in Denmark, and was started in 1923 by the German Messmer family in Hamburg?", "answer": "hummel International", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Slaven Bili\u0107 who described Ivica Olic as a typical \"match-winner\" and \"king of important matches\" is a manager of which club?", "answer": "Premier League club", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Patradevi is a town in the Pernem taluk of Goa, a state in which country?", "answer": "India", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Who, out of Hrach Gregorian and Sue Sarafian Jehl, served as a personal secretary to General Eisenhower between 1943 and 1947?", "answer": "Sue Jehl", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "What type of group does Col\u00e9gio Diocesano de S\u00e3o Jos\u00e9 5 and Nossa Senhora de F\u00e1tima, Macau have in common?", "answer": "Parish", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which song is commonly taught as an alternative to the Australian national anthem \"Advance Australia Fair\"?", "answer": "\"I Am Australian\"", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Who is featured in the Coolio song that shares a background sample music with the song \"Curtain Falls\"?", "answer": "L.V.", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "When You Really Loved Someone was a song by the ABBA member who released a self-titled album in what year?", "answer": "1968", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which Genus has around 30 species of flowering plants, Schoenoplectus or Isatis?", "answer": "Isatis", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "What is the population size of the place that is connected by the Lotus Bridge to the Cotai reclamation area of Macau?", "answer": "3,000", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What genre of movie was the 2005 movie The Fog that features \"Invincible\" by OK Go?", "answer": "supernatural horror", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which documentary film was released first, Super High Me or Quantum Hoops?", "answer": "Quantum Hoops", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Ivan Cooper led an anti-internment march which developed into a massacre where how many people died ?", "answer": "Fourteen people died", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "The hamlet Ashton is part of a city located on what river?", "answer": "River Nene", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Who originally voiced Honey Bunny's ex-boyfriend ?", "answer": "Mel Blanc", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "in 2003, Arizona Cardinals fired head coach Dave McGinnis and replaces him with a coach born in which year ?", "answer": "1949", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Both Lacey Sturm and Natalie Maines have what occupation?", "answer": "American singer-songwriter", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Were both Carole Penny Marshall and Randal Kleiser producers at some point in their life?", "answer": "yes", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "What is the nickname of the husband of the real life person portrayed by Sharon Stone in the movie \"Casino\"?", "answer": "Lefty", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Jacopo Bertucci, was an Italian painter of the Renaissance period, he painted for the \"Basilica of San Vitale\" is a church in Ravenna, in which country?", "answer": "Italy", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What year was the singer of \"Hang Down Your Head\" born?", "answer": "1949", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What region whose name means \"Estate of the Salt Chamber\" has Austria's third largest lake?", "answer": "Salzkammergut", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What are the names of the singers from Sony Wonder's 1995 album When You Wish Upon a Chipmunk?", "answer": "Alvin, the mischievous troublemaker, who quickly became the star of the group; Simon, the tall, bespectacled intellectual; and Theodore, the chubby, impressionable one.", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "The MacBook uses a series of IPS panel displays that offer what compared to traditional displays?", "answer": "higher pixel density", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Scout's Safari's creator produced and created what American television series that ran from October 8, 1994 to January 15, 1998?", "answer": "The Secret World of Alex Mack", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Monta Vista lies near what other town that had origins as a stagecoach stop?", "answer": "Mountain View", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What is the name of the unofficial grouping of elite universities that are part of the C9 Leaugue?", "answer": "The \"golden triangle\"", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What label did Set the Thames on Fire ensemble star run until its closure in 2011?", "answer": "Frost French", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which was a computer that also played video games, APF Imagination Machine or Grundy NewBrain?", "answer": "APF Imagination Machine", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "What show , hosted by  an English television presenter, was originally broadcast on Radio Luxembourg, it transferred to ITV in 1955?", "answer": "Double Your Money", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which Japanese horror film was based on a seinen horror manga series written and illustrated by Junji Ito?", "answer": "Uzumaki", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What is the middle name of the character Ellie Kemper portrays in the Netflix original series, \"Unbreakable Kimmy Schmidt\"?", "answer": "Couger", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which was published first The Fader or OK!?", "answer": "OK!", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Were the movies Benji the Hunted and Winnie the Pooh both released by Walt Disney Pictures?", "answer": "yes", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Who was the founding lead guitarist in the band whose single was used with \"Bridge over Troubled Water\" to create the charity single \"A Bridge over You\"?", "answer": "Jonny Buckland", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What was the production company that released the album that contained \"The Black Angel's Death Song\"? ", "answer": "Verve Records", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Are Bernard Rose and Doug Langway both film directors?", "answer": "yes", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "What is the name of the first live DVD by the black metal band for which Abbath Doom Occulta is the bassist?", "answer": "The Seventh Date of Blashyrkh", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What is the name of the Adult Swim pilot that was created by Aaron Springer and directed by Genndy Tartakovsky?", "answer": "Korgoth of Barbaria", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Who was born earlier, Andrew Strauss or Peter Moores?", "answer": "Peter Moores", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What school did Joseph Otsiman attend that is located in Takoradi?", "answer": "Takoradi Senior High School", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Johnny Hallyday is a French singer and actor once married for 15 years to popular Bulgarian-French singer Sylvie Vartan whose performances often featured what type of choreography? ", "answer": "show-dance", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Eric Harold Neville, known as E. H. Neville, was an English mathematician, and is the one who convinced Srinivasa Ramanujan to come to England, Ramanujan independently compiled nearly how many results, mostly identities and equations?", "answer": "3,900", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Arthur Wakefield founded a settlement at Nelson, New Zealand with his brother, who had what profession?", "answer": "politician", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "The Chain starred an American actor who has appeared in over 150 films. What did the actor make guest appearences on?", "answer": "\"Gunsmoke\", \"Walker, Texas Ranger\", \"Law & Order\", \"Scrubs\", and \"Entourage\"", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Who is a supervillain by Marvel Comics that leads the Reavers?", "answer": "Donald Pierce", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Old Brown Shoe was included on the compilation album released in what year?", "answer": "1988", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What is the nationality of Alexa Ray Joel's mother?", "answer": "American", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "The 1960 VMI Keydets football team represented which state-supported military college in Lexington, Virginia, the oldest such institution in the United States?", "answer": "Virginia Military Institute (VMI)", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which of the film in which Jimmi Harkishin was featured is a 1999 British comedy-drama film written by Ayub Khan-Din and directed by Damien O'Donnell?", "answer": "East Is East", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "How many films did the studio Iosif Boyarsky produce in 2017?", "answer": "1528", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Bernd H\u00f6lzenbein, is a German former footballer, best known for being fouled, in the final against Netherlands in 1974, what was this event called?", "answer": "1974 FIFA World Cup Final", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What technology company created the Group Control System operating system and is located in Armonk, New York?", "answer": "International Business Machines Corporation", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What country does Games and Official Xbox Magazine have in common?", "answer": "United States", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "What is the latin name for the highest degree David Favrholdt obtained from Copenhagen University?", "answer": "Philosophiae Doctor", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Michele Campanella specialises in the music of which Hungarian composer?", "answer": "Franz Liszt", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What do Jimi Goodwin and Sarah Nixey have in common?", "answer": "vocalist", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Into what company did the railroad which had operated the Twin Cities Zephyr merge in 1970?", "answer": "Burlington Northern", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Jeremy Bates and Patrick Galbraith both played what sport?", "answer": "tennis", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Which contains more species, Calendula or Serissa?", "answer": "Calendula", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "What number season was the Brazillian central defender signed, who was previously a left back?", "answer": "114th", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which contributor to Izzard won the 2016 Hugo Award for Best Fan Artist?", "answer": "Steve Stiles", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which coast is the city, in which the coins were found at the wreckage in which the Antikythera Ephebe was also found, located on?", "answer": "Ionia", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Saint Janet is a film that stars the actor who plays Samuel on the show Mike and Molly who was born on what day?", "answer": "April 26, 1979", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "The 2011 New York City Marathon was sponsored by which Dutch multinational banking corporation?", "answer": "ING Group", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which car features BMW xDrive and is a compact luxury crossover SUV?", "answer": "BMW X1", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Who won more Grammy Awards, Mike Nichols or Rowland Brown?", "answer": "Mike Nichols", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Which film won more Academy Awards, The Thin Blue Line or Target for Tonight?", "answer": "Target for Tonight", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Eugene Lee's set design works include one for a musical based on an English slave trader by the name of what?", "answer": "John Newton", "type": "bridge"}, {"questio