?", "answer": "Starships", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Where was the mixed martial arts event that Sabah Homasi competed in?", "answer": "T-Mobile Arena in Paradise, Nevada", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which Rihanna album is the song that inspired \"I Was a Fool\" on?", "answer": "\"A Girl like Me\"", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "One More Night was Written by Tom Davis and Al franken. What NBC Show was Franken and Davis best known for ?", "answer": "Saturday Night Live", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Was Bob Boone's father right or left-handed?", "answer": "right-handed", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Who has won more doubles tennis titles: Svetlana Kuznetsova or Kateryna Bondarenko?", "answer": "Svetlana Aleksandrovna Kuznetsova", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "What denomination is the church J\u00f8rgen Tandberg served as a bishop in?", "answer": "Lutheran", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Are Quincy Perkins and Jerzy Skolimowski both directors?", "answer": "yes", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Who also was male vocalist on a different recording of a 1983 song written and performed by Paul McCartney and Michael Jackson?", "answer": "Scott Klopfenstein", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which canal was the first venture of the Delaware and Hudson Canal Company, the Delaware and Hudson Canal or the Delaware and Raritan Canal?", "answer": "The Delaware and Hudson Canal", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Who directed more well known movies Jim Sharman or John Hughes?", "answer": "He directed and/or scripted some of the most successful comedy films of the 1980s and early 1990s including the comedy \"National Lampoon's Vacation\" (1983), the coming-of-age comedy \"Sixteen Candles\" (1984), the teen sci-fi comedy \"Weird Science\" (1985), the coming-of-age comedy-drama \"The Breakfast Club\" (1985), the coming-of-age comedy \"Ferris Bueller's Day Off\" (1986), the romantic comedy-drama \"Pretty in Pink\" (1986), the romance \"Some Kind of Wonderful\" (1987), the comedies \"Planes, Trains and Automobiles\" (1987) and \"Uncle Buck\" (1989), the Christmas family comedy \"Home Alone\" (1990) and its sequel, \"\" (1992).", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Which city hosted a march in the Nichidatsu Fujii's movement and is the site of Alcatraz island?", "answer": "San Francisco", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What position did the former footballer and racing driver play in the 2003-04 Olympique de Marseille season?", "answer": "goalkeeper", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Zone of the Enders is a video game franchise created by a producer regarded as a what?", "answer": "an auteur of video games", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "A compact van was roughly the same size as a Volkswagen model introduced in what year?", "answer": "1950", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What scarface actor was also in the movie The Abandoned?", "answer": "Mark Margolis", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "\"The Hunt for the BTK Killer\" is based on the true story of murders that took place in what county?", "answer": "Sedgwick County", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Carl Macek and Darren Aronofsky, are of which nationality?", "answer": "American", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "What type of category does Pitcairnia and Evolvulus have in common?", "answer": "genus", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "The actress that played Joanna Loudon on \"Newhart\" also co-stared with Waylon Jennings in a film released in what year?", "answer": "1966", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "David upheld his support for his niece, the former Empress-consort, who had how many children?", "answer": "no children", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Benjamin Richard \"Yahtzee\" Croshaw is best known for his acerbic video game review series for an online magazine published by who?", "answer": "Alexander Macris", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "The producer of \"I Am That Change\" made his adult acting debut in what film?", "answer": "\"Gangotri\"", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which case had a larger majority ruling, Stromberg v. California or United States v. Wheeler?", "answer": "United States v. Wheeler", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Which character did British actor Christian Bale play in the 1999 film A Midsummer Night's Dream?", "answer": "Demetrius", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Tell Me O Kkhuda, is a 2011 Bollywood drama film directed by Hema Malini, stars include which Indian film actor, producer and politician, and in 1997,  he received the Filmfare Lifetime Achievement Award for his contribution to Hindi cinema?", "answer": "Dharmendra", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "How long did the rebellion led by Samuel Sharpe last?", "answer": "eleven-day", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "How is a Treeing Walker Coonhound and an Otterhound differnt ?", "answer": "yes", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "What is the name of the monthly journal published by Rishab Aiyer Ghosh?", "answer": "First Monday", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "When did the group, in which Canadian writer Wayson Choy is a member, develop a romanisation system for Catonese?", "answer": "1993", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Michael Jeffrey Lloyd was a producer of which teen idol pop star that also worked as a child actor in the 1970s?", "answer": "Leif Garrett", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What NBS drama series from 1991-1996 did Elizabeth Hoffman appear as Beatrice Reed Ventnor and Patricia Lalembar appear as Georgiana \"Georgie\" Reed Whitsig appear?", "answer": "Sisters", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which canal, the North Shore Channel or the Eastside Canal, originates from a common diversion at Manor Street in Bakersfield, which also serves the Carrier Canal and Kern Island Canal?   ", "answer": "Eastside Canal", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Who directed, produced, and wrote a Thomas and Friends film that incorporated elements from Shining Time Station?", "answer": "Britt Allcroft", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "The Holy Trinity, an episode of British motoring series \"The Grand Tour\" was produced by which  independent television production company founded in 2015 in the UK?", "answer": "W. Chump and Sons", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Edward William Fitzalan-Howard, 18th Duke of Norfolk, (born 2 December 1956), styled Earl of Arundel between 1975 and 2002, is a British peer, Earl Marshal and son of which male British Army general and peer, and he eldest son of Bernard Fitzalan-Howard, 3rd Baron Howard of Glossop?", "answer": "Miles Francis Stapleton Fitzalan-Howard, 17th Duke of Norfolk", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What city with an urban population of 430,299 also houses the fourth tallest building in Latin America?", "answer": "Panama City", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Tin Kai-Man was in what 2004 Hong King-Chinese martial arts gangster comedy film that was produced by Chui Po-chu and Jeffrey Lau?", "answer": "Kung Fu Hustle", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Who was the director of the 2003 Christmas-themed romantic comedy film in which Reg Presley's \"Love Is All Around\" was featured?", "answer": "Richard Curtis", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which United States Airforce installation has a large cantilever hangar and is located in northeastern Maine?", "answer": "Loring Air Force Base", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which professional soccer club based in Adelaide plays at T.K. Shutter Reserve?", "answer": "North Eastern MetroStars Soccer Club", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which professional footballer is uncle to the African Footballer of the Year for 2008?", "answer": "Alex Harlley", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which person on the Angel of Retribution album is gay?", "answer": "Rob Halford", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What is this produced by Willett distillery, which was originally aged in charred oak barrels until mature at 15 years old?", "answer": "Noah's Mill", "type": "bridge"}, {