dge"}, {"question": " Conquest is a 1937 Metro-Goldwyn-Mayer film staring a British character actor for his many roles in British and American films and later in what?", "answer": "television programmes", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What man, widely considered to be the greatest sprinter of all time, participated in the 2012 Summer Olympics?", "answer": "Usain Bolt", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Who is a guest appearance on Live @ Club U, Volume II?", "answer": "Doug E. Fresh", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Where is the company, in which TIGCC is related to, headquartered? ", "answer": "Dallas, Texas", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Ivo Andri\u0107 and Eldridge Cleaver, have which shared occupation?", "answer": "writer", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Where is the 2014 independent crime drama film, that stars the actor who played the role of James Crockett in Miami Vice, set?", "answer": "Texas", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "For what war did the \"Stuka\" plane beat the Heinkel He 118?", "answer": "World War II", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "During the 1985 World Games that took place at Slazenger Racquet Club, what days did it take place?", "answer": "July 25 to August 4", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "On what channel was BVS Entertainment's Monster Farm aired?", "answer": "Fox Family Channel", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What type of organization now runs the cattle ranch founded by John Palmer Parker?", "answer": "charitable trust", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "A Silent Film and Needtobreathe, have which genre in common?", "answer": "rock", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "What Brittonic dialect was spoken in the kingdom who had the father of Owain mab Urien as king?", "answer": "Cumbric", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What instrument does Maddie Rice play in the band on American late-night talk show The Late Show with Stephen Colbert?", "answer": "lead guitar", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Who was born first, Berthold Viertel or Wes Anderson?", "answer": "Berthold Viertel", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "The murder of nicole brown simpson and ron goldman was published in what collection of work?", "answer": "Crime Wave", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Were Miracle and Dinosaur released in the same year?", "answer": "no", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "How tall is the athlete that is on the cover of the video game MLB 08: The Show?", "answer": "6 ft", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Who directed a 1975 British-American musical screwball comedy horror film which features the song \"Science Fiction/Double Feature\"?", "answer": "Jim Sharman", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Who directed the 1968 thriller film that featured the actor of the \"Harry Potter\" films' Rubeus Hagrid in a supporting role?", "answer": "David Drury", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which movie came out first, Still Kicking or American Jobs ?", "answer": "American Jobs", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "The grandson of Dorothy Bridges was born in what year?", "answer": "1973", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "A contestant on Season 3 of the boxing reality television series \"The Contender\", Jaidon Codrington  went on to lose in the final to Sakio Bika,   a Cameroonian-Australian professional ?", "answer": "boxer", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Raffles is a film, released in what year, starring James David Graham Niven, his commonly known as David Niven, an English actor, memoirist and novelist? ", "answer": "1939", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "The Monkey King Festival, is celebrated in China on the 16th day of the eighth Lunar month of which traditional,  lunisolar calendar which reckons years, months and days according to astronomical phenomena?", "answer": "Chinese calendar", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "The 2016 UCF Knights football team represented the University of Central Florida in the 2016 NCAA Division I FBS football season, they were led by first-year head coa