untled ranchers and Unitarian revolutionaries, the Freemen briefly took control of Dolores, Chascom\u00fas and which main city of the homonymous partido (department), located in Argentina, in the southeast of Buenos Aires Province, just north-northwest of the Tandilia hills?", "answer": "Tandil", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "In early years of sprinting besides an American former track and field sprinter who specialized in the 100-meter dash who was a record holder?", "answer": "Donovan Bailey", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Who works with the senior executive vice president in charge of Adult Swim at Williams Street?", "answer": "Keith Crofford", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "The big winner of the 63rd Bodil Awards was the 2009 English-language film that came from what country?", "answer": "Danish", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Knat Scatt Private Eye is a two-act, 1930s-style film noir musical featuring an American actor known for playing Michael Scott on the American version of what?", "answer": "The Office", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Franklin Armstrong is a comic strip character create by a man that died in what year?", "answer": "2000", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which American rock band was founded first, Mutemath or SWMRS?", "answer": "Mutemath", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "What type of band was the Texas Tornados when Doug Sahm was a member?", "answer": "Tejano band", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Are Sazerac and Hangman's Blood both alcoholic drinks?", "answer": "yes", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Are Veratrum and Leontopodium genuses of plants that are found in the same family?", "answer": "no", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "What was the nickname of one of the members of the Eastern Conference Southeast Division that was viewed as one of the best dunkers in the National Basketball Association's history?", "answer": "The Human Highlight Film", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "In between Zigadenus and Mutis