: "Galatasaray", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Some of the interior and front of the Jumbo's Clown Room building is shown on the video for Let Me Go by an American rock band who roase to international fame with what single?", "answer": "Kryptonite", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "\"Sebben, crudele\", is an aria from Antonio Caldara's opera, released in what year, \"La costanza in amor vince l'inganno\", it has been recorded by Cecilia Bartoli, an Italian coloratura mezzo-soprano opera singer and recitalist?", "answer": "1710", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "In the 2008-09 Houston Rockets season, which 2.29 meter player missed most of the second round due to a foot injury?", "answer": "Yao Ming", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "A private U.S. for-profit company founded in 1989 that specializes in information security and cybersecurity training founded the certification entity in what year?", "answer": "1999", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "B. F. Shelton recorded a number of songs for which Victor Talking Machine Company producer?", "answer": "Ralph Peer", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Who is the founder of Intel?", "answer": "Gordon Moore", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "When was the Scottish historian born who coined Chimerica?", "answer": "18 April 1964", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Spider-Man was a 2002 film that co-starred the American actress who made her debut in what Woody Allen short film?", "answer": "Oedipus Wrecks", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "When was the stage performer  who is also was Paul Daniels wife born", "answer": "31 October 1958", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "The Luna Jacal or Luna's Jacal was the residence of Gilberto Luna, a Mexican pioneer farmer in the area of Texas that would become which U.S. national park located in Western Texas, bordering Mexico?", "answer": "Big Bend National Park", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What actor, who starred in The Flight of the Phoenix, also starred in Cool Hand Luke?", "answ