t Cal McCrystal?", "answer": "film was directed by Marc Webb", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "The Indian Air Force's rank structure is based on that of the Royal Air Force, the highest rank attainable in the Indian Air Force is Marshal of the Indian Air Force, conferred by the President of India, MIAF Arjan Singh is the only officer to have achieved this rank, he was an Indian Air Force marshal who served as Chief of the Air Staff from 1964, to which year?", "answer": "1969", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Heavy Metal 2000 is a follow-up to a film which was produced by what two people?", "answer": "Ivan Reitman and Leonard Mogel", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Watch Mr. Wizard was created by the host of programs dedicated to what educational fields?", "answer": "science and technology", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Favre Lake can be found in what corner of the state of Nevada?", "answer": "the northeastern corner", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which educational organization did Amir Ullah Khan study at which is located in Anand in Gujarat, India?", "answer": "Institute of Rural Management Anand", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "The father of Rose Wilder Lane lived in his boyhood home in what state? ", "answer": "New York", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Khalil Al Ghamdi, from a sovereign Arab state in Western Asia, is a referee for what sport?", "answer": "football referee", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Damernas V\u00e4rld, a Swedish language magazine and The Lady's Realm, a British magazine both target which demographic as their key audience?", "answer": "women", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Diego Schwartzmann won the annual finals tournament in 2014, but failed to qualify to defend it in 2015, at which sport?", "answer": "tennis", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Kristofor Brown was the head writer of an MTV show created by who?", "answer": "Mike Judge", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Did Peterson's Magazine or Janus have a longer publication run?", "answer": "Peterson's Magazine", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "What type of weapon did a British Royal Marine help a soldier and firearms expert create?", "answer": "Fairbairn-Sykes Fighting Knife", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "The Hungry Hustlerz: Starvation Is Motivation is the fifth studio album by a rapper that was nominated for a Grammy award in what year?", "answer": "2002", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "\"Lionhearted\" is a song from an album released internationally under which record label ?", "answer": "Virgin EMI Records", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What year was Suspicious Partner actress Nam Hi-hyun born?", "answer": "1995", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which genus has more known species, Podocarpus or Dipsacus?", "answer": "Podocarpus", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Elizabeth Christ Trump founded a real estate company with her son, who operated primarily in what city?", "answer": "New York City", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Christine Harper covered what company that is headquartered at 1585 Broadway?", "answer": "Morgan Stanley", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "The 2013\u201314 Toronto Raptors season included a trade to the Sacramento Kings for the player of what nationality who played college for Maryland?", "answer": "Venezuelan", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "The Masquerade is a mid-sized concert venue that is located in the lowest level of what shopping and entertainment district in the Five Points neighborhood of downtown Atlanta?", "answer": "Underground Atlanta", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What star of Silver River became a U.S. citizen in 1942?", "answer": "Errol Leslie Flynn", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Who was born first, John Wetton or Gackt?", "answer": "John Kenneth Wetton", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "David Cross voiced Crane in which DreamWorks Animation franchise?", "answer": "Kung Fu Panda", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What Japanese light novel series a