n Dublin, Ireland, was founded in Minneapolis in 1949?", "answer": "Medtronic", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which battleship class had a lead ship that carried the first 14 in /45-caliber gun and was formed between 1908 and 1914?", "answer": "The \"New York\" class of battleship", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What year did Mark Holton star as Francis Buxton?", "answer": "1985", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Pursuit of Honor is a novel by Vince Flynn and the tenth novel in the series by who?", "answer": "Mitch Rapp", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Are Jackson Hole Airport and St. Mary's Airport in the same state?", "answer": "no", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Garry Elmendorf has done special effects for a 1997 American supernatural superhero horror film directed by whom?", "answer": "Mark A.Z. Dipp\u00e9", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Dubhghall mac Suibhne was a prominent 13th-century noble, the Earl of Menteith also obtained Lochranza Castle, an L-plan tower house situated on a promontory in Lochranza, on the north of the Isle of Arran, in which country?", "answer": "Scotland", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Who orchestrated the score on the album that \"Fathoms Below\" was featured on?", "answer": "Thomas Pasatieri", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What Russian film and theater actor, and director was in a 2006 Russian gothic horror film directed by Oleg Fesenko?", "answer": "Valery Valeryevich Nikolaev", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What English television presenter originally hosted the British television and radio talent show Opportunity Knocks?", "answer": "Hugh Hughes Green", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Did F. Richard Jones and R\u00e9mi Lange have the same profession?", "answer": "yes", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "In 1896, \"If\u2014\", first published this year, a poem by British Nobel laureate Rudyard Kipling, written in which year?", "answer": "1895", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Farrukh Saleem is an expert in which study of mathematical models of conflict and cooperation between intelligent rational decision-makers?", "answer": "Game theory", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which theater of the United States' War on Drugs inspired the film \"El Infierno\"?", "answer": "The Mexican Drug War", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": " Andy Halls plays as a defender for a football team that plays at what stadium", "answer": "Deva Stadium", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What number season was the first for the Raide4rs without the commissioner of the AFL in 1966?", "answer": "43rd", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Where did the serial killer that the novel The Spider and the Fly was based on die? ", "answer": "Wende Correctional Facility", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "To which professional American basketball team was a former Atlanta Hawks and Los Angeles Clippers player traded during a season for the Chicago Bulls in which they finished in last place in the Central Division?", "answer": "New York Knicks", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What Australian comedian and musician worked with Hamish Blake since 2003?", "answer": "Andy Lee", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Dreamslayer is a homage to a character created by whom?", "answer": "Stan Lee and Steve Ditko", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What is the birth date of the actor who played Dr. Loveless?", "answer": "October 20, 1934", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "The Ring of Honor 13th Anniversary Show took place at a hotel and casino that is owned and operated by Boyd Gaming, and includes an arena that can be converted into what?", "answer": "ice rink", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What website dedicated to United States technology business news did John Battelle launch during the dot-com boom? ", "answer": "The Industry Standard", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "The Jacob Straus House is a historic home open to visitors by one of the few surviving 19th-century what?", "answer": "synagogues", "type": "bridg