a,is a genus of legume in the Fabaceae family?", "answer": "Colvillea", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "What film marked the directorial debut of the director and screenwriter who wrote and directed the film \"Monster\" in 2014?", "answer": "Spellbound", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What is a club who's player wears Nike Hypervenom boots?", "answer": "Leicester City", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What sport does Rohan Bopanna and Cara Black have in common?", "answer": "tennis", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Church of St. Anthony of Padua, Istanbul and Galatasaray High School are both located where?", "answer": "Turkey", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "What song does Ozzy refer to in his song \"Dreamer\"  that was written by John Lennon, that encourages a world at peace?", "answer": "Imagine", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What prize was won by the American economist whose life story is included in those in Radicals for Capitalism? ", "answer": "Nobel Memorial Prize in Economic Sciences", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Geoff Bell had a role in the 2005 British-American film about what subject?", "answer": "football hooliganism", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "How many destinations are served by the airline that Indian merged into on 26 February 2011?", "answer": "60 international destinations", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What is the nationality of the singer of \"Gonna Make You A Star?\"", "answer": "English", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What is the name of the automotive nameplate used by Fuji Heavy Industries, whose name is derived from the Lexicon Branding?", "answer": "Subaru Outback", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What 19-year MLB veteran who was initially a shortstop was also featured as a cover athlete on the collectible card game MLB Showdown?", "answer": "Chipper Jones", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Tadpole is a 2002 American romantic comedy film directed by Gary Winick, it stars which American actress, singer and dancer?", "answer": "Beatrice \"Bebe\" Neuwirth", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Jon B. Perdue previously wrote for a channel commonly abbreviated to FNC - What was the full name of the channel? ", "answer": "Fox News Channel", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Are Andrew Vachss and Lorine Niedecker both poets?", "answer": "no", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Which mathematician, who was among many who proposed the SYZ conjecture, won the Fields medal in 1982?", "answer": "Shing-Tung Yau", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What state of Germany was the 2012\u201313 DFB-Pokal defending champions from?", "answer": "North Rhine-Westphalia", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Love in a Wood is a 1915 British silent comedy film directed by Maurice Elvey, the film is a contemporary-set version of the play \"As You Like It\", a pastoral comedy by who?", "answer": "William Shakespeare", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which magazine covers a wider range of topics, Decibel or Paper?", "answer": "Paper", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "who produced the modern bolt-action sniper rifle  which Steyr SSG 04 was the basis of ", "answer": "Steyr Mannlicher", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What is a classification scheme that assigns an animal and its reputed attributes to each year in a repeating 12-year cycle, which has the 2nd of the 12-year cycle of animals appear in it?", "answer": "Chinese zodiac", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Who was an american author and screenwriter who wrote Something Wicked This Way Comes?", "answer": "Ray Bradbury", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Willi Rinow attended the Humboldt University of Berlin, studying under professors that included what German theoretical physicist who won the Nobel Prize in Physics in 1918?", "answer": "Max Karl Ernst Ludwig Planck", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What is the location of the site of the upper school founded by James Pilkington? ", "answer": "Rivington Lane in Rivington, Lancashire", "