y", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What dish do both Gino's Pizza and Spaghetti and the Pizza Factory both make?", "answer": "Pizza", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "what role did  American actor, who also stars in Poor Paul play in Cheaper by the Dozen", "answer": "Henry", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "When was the school that  Raoul Alexander Mulder is based in founded?", "answer": "1853", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "During the 32nd season of the Utah Jazz franchise they traded an American professional basketball player who was a gold medal winner on what Summer Olympic team?", "answer": "United States national team", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Mullah Mohammad Rabbani Akhund, was one of the main leaders of the Taliban movement, he was second in power only to which supreme leader?", "answer": "Mullah Mohammed Omar", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What is the name of this American film and television actor born in 1974 who starred in \"Mind Ripper?\"", "answer": "Giovanni Ribisi", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": " Great Conewago Presbyterian Church used as a Confederate Army hospital during a military invasion of Pennsylvania by the main Confederate army under who?", "answer": "General Robert E. Lee", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Halfdan Ragnarsson was a commander of a coalition of Norse warriors, originating from where?", "answer": "Denmark", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Rod Sterling narrated a series based on a book by what German author?", "answer": "Erich von D\u00e4niken", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Were either The Creatures or Soundgarden formed in the 1990's?", "answer": "no", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "What nationality are the Johan Cruyff Shield and SBV Vitesses football clubs?", "answer": "Dutch", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Smoke Break was a song written by the singer-songwriter who received an Academy Award nomination for what 2011 song?", "answer": "Coming Home", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "National Sports Stadium is a multi-purpose stadium in Ulaanbaatar, Mongolia, The Naadam festival, which celebrates Mongolian independence, is held there every when? ", "answer": "July", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What type of sport did this musician play professionally for whom the American country music artist Toby Keith wrote a tribute to in his album American Ride?", "answer": "basketball", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What host of Going, Going, Gone became known for \"It's a Knockout\"?", "answer": "Stuart Hall", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "The Estadio Nacional de Panam\u00e1 is also named after a person who played which sport?", "answer": "Baseball", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "In what year was the microbiologist who first developed the MMR vaccine born?", "answer": "1919", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Who has the highest scope of profession in Arthur Rosson or  Hall Bartlett", "answer": "Hall Bartlett", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "What is the name of the band that features a person that has also worked with Talas, Steve Vai, David Lee Roth, Mr. Big and The Winery Dogs?", "answer": "Niacin", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "The 21st Foyle Film Festival included the Northern Ireland premiere of a movie based on a novel by whom?", "answer": "Evelyn Waugh", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Fine Line Features marketed the 1991 film written and directed by whom?", "answer": "Jim Jarmusch", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "In what country was Umoe founded?", "answer": "Buskerud", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "The author of Method of Fluxions was born in what year?", "answer": "1642", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "In which suburb is found the University where Naguib Kanawat teaches?", "answer": "Macquarie Park", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What award is issued by the Georgia Institute of Technology's previously known as Ivan Allen Jr. Prize for Progress & Service until 2010 which recognizes the late Ivan Allen Jr,. A Georgia Tech 