alled Telebehi by what Iron Age people?", "answer": "=\"Lycians\">Lycians", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Children's National Medical Center and Sibley Memorial Hospital, are both located in which US location?", "answer": "Washington D.C.", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Colin Campbell, 1st Baron Clyde commanded the first opium war and then commanded a war called?", "answer": "Second Anglo-Sikh War", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which fortress that controlled the entranceway between Kattegat and \u00d8resund was in \"Hamlet\"?", "answer": "Kronborg", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Were the TRS-80 Color Computer and CCE MC-1000 both home computers?", "answer": "yes", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Both Manny Coto and B\u00e9la Tarr are American director?", "answer": "no", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Coatbridge is a town in a country that has how many Islands ?", "answer": "more than 790 islands", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which print outlet, \"Wizard or Wizard\" or \"The Brown Spectator\", is known as a student-run conservative political outlet?", "answer": "The Brown Spectator", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "What was the occupation of the person whose first serious lover was Richard Chanlaire?", "answer": "composer and pianist", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which Baroque composer was known for writing single movment sonatas? ", "answer": "Domenico Scarlatti", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Greg Hoffman was working on \"Saw III,\" a 2006 American horror film, but was unable to finish his work on the film, which was directed by who?", "answer": "Darren Lynn Bousman", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Who publishes the magazine where The Lost Boy was first published?", "answer": "the Hearst Corporation", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which town located in the county seat of Oktobbeha County Mississippi is the Cotton District located?", "answer": "Starkville", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "The 2000 coach of the coll