ed Schoonmaker Reef significant ?", "answer": "American", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What association hosted the Banting Lecture which was named after the co-discoverer of insulin?", "answer": "American Diabetes Association", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Andrew Wyatt is the vocalist in which band often represented by a silhouette image of a jackalope?", "answer": "Miike Snow", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "In the 2016 American adult computer-animated comedy film directed by Greg Tiernan, which song features Snoop Dogg?", "answer": "Wiggle", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which American beer had been a sponser for the 1995-1996 season of the British Basketball League?", "answer": "Budweiser", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "SkyWest Airlines is a North American airline owned by SkyWest, Inc. and headquartered in which city in Utah, U.S., it flies as SkyWest Airlines in a partnership with Alaska Airlines, an American airline based in the Seattle metropolitan area of the state of Washington?", "answer": "St. George", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which drink contains raw egg as one of the three primary ingredients, The Matador and Tamagozake?", "answer": "Tamagozake", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "In what year did the voice actor of \"Doc Hudson\" in the animated film \"Cars\" die?", "answer": "2008", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What nationality where Terry Disley and Billy Bragg?", "answer": "English", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which state is home to the music hall of fame that was both incorporated in 2005 and has inducted the singer Randy Jackson?", "answer": "New York", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "This British-Australian singer was a member of a rock duo which became associated with the members of what band?", "answer": "Bee Gees", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Paul Warren starred in what 2010 movie along side Liam Neeson, Ralph Fiennes and Sam Worthington?", "answer": "Clash of the Titans", "type": "bridge"}, {"question