es Senate Committee on Environment and Public Works", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Overload is an upcoming video game being developed by Revival Productions, the game has been described as a 'spiritual successor' to the video games \"Descent\" and which 1996 first-person shooter video game developed by Parallax Software and published by Interplay Productions?", "answer": "Descent II", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Jameel McCline lost four attempts at the world heavyweight title to a boxer of what nationality?", "answer": "Ukrainian", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which director directed more films, Sydney Pollack or Millard Webb?", "answer": "Sydney Irwin Pollack", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Game Face and March of the Penguins, are which type of film?", "answer": "documentary", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Which city did the writer of Enion spend most of his life?", "answer": "London", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Damien Derek Trotter is a fictional character in the BBC series \"Only Fools and Horses\", a British television sitcom created and written by who?", "answer": "John Sullivan", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What is the name of this American actress, musician, and director, borh in October 1989, who starred in Sleepover?", "answer": "Brie Larson", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Between the two colleges, Illinois Institute of Technology and University of Salento, which offers more academic faculties?", "answer": "Illinois Institute of Technology", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "What is the name of this independent, Anglican, co-educational, private day school that is located on South Terrace in South Australia?", "answer": "Pulteney Grammar School", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which mountain is highest, Saltoro Kangri or Gasherbrum IV?", "answer": "Gasherbrum IV", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Which virtual channel is a multi-channel video retailer and American cable, satellite and broadcast television ne