ington", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Who helped found one of the top 50 largest craft breweries in the US in 1983?", "answer": "Brian McMenamin", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Who founded the tire company who was used by Saab in the 1993 Barber Saab Pro Series?", "answer": "Frank Seiberling", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Who is a former member of a Afghan party established in 1965?", "answer": "Nur ul-Haq Ulumi", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "A carotid Doppler machine uses what change in frequency or wavelength of a wave for an observer who is moving relative to the wave source?", "answer": "Doppler effect", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "In what year was the winner of the 57th Macau Grand Prix born?", "answer": "1987", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What cricket series did Ashton Agar play in for Australia?", "answer": "The 2013 Ashes series", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Seneca white deer live in the confines of the Army Depot that was officially shut down in what year?", "answer": "2000", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What is the name of the 60.3 acre parcel park and has the oldest oldest surviving building in the summit area of Mount Washington?", "answer": "Mount Washington State Park", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Was South Park episode \"The Poor Kid,\" the season premier or season finale?", "answer": "season finale", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Who directed a film that used \"Zenzenzense\" as a theme song?", "answer": "Makoto Shinkai", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "The bridge spanning the River Truyere near Ruynes-en-Margeride was built by a graduate of which university?", "answer": "\u00c9cole Centrale Paris", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Neil Canton worked on a film, in which year, with Christopher Lloyd?", "answer": "1985", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What is the nationality of the driver who was awarded the victory in the 2016 Mexico City ePrix ?", "answer": "Belgian", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Who is the male star of the film that closed The 27th Toronto International Film Festival ?", "answer": "Antonio Banderas.", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What six season television series first aired in October 2005?", "answer": "Lost", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "The Seychelles parakeet, occurred in the Indian Ocean islands of the Seychelles group, it resembled the Alexandrine parakeet, a member of the psittaciformes order and of the family Psittaculidae, the species is named after who?", "answer": "Alexander the Great", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Noel Sheppard had contributed to which conservative U.S. monthly magazine covering news and politics, edited by R. Emmett Tyrrell, Jr.?", "answer": "The American Spectator", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Sheldon Adelson is the founder, chairman and chief executive officer of a corporation that is based in which US state ?", "answer": "Nevada", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Who has served as Acting United States Attorney for the District of Arizona and as United States Secretary of Homeland Security in their lifetime, Daniel G. Knauss or Janet Napolitano?", "answer": "Janet Napolitano", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What states does the wilderness containing the Bad Luck Creek span?", "answer": "Idaho and Montana", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Young Earth creationism, believed by Andrew A. Snelling, holds that the universe, Earth, and all life on Earth were created by who?", "answer": "God", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "The 1923 college football team coached by Bill Roper was from which state?", "answer": "New Jersey", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What is the name of the Vietnamese beer that the Vietnam's leading beer producer make and whose name was changed by the communist government?", "answer": "33 Beer", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Karamdaata was a Hindi-language Indian film starring which actor who also won a Filmfare award in 1968 for best performance in \u201cBrahmachari\u201d?", 