uel to the 2008 film directed by whom?", "answer": "Paul W. S. Anderson", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which writer won the Nobel Prize, Alice Munro or T. F. Powys?", "answer": "Alice Ann Munro", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "The artwork of Gustav Klimt's prot\u00e9g\u00e9 is featured in which city in Austria?", "answer": "Vienna", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "When was the Greenup County resident for whom a 36-room lodge is named after born?", "answer": "August 8, 1906", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "In which university stadium the Golden Gophers played their home games?", "answer": "University of Minnesota", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What is the birthday of the Argentine defender Associazione Sportiva Roma signed before the 2001 season?", "answer": "23 March 1978", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Who is the cover athlete of the videogame in which The Walker appears in the soundtrack?", "answer": "Kyrie Irving", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which director also worked as a make-up artist, Josh Trank or D.W. Kann?", "answer": "D.W. Kann", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Toy Story and Unidentified Flying Oddball, are Walt Disney ?", "answer": "Walt Disney", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Which genus has more known species, Eucommia or Rhoicissus?", "answer": "Rhoicissus", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Who started Penn Radio?", "answer": "Penn Fraser Jillette", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Were was the company based to which David Vogel Uihlein, Sr was the heir ?", "answer": "Milwaukee, Wisconsin,", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What Vietnamese-born actor starred in Dragon Eyes with Jean-Claude Van Damme?", "answer": "Cung Le", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which came out first, Jungle Cat or The Lion King?", "answer": "Jungle Cat", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Which bishop founded Louth Park Abbey and served as a royal justice in Lincolnshire?", "answer": "Alexander of Lincoln", "type": "bridge"}, {"ques