ed in New York City in 1995?", "answer": "Fountains of Wayne", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Rebel Without Claws was directed by an animator born in which year ?", "answer": "1906", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "From when the British pub chain is owning the Flask public house who also operates nearly 220 pubs?", "answer": "1904", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "When was the Argentine politician which  Rodolfo Gabrielli served as a minister of Interior during their presidencies born ", "answer": "October 5, 1941", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What is the alternative title of the official national anthem of Bermuda?", "answer": "God Save the King", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Chef Goes Nanners is the seventh episode of a season of South Park containing how many episodes total?", "answer": "17", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Are Thyme and Cortaderia both aromatic plants?", "answer": "no", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "What Moonrunners father co-wrote the theme song to Thunder Road?", "answer": "James Mitchum", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Are Haiyang and Nanchuan District both in China?", "answer": "yes", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Only the Brave is a movie about a unit in what branch of the military?", "answer": "United States Army Reserve", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What record company was the song Oh My My released on? ", "answer": "Apple Records", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "When was the American industrialist died who built the Memorial Presbyterian Church?", "answer": "May 20, 1913", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "The Zionskirche was damaged during what British/American attack during World War II?", "answer": "bombing of Dresden", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "When does the recorder of Got No Reason Now for Goin' Home born?", "answer": "October 11, 1943", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which song by Francesco Sartori does Jackie Evancho include in her debut album?", "answer": "Con te partir\u00f2", "type"