uffer and Blind Melon have in common?", "answer": "American", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Of the two singers/musicians, Bae Suzy and Peter T\u00e4gtgren, one is also known for his/her acting. Which of these two musicians also has the title of \"actor\" on their resume?", "answer": "Bae Su-ji (; born October 10, 1994), better known by the mononym Suzy, is a South Korean singer and actress.", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Not including Neidpath, who owned the other castle that Sir Simon Fraser had for most of its existence?", "answer": "the Tweedie family", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Robert N. Charrette (born 1953) is an award-winning graphic artist, game designer, sculptor and author, Charrette produced gaming products for FASA Corporation, an American publisher of role-playing games, wargames and board games between 1980 and 2001, after which they closed publishing operations for several years, becoming an IP holding company under the name FASA Inc, in which year,a wholly owned subsidiary called FASA Games Inc. went into operation, using the name and logo with permission of the parent company.?", "answer": "2012", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What was the nickname of a lefthanded player on the Princeton Rays?", "answer": "The Perfect Storm", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "are Yuma International Airport and  Minot International Airport in the same state", "answer": "no", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "What is the name of the small railroad junction seven miles north of the Savanna Army Depot?", "answer": "Blanding", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "L. William Seidman was an economic adviser to the President who was the 33rd governor of what state?", "answer": "California", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which athletic stadium, built on the same site as the former FA Cup Final venue, also hosted the World Cup?", "answer": "Crystal Palace National Sports Centre", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What was the breakout movie for the ac