nown for his voyages of 1642 and which year, in the service of the Dutch East India Company (VOC)?", "answer": "1644", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What is the birthdate of the man that is being succeeded by Stuart Chambers?", "answer": "8 April 1942", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Emma Watson received critical accolades for what character role in a movie based on J.K. Rowling's book of the same name?", "answer": "Hermione Granger", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Craig Frost is known as the keyboardist fo an American rock band whose names is a play on words of what?", "answer": "Grand Trunk Western Railroad", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": " Jon Amiel and Kurt Gerron have what in common?", "answer": "film director", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "The Commanding Army General during the United States Forces - Iraq was the 12th commander of what unit?", "answer": "United States Central Command", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Edward Keonjian and Edward Avedisian, have what in common?", "answer": "Edward", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Which organization manages the Colne and Blackpool South railway stations?", "answer": "Northern", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which is a magazine that has a subscription service available for mobile devices, The New York Enterprise Report or Hour Detroit?", "answer": "Hour Detroit", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "What French hard rock metal band dedicated a studio disc to an Australian singer and songwriter born 9 July 1946?", "answer": "Trust", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Edward F. Cline and Mike Hodges, are screenwriters?", "answer": "yes", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "What actress and singer is overdubbed in German by Gabrielle Pietermann?", "answer": "Selena Gomez", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "A band that formed in 1996 and obtained a Grammy Award working with Jack Joseph Puig is fronted by what female singer?", "answer": "Gwen Stefani", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Black existentialism or Africana critical theory is a school of thought that \"critiques domination and affirms the empowerment of Black people in the world\" and may also be seen as method, which allows one to read works by African-American writers such as W. E. B. Du Bois, James Baldwin, and Ralph Ellison, best known for what novel?", "answer": "\"Invisible Man\"", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Who is credited with composing the music for the song named in a famous Guatemalan lottery dedicated to help the deafblind?", "answer": "A. Longo", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Prasad's dance choreographer is what Indian choreographer, who was noted as one of the first to bring contemporary jazz and western forms of dance to India?", "answer": "Shiamak Davar", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Blood Link starred which actor and musician, known for his role on Law and Order?", "answer": "Michael Moriarty", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Lee Towndrow worked as a visual effects artist on what 2015 British-American romantic drama film that was directed by Todd Haynes?", "answer": "Carol", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What magazine launched in August 2001, Filament or Elle Girl?", "answer": "Elle Girl", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Which Caldwell County native founded J.C. Penney stores in 1902? ", "answer": "James Cash Penney", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What NCAA Division II conference featured former NFL and CFL star SHadrick McAfee?", "answer": "Gulf South Conference", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What is the king of this ancient nation, in which the people worshiped Imentet as a goddess representing the necropolises west of the Nile, called?", "answer": "pharaoh", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Westport Airport, in the district of Wichita, is in the Class C airspace of which neighbouring airport which is the largest and busiest in the state of Kansas?", "answer": "Wichita Dwight D. Eisenhower National Airport", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Racism without Racists was published by the house founded in what year?", "answer": "1949", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Vanessa Seward worked for an American fashion designer who directed what 2009 film?", "answer": "A Single Man", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "In what year was the executive producer of Mannix born?", "answer": "1930", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "When was the Isle of Man transferred from ITV Granada to ITV Border, previously Border Television?", "answer": "15 July 2009", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What animal does Galgo Espa\u00f1ol and Akita have in common?", "answer": "dog", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "The current holder of Ligue 1 Young Player of the Year plays for what Spanish football club?", "answer": "FC Barcelona", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Sofia Black-D'Elia, is an American actress, as of 2017, she stars as Sabrina on comedy \"The Mick\", an American sitcom television series broadcast, on which organization?", "answer": "Fox", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "When did Olav Bjaaland arrive at the South Pole?", "answer": "14 December 1911", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Roland Harper, is a former professional American football player who played running back for eight seasons for the Chicago Bears, he was a starting fullback known in his playing days as a punishing blocker who opened holes in opposing defenses for which star halfback, and an American football running back who played for the Chicago Bears of the National Football League (NFL) for thirteen seasons?", "answer": "Walter Jerry Payton", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which area, known for gambling, was the 2015 Miss Universe Pagent held?", "answer": "Las Vegas", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which river crossed the city which was at 40 km southwest from Fabro?", "answer": "Tiber", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Deconstructed contained a song that was used in the comedy horror film directed by whom?", "answer": "Anthony Waller", "type": "bridge"},