e 2015\u201316 Hofstra Pride men's basketball team represented Hofstra University is a private, non-profit, nonsectarian university in which country, during the 2015\u201316 NCAA Division I men's basketball season?", "answer": "United States", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What was the occupation of the man from the fifth-largest city in the state of Ohio who was declared dead in 1960 and later found alive?", "answer": "cookware salesman", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What genre is the 2000 film that Todd Phillips is best known for?", "answer": "comedy", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Both MedStar Georgetown University Hospital and Children's National Medical Center are located in which U.S. city?", "answer": "Washington, D.C.", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Criminal is a film that features which Israeli actress and model?", "answer": "Gal Gadot-Varsano", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "A Brilliant Genocide was written about a revolution started by which resistance leader?", "answer": "Joseph Kony", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Who were the other two people of the trial that John Port was involved in besides the second wife of King Henry VIII?", "answer": "Sir Thomas More, John Fisher", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Glimpse of the Garden (1957) was created by a filmmaker that was this nationality?", "answer": "American", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Do both Brian Molko and Tony Harnell have connections to the music industry?", "answer": "yes", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "which affiliate of Nixon has its headquarters in New york, New York?", "answer": "Barneys New York", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which mountain range is located in both Georgia and Virginia?", "answer": "The Blue Ridge Mountains", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What is the name of the series of poems written between 1949 and 1955 by an English-American poet best known for \"Funeral Blues\"?", "answer": "Horae Canonicae", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What is the population as of the 2010 census of the city the 2016 Central Oklahoma Bronchos football team played their home games in?", "answer": "81,405", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which opera has more acts, Lucrezia Borgia or Nixon in China?", "answer": "Nixon in China", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "What is the green that centres the village where Greystoke Castle is located, surrounded by?", "answer": "stone houses and cottages.", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What television series is based on a film starring an actor who appeared in Mickey Blue Eyes and Notting Hill?", "answer": "About a Boy", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Who has more scope of profession, Ren\u00e9 Clair or Max Linder?", "answer": "Max Linder", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Tim Daggett appeared in the 1984 LA Olympics alongside which owner of a Norman, Oklahoma-based gymnastics academy?", "answer": "Bart Conner", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Falmouth is a census-designated place (CDP) within the town of Falmouth in Cumberland County, a county located in the state of Maine, in which country?", "answer": "United States.", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Are Boy George and Florence Welch both from England?", "answer": "yes", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "In what year was Bruno Rezende's sport added to the Pan American Games?", "answer": "1955", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What is the name of the dealer typically employed by casinos who might work the game Blackjack Switch patented in 2009?", "answer": "croupier", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Are Ceropegia and Pilea in the same family?", "answer": "no", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Which of the navel leader was replace by the man who succeeded Adolf Hitler?", "answer": "Erich Johann Albert Raeder", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Peter Gene Hernandez wrote the song \"Long Distance\" for which studio album?", "answer": "Human", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which English Romantic poet wrote the sonnet that inspired the character Ozymandias on the children's television show Ace of Wands?", "answer": "Percy Bysshe Shelley", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Ty Dolla Sign appeared on the 2014 album Ohio belonging to which American rapper? ", "answer": "Stalley", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What American playwright, stage director and screenwriter of a screenplay \"Rope\"?", "answer": "Arthur Laurents", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which animated Walt Disney Feature had original songs written by Elton John and scores composed by Nick Glennie-Smith?", "answer": "The Lion King", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "For what team is the cricket bowler, who is considered to be the fastest, play a role of captain?", "answer": "Karachi Dolphins", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "One of the film stars in the Australian comedy film \"Now Add Honey\", is recognized for playing Elle Woods in the Australian production of which film?", "answer": "\"Legally Blonde: The Musical\"", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "In Brierley Hill what factory was closed down in 1980s to develop a shopping center made in the 1985 and 1990?", "answer": "Round Oak Steelworks", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What is formerly the Cowboys Stadium where the 2015 Cotton Bowl classic was played?", "answer": "AT&T Stadium", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Wendell Phillips Before the Concord Lyceum, is an essay style letter-to-the-editor written by Henry David Thoreau, an essayist, poet, philosopher, abolitionist, naturalist, tax resister, development critic, surveyor, and historian, of which nationality? ", "answer": "American", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which tennis player is from the United States, Shelby Cannon or Pierre-Hugues Herbert?", "answer": "Shelby Cannon", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Based on their current home, is The Fray or OK Go based further west?", "answer": "OK Go", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "What American actor had roles in both films \"The L