ompany that provides listings for self-storage units similar to what  online marketplace and hospitality service?", "answer": "Airbnb", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Where was the boxer from Shadow Boxers born?", "answer": "Dutch professional female", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Arena is a documentary series that has aired a show chronicling which Canadian filmmaker?", "answer": "Mary Harron", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Breno Giacomini founded Football Without Barriers along with which tight end drafted in 2008?", "answer": "Gary Michael Barnidge", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Who tried for second degree murder from an incident that happened at The Retreat at Twin Lakes?", "answer": "George Zimmerman", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Do Griffon Bleu de Gascogne and Leonberger originate in the same country?", "answer": "no", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Which  \"Star Wars\" spin-off of 1978, directed by Steve Binder, did Wookiee Planet C make appearances in?", "answer": "Star Wars Holiday Special", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Who is an English comedian that was also involved in High Heels and Low Life's?", "answer": "Mel Smith", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "The Logie Awards of 1998 featured guests including one of the stars of what popular NBC sitcom?", "answer": "\"Friends\"", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What 2002-2003 mini series that chronicled the American/Soviet space race featured one of the original 7 Project Mercury astronauts in an interview?", "answer": "Rocket Science", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Who directed a 1979 American horror film that starred one of only 12 athletes in the history of American professional sports to have played both Major League Baseball and in the National Basketball Association?", "answer": "David Schmoeller", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What pageant did Halima Aden win", "answer": "Miss Minnesota USA", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What is the name of the Canadien-American actress who has gotten nominations in the Annie Awards and the Daytime Emmys who plays a main character in the animated television series \"Teen Titans\"?", "answer": "Tara Strong", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Mirza Ahmad Ispahani was the first chairman of an airline out of what main hub?", "answer": "Karachi", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Who served as a congressman for the the district which contains the cities of Lexington (including its suburbs), Richmond, and Frankfort, the state capital?", "answer": "Ben Chandler", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Were the makers of the board game \"Titan\" the same makers of \"The Farming Game?\"", "answer": "no", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "The Internet Tax Freedom Act was co-authored by which Oregon Senator?", "answer": "Ronald Lee Wyden", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What California highway is the longest in the state and is associated with the Ventura River?", "answer": "U.S. Route 101", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Who is directing the American noir thriller-drama film that starts the Australian actor best known for playing Tommy Caffee on the television series \"Brotherhood\"?", "answer": "Steven Knight", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Where did the runner up in the Arizona Democratic primary of 2004 graduate college from?", "answer": "West Point", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What 1986 American animated mystery comedy was storyboarded by Matthew O'Callaghan?", "answer": "The Great Mouse Detective", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "ZZ Ward was a guest appearing in the release of what artist's hip hop recording?", "answer": "Asher Roth", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Dale Crover was briefly a drummer for a band that dissolved in what year?", "answer": "1994", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What does the then-Minister of Foreign Affairs painted by Thijs Niemantsverdriet currently serve as?", "answer": "First Vice-President of the European Commission", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Davi