ision crime drama series, starring David Suchet, the series notably starred which Irish actor, whose feature film debut was in the fantasy war epic \"300\" (2007)?", "answer": "Michael Fassbender", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "The Russian novel \"Antonina\" was influenced by an English novel by what author?", "answer": "Charlotte Bront\u00eb", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which film, based on a novel, featured Jung Yu-Mi?", "answer": "The Crucible", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Though usually directing films, who recently starred in the film Swades?", "answer": "Lekh Tandon", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Where were the Aztecs located?", "answer": "a sub-valley of the Valley of Mexico", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "History is the twelfth studio album by which American singer-songwriter, who was the father of folk singer Loudon Wainwright III, and singer Sloan Wainwright?", "answer": "Loudon Snowden Wainwright Jr.", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What studio owned by the Toei Company produces the TV series Pretty Cure?", "answer": "Toei Animation", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Are Sparaxis and Salvinia both types of plant?", "answer": "yes", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Romance & Cigarettes included which singer, who came to prominence with her single \"Candy\"?", "answer": "Amanda Leigh Moore", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Who was the kicker for the college team of the player drafted by the Ravens in the second round of the 2008 NFL Draft in 2006?", "answer": "Jeremy Ito", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Are Danny Shirley and Serri both singers?", "answer": "yes", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Isidro Ros R\u00edos plays for a team that plays in which division ?", "answer": "Segunda Divisi\u00f3n B \u2013 Group 4", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What dog breed is more likely a better swimmer, Mucuchies or Flat-Coated Retriever?", "answer": "Flat-Coated Retriever", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Name of autobiography written by advisor and confidant of Queen catalina of castile who  governed Castile as regent from 1406 until 1418 during the minority of her son.", "answer": "Memorias", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "In what year did The Wild Thornberrys air on Nicktoonsters?", "answer": "2008", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What 2011 movie did the actress known for the role of Nina Cassady appear in?", "answer": "A Novel Romance", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Would Bob Woodward or Edgar Rice Burroughs be more likely to produce a work of fiction depicting an epic hero?", "answer": "Edgar Rice Burroughs", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "In the Crosswind is a drama about this, a mass deportation by the Soviet Union in 1940-1941?", "answer": "June deportation", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which battle of the Hundred Years' War is the subject of Leslie Barringer's historical novel?", "answer": "The Battle of Agincourt", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Where is a famous tourist definition named after the common term for maize located?", "answer": "Mitchell, South Dakota", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Where is the company that Jenny Ming is CEO of headquartered?", "answer": "San Diego, California", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which Jacksonville Jaguars season featured some games coached by Doug Marrone, and some games coached by Gus Bradley?", "answer": "2016 Jacksonville Jaguars season", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "When did the inspiration of Supermac service as Prime Minister of the United Kingdom?", "answer": "1957 to 1963", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Who was the member of the \"Jonas Brothers\" that released the song \"Body Moves\"?", "answer": "Joe Jonas", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What research group is an independent source of information for the group of countries consisting of Canada, France, Germany, Italy, Japan, the United Kingdom and the United States", "answer": "G7 Research Group", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What is t