spired by his daughter?", "answer": "Offside", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Who was born in 1954 and appointed Arthur Sinodinos as Cabinet Secretary?", "answer": "Malcolm Turnbull", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Peter Rabbit contains a live action role played by what Irish actor and writer who is the son of actor Brendan Gleeson?", "answer": "Domhnall Gleeson", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which french drama was nominated for the  Palme d'Or at the 2013 Cannes film festival?", "answer": "Young & Beautiful", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "The 22 acre complex located between 48th and 51st streets in New York City was designed by what architect?", "answer": "Wallace K. Harrison", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Were Operation Nordwind and the Battle of Peleliu both fought in World War II?", "answer": "yes", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Who would be older in 2017, Brian Connolly or Chris Daughtry?", "answer": "Brian Francis Connolly", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "what job/hobby do Andy Ram and Arnaud Cl\u00e9ment have in common?", "answer": "professional tennis", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "The Latino World Order was led by a wrestler born in which year ?", "answer": "1967", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "The Agrotis alluaudi moth is found on an island in what ocean?", "answer": "Indian Ocean", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Who had only one brother and was a british executioner for 23 years?", "answer": "John Ellis", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Simmons Bedding Company is the sister company of the mattress manufacturer based in what city?", "answer": "Hoffman Estates, Illinois", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What album was also the name of a tour and film directed by Albert Magnoli?", "answer": "Purple Rain", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Lamedh is part of what type of script used in writing the Hebrew language?", "answer": "abjad", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Garnett Brown has worked with what inductee into the