ctor", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "What is the name of the hurricane that made landfall on Belize on August 4, 2016 and ultimately left 81 fatalities in Mexico?", "answer": "Hurricane Earl", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "The Minneapolis-St. Paul Airport Trams and the airport also known as World Chamberlain Field were both constructed by whom?", "answer": "Poma-Otis Transit Company", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": " Dan Balan, along with O-Zone, produced a hit single that was sung in what language?", "answer": "Romanian", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What Indian amusement park did Jagdish Narain Sapru serve as the chairman of?", "answer": "Nicco Park", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What Soviet political leader held high regard for the author of Mozg Armii, a 3 volume military theory book?", "answer": "Joseph Stalin", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What do the collection of andesite stones found in Ica Province, Peru offer proof of?", "answer": "humans and dinosaurs coexisted", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "A county in the East of England has one of the largest self-suffcient communities which posses 1500 acres of local land. What is this called?", "answer": "The Abbey", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What type of drug is Oxandrolone that was found in the system of  Cinthya Dom\u00ednguez in 2015?", "answer": "steroid", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "This South-African born actress played a real-life person who was executed in 2002 for crimes committed in what movie?", "answer": "Monster", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Are Buckinghamia and Stipa plants?", "answer": "yes", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Which Canadian singer sang \" something stronger\" in the musical applause?", "answer": "Len Cariou", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What turbojet engine produced by Teledyne CAE is also known as The Turbomeca Marbore?", "answer": "Teledyne CAE J69", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "When did the ninth season of Will & Grace premiere?", "answer": "September 28, 2017, on NBC", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What was a mixed martial arts event held by the Ultimate Fighting Championship on March 11, 1994, was the first bout an American mixed martial arts referee officiated who also officiated bouts in Bellator, and is a qualified boxing referee?", "answer": "Ultimate Fighting Championship Part II", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What is the code name for a German assault during WWII that was the invasion of Denmark and Norway in April 1940?", "answer": "Weser\u00fcbung", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What show did the Russian professional latin and ballroom dancer born on January 19, 1980 appear on?", "answer": "Strictly Come Dancing", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which member of a collegiate athletic conference comprising sports teams from eight private institutions of higher education in the Northeastern United States played their home games at Robert K. Kraft Field at Lawrence A. Wien Stadium?", "answer": "The 2011 Columbia Lions", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "In what year did this pilot episode air of this American animated television series, whose title character held the same name as the show and also included the character Mrs. Puff?", "answer": "May 1, 1999", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What is the active ingredient in the product Freederm that treats acne?", "answer": "Nicotinamide", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What Australian sportsman died in a suburb of Adelaide in the City of Burnside and the City of Campbelltown?", "answer": "Ernest Jones", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What Big 12 Conference basketball team did Myles Turner play for?", "answer": "Texas Longhorns men's basketball", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which  districts in the Ashanti Region of Ghana is Jachie-Pramso  a village in", "answer": "The Bosomtwe District", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What nationality are the artists Axl Rose and Lux Interior?", "answer": "American", "type": "co