 in which year ?", "answer": "1961", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What actor starred in both \"Judgement at Nuremberg\" and \"The Defector?\"", "answer": "Montgomery Clift", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What character did actor Paul L. Smith play opposite Robin Williams in the 1980 American musical comedy film directed by Robert Altman?", "answer": "Bluto", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "America's Music: The Roots of Country is a film that touches on which bar-style music, common in the South US?", "answer": "honky-tonk", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Of the two possible places where Abdemon, king of Cyprus, was born, which one was also known as Sour?", "answer": "Tyre", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What is the age of these mountains that start in the northeast corner of Georgia and had the Georgia Gold Rush spread throughout it in 1829?", "answer": "over 1 billion years", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What is the place where NSMRL is located on known as?", "answer": "\"Home of the Submarine Force\"", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Wing warping, a system for lateral aircraft control, was pioneered by the Wright brothers during their first controlled, sustained flight near which now-famous location?", "answer": "Kitty Hawk, North Carolina", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Anthony Joseph Daniher and Neale Francis Daniher both played for which Australian Football League?", "answer": "Essendon Football Clubs", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Golden Circle is a subsidiary of a company that had how many brand in 2015?", "answer": "13", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What 1993 comedy film stars  an American actor, stand-up comedian, and voice actor who appeared on May 28, 1959, episode of the TV quiz program \"You Bet Your Life\"?", "answer": "Dorf Goes Fishing", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What is the birthdate of this prominent sufferer of severe combined immunodeficiency, referred to as the bubble boy, famous for living in a sterile environment?", "answer": "September 21, 1971", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What work by Chinua Achebe did Benedicto Wokomaatani Malunga translate, is the most widely read book in modern African literature? ", "answer": "Things Fall Apart", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What company has a brewing company is Nova Scotia and is the result of merger between Interbrew and AmBev?", "answer": "InBev", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "This pale is 4.7% ABV and brewed by Desnoes & Geddes in Jamaica", "answer": "Red Stripe", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What other attorney was along with  the attorney who specializes in constitutional law litigation and was Senior Trial Counsel at the Ann Arbor-based Christian, conservative, nonprofit, public interest law firm based in Ann Arbor, Michigan?", "answer": "David Yerushalmi", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "How old was the man for whom \u0100ryabha\u1e6da numeration is named when he wrote \u0100ryabha\u1e6d\u012bya?", "answer": "23", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "He was born into an ecclesiastical family on 28 April 1912, educated at Shrewsbury and Christ Church, Oxford and ordained in 1937, he was a curate at which Church of England parish church of the city of Lancaster, Lancashire, England, formally the Priory Church of St Mary?", "answer": "Lancaster Priory", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Is the North East railway line between the two largest cities in Australia?", "answer": "The Sydney\u2013Melbourne rail corridor is an approximately 960 km standard gauge railway corridor that runs between Melbourne and Sydney, the two largest cities in Australia.", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "The 2017\u201318 Pittsburgh Penguins season will be the 51st season for the National Hockey League ice hockey team that was established on June 5, 1967, the first season since the team will play without goaltender Marc-Andre Fleury, who was drafted to the Vegas Golden Knights in the expansion draft, what's the title of the expansion dr