ck", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": " Bruce Lester himself for a time appearing alongside stars such as an American film and television actress who began her career as a dancer and what?", "answer": "stage showgirl", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What is the name of the half-elven character that Hugo Weaving played?", "answer": "Elrond", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which district, Echeng District or Taonan, is one of three administrative districts of the prefecture-level city of Ezhou?", "answer": "Echeng District", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Take a Little Trip was recorded by a band formed in which city ?", "answer": "Fort Payne, Alabama", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Super High Me and Superjews, share which genre?", "answer": "documentary", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "What Latvian deity ranks just below the solar goddess of Latvian mythology in popularity?", "answer": "Auseklis", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What type of media does Die Another Day and Metro-Goldwyn-Mayer have in common?", "answer": "film", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Pleasant Valley State Prison has housed convicted murderers, including what man who foundd Namesys in 2004?", "answer": "Hans Thomas Reiser", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Sports in Charlotte, North Carolina have a long and varied history, The city is home to teams at nearly every level of American sports including which American professional basketball team based in Charlotte, North Carolina?", "answer": "Charlotte Hornets", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What 2017 movie did Darren Aronofsky and Matthew Libatique work together to film?", "answer": "Mother!", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Sir Andrew Dudley commanded the English garrison of castle on the banks of what river?", "answer": "the river Tay", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "who was born first, Marc Almond or Ray Davies?", "answer": "\"Ray\" Davies", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Charles McHugh served on the town council of which Adelaide, South Austrialia suburb?", "answer": "Thebarton", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which Pizza place, Pizzeria Venti or Mountain Mike's Pizza, has locations in more US states ?", "answer": "Pizzeria Venti", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "How long is the loop for the 2016 installment of the rally which owes its origin to Ed Pearlman?", "answer": "800-mile", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Were Donald Sawyer and Ken Annakin both film directors?", "answer": "yes", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "What position did Cristian Dario Alvarez play for the Spanish football team based in Zaragoza?", "answer": "as a goalkeeper.", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Where is the headquarters of the conglomerate managed by Essence Global known as NBCUni?", "answer": "Midtown Manhattan, New York City", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "who wrote the time traveler's wife published by macadam/cage", "answer": "Audrey Niffenegger", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "The Violin Sonata in A major was the only alternative version of which composer born on December 10, 1822?", "answer": "C\u00e9sar Franck", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What Swiss lawyer announced the new Mobility Pricing system?", "answer": "Doris Leuthard", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Piero Mingoia played as midfielder for the ffootball club, established in 1948, that has a local rivalry with what other team?", "answer": "St Albans City", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which Missouri city made the Money magazine list of best cities to live in the U.S. and has an office of a natural gas company that serves 155 Missouri communities?", "answer": "Lee's Summit", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Are Rosa von Praunheim and Robert Butler both German?", "answer": "no", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Which Bengali film stars Koyel Mullick and a former Rajya Sabha Member of Parliament?", "answer": "Minister Fatakeshto", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "The author of \"-And He Built a Crooker House-\" is known by what nickname?", "answer": "dean of science fiction writers", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Who illustrated the novel in which the fictional location \"The Underland\" mainly appears?", "answer": "Pauline Baynes", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Cestrum and Ericaceae, are types of what?", "answer": "flowering plants", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "When was this British Indian novelist and essayist born, who wrote a novel in 2010 that was published by Jonathan Cape, Random House?", "answer": "19 June 1947", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Miss Ripley, is a 2011 South Korean television drama series, starring which South Korean actress, and first achieved recognition for her role in the arthouse film \"Nabi\" (2001)?", "answer": "Kang Hye-jung", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What black comedy crime film was awarded the Palme d'Or at the 47th Cannes Film Festival in 1994?", "answer": "Pulp Fiction", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What is the birthdate of the author of The Vampire Huntress Legend Series?", "answer": "December 11, 1959", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which senior pastor, working at many churches, works with lead pastor Adam Johnson?", "answer": "Andy Stanley", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Leanne Caret is an American businesswoman serving as Executive Vice President of Boeing and President and CEO of a company formerly known as what ?", "answer": "Boeing Integrated Defense Systems (IDS)", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Le comte Ory and The Magic Flute, are which type of theatre?", "answer": "opera", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Jaana (Kannada: \u0c9c\u0cbe\u0ca3 ) is a 1994 Indian Kannada language romantic drama film, written and directed by Shivamani, the film was a musical blockbuster hit upon release with the songs composed and written by which Indian film composer and a songwriter who works in South Indian cinema, predominantly in the Kannada film industry, was received well?", "answer": "Hamsalekha", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What record company released the song \"Digital Bath\" by the alternative metal band, Deftones? ", "answer": "Maverick Records", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "The 2010 ANZAC test coincided with the official opening of AAMI Park in Melbourne, what is the formal name of AAMI Park?", "answer": "Melbourne Rectangular Stadium", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Valentina is made with chilies that are similar to which variety that is part of the species Capsicum annuum?", "answer": "guajillo chili", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "This rapper also known under his disc jockey name, mcDJ, featured the song Kari Faux \"No Small Talk\" on what mixtape?", "answer": "STN MTN", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "The Carson River is named for a U.S. what?", "answer": "Army officer", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Michael Faraday was an early 19th-century British scientist, he contributed to the study of electromagnetism and electrochemistry, and died on which date?", "answer": "25 August 1867", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Who started the band that began at an earlier date between Being No One, Going Nowhere and STRFKR?", "answer": "Joshua Hodges", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What label produced the early 1990s music of the artist who was featured as a guest performer along with Spice 1 on the album We Come Strapped?", "answer": "Def Jam", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which university was founded first Swarthmore College or George Washington University ?", "answer": "George Washington University", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": " ESPN College Football Primetime is a live game presentation of Division 1-A college football on ESPN preceded by a 30-minute segment with Adnan Virk, Joey Galloway and Jesse Palmer, a Canadian sports commentator and former college and professional football player who was a quarterback in what league?", "answer": "National Football League", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which opera has more acts, Iolanta or The Midsummer Marriage?", "answer": "The Midsummer Marriage", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Which company headquartered North of Bloomington is headquartered in the same county named after Father Louis Hennepin? ", "answer": "Best Buy", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Who was Baker Mayfield's football coach in 2015?", "answer": "Bob Stoops", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "How many Canadians lost their lives in the deadliest conflict in history in absolute terms of total casualties?", "answer": "More than 44,000 lost their lives", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Who created a martial art style that has its oldest origins in shamanism?", "answer": "Myung Jae-nam", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What history based comedy series stars the creator of the show Community?", "answer": "Great Minds with Dan Harmon", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which song, a collaboration with the band Alabama, was the third single off NSYNC's U.S. debut album?", "answer": "(God Must Have Spent) A Little More Time on You", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What kind of psychologists study houses with the same defining quality as the psychiatric hospital in the film Grave Encounters?", "answer": "Parapsychologists", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which film director has also worked as an actor, Percy Adlon or Duccio Tessari?", "answer": "Duccio Tessari", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "In what city did Frank Fertitta III found his current company?", "answer": "Las Vegas", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "The Tomb of Sheikh Salim Chishti is famed as one of the finest examples of Mughal architecture in India, built during the years 1580 and 1581, along with the imperial complex at which town in the Agra District of Uttar Pradesh, India?", "answer": "Fatehpur Sikri", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which is taller, the design for building planned for 80 South Street or Central Park Place?", "answer": "80 South Street", "type": "comparison"}, {"question":