y?", "answer": "New York", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Are Suzanne Vega and Glasvegas both part of the music industry?", "answer": "yes", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Lucky Star is a 1929 American romantic drama silent film starring which now passed, American film, stage and television actress and painter?", "answer": "Janet Gaynor", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "In which year was this American country music singer, author, actress, and chef who recorded many songs by Dean Miller inducted into the Georgia Music Hall of Fame?", "answer": "2000", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Live, is a song and music video composed by Igor Matvienko, how many artists participated in the music video, among them Grigory Leps, a Russian singer-songwriter of Georgian origin?", "answer": "28", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What is the name of Alexander \"Alex\" Russell character in the movie Chronicle?", "answer": "Matt", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Who was born in 1936 and committed the Massacre of Braybrook Street?", "answer": "Harry Roberts", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What member of the band Pendulum also co-wrote a Rihanna song?", "answer": "Gareth McGrillen", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "The Diamond Jubilee World is the concert tour by American recording artist, Frank Sinatra, with Steve Lawrence and Eydie Gorm\u00e9, Gorm\u00e9 was an American singer who performed solo as well as with her husband, who , in popular ballads and swing?", "answer": "Steve Lawrence", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Into how many categories do scholars group the early works of the author of the play A Midsummer Night's Dream?", "answer": "three", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which studio produced the movie which had a 21-minute Halloween television special based on it that premiered on Wednesday, October 16, 2013?", "answer": "Pixar Animation Studios", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Paul Greengrass was nominated for an Academy Award for the 2010 movie made from