ge for the Oldsmobile 442?", "answer": "Oldsmobile Cutlass", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "how is Springbokkie and Punch connected?", "answer": "drink", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Melissa Crystal O'Neill starred in what series created by Joseph Mallozzi and Paul Mullie?", "answer": "Dark Matter", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "who died first Arthur Wahl or Glenn T. Seaborg ?", "answer": "Glenn Theodore Seaborg", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "The animated movie \"Big Bug Man\" starred both the star of \"The Mummy trilogy\" and who else?", "answer": "Marlon Brando", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Where was the performer of \"A Night at Salle Pleyel\" born? ", "answer": "Haugesund", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What is the name of the album released in 2005 by the son of country music legend Waylon Jennings?", "answer": "Put the \"O\" Back In Country", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What type of publication does Star Wars Insider and National Geographic have in common?", "answer": "Magazine", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "What pharmaceutical and consumer packaged goods manufacturing company was Verne M. Willaman a director for?", "answer": "Johnson & Johnson", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Hypnomys and Dormouse are from what rodent family?", "answer": "Gliridae", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which South Australia city's suburb's contain both Pennington and the local government area,The City of Charles Sturt?", "answer": "Adelaide", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Who developed the video games UFC 2009 Undisputed and UFC Undisputed 2010?", "answer": "Yuke's Osaka", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Do Anthony Green and Suggs have the same nationality ?", "answer": "no", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "The imperative that acts as the opposite of the Hypothetical Imperative may be defined as a way of evaluating what?", "answer": "motivations for action", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "In which musical-romantic comedy did Juli