 and Anne Hathaway, and the fraternal twin of who?", "answer": "Judith Shakespeare", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Who directed the  2006 German-American movie starred an actor who also starred in \"Gladiator\" and \"In America?\"", "answer": "Edward Zwick", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Who is younger, Patrick Stump or Jun. K?", "answer": "Jun. K", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "What country of origin does Billy L. Sullivan and The Golden Girls have in common?", "answer": "American", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which Save The Children artist ambassador, who joined in a call to action asking people to participate in World Pneumonia Day, was one half of the Fry and Laurie comedy double act?", "answer": "Hugh Laurie", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Henri\u00ebtte Elisabeth de Swart linguist of a Germanic ethnic group native to where?", "answer": "Netherlands", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "The 40\u201340 club includes a Cuban-American player who also competed in which two other sports?", "answer": "boxing and mixed martial arts", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Who was involved with more films, Grover Jones or Norman Tokar?", "answer": "Grover Jones", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Where is the organization located which Stephen M. Schwebel served from 1997-2000? ", "answer": "The Hague, Netherlands", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which director did the American actor and stuntman best known for playing heavy, menancing characters in films and television assist in creating a western film?", "answer": "Jack Starrett", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "The Dolbina exacta is found on this sovereign island nation located in what ocean?", "answer": "Pacific Ocean", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Whose father was an Anglo-Saxon king of Mercia from 852 to 874?", "answer": "Beorhtweald Ealdorman of Kent", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Melvin H. Knisely was an American physiologist who first observed the pathological clumping of red blood cells which are also called what?", "answer": "erythrocytes", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "German musicologist Beatrix Borchard spent a great deal of her career focusing on female musicians, including which 19th-century Romantic-era professional pianist?", "answer": "Clara Schumann", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "which genus of flowering plants that is endemic to Australia ,Plumeria or Derwentia ?", "answer": "Derwentia", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Are Reunions magazine and Autograph Collector Magazine both US publications ?", "answer": "yes", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Who was the victim of The Heisman curse after being awarded the trophy in 2003?", "answer": "Jason White", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What law enacted in 1976 has the EPA delegated to the Oregon Department of Environmental Quality the authority to administer in within the state of Oregon?", "answer": "Resource Conservation and Recovery Act", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Was Salford Quays regenerated before or after the opening of Harbour City tram stop?", "answer": "following the closure of the dockyards in 1982.", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "In between The Light in the Forest and The Apple Dumpling Gang which one is a 1975 American comedy-western film?", "answer": "The Apple Dumpling Gang", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "\"For Free? (Interlude)\" is a song from an album released by which record labels ?", "answer": "Top Dawg Entertainment, Aftermath Entertainment and Interscope Records", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which Spanish professional basketball player has won two NBA championships and was drafted by the Atlanta Hawks in 2001?", "answer": "Pau Gasol", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What intelligence agency was the subject of the drama film Sarbjit a spy for?", "answer": "Indian Research and Analysis Wing", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Jang Joon-hwan and Sidney Morgan, have which mutual occupation?", "answer": "film director", "type": "c