y movement in the 1950s, Neal Stephenson or Terry Southern ?", "answer": "Terry Southern", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "What is the main occupation of Hiroshi Sakaguchi, founder of Ki Arts, a traditional Japanese company in Northern California and who features in the 2010 documentary film directed by Tao Ruspoli, based on Martin Heidegger's philosophy?", "answer": "carpenter", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "When was the journal, for which Mark Buchanan writes a monthly column, first published ?", "answer": "October 2005", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Ulf Merbold and Lodewijk van den Berg, both flew in ?", "answer": "space", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "What category do the films Beyond the Call and Without the King fall into?", "answer": "documentary film", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Which booster was used to send the 1st American into orbit?", "answer": "Atlas 109-D booster", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Black Hours is the debut solo studio album, of singer Hamilton Leithauser, from which indie rock band,?", "answer": "The Walkmen", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "British biographer and translator of German philosophy and literature R.J. Hollingdale was elected president of what in 1989, partly because of his work with the posthumously published notebooks of G. C. Lichtenberg?", "answer": "The Friedrich Nietzsche Society", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Queen Clea was a villainess along with the fictional character created by whom?", "answer": "William Moulton Marston", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Pug and Weimaraner are breeds of what?", "answer": "dog", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Are either Robert Lamm or Fher Olvera British musicians?", "answer": "no", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Are Black Light Burns and Sixpence None the Richer both American bands?", "answer": "yes", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Frankie Fleming faced what hall of famer who held the World Featherweight title from 1912 to 1923?", "answer": "John Patrick \"Johnny\" Kilbane", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Margaret Mary \"Madge\" Bishop (also Ramsay and Mitchell) is a fictional character from the Australian soap opera \"Neighbours\", played by which Australian actress best known for playing the character of Madge Bishop in the Australian soap opera \"Neighbours\"?", "answer": "Anne Charleston", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "the album COnfidential by M-1 features guest appearances from a musician born on which day ?", "answer": "December 4, 1955", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What was the release date of the final album produced by Creedence Clearwater Revival?", "answer": "April 11, 1972", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Andrew Stahl was an actor on the CBS drama that aired during which period?", "answer": "April 1994 to August 1995", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Who was a physician, Al-Kindi or Abu Yusuf?", "answer": "Al-Kindi", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Are Born Rich and Death Faces both mockumentaries?", "answer": "no", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "What do Walter Lippmann and Michael Shaara have in common?", "answer": "American writer", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "The Qube is home to the operations center of what type of lending company?", "answer": "mortgage", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What was the color of the twin-rotor Wankel rotary engine car driven by Peter McLeod?", "answer": "yellow and black", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Margot Sanger-Katz is an American health care journalist who currently works for which organization, prior to joining the Times, she worked for \"National Journal\" and the \"Concord Monitor\"?", "answer": "New York Times", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "\u00c1lvaro Raposo De Oliveira was born in a city located in the valleys of which rivers ?", "answer": "the Chill\u00f3n, R\u00edmac and Lur\u00edn rivers", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which album by End of Everything received a 7/10 from the monthly 