orical Park", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "The Battle of the Labyrinth is the fourth novel in a pentalogy of adventure and mythological fiction books that have sold more than 45 million copies, and have been sold in how many countries?", "answer": "35", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "The Murder of John Lennon was committed by the man who read which book until he was arrested?", "answer": "The Catcher in the Rye", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which of Robin Gibb's siblings were featured in Mythology?", "answer": "Barry and Maurice Gibb", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What movie staring Joaquin Phoenix was created by the same man who released \"Unbreakable\"?", "answer": "The Village", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which was a solo artist, Faye or Benjamin Burnley?", "answer": "Faye", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Where did John Ebersole perform x-rays in the autopsy of a president?", "answer": "Bethesda Naval Medical Center", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What local government area oversees the city where the Lake Oval is located?", "answer": "City of Port Phillip", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "How many passengers did the airport near Poyle handle in 2016?", "answer": "75.7 million", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Fort Richardson National Cemetery is part of the installation that merged with what nearby Air Force Base?", "answer": "Elmendorf", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which Hall of Fame was the founder of the Ivey League elected to?", "answer": "Poker Hall of Fame", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Brenton Thwaites had a role in the 2014 social science film directed by whom?", "answer": "Phillip Noyce", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which South Korean singer/actress was a member of both DIA and I.O.I?", "answer": "Jung Chae-yeon", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "The company that has bought Canal Digital in 2003 is headquartered in which city?", "answer": "Fornebu", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Dick Bush created the cinematography to the 1979 drama film starring which actor?", "answer": "Richard Gere", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Tyrone Dobbs, the character from \"Coronation Street\", had a storyline with what actress who was a runner-up in the 2013 series of \"Strictly Come Dancing\" on BBC One?", "answer": "Natalie Gumede", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "St Martin de Porres, Adelaide is a feeder school to which school that was founded in 1886?", "answer": "Cabra Dominican College", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Bad Kitty was written by what American writer who has authored novels in several genres, including historical romance and suspense thrillers?", "answer": "Michele Sharon Jaffe", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Sange-e-Masha and Jaghori District are both located in what country?", "answer": "Afghanistan", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Peter Collinson (January 1694 \u2013 11 August 1768) was a Fellow of the Royal Society, an avid gardener, and the middleman for an international exchange of scientific ideas in mid-18th century London, best known for his horticultural friendship with John Bartram, was an early American botanist, horticulturist and explorer, that died on which date?", "answer": "September 22, 1777", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What country is the competitive swimmer from who competed three times in the sporting event overseen by the Commonwealth Games Federation?", "answer": "New Zealand", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "The song \"Chasing Colors\" featured the vocals of this American actress and singer born in 2000 who released her debut single in which year?", "answer": "2016", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "After playing freshman year in Belle Glade, Florida, Willie Snead IV moved to which state?", "answer": "Michigan", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which film director, born in 1945, directed a 1983 comedy film starring Tom Cruise and Shelley Long?", "answer": "Curtis Hanson", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Evan Crawford has played for an MLB team in what league?", "answer": "American League", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "A Raisin in the Sun is a 1961 drama film, stars included is Roy Glenn, he was an American character actor who was born in Pittsburg, in which U.S. state?", "answer": "Kansas", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Are both Christopher Amott and Stephen Malkmus guitarists?", "answer": "yes", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Special 26, also known as Special Chabbis, is a 2013 Indian period heist crime thriller film directed by Neeraj Pandey, the film is inspired by which 1987 titled event, a group posing as CBI officers executed the fake income tax investigation raid on the Opera House branch of Tribhovandas Bhimji Zaveri & Sons Jewellers in Mumbai, India?", "answer": "1987 Opera House heist", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Kew Cottages is located in the eastern suburb of Melbourne how far away from the Central Business District?", "answer": "6 km east", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Who recorded an album at \u00d6ster\u00e5ker Prison and San Quentin Prison?", "answer": "Johnny Cash", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Are Sinningia and Hyoscyamus in the same family?", "answer": "no", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "The Arab nationalist who helped inspire the Aden Emergency was born in what year?", "answer": "1918", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "The Ferryman, a 2017 play by Jez Butterworth, casts which British film, television, and stage actor, who was born in 1967?", "answer": "Stuart Graham", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "The Axis Is a mid-sized auditorium located inside Planet Hollywood Las Vegas located where?", "answer": "Paradise, Nevada", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What was the debut single by the singer of the 2009 single \"I'll Just Hold On\"?", "answer": "Austin", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "The Purpose Driven Life was written by the pastor who founded what church?", "answer": "Saddleback Church", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Venus of