rse 2009 was held at the Atlantis Paradise Island in Nassau, which is in an archipelagic state within what Archipelago?", "answer": "Lucayan", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which author has more categories of published works Alfred Bester or Ishmael Reed?", "answer": "Alfred Bester", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "What cities are the headquarters for the company that owns Avra Valley Solar Generating Station?", "answer": "West Windsor Township, New Jersey, and Houston, Texas", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "To whose Neoclassical design was the major listed building in the parish of Siddington built?", "answer": "William Smith", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Are Yanzhou District and Haidong in the same country?", "answer": "yes", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Are Naguib Mahfouz and W. H. Auden both English?", "answer": "no", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "What famous singer did the director of \"The Help\" direct a movie on?", "answer": "James Brown", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Sugarland's song Stay stayed right behind Taylor Swift's Our Song, which was driven by which instrument?", "answer": "banjo", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Where was the female star of the film The Sound born ?", "answer": "Italian-born", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What is the name of the Polynesian-themed resort and casino resort located on the Las Vegas Strip where Terry Fator headlines?", "answer": "The Mirage", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which game was invented in India and played more by children, Pay Day or Aksharit?", "answer": "Aksharit", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Of what material is an enclosed bridge made from which can be viewed from the Ponte dela Paglia bridge in Venice, Italy?", "answer": "white limestone", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Are James P. Bagian and Paz Lenchantin both Americans?", "answer": "yes", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Griggstown cow is believed to be a New Jersey myth, similar to what legendary creature that is said to inhabit the Pine Barrens in Southern New Jersey?", "answer": "Jersey Devil", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Ed Guiney produced the 2015 drama written by whom?", "answer": "Emma Donoghue", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Around how many members does the triad group, for which Michael Chan admitted being the No. 2, have?", "answer": "25,000", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "The Goldeneye and Prince of Wales are both cocktails, but differ in what way?", "answer": "The Goldeneye is a smooth cocktail made from rum and pineapple juice", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Who founded the radio show that The Carter Sisters joined in 1950 ? ", "answer": "George D. Hay", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "The Wuerffel Trophy is an award given annually to the college football player \"who best combines exemplary community service with athletic and academic achievement.\", its named in honor of former University of Florida quarterback Danny Wuerffel, by which organization?", "answer": "All Sports Association", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "La sonnambula used themes from a Vincenzo Bellini opera that had a libretto by whom?", "answer": "Felice Romani", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What is the county code for Lakeside Village?", "answer": "JF", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Gaetano Giallanza represented a football who played for the Swiss Olympic team in what year?", "answer": "2012", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "When was the rock band which Joe Puerta is the bassist for founded?", "answer": "1970", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Nightwish is a symphonic metal band from which city in Finland, the band was formed in 1996 by lead songwriter and keyboardist, Tuomas Lauri Johannes Holopainen (born 25 December 1976) is a Finnish songwriter, multi-instrumentalist musician (but mainly keyboardist) and record producer, best known as the founder of Nightwish?", "answer": "Kitee", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Who established the Journal 