ported by Marquis de Lafayette?", "answer": "Benedict Arnold", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What year did the author, who published a criticism of Shakespeare's plays in 1817, die?", "answer": "1830", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "In the biographical film Rainbow, which actress played the singer-actress Judy Garland?", "answer": "Andrea McArdle", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What name did Patrick Keeler's The Racounteurs use in Australia?", "answer": "The Saboteurs", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What country was the Auto company responsible for sponsorship of the 2016 World Club Series located in?", "answer": "Romania", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Ricardo \"Ricky\" S\u00e1nchez Rosa, is a Puerto Rican professional basketball player who currently plays for Fuerza Regia of the Liga Nacional de Baloncesto Profesional (LNBP), he was drafted by the Portland Trail Blazers with 35th pick of the 2005 NBA Draft, and was immediately traded to the Denver Nuggets for their selection, which American professional basketball player for the New York Knicks?", "answer": "Jarrett Jack", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Jack Snow was an American radio writer, and scholar, who wrote the thirty-eighth book, in the series of Oz books, titled ?", "answer": "The Shaggy Man of Oz", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What was the nationality of the person who wrote the lyrics for \"Suzanne\"?", "answer": "Canadian", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "A English former radio and television presenter who was known for presenting \"It's a Knockout\" was represented in criminal trial by the man who is current chairman of what football club?", "answer": "Barnsley", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "The coach of the 2007-08 Feyenoord season was born in what year?", "answer": "1952", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": " Mabee House is part of the society that was established on what date?", "answer": "July 14, 1905", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What is the year of the event that occured first, Lawrence Brownlee was born, or Joyce DiDonato was born?", "answer": "1969", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What 2012 hurricane was known for destroying the Long Beach Medical Center?", "answer": "Hurricane Sandy", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "The song Rainbow Connection is a song from \"The Muppet Movie\" that won a Golden Globe award for what?", "answer": "Best Original Song", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Who was the vice-president of the Romantic Novelists' Association under the president who died in 1985?", "answer": "Barbara Cartland", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What is the nationality of the co-creator of Timeslip (along with Evan Skolnick)?", "answer": "American", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Peoples redemption Council consisted of 17 soldiers and this Liberian politician who once served as the leader of Liberia.", "answer": "Samuel Doe", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which American actress co starred beside Sean Penn in This Must Be the Place?", "answer": "Frances McDormand", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "When was the only album by the firm released?", "answer": "1997", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Margaret \"Maggie\" Black (March 31, 1930 \u2013 May 11, 2015) was a ballet teacher who taught in New York City during the 1970s and 1980s, she coached dancers such as which American ballerina, who joined the New York City Ballet in 1968 at age fifteen, at the invitation of George Balanchine?", "answer": "Gelsey Kirkland", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "The singer who released the single \"Kid Stuff\" in 1973 is best known for what other song?", "answer": "The Teddy Bear Song", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Penn Central opened Kent Road station to serve what American multinational corporation?", "answer": "PerkinElmer", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Olga Pershankova competed with an ice dancer who was a five time what?", "answer": "U.S. national champion", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Who played Dr. David Camero