ared in \"Dune\" (1984) and \"Twin Peaks\" (1990)?", "answer": "Alicia Witt", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "The magazine Mothering, and news publication Foreign Policy share which nationality? ", "answer": "American", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Xinjiang University is a national key university, and The University of California, San Diego is what?", "answer": "a public research university", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Benjamin Furly was a friend of a philosopher born in what year ?", "answer": "1632", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What year were the films Hero of the Rails and Superman/Batman: Public Enemies released?", "answer": "2009", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Who coached the team who the 2007 Heisman Trophy winner played for?", "answer": "Zach Azzanni", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which university founded in 1818 is the oldest university west of the Mississippi River: Saint Louis University or Marquette University? ", "answer": "Saint Louis University", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "\"Letting In the Jungle\" is a short story by Rudyard Kipling which continues the adventures of a fictional character from which country ?", "answer": "India", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Cliff Clavin was a character on the show that was produced by what company?", "answer": "Charles/Burrows/Charles Productions", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What type of college is the Atlanta, Georgia Morehouse College  and where it puts an emphasis on undergraduate study in the liberal arts and sciences?", "answer": "liberal arts college", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Who produced this 2006 American science fiction thriller film directed by the English film director and producer of \"Top Gun\" (1986)?", "answer": "Jerry Bruckheimer", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What time of game is Aberrant which is also a type that Onyx Path Publishing produces?", "answer": "role-playing game", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "How many versions of a d