elist, Mark Powell, is the author of the the novel \"The Dark Corner\", and serves as what for the private four-year co-education liberal arts college, Lincoln Memorial University?", "answer": "fiction workshop leader", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Are Adriano Panatta and Kevin Ullyett both Italian tennis players?", "answer": "no", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "What borough of New York City was Ben Jeby from?", "answer": "Manhattan", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Who supervised the FBI operation that the movie American Hustle was inspired by?", "answer": "Neil J. Welch", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which guest on VH1's Big in '06 is also known by her nickname New York?", "answer": "Tiffany Pollard", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Was British barrister and detective story writer Sarah Caudwell or American writer Laurie Colwin known for her portrayals of New York society and food columns?", "answer": "Sarah Caudwell", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Which left handed international cricketer was involved in Spot-fixing allegations, leading to Asad Shafiq being selected?", "answer": "Mohammad Amir", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "18 Days is a single that was also used in the iPhone OS game that had music created by whom?", "answer": "Nate True", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What artist released an album in 2016, produced by a member of Detroit rap group D12?", "answer": "Torae", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Where is the University, for which Julius Cherry Powell was the seventh president, located ?", "answer": "Richmond", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What professional road bicycle racer from the country known informally as Holland, won one stage in the 1954 Tour de France?", "answer": "Henk Faanhof", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Who directed the 2007 horror starring the actor who played John Kramer in Saw, and Danielle Savre as Laura Porter?", "answer": "Jeff Betancourt", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What city does 2015 Co