at was run by the singer from what New Jersey city?", "answer": "Lodi", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Lucienne \"Lucy\" Rokach, an English professional poker player from Stoke-on-Trent, was born in  a city whose metropolitan area is the largest in the Middle East and the Arab world, and the 15th-largest in the world, called what?", "answer": "Cairo", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Paula Abdul and Nadirah Shakoor are both part of what industry?", "answer": "Music", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Ermac is a fictional character from which video game franchise originally developed by Midway Games' Chicago studio in 1992, and the development team was acquired by Warner Bros. and turned into NetherRealm Studios?", "answer": "Mortal Kombat", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Heroes Unlimited is a role-playing game that was written by which American artist and writer?", "answer": "Kevin Siembieda", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "In what year was the University that Clive Baldock received his Masters of Tertiary Education Management degree from founded?", "answer": "1853", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which song was written by John Lennon and Paul McCartney, released on the 7th Capitol Records release in the United States and Canada, and peaked at #1 in the United States?", "answer": "I Don't Want to Spoil the Party", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What was the Filipino-owned regional boutique airline company, which owns an airstrip at El Nido Airport, formerly known as?", "answer": "Island Transvoyager", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What Disney consultant was stalked by Margaret Mary \"Peggy\" Ray? ", "answer": "Franklin Story Musgrave", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "This British Territorial Army general was succeeded by his son who is estimated to be worth what?", "answer": "US$13 billion", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which is a skyscraper under construction, 55 Water Street or 111 Murray Street?", "answer": "111 Murray Street", "type": "compariso