e nationality?", "answer": "no", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Gansito is a chocolate and strawberry snack created by Bimbo, the world's largest bakery. In which country are their headquarters?", "answer": "Mexico", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "The Staunton Mall has 4 anchors in operation include Belk, JCPenney, Gold's Gym, and a department store owned by what company?", "answer": "Stage Stores, Inc.", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "have Bob Bryan and Samantha Stosur both been world No. 1 in doubles?", "answer": "yes", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "What city, other than San Jose del Cabo, is at the the southern tip of Baja California Peninsula and is also encompassed in the Los Cabos Municipality?", "answer": "Cabo San Lucas", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Can you find Peter Piper Pizza where Pizza Fusion is based?", "answer": "no", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Who worked with Lynn Ahrens on Dessa Rose and multiple other musicals including \"Lucky Stiff\", \"Once on This Island\", and \"My Favorite Year\"?", "answer": "Stephen Flaherty", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What theme park plays an educational role in regards to protecting a large area of land around the Rhine-Meuse-Scheldt delta from the sea?", "answer": "Deltapark Neeltje Jans", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which served as chairman of he board of Governors at the British Film Institute, Anthony Minghella or Michael Lembeck?", "answer": "Anthony Minghella", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "What road is the entrance for the Naval Center named after Rear Admiral John A. Dahlgren located at?", "answer": "State Route 206 (SR 206)", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Matthew Olosunde plays for which tier of the Professional Development League? ", "answer": "Premier League 2", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Ben Moore, is an American composer whose works include art song, musical theatre, cabaret, chamber music, choral music and opera, his song cycles include which song,