mplified by The Mysterious Mr. Wong?", "answer": "Fu Manchu", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which former American professional basketball player, current sports analyst for ESPN, and cofounder of the Jalen Rose Leadership Academy did the Indiana Pacers trade for other players to the Chicago Bulls during their 2001-02 season?", "answer": "Jalen Rose", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which Opera has more acts Nabucco or Mitridate, re di Ponto ?", "answer": "Nabucco", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Which country is the chain that owns WingStreet operated by a separate company?", "answer": "China", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Prior to playing for the Milwaukee Bulls, which team did the former National Basketball Association (NBA) player who is currently a television analyst for CBS Sports play for?", "answer": "Chicago Bulls", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Where is the head office of the agency that designed the Tour Triangle?", "answer": "Basel, Switzerland", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Are both Shuangyashan and Longnan in China?", "answer": "yes", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "What community were the founding members of Islander 23's rival gang from?", "answer": "Victoria's South Sudanese community", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Who was the author of both The Snowman and The Fir-Tree?", "answer": "Hans Christian Andersen", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "The 2002 Arkansas Razorbacks football team represented the University of Arkansas in the 2002 NCAA Division I-A football season, they reached the 2002 Music City Bowl in Houston Nutt's fifth season as head coach, born Houston Dale Nutt Jr., is a former American football coach and former player, born on which date?", "answer": "October 14, 1957", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Shim Eun-kyung appears in a 2001 South Korean comedy film about a middle-aged woman trying to reunite friends who were in high school in what decade?", "answer": "the 1980s", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "T