y decorated in what war?", "answer": "World War II", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which band originated in a country further south, Bodyjar or Go Radio?", "answer": "Bodyjar", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "what does Pimpinella and Digitalis have in common?", "answer": "genus", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "The band At the Drive-In from El Paso, Texas released its first EP entitled what?", "answer": "Hell Paso", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What film was made for the Seafarers International Union, The Seafarers or One Big Hapa Family?", "answer": "The Seafarers", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "what is the name of the South Korean romantic drama film in which Jae Hee had a leading role?", "answer": "3-Iron", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Name the British breed of domestic pig which shares its name with a village and parish on the edge of The Fens in Lincolnshire, England?", "answer": "Baston", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which mall that A Line serves has 12 million visitors a year?", "answer": "Rosedale Center", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What is the year of the event that happened first, When Louis Met originally aired, or Mostyn Hamilton was born?", "answer": "1949", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Roger Booth  appeared in many British television series and films including \"The Tomorrow People,\" a British children's science fiction television series, created by who?", "answer": "Roger Price", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which biography written by Philip Carlo is based on an American contract killer and serial killer convicted of murdering five people?", "answer": "Richard Kuklinski", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Where was the  Citro\u00ebn vehicle designed with influences from what is called a beach buggy in the United Kingdom presented?", "answer": "the Madrid Motor Show", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Where was the company located that the Radium Girls sue?", "answer": "Orange, New Jersey", "type": "bridge"}