d Darlene Conner in a television series that focused on a family living in what US state?", "answer": "Illinois", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Who is a professor Robert Zildjian or Barbara Sahakian?", "answer": "Barbara Jacquelyn Sahakian", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Who was the film editor for the movie that was a loose adaptation of the novel \"Q&A\"?", "answer": "Chris Dickens", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Who was the retired American astronaut who transferred from Expedition 44 to 45 on the International Space Station?", "answer": "Scott Kelly", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Daniel Poneman's predecessor as Secretary of Energy won a Nobel Prize in what field?", "answer": "Physics", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "The New River, a London waterway opened in 1613, supplies drinking water from the springs of which river?", "answer": "River Lea", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "The Oklahoma City bombing was a domestic terrorist truck bombing on the Alfred P. Murrah Federal Building in downtown Oklahoma City, Oklahoma, United States on which date, Terry Lynn Nichols, is an American who was convicted of being an accomplice in the Oklahoma City bombing?", "answer": "April 19, 1995", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What is the name of the Swedish heavy metal band which was formed by guitarist Jesper Stromblad in 1990 who later went on to form Sinergy with Kimberly Goss from Dimmu Borgir?", "answer": "In Flames", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Roger Leonard was a professional boxer, from Palmer Park, Maryland, he is the older brother of which boxing legend, an American former professional boxer, motivational speaker, and occasional actor, best know as?", "answer": "\"Sugar\" Ray Leonard", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "In what state did Reverend Frederick Lehrle Barry operate a church?", "answer": "New York", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Katniss Everdeen, a fictional character and protagonist of Susan Collins' dystopian novel trilogy, is played by what actress?", "answer": "Jennifer Lawrence", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which company sold in over 180 countries outside the United States and developed Codentify.", "answer": "Philip Morris International", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What was the July 2017 net worth of the incumbent mayor of New York in 2013", "answer": "53.4 billion", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Put You on the Game is a single by the rapper who was part of the group that released their debut album in which year?", "answer": "2003", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "On what 2012 film about a Scottish princess did Pixar use its industry-standard RenderMan image-rendering application programming interface?", "answer": "Brave", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "The Big Drift is in Glacier National Park, in the U.S. state of Montana, and is an area along which scenic mountain road in the Rocky Mountains of the western United States, in Glacier National Park in Montana?", "answer": "Going-to-the-Sun Road", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "On which Hawaiian island is Turtle Bay Resort, home of the SBS Open women's golf tournament?", "answer": "Oahu", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Who was responsible for the massacre that led to suzanna hupp's book \"From Luby\u2019s to the Legislature: One Woman\u2019s Fight Against Gun Control\"?", "answer": "George Hennard", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": " After what date are additions to each club's playing list allowed for the 121st season of the Austrailian Football League (AFL)?", "answer": "30 September", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "How many goals were scored when 2007\u201308 Blackburn Rovers F.C. season?", "answer": "scoring 19 league goals", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Are both Samuel R. Delany and Aldous Huxley from the same country?", "answer": "no", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "What is the japanese company who hired Camelia as a spokesmodel traditionally known for?", "answer": "timepieces", "type": "bridge"}, {"