e Thorne or Greg Costikyan ?", "answer": "Greg Costikyan", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "\"Forbidden Archeology\" is a book written by a researcher born in which year ?", "answer": "1948", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "In what year was the author of Killing Reagan: The Violent Assault That Changed a Presidency born?", "answer": "1949", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Who wrote and directed the 1998 British crime comedy film which starred Matthew Vaughn?", "answer": "Guy Ritchie", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "The Siege of Pskov took place during the final stage of a war that fought for control of what area?", "answer": "Old Livonia", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Blood Mountain is the highest peak on the Georgia section of a marked hiking trail in the Eastern United States that is about how many miles long?", "answer": "2,200", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Valerian and the City of a Thousand Planets, is a 2017 English-language French 3D science fiction adventure film written and directed by Luc Besson, it stars Kris Wu, a Chinese-born Canadian actor, singer, and model, and former member of which South Korean-Chinese boy band?", "answer": "EXO", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which macroregion was \u00d3scar Su\u00e1rez born in?", "answer": "Baj\u00edo.", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Fame was a song partially written by the singer and activist of what nationality?", "answer": "English", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Are  Matt Reeves and Farrelly brothers both producers?", "answer": "no", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Which politician from the United States Senate election in Georgia, 2008 was a previous U.S. representative?", "answer": "Saxby Chambliss", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Are the bands LCD Soundsystem and Against the Current based in the same New York cities?", "answer": "no", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "What was the actor Keith from the show Watch my chops nationality? ", "answer": "British", "type": "brid