es?", "answer": "13 million", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "The song \"Errol\" by Australian Crawl is an lyrical biography about an actor that became a U.S. citizen in what year?", "answer": "1942", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Who has won more medals, Daniel Nestor or Piet Norval?", "answer": "Pieter (\"Piet\") Norval", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Jimmy Tatro starred in the true-crime satire co-created by whom?", "answer": "Dan Perrault and Tony Yacenda", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "When was father of the Carter Family born?", "answer": "December 15, 1891", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": " The initial tornado of the Late-May 1998 tornado outbreak hit a state named after which Native American tribes?", "answer": "Lakota and Dakota Sioux", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What computer program does MGM wireless provide to run on a mobile device?", "answer": "A mobile app", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Stephen Stepanek is an American politician representing a town with a population of what at the 2010 census?", "answer": "11,201", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "When was the German politician died who was appointed as Deputy F\u00fchrer by  Rudolf Walter Richard Hess?", "answer": "30 April 1945", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Who directed the 2016 film that Partizan Midi-Minuit produced?", "answer": "Antoine Bardou-Jacquet", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Where did the 2010 coach of the Ohio Bobcats coach from 1998 to 2003?", "answer": "University of Nebraska\u2013Lincoln", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "W. H. Conn was a staff artist for what publication by Independent News & Media?", "answer": "Belfast Telegraph", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Who wrote the single that Gun released in 1994 ?", "answer": "Larry Blackmon and Tomi Jenkins", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Are Steve Lukather and Andy Biersack both members of a band?", "answer": "yes", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "What term has been applied to the town where Louis Alan Hazeltine was born ?", "answer": "\"the military capital of the American Revolution\"", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Who is the 2006 coach of the California Golden Bears currently head coach of? ", "answer": "Fresno State Bulldogs", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What team finished runner up in the 2005 Gold Cup and boasts Valentin Pimentel as their player?", "answer": "Panama national football team", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Did Ivan Magrin-Chagnolleau and Upendra Rao both originate from France?", "answer": "no", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "What is the name of the American sportscaster born in 1969 that what part of the family that had the restaurant J. Buck's named after them", "answer": "Joe Buck", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "When did the Bengali polymath, physicist, biologist and biophysicist died based on who's name the Lower Circular Road was renamed?", "answer": "23 November 1937", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What is the name of the Australian cinematographer who collaborated on a 2016 American science fiction action adventure film based on the video game franchise of the same name?", "answer": "Adam Arkapaw", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What county in Montana was home to St. Benedict's Catholic School?", "answer": "Musselshell County", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Was Joe Gittleman or Mickey Thomas, both whom are known in America, was known by the name \"The Bass Fiddleman\"?", "answer": "bass earned him the nickname \"the Bass Fiddleman.\"", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "What uncompleted opera was composed by the composer of Il signor Fagotto?", "answer": "\"The Tales of Hoffmann\"", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which building is across the street from 5 World Trade Center, 125 Greenwich Street or 50 Hudson Yards?", "answer": "125 Greenwich Street", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "What is the maiden name of the person who used the phrase \"Alternative facts\" during a \"Meet the Press\" interview on January 22, 2017?", "answer": "Fitzpatrick", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What is the name of the of the company who's Executive Chairman is Vijay Eswaran and owns Qnet?", "answer": "QI Group", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Skil Brum and Chamlang are both names of a what?", "answer": "mountain", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "What pizza chain was founded by the former owner who died before the 117th season of the Detroit Tigers? ", "answer": "Little Caesars Pizza", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which dog is more likely to be employed by farmers, the Austrian Pinscher or the Lagotto Romagnolo?", "answer": "Austrian Pinscher", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Which movie is the original film, Choices of One or Star Wars?", "answer": "Star Wars", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "In which season and league did the Hellas Verona Football club compete against 21 other teams?", "answer": "2016\u201317 Serie B", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "In what conflict was Heinz-Wolfgang Schnaufer a commanding officer of a night fighter-wing?", "answer": "World War II", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What award did the host of Pot Luck win?", "answer": "Gold Logie", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "ACE TV was superseded by the station that was previously known as what on analog television?", "answer": "C31", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Who is the presenter of Copa Movistar which is one of the latgest surfing company in Australia? ", "answer": "Rip Curl", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What is the year of the event that happened first, \"All Things Must Pass\" was produced, or the film Wonderwall was produced?", "answer": "1968", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "In what year was the actor known for his role as Tyler Duncan in a movie directed by Paul Feig?", "answer": "2011", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What do Robert G. Vignola and Vincent Kok Tak-Chiu have in common?", "answer": "screenwriter and film director", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "What landlocked country in Eastern Europe is composed of two villages, Condr\u0103te\u0219ti and Curtoaia?", "answer": "Moldova", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which University has more accalaides' Bahauddin Zakariya University or Makerere University?", "answer": "Bahauddin Zakariya University", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Sebastian Pawel Janikowski (] ; born March 2, 1978) is a Polish-born American football placekicker for the Oakland Raiders of the National Football League (NFL), against the Denver Broncos, he tied the previous NFL record for the longest field goal at 63 yards, sharing the record with which former American football placekicker?", "answer": "David Roy Akers", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which song from Badfinger's third album is featured in the series finale of AMC's \"Breaking Bad\"?", "answer": "Baby Blue", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Stay never reached #1, staying behind the song created by the singer-songwriter of what nationality?", "answer": "American", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What conference does the team that represents a private university located in West Long Branch, Monmouth County, New Jersey, United States, play in ?", "answer": "Metro Atlantic Athletic Conference", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Are both Ivan Tors and Jason Bateman a filmmaker?", "answer": "yes", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Are both Chris Robinson and Tom Chaplin musicians?", "answer": "yes", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Are Alan Mak and David Attwood in the same industry?", "answer": "yes", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "PopRocks is a full-time channel devoted to pop music, like which American singer-songwriter and actress, born in 1962?", "answer": "Sheryl Suzanne Crow", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "The Balmoral Furniture Company bombing was a paramilitary attack that took place on 11 December 1971 in Belfast, Northern Ireland, which Ulster loyalist paramilitary group, had carried out that bombing in Northern Ireland?", "answer": "Ulster Volunteer Force (UVF)", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Gong Hyo-jin  is best known for her leading role in the feature film debut of what director?", "answer": "Lee Kyoung-mi", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "When was the democrat defeated by William Milliken  at the Michigan gubernatorial election, 1970 born? ", "answer": "September 6, 1931", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "On what day was the person born who wrote the screenplay for \"Mr. Horn\"?", "answer": "August 12, 1931", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What 2011 movie stars Gong Ji-Chul, better known as Long Yoo?", "answer": "The Crucible", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "The team that played against the Florida state Seminoles in the 2001 orange bowl was coached by who? ", "answer": "Bob Stoops in his second season as head coach", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What country of origin does Harold Macmilla and John Profumo have in common?", "answer": "British", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Who did Indianapolis-born drummer John Von Ohlen work with twice in the 60s?", "answer": "Woody Herman in 1967", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Who was the head coach during the 1999 season in which Ben Wallace was traded from the Washington Wizards?", "answer": "Doc Rivers", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What military engagement fought near Gonzales, Texas involved the Army of the People?", "answer": "The Battle of Gonzales", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "In Morphett, South Australia, which Gulf St. Vincent bay bounds the district to the west?", "answer": "Holdfast Bay", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What Mexican state were La Familia Michoacana and Knights Templar Cartel organized in?", "answer": "Michoac\u00e1n", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Carlsen Verlag is a publisher of an animated television series created for what network?", "answer": "Nickelodeon", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "The wise Kids is what kind of film, written and directed by Stephen Cone>", "answer": "drama film", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Do both CQ Amateur Radio and Electronic Gaming Monthly both review video games?", "answer": "no", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "The 23rd AVN Awards ceremony was hosted by Greg Fitzsimmons and an an American pornographic actress inducted in to the XRCO what?", "answer": "Hall of Fame", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "The River Ravensbourne is a tributary of a river that is how many miles long?", "answer": "215", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Who wrote \"Lost and Forgotten\" which came 11th in Eurovision Song Contest 2010 in Oslo?", "answer": "Peter Nalitch and Friends", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What type of water transportation system did both the Rapidan Dam Canal of the Rappahannock Navigation and the Main Line of Public Works work to establish?", "answer": "Canal", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "What was the name of the former Member of Parliament whose son was elected as Secretary of State at the Department for Transport?", "answer": "John Gummer", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": " Marie Mattingly Meloney organized a fund drive to buy radium for a French physicist who was the first woman to win what?", "answer": "Nobel Prize", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What was the middle name of the actor who starred in \"Romolo e Remo\" opposite Gordon Scott and Virna Lisi?", "answer": "Lester", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Worker: What is the nickname of the athlete featured on the cover of the video game \"MLB 14: The Show\"", "answer": "Miggy", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "The 22nd TCA Awards were hosted by an american actress best known for portraying who in the Fox action thriller series \"24\"?", "answer": "Chloe O'Brian", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Are both Supergrass and Modest Mouse American rock bands?", "answer": "no", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Of the two rock group and band, Secondhand Serenade and Thinking Fellers Union Local 282, which is originated in San Francisco?", "answer": "Thinking Fellers Union Local 282", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Jang Jin-young is currently more active as a vocal trainer for a company established in which year ?", "answer": "1995", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Are Bombay Bicycle Club and The Flaming Lips from the same country?", "answer": "no", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Mutant Meeples and Icehouse pieces are both what?", "answer": "game", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Which of these provide more regular news, The Christian Science Monitor or Electronic Gaming Monthly?", "answer": "The Christian Science Monitor", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Who is younger, Clive Cussler or Anita Diamant ?", "answer": "Anita Diamant", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "What is the nationality of the man whom Rocky Wood met, along with J. Allen Hynek, while researching extra-terrestrial life and UFO-related phenomenon?", "answer": "Swiss", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Greta Garbo starred in a film with an American film actor often referred to as what?", "answer": "The King of Hollywood", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Are Frida, en trotj\u00e4narinna and Stations of the Elevated both documentaries aired in Denmark?", "answer": "no", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "What is the nationality of the corporation that owns and operates Ramada Hotel Chains ?", "answer": "American", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Who is the president of the university which is represented by the Oklahoma Sooners?", "answer": "David Lyle Boren", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Deirdre Connelly (born in 1961) is a Puerto Rican and Irish-American business professional, she has been president of North America Pharmaceuticals for GlaxoSmithKline since 2009, reporting to which CEO of GlaxoSmithKline between 2008 and 2017?", "answer": "Andrew Witty", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Martin Holm fought this K-1 Dutch kickboxer", "answer": "Ernesto Hoost", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Who is the general gender audience target of Claudia and Velvetpark", "answer": "women", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "What is the nickname of the actress who costarred with Julie Andrews, Mary Tyler Moore, James Fox, John Gavin, and Carol Channing in Thoroughly Modern Millie?", "answer": "Bea Lillie", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "The county seat of Suffolk County, NY lies at the mouth of a river that flows into which body of water?", "answer": "Flanders Bay", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "The duet known as \"Picture\" features Sheryl Crow in Kid Rock's third major album \"Cocky\", but was later replaced with this country singer for the radio.", "answer": "Allison Moorer", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which genus has more known species, Cissus or Digitalis?", "answer": "Cissus", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "What is the nickname of ''Cryin'' singer Steven Tyler of Aerosmith?", "answer": "\"Demon of Screamin'\" due to his high screams", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which film was produced by Walt Disney Pictures, Return to Oz or George of the Jungle?", "answer": "George of the Jungle", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Matthew Settle is known for his role on Band of Brothers as what United States Army officer who served in the 506th Parachute Infantry Regiment of the 101st Airborne Division during World War II?", "answer": "Lieutenant Colonel Ronald C. Speirs", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What German composer born in 1900 had a premier in Berlin in 1928 at the Theater am Schiffbauerdamm?", "answer": "Kurt Weill", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Who was the writer of the 1997 American-French drama film for which Howard Atherton is known?", "answer": "Stephen Schiff", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which restaurant pizza chain has been around longer, LaRosa's Pizzeria or Mr. Jim's Pizza?", "answer": "LaRosa's Pizzeria", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "What is the born name of the actress who starred in Broadway Bad?", "answer": "Virginia Katherine McMath", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which pizza chain operates in more countries, Sarpino's Pizzeria or Pizza Fusion? ", "answer": "Sarpino's Pizzeria", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "What county seat of Clark County, Kansas, is also north of the Cimarron Redoubt?", "answer": "Ashland", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which former italian professional footballer, born in 1970, participated in the 1999\u20132000 FA Cup Final between Chelsea and Aston Villa?", "answer": "Roberto Di Matteo", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "A half-hour series that starred an actress who played Natalie Lane in The Patty Duke Show, also starred what other actress?", "answer": "Dyan Cannon", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "The Valachi hearings were named after which American gangster and first member of the Mafia to acknowledge it existed?", "answer": "Joseph Michael \"Joe Cargo\" Valachi", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "l'Espresso, featuring contributions by Lirio Abbate, is one of Italy's leading weekly news magazines. What's its biggest rival called?", "answer": "Panorama", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which is composed of more institutions, the University of Texas System or Berea College?", "answer": "The University of Texas System", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "What is the Swabian name of the city in Baden-W\u00fcrttemberg with a T-Systems Multimedia Solutions office?", "answer": "Schduagert", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Who was declared champion at a 1983 event sanctioned by an automobile club that was formed in 1944?", "answer": "Jacques Villeneuve, Sr.", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Are FPT University and Duke University in the same country?", "answer": "no", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Guardians of the Galaxy the movie is based on the comic book by what authors?", "answer": "Dan Abnett and Andy Lanning", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What is the seating capacity of the stadium as of 2015 in which 1971 Oklahoma Sooners football team payed their home games?", "answer": "86,112", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What sport did brothers Steve and Tinker Owens play?", "answer": "football", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which writer first published their work, Emma Goldman or Peter Straub?", "answer": "Emma Goldman", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Which documentary film, Monster Camp or Manson, was directed by a larger number of people?", "answer": "Manson", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Patches from the Quilt is a digital EP released by an American Band that is from which state?", "answer": "New York", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What year did Jennifer Lopes, the highest paid Latin actressin Hollywood, appear iin the film Bordertown?   ", "answer": "2006", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "William Henry Huddle painted official portraits of the states's chief executives, including an American folk hero who was commonly referred to in popular culture as what? ", "answer": "King of the Wild Frontier", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Between Chisholm v. Georgia and Edwards v. Aguillard , which seminal Supreme Court case in US history found that the first amendment law was specifically intended to advance a particular religion when it was written?", "answer": "Edwards v. Aguillard", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Who directed the film where Jared Van Snellenberg played a caddy?", "answer": "Dennis Dugan", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "In which group did the singer whose debut extended play was \"Full Moon\" make her debut?", "answer": "Wonder Girls", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which place was founded in 1680, and has Napeague State Park between it and another place?", "answer": "Amagansett", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What country of origin does WGBL and Biloxi, Mississippi have in common?", "answer": "United States", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Lakshmi Niwas Mittal is the CEO of what Luxembourg-based multinational steel manufacturing corporation?", "answer": "ArcelorMittal", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What Norm Smith Medal winner in 2017 played for the Bendigo Pioneers?", "answer": "Dustin Martin", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What military organization featured the general who was declared dead by the Ansar Allah, after a missile attack?", "answer": "Royal Saudi Air Force", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which plant has more species, Maianthemum or Diplolaena?", "answer": "Maianthemum", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "What position did both Phil Mustard and Adam Gilchrist play in wicket?", "answer": "wicketkeeper", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which film was released first, The Story of Robin Hood and His Merrie Men or Lt. Robin Crusoe, U.S.N.?", "answer": "The Story of Robin Hood and His Merrie Men", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "The 2015 MTV Video Music Awards were held on which date, Swift's \"Wildest Dreams\" music video premiered during the pre-show?", "answer": "August 30, 2015", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "David Alan Miller, the Grammy Award winner, is known for conducting which orchestra?", "answer": "Albany Symphony Orchestra", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "The actor that played Landry Clarke in the series \"Friday Night Lights\" stars with Jason Bateman and Rachel McAdams in an upcoming thriller film written by who?", "answer": "Mark Perez", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Is the \"capsicum annuum\" milder or hotter than the jalapeno pepper?", "answer": "It is wider and generally milder than the similar Serrano pepper.", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What is the name of a character from the cartoon \"Hittin' the Trail for Hallelujah Land\" that is now considered derogatory?", "answer": "Uncle Tom", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which Sooner was drafted by the Giants in the second round of the 2016 NFL drafter?", "answer": "Sterling Clay Shepard", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "artist Rajko M\u00fcller plays a genre of music that is a subgenre of what music ?", "answer": "house music", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What Argentine American actor portrayed a character that supposedly died in November 2006?", "answer": "Ignacio Ariel Serricchio", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Who won an award for the soundtrack for the 2014 comedy film written and directed by Wes Anderson? ", "answer": "Alexandre Michel G\u00e9rard Desplat", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "In what year was the actor born who appeared in both Assault on Precinct 13 and every Rocky installment?", "answer": "1937", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which documentary was released earlier, Pride Divide or What Would Jesus Buy?", "answer": "Pride Divide", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "What is the 2010 census population of the town at which  Miss America 2007 was held? ", "answer": "223,167", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Are Bothriochloa and Bystropogon both types of plant?", "answer": "yes", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Arnhold Holdings Ltd (Stock Code: SEHK 0102) is a public company listed on the Hong Kong Stock Exchange and is a leading name in the distribution of building materials and engineering equipment in China, the Stock Exchange of Hong Kong Limited (SEHK) is a stock exchange located in Hong Kong, it's East Asia's and Asia's which rank, largest stock exchange>", "answer": "third", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Who was born first Yves Simoneau or Edgar Wright?", "answer": "Yves Simoneau", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Antonio Comi is the current general manager of a football club based in what city?", "answer": "Turin, Piedmont", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What is the diameter of this mass concentration of galaxies that contains the Local Sheet?", "answer": "33 megaparsecs", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "\"Talk That Talk\" is a song recorded by Barbadian singer Rihanna, for her studio album same name, released in which year, the song was written by Ester Dean, an American