ear was the band who had a Counterparts Tour formed?  ", "answer": "1968", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which of these is in the grass family, Mertensia or Cymbopogon?", "answer": "Cymbopogon", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "John Taylor Wood served on a Civil War ship which engaged in battle with what iron-hulled steamship in one of the most famous naval battles in Civil War and U.S. Naval history?", "answer": "USS \"Monitor\"", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What ballad is the lullaby written and composed by Effie Crockett based on?", "answer": "Lillibullero", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Maryse Alberti was a cinematographer who worked on the Todd Haynes drama film set in Britain during what time period?", "answer": "1970s", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What is the ratio of the building material that is named for the Latin word \"crushed\" and sand used to stabilize buildings?", "answer": "1:5", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Other then Josh Deu and Win butler who else is in Arcade fire?", "answer": "R\u00e9gine Chassagne and younger brother Will Butler", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Leonid Kantorovich and Vladimir Arnold both acted as what in the Soviet Union?", "answer": "mathematician", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "In early September 2009, Robert Flores was replaced by which American sportscaster who has been an anchor for ESPN since 1996?", "answer": "John Buccigross", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Who lived a longer life Hampar Kelikian or Arthur T. Gregorian?", "answer": "Arthur T. Gregorian", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Which record producer wrote \"Love Story\"?", "answer": "Taylor Swift", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "When was the Colombian drug lord which was one of the Medell\u00edn Cartel with Jorge Luis Ochoa V\u00e1squez born? ", "answer": "1 December 19492", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Once Upon a Time in London is an upcoming British crime film directed by Simon Rumley, the film is about the notorious gangsters Billy Hill and which English gangster, that died on 12 March 1996?", "answer": "Jack Comer", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Who is the writer of the 2011 sci-fi thriller starring Warren Christie?", "answer": "Brian Miller", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What is the name of this current children's park in Pleasure Beach Blackpool, England, that features a roller coaster name Blue Flyer?", "answer": "Nickelodeon Land", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Nathan Lyon was born in the largest town in what council?", "answer": "Hilltops Council", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "The Protecting Internet Freedom Act was introduced by a senator from which state ?", "answer": "Texas", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What by birth is the woman who was to get married to Prince Charles known by?", "answer": "Infanta of Spain", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What is the name of the only \"Des Moines\" cruiser that still exists?", "answer": "USS \"Salem\"", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which American sports drama television series on VH1 series created by James LaRosa features Jonathan McDaniel?", "answer": "Hit the Floor", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Are Peter Faiman and Harry d'Abbadie d'Arrast from the same country?", "answer": "no", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "What rugby game featured James Harris in 2012 and 2013?", "answer": "The Varsity Match", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which instrument was the pre-eminent one in the five books of sonatas and the twelve \"concerti grossi\" published by Benjamin Cooke?", "answer": "violin", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Warner von Trapp, the grandfather of The von Trapps, was the inspiration for what movie?", "answer": "The Sound of Music", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What city is both the site of the Staples Center and the hometown of Motley Cr\u00fce?", "answer": "Los Angeles", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Michael H. Weber was part of the team who wrote the screenplay for the 2013 c