osa's Pizzeria have in common?", "answer": "pizza", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Who created the television series in which Sean Harris had the role of Micheletto Corella ?", "answer": "Neil Jordan;", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What is the independent private, co-educational, day and boarding school in a town with a population of 3,677?", "answer": "High Mowing School", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Where are the headquarters of the church founded by Dag Heward-Mills?", "answer": "Accra, Ghana", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What 16h century church is near  the seat of Portugese Macau's government?", "answer": "St. Dominic's Church", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Are Gene Loves Jezebel and Disciple from the same country?", "answer": "no", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Which national forest (apart from the Pisgah National Forest) does this river, of which Spring Creek is a tributary stream, drain?", "answer": "Cherokee National Forest", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Giacomo Domenico Mario Antonio Pasquale Giuseppe Tritto, was an Italian composer, known primarily for his 54 operas, amongst his pupils were Vincenzo Bellini, around which year?", "answer": "1821", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "When did the club for which Bobby Shuttleworth presently plays begins play? ", "answer": "2017", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What is the other name for the world's largest d\u014djinshi fair, held twice a year in Tokyo, Japan that was the location of the first release of a Japanese adult d\u014djin visual novel created by Type-Moon in 2000?", "answer": "Comic Market", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Is Czes\u0142aw \u015apiewa\u00a0from the same country as Wolf Parade?", "answer": "no", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "What type of media does Caracal and The Weeknd have in common?", "answer": "music", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "\"Habla Blah Blah\", is a song by Mexican recording artist, and songwriter Gloria Trevi, and was released on which date?", "answer": "August 1, 2014", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": " The President of the United States who was involved in the Teapot Dome scandal and Nan Britton were the parents of what daughter?", "answer": "Elizabeth Ann Blaesing", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Frank Lennon was know for taking photographs regarding which sport at the Summit Series?", "answer": "ice hockey", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": " Susan E. Dietter, usually credited as Susie Dietter, is an American director, known primarily for her work on television cartoons, she also worked as an animator for Looney Tunes, a modern-day American animated series of comedy short films produced by which organization, from 1930 to 1969?", "answer": "Warner Bros.", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What is the name of the German Army's standard machine gun that has a narrow constructive relationship with the MG 11?", "answer": "MG 08", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Who was the coach of the team that the 2008 Kansas Jayhawks football team finished the regular season with a victory over?", "answer": "Gary Pinkel", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which forested highland is located in Lower Austria and Vienna?", "answer": "Vienna Woods", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What agency did the breakout star of Lee Kyoung-mi's 2008 directorial effort?", "answer": "Cube Entertainment", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "The Incredibles and Never a Dull Moment, are American films, which company made them both?", "answer": "Walt Disney", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Is Mark Shuttleworth or Ivan Bella a Slovak Air Force officer?", "answer": "Ivan Bella (born 25 May 1964 in Brezno, Czechoslovakia (now Slovakia)) is a Slovak Air Force officer", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "What actor born in 1938 starred in the 1972 film Deliverance?", "answer": "Jon Voight", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What was the real name of the criminal in which a 2008 British fictionalized biographical crime film was based on?", "answer": "Michael Gordon Peterson", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What job did both Paul Claudel and Ry\u016bnosuke Akutagawa hold?", "answer": "writer", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Furka\u2013Oberalp-Bahn Deh 4/4 I was operated in which southwestern Swiss canton?", "answer": "Valais", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Who contributes the sole guest verse on Jay-Z's album that includes the song \"Song Cry\"?", "answer": "Eminem", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "In what Rock film did Sylvestor Stallone star with a family member?", "answer": "Rocky V", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "The tennis player who partnered with Peter Flemin in 1979 Wimbledon Championships was born in which year?", "answer": "1959", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Park Bo-young was in what him film", "answer": "Scandal Makers", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which film was released first, The BFG or Perri?", "answer": "Perri", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Which member of the Chrissie and Jane Australian breakfast show was born in January 1971?", "answer": "Jane Hall", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which guitarist played for both The Dandy Warhols and Pete International Airport?", "answer": "Peter Holmstr\u00f6m", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "are Jorge Amado and Anna Quindlen authors?", "answer": "yes", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "What is the county seat of a county located in the U.S. state of Nevada where the Sheep Range is found?", "answer": "Pioche", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which British poet's writings were the basis for In the Region of the Summer Stars?", "answer": "Charles Williams", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What brand released the games \"Sorry\" and \"Montezuma's Revenge\"?", "answer": "Hasbro", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which American neo-noir science fiction film was the film to which 2036: Nexus Dawn was a prequel?", "answer": "Blade Runner 2049", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What was the 2010 population of the city in which the West Texas Wildcatters played their home games at the Ector County Coliseum?", "answer": "118,918", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Are Dashiell Hammett and Julio Cort\u00e1zar both nationals of the same country ?", "answer": "no", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Which drink is more ingrained in a particular nation's culture, Rum Swizzle or Mulled wine?", "answer": "Rum Swizzle", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "In The Simpsons episode \"Apocalypse Cow\" who voices the father of the farm girl Mary?", "answer": "Hank Azaria", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "William E. Kapelle is a medieval historian at a university in a city which was the prototype for what?", "answer": "19th century industrial city planning", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Forward for Premier League club Manchester United and the England national team and who wears The \"Nike Hypervenom\" was born on what day? ", "answer": "born 31 October 1997", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What year was the United Nations Security Council resolution 1067 adopted after noting various resolutions by the International Civil Aviation Organization?", "answer": "1996", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "At which University, did the LA Rams player who made his NFL debut in November 1990 against the New York Giants, finish college ?", "answer": "University of Southern Mississippi", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Michael Bennett Jr., is an American football defensive end for which sports team, of the National Football League (NFL), he is the brother of which American football tight end for the Green Bay Packers? ", "answer": "Seattle Seahawks", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What United Kingdom government is based in \"The Doughnut\" in the suburbs of Cheltenham and works alongside MI5 as part of the United Kingdom's intelligence machinery?", "answer": "Government Communications Headquarters", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "When was Dwayne Johnson's father born? ", "an