ype": "bridge"}, {"question": "What state is the town and village, who share the same name and are both located southwest of Syracuse, located in?", "answer": "New York", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which is from further east in the United States, 3 Doors Down or Edward Sharpe and the Magnetic Zeros?", "answer": "3 Doors Down", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "When was the film distribution company who released \"A Violent Prosecutor\" founded?", "answer": "1996", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Whats Spanish explorer and former governor of Florida was featured in the History Channel miniseries Conquest of America/.", "answer": "Pedro Men\u00e9ndez de Avil\u00e9s", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Henschel Hs 132 was a part of  the aerial warfare branch of the combined German Wehrmacht military forces during what war", "answer": "World War II", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "The Charles H. Spencer hulk was used for gold refining operations in a state with what capital?", "answer": "Phoenix", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "In which year did the husband of Jean Case of the Case Foundation retire from the company he had co-founded?", "answer": "2003", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Sweet Girl is the sixth mini-album released by B1A4 under WM Entertainment, the  title song of the album, \"Sweet Girl\", along with the other songs, was produced by which South Korean singer, songwriter, record producer, and actor?", "answer": "Jung Jin-young", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "who was born first, Sergei Prokofiev or Maurice Ravel ?", "answer": "Maurice Ravel", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "The Media Project have panelists that include which president and chief executive officer of WAMC/Northeast Public Radio, a National Public Radio affiliate, a position he has held since 1981?", "answer": "Alan S. Chartock", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Corinne Marchand played the title role in what Agnes Varda film?", "answer": "Cl\u00e9o from 5 to 7", "type": "