ctions on ", "answer": "New York City", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Are both David Giler and Brian G. Hutton film actors?", "answer": "no", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "What are the names of the brothers who produced In Our Image?", "answer": "Isaac Donald \"Don\" Everly (born February 1, 1937) and Phillip \"Phil\" Everly", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Jacques Vall\u00e9e, a computer scientist, author, ufologist and former astronomer, describes allegations of the Montauk Project as an outgrowth of stories about what experiment?", "answer": "the Philadelphia Experiment", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Who hosts a national sports radio show on an American broadcasting company that provides three satellite radio and online radio services?", "answer": "Gerrie Burke", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Where was the dual placed between Ohio Bobcats and a university team of Youngstown, Ohio, United States?", "answer": "Ohio University's Aquatic Center", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "The Market Street Bridge was named in honor of the principal of the cherokee nation from 1828-1866, and was described as what?", "answer": "the Moses of his people", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Blue Crush is a 2002 sports film that tells the story of three friends who have one passion: living the ultimate dream of surfing on a beach located on which island ?", "answer": "Island of O\u02bb ahu", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What is the name of a medication used to within a chemotherapy regimen?", "answer": "Cisplatin", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Dallas Love Field and William P. Hobby Airport are both located in which state?", "answer": "Texas", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Dalton Trumbo and David Payne are both which nationality?", "answer": "American", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "American cooking magazine, along with World Wide Country Tours was founded by what man?", "answer": "Roy Reiman", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What American singer had a debut single \"Hide Away\" that was part of the debut album \"Sit Still, Look Pretty\" released on October, 7,2016?", "answer": "Daya", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What digest-size science fiction magazine did the man known as the \"Dean of Science Fiction Artists\" provide artwork for?", "answer": "Science Fiction Adventures", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "When was the founder of Yakira, L.L.C. born?", "answer": "August 29, 1972", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Jared Zabransky played college football at Boise State and was named Offensive Player of the Game which was played in what stadium? ", "answer": "University of Phoenix Stadium", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What is the birthdate of this English professional footballer, who played with Chris Jones during his spell with the Yorkshire outfit?", "answer": "4 January 1986", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "The former owner and principal of the Caterham F1 Team founded what company?", "answer": "Tune Air Sdn.", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "When did the producer of the 1987 version of 21 Jump Street die?", "answer": "September 30, 2010", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "April Kelly co-created what sitcom that premiered in 2014?", "answer": "Girl Meets World", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which world record are held by the swimmer who beat Ross Murdoch in the European 100 metre breaststroke?", "answer": "50 and 100m breaststroke", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Who was the founding owner of the Pittsburgh Steelers whose son spearheaded a requirement known as the \"Rooney Rule?\"", "answer": "Arthur Joseph Rooney Sr.", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Cruciada \u00eempotriva comunismului was named in reference to which Axis invasion of the Soviet Union?", "answer": "Operation Barbarossa", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": " French migration to the United Kingdom, occurred at various points in history, which Protestant group in the 16th and 17th centuries,fled religious persecution?", "answer": "Huguenots", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which quarterback in the Panthers\u2013Seahawks rivalry was born in 1988?", "answer": "Russell Carrington Wilson", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "The sixth season of the \"Tyler Perry's House of Payne\" began airing on November 4, 2009, it starred Cassandra \"Cassi\" Davis, an American actress and singer, best known for her role as who, on \"Tyler Perry's House of Payne\"?", "answer": "Ella Payne", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Tutu Jones (born September 9, 1966) is an American electric blues and soul blues guitarist, singer and songwriter, she has cited  Freddie King (September 3, 1934 \u2013 December 28, 1976), as an influence on his playing style, he was an American blues guitarist and singer, he has been described as one of the \"   \" of electric blues guitar?", "answer": "Three Kings", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "what does Nic Offer and Johnny Bonnel have in common?", "answer": "band", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Were The Rape of Europa and Down from the Mountain both released as films?", "answer": "yes", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Along with the town Belmont, what is the population of the other town that is a part of the Shaker Regional School District?", "answer": "2,352", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which band has released more albums, Seven Mary Three or Django Django?", "answer": "Seven Mary Three", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Zora Fair was a native to South Carolina who nearly exposed the military campaign conducted through Georgia from when to when?", "answer": "November 15 to December 21, 1864", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What is the name of the YouTube Channel that was founded by the Lead Vocalist of the English rock band Asking Alexandria who was featured in the band's fourth studio album \"The Black?\"", "answer": "above92", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which Australian trail which passes through the northern suburbs of Melbourne connects to the Melbourne Zoo?", "answer": "Capital City Trail", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Who is younger, Patricio Guzm\u00e1n Lozanes or Gil Kenan?", "answer": "Gil Kenan", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Conoclinium and Catalpa, have which mutual two attributes?", "answer": "flowering plants", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "What came out first, Cancer or Almost Sunrise?", "answer": "Cancer", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "To which country was the historical figure used for the basis of the novel Strandloper transported to?", "answer": "Australia", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "When was the founder of TruthRevolt born? ", "answer": "January 15, 1984", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What is the editorial stance of the newspaper that featured Paul Rimstead as a page 5 columnist?", "answer": "populist conservative", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Kamp Krustier featured a script by which screenwriter who had previously worked on The Wonder Years?", "answer": "David Michael Stern", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Flying Officer Dinshaw Edulijee received the AFC from what auxiliary air force of the British Empire?", "answer": "The Indian Air Force", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "The son of who was a German botanist, horticulturist, and microscopist, who joined the Schleswig-Holstein army to fight the first round of military conflict in southern Denmark and northern Germany rooted in the Schleswig-Holstein Question?", "answer": "Johann Friedrich Gr\u00f6nland", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What year did jango fett debut?", "answer": "2002", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Crabtree Creek is a tributary that begins in the western foothills of a major mountain range whose highest peak is how tall?", "answer": "14411 ft", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which of the singles in Tim McGraw's Two Lanes of Freedom album features Taylor Swift on vocals and Keith Urban on guitar?", "answer": "Highway Don't Care", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Angel Co