: "Truso, situated on Lake Dru\u017cno, was an Old Prussian (Pomesanian) town near the Baltic Sea just east of the Vistula River, in the words of Marija Gimbutas, \"the name of the town is the earliest known historically in the Baltic Sea area\", Gimbutas was a Lithuanian-American archaeologist known for her research into the Neolithic and Bronze Age cultures of \"Old Europe\" and for her Kurgan hypothesis, which located the Proto-Indo-European homeland in which location?", "answer": "Pontic Steppe", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": " Magnano in Riviera is a \"comune\" and one of how many regions of Italy?", "answer": "20", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "American food company, Progresso, produces what food that is a spicy stew containing chili peppers, meat (usually beef), and often tomatoes and beans?", "answer": "Chili con carne", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What is the middle name of the person that hosted the Logie Awards of 2003?", "answer": "Joseph", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Love in the Time of Money stared a Canadian actress best known for her 3 seasons in what American television series? ", "answer": "Law & Order", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which artist created a series of 60 paintings in 1985 based on scenes and images of the 17th-century play Othello?", "answer": "Nabil Kanso", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "United States naval reactors included those found at the R&D facility in what New York city?", "answer": "Niskayuna", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Dheepan was partly inspired by the literary work written in what year?", "answer": "1721", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Sir Anthony James Allan Havelock-Allan, 4th Baronet (28 February 1904 \u2013 11 January 2003) was a British film producer and screenwriter whose credits included Oliver Twist , a 1948 British film and the second of David Lean's two film adaptations of who's novels?", "answer": "Charles Dickens", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Hamza Bencherif plays as a defen