ilm did pornographic actress Lily Carter lead in alongside Lily LaBeau?", "answer": "Wasteland", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Who directed the 2010 mystery erotic film that Kim Ji-hoon appeared in?", "answer": "Ju Kyung-jung", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "\"A Midsummer's Nice Dream\" is the sixteenth episode of \"The Simpsons\"' whose twenty-second season began airing on what television network?", "answer": "Fox", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What song is an alternative mix of the Beatles' 1970 album \"Let It Be\" released in 2003, which replaced the 39-second \"Maggie Mae\" with \" Let Me Down\"?", "answer": "Dig It", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What was the population in 2000 of the town in which Hugh White died ? ", "answer": "8,515", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What was the middle name of the creator of the show The Honeymooners ?", "answer": "Herbert", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Who was born first, John P. Kennedy or Millard Fillmore?", "answer": "John Pendleton Kennedy", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What British academic philosopher has this quote attributed to him regarding the principle of charity \"it constrains the interpreter to maximize the truth or rationality in the subject's sayings.\"?", "answer": "Simon Blackburn", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "The men's ice hockey that won seven national championships while Emil Iverson was coach won how many NCAA national championships?", "answer": "five", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Brian London lost in 1966 to what professional boxer born 1942", "answer": "Muhammad Ali", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Righteous Love, is the American singer Joan Osborne's  which number studio album?", "answer": "second studio album", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Buried Alive was from the studio album that was released on what date?", "answer": "October 21, 2014", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Who has worked on films in more countries, Marco Ferreri or Peter Faiman?", "answer": "Marco Ferreri", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Me Estoy Enamorando (English: \"I'm Falling in Love\" ) is the sixth studio album by Mexican singer Alejandro Fern\u00e1ndez, Fern\u00e1ndez asked Emilio Estefan to produce his next project after listening to \"Mi Tierra\", released in which year, by his wife Gloria Estefan?", "answer": "1993", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "The House of Assembly, or lower house, is one of the two chambers of the Parliament of South Australia, it sits in Parliament House in the state capital, in which city city, Parliament House, on the corner of North Terrace and King William Road, is which city, is the seat of the Parliament of South Australia?", "answer": "Adelaide", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "David T. Beito was a mentor to  Fannie Lou Hamer and this american civil rights activist who was murdered by who", "answer": "white supremacist and Klansman", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Who was the Slovenian player for the Suns team in 2000-01? ", "answer": "Goran Dragi\u0107", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Who produced the American animated television series based on the \"Spider-Man", "answer": "Eric Radomski", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which film exposes the former President of the Fundamentalist Church of Jesus?", "answer": "Banking on Heaven", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "In which province is the race held that Reinier Paping won in 1963 ?", "answer": "Friesland", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Carl Chang, is the older brother and former coach of which tennis star, a now retired, American professional tennis player, that won 34 top-level professional singles titles?", "answer": "Michael Chang", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Great WAgon Road was an improved trail through one of the major landform features of eastern North America, and stretches about 1200 miles from Quebec to where?", "answer": "Alabama", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which University has 5 Nobel laureates on their faculty, Rockefeller