d Duke of Lithuania, then the King of Poland, who reserved the rights of the overlord under the Pact of Vilnius and Radom?", "answer": "W\u0142adys\u0142aw II Jagie\u0142\u0142o", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Paul Shelving worked at the Stratford-upon-Avon theatre that has how many seats?", "answer": "1,040+", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Who starred in Harry Potter and Megan Leavey?", "answer": "Tom Felton", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Both Gert Bo Jacobsen and Greg Haugen were professionals at what sport?", "answer": "boxer", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What is the name of the first single from the third album made the member of Take That that was born on 27 January 1972?", "answer": "Makin' Out", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Boxing in the 1980s was filled with important fights, events and personalities that shaped the sport, WBO and which one of how many major organizations recognized by the International Boxing Hall of Fame (IBHOF) which sanction world championship boxing bouts, began operating?", "answer": "four", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "TKB-408 was a precursor to which heavily-modified Kalashnikov rifle as selected by the Red Army?", "answer": "AK-47", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "The Battle of Brooklyn references a battle during the Revolutionary War that was fought on whta date?", "answer": "August 27, 1776", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which of David Guetta's albums featured a song with vocals by the same singer who recorded \"Phresh Out the Runway?\"", "answer": "One Love", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "In what year was the composer of \"Ave Maria\" born?", "answer": "1925", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "How many seasons did the science based cooking show hosted by Alton Brown air? ", "answer": "14 seasons", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Who was born first, Phil Joanou or Tod Browning?", "answer": "Tod Browning", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "When was the recorder of \"Lonely Eyes\" declared as the wi