t played Sif in the film \"Thor\" also starred in a 2016 American psychological thriller that was directed by who?", "answer": "Bram Coppens", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Who wrote Les Erinnyes, the French verse drama based Aeschylus' Oresteia?", "answer": "Leconte de Lisle", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Who directed the Michael Jackson film for which Universal Hartland provided the visual effects?", "answer": "Francis Ford Coppola", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which german medium tank was developed in late 1930s to provide the close-in fire support for standard Japanese medium tanks in Second World War?", "answer": "Panzer IV", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Both Genghis Blues and To Shoot an Elephant are considered what type of film?", "answer": "documentary", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "What Oslo-based Norwegian singer-songwriter provided guest vocals for the Tyler album Flower Boy?", "answer": "Anna of the North", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Are Walt Disney and Sacro GRA both documentry films?", "answer": "yes", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Jennifer Pharr Davis has hiked on the long-distance walk in Europe around Mont Blanc that covers approximately what distance?", "answer": "170 km", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Anatomy is an album by the group in the genre that developed in what decade?", "answer": "1980s", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "In what year was the writer of \"Anne of the Island\" born?", "answer": "1874", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Danish Viking, who ruled over parts of Friesland between 841 and 873 was the uncle of a Viking leader who raided the British Isles, West Francia, Frisia, and Lotharingia in the 860s and 870?", "answer": "Roricus, Rorichus", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which banker is considered the second largest in the world, BNP Paribas or China Construction Bank?", "answer": "China Construction Bank", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Meridiana destinations are also served by which subsidiary headquartered in Milan?", "answer": "Air Italy S.p.A.", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "The M20 is a motorway in Kent, England, although not signposted in England, this road is part of the European route E15, The European route E 15 is part of which entity's international E-road network?", "answer": "United Nations", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which magazine is published more frequently, The Believer or Democracy?", "answer": "The Believer", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Stone Sour's sixth album Hydrograd, which was also the first album to feature Christian Martucci and Johny Chow, was released worldwide on June 30, 2017 from which record label?", "answer": "Roadrunner Records", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Needtobreathe and Imagine Dragons, have which mutual genre?", "answer": "rock", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": " Bob Valesente played football at a college founded by what man?", "answer": "William Egbert", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "what does Berserk and Berserk have in common?", "answer": "anime", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Joyce Anita Hytner sits on the board of a not-for-profit producing theatre that was damaged during air raids in what year?", "answer": "1940", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What song composed by Robert Alexander Anderson is the best known Hawaiian Christmas song?", "answer": "Mele Kalikimaka", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Roses Are Red and The Hives, share which genre?", "answer": "rock", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "What is the name of the Pornographic film collected at the Kinsey Institute for research in Sex, Gender and Reproduction that includes possibly the first use of extreme close-ups of genitalia?", "answer": "El Satario", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Savita Kovind is the wife of the politician who has been the President of India since what year?", "answer": "2017", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What anchor store appear at Shops at Billerica besides Market Basket and the store that was acquired by Bain Capital in a take-private transaction?", "answer": "Kmart", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Song \"English Sunset\" from English rock band The Moody Blues album \"Strange Times\" often gets confused with song \"The Sunset\", which is on what album?", "answer": "Days of Future Passed", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Huh Jung directed which film, released on August 17, 2017?", "answer": "The Mimic", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "The Garde Civique or Burgerwacht, was a Belgian paramilitary militia created in October 1830 shortly after the Belgian Revolution, it was the conflict which led to the secession of the southern provinces (mainly the former Southern Netherlands) from the United Kingdom of the Netherlands and the establishment of an independent Kingdom of which country nation?", "answer": "Belgium", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "The East of the Jordan, Two Banks to the Jordan, is a poem written by Ze'ev Jabotinsky, which type of leader, Zionism (Hebrew: \u05e6\u05b4\u05d9\u05bc\u05d5\u05b9\u05e0\u05d5\u05bc\u05ea\u200e \"Tsiyyonut\" ] after \"Zion\") is the national movement of the Jewish people that supports the re-establishment of a Jewish homeland in the territory defined as the historic Land of Israel, roughly corresponding to Canaan, the Holy Land, or the region of Palestine?", "answer": "Revisionist Zionist", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Where was the group from that collaborated with Eazy-E on \"Only if you want it\"?", "answer": "East Orange, New Jersey", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Who directed the film that Im Auftrag des Herrn... \u2013 Die Toten Hosen Live's title is a reference to?", "answer": "John Landis", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What was the partnership of guitarist Luke Wood and guitarist/vocalist Jesse Hartman, The Get Up Kids or Sammy ?", "answer": "Sammy", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "How many members are in the band that includes Woo Ji-ho under a stage name?", "answer": "seven", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which American statesman and one of the Founding Fathers of the United States chose William Coleman to be the first editor of \"The New York Evening Post\" (today known as the \"New York Post\")", "answer": "Alexander Hamilton", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which group, Philly's Most Wanted or the Neptunes, is composed of Pharrell Williams and Chad Hugo, who are credited with contributing the sound for many successful hip hop and R&B artists in the late-1990s and 2000s?", "answer": "The Neptunes", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which country do Rolf de Heer and Ralph Smart have in common?", "answer": "Australia", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "What do Theodore Wharton and Fatih Akin have in common?", "answer": "film director", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "What country do the Chichele Lectures take place in?", "answer": "in England", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What country did Eselealofa 'Ese' Apinelu manage Tuvalu's volleyball team in?", "answer": "Fiji", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which company did the great nephew of the commander of the Civil war work for?", "answer": "Goldsboro", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Carlos Andr\u00e9s Baldassari, is a former Uruguayan rugby union player and a current coach, and was born in Salta, a city located in the Lerma Valley, at 1,152 metres (3780 feet) above sea level in the northwest part of which country?", "answer": "Argentina", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "USS Plainview was named for one of the cities in what town in New York?", "answer": "Oyster Bay", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What company published Bop magazine?", "answer": "The Laufer Company", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "In what year was the musican born that composed the music for the film Honour Killing?", "answer": "1948", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Are St. Mary's University, Texas and University of Michigan in Great Britain?", "answer": "no", "type": "comparison"