lm company founded in 2001, originally as a subsidiary of Lars von Trier's film company Zentropa, which is best known for the production of the erotic feature film, All About Anna is a Danish film released in which year, directed by Jessica Nilsson?", "answer": "2005", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Midnattssol in english is which natural phenomenon that occurs in the summer months in places north of the Arctic Circle or south of the Antarctic Circle?", "answer": "Midnight sun", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What American rock band has a song title that refers to the nickname of the Paul Brown Stadium?", "answer": "Guns N' Roses", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What had four separate designs and replaced The PowerBook and iBook lines?", "answer": "MacBook", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "When was the American entrepreneur died who founded The Center for Governmental Research, Inc?", "answer": "March 14, 1932", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which American adult animated sitcom on Adult Swim featured the \"The Fried Chicken Flu\" episode?", "answer": "The Boondocks", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "ECI was established by Ben Affleck and another who if the daughter of who?", "answer": "former Congressman Pat Williams and former Montana Senate Majority Leader Carol Williams", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "A water dragon in England known as a peg powler is similar to a water spirit connected to the monster in 'Beowul' called what?", "answer": "Grindylow", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which actor played the physically abusive teacher in a 2001 highest grossing film?", "answer": "Kim Kwang-kyu", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What American rapper was a guest judge for \"Project Runway:  Under the Gunn\"?", "answer": "Macklemore", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which movie is an American animated film, The Watercolor or Fantastic Mr. Fox?", "answer": "Fantastic Mr. Fox", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Which former roommate of Mark Zuckerberg owns 53 million Facebook shares? ", "answer": "Eduardo Saverin", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Who created the fictional character that became the star of the War is Hell series in issue #9?", "answer": "Mike Friedrich and Jim Starlin", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Who wrote the song, originally recorded in 1956 and one of the Rock and Roll Hall of Fame's 500 Songs that Shaped Rock and Roll, \"I Put a Spell on You\" that appeared on British singer Sonique's debu studiot album?", "answer": "Jay Hawkins", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "The guitarist and writer of \"Whole Lotta Rosie\" was ranked 24th in a list of 100 greatest guitarists by what magazine?", "answer": "Rolling Stone", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What style music are both the band The Coral Sea and the band The Mountain Goats?", "answer": "indie", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "What beverage dates back to 5th millienium and has some of the oldest recipes written in Summerian", "answer": "Beer", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What University located in New Jersey did William Trager attend?", "answer": "Rutgers University", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What position does the individual who collaborated with Wolfgang Rindler to popularize the use of spinors in general relativity hold at the Mathematical Institute of the University of Oxford?", "answer": "Emeritus Rouse Ball Professor of Mathematics", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which DC comics fictional character is played by Sirena Irwin using only voice?", "answer": "Mera", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which Belizean rapper, also known as Shyne, is famous for the song \"Bad Boyz\"", "answer": "Moses Michael Levi", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Were Dolan v. City of Tigard and Gravel v. United States heard in the same year?", "answer": "no", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Ralph Schuckett played on albums by what American musical duo from Philadelphia?", "answer": "Hall & Oates", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Whi