d by a singer known for his four-octave what?", "answer": "vocal range", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What building in the 14th largest city in Georgia was a work of architect Lloyd Barton Greer?", "answer": "Barber-Pittman House", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which English military advisor on the \"Mayflower\" had a fort named after him on Lovell's Island, Massachusetts?", "answer": "Myles Standish", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Andrea Ojeda represents Argentina at international and Olympic level at football, and plays for which famous Buenos Aires club?", "answer": "Boca Juniors", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What junior rollercoaster is designed to look like it has actual animals in the train in the FantasyLand section at Magic Kingdom?", "answer": "The Barnstormer", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What movie is show in a the link language of Mahl-dominated Minicoy Island?", "answer": "Onnu Muthal Poojyam Vare", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Who has played in more bands, Nell Sigland or Ezra Koenig?", "answer": "Nell Sigland", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Joseph Aloysius Riggert played for an American professional baseball team that was offically renamed in what year?", "answer": "1900", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Are both Kai Hansen and Piotr Wiwczarek known for being guitarists for their respective bands?", "answer": "yes", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "What year was the person who played Shelby in Glee born?", "answer": "1971", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "From what album was Late Orchestration's bonus track?", "answer": "Late Registration", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Are Driver Friendly and Candlelight Red from the same country?", "answer": "yes", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Which British economist was Erwin Rothbarth a research assistant for that changed the theory of economics?", "answer": "John Maynard Keynes", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What role did Ephraim Sykes play in a Broadway musical