o a hobby which has harmful negative consequences. What is severe cases diagnosed as?", "answer": "Severe problem gambling may be diagnosed as clinical pathological gambling", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "In what 2016 film did Chad Willett star in with Danny Glover?", "answer": "Monster Trucks", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Rush City was packaged with a magazine that is a subsidiary of which media, events, and research technology group?", "answer": "International Data Group", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "In what region of Italy did Wilfried Thurner earn his best finish in the Winter Olympics?", "answer": "Veneto", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which school was founded first, Bahauddin Zakariya University or Cleveland State University?", "answer": "Cleveland State University", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "What is the name of the association that the Chelsea Building Society is a member of?", "answer": "Building Societies Association", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What is the name of the band in which the member, who is known as the \"Five Foot Assassin\" and is featured on the song \"La Schmoove,\" is part of?", "answer": "A Tribe Called Quest", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Both have travelled in space but which has completed more Space Shuttle missions: Jean-Fran\u00e7ois Clervoy or Mark Shuttleworth?", "answer": "Jean-Fran\u00e7ois Andr\u00e9 Clervoy", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Mixed Blood Majority shared a stage with the hip hop artist from what Minnesota city?", "answer": "Minneapolis", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Jon Arbuckle appeared in the computer animated television series based on the comics by whom?", "answer": "Jim Davis", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "who is the lead singer of the Belgian band K's Choice, Marcus Cooper or Sarah Bettens ?", "answer": "Sarah Bettens", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "For which sport did the star of film Valley of the Head Hunters win an Olympic bronze medal ?", "answer": "water polo.", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Before March 2008 which of the following BBC Radio studios were you able to listen to the David Bussey Show: Newport Arch in Lincoln on 94.9 (most of the county) and 104.7 (Grantham) FM, 1368 (Swanpool, west Lincoln) AM, and/or BBC Radio Humberside?", "answer": "Newport Arch in Lincoln on 94.9 (most of the county) and 104.7 (Grantham) FM, 1368 (Swanpool, west Lincoln) AM", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What American actress from the early 1990s starred in the American comedy-drama film Roommates?", "answer": "Julianne Moore", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which company owned by Matt Groening features a logo with the letter \"C\" formed by a reflected surfboard?", "answer": "The Curiosity Company", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Who wrote the book from which the movie was adapted that Elliot Goldenthal won the Academy Award for Best Original Score in 2002 for?", "answer": "Hayden Herrera", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Good-bye, My Lady features a boy taking in what stray breed of hunting dog?", "answer": "Basenji", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Led Zeppelin Deluxe Edition was a set of albums released by the group who formed on what date?", "answer": "12 January 1969", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Don Bradman, who was in the movie The Flying Doctor, was known as the greatest what of all time?", "answer": "batsman", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Where did the actor who created the characters Jiminy Glick and Ed Grimley star in a performance with Jennifer Chambers?", "answer": "Los Angeles", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Coleman Francis and William Dieterle, have which occupations in common?", "answer": "actor and film director", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "By which professor from the territory's second oldest university (CUHK) the post-reform era Socialism 3.0 was proposed?", "answer": "Professor Wang Shaoguang", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "The 1997 Brownlow Medal nominees included