ere published by Cahiers d'Art?", "answer": "8 April 1973", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "When was the job site created that has Jeff Taylor as it's founder ?", "answer": "1999", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Jimmy Urine and Mark Hoppus, have which mutual occupations?", "answer": "singer, songwriter, and musician", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Which band was created earlier, EMF or the Nine Black Alps?", "answer": "EMF", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "The owner of the YouTube channel WinterSpringPro was partnered with which other YouTube personality for Amazing Race 22?", "answer": "Meghan Camarena", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which summer resort colony is part of Southport, Maine?", "answer": "Squirrel Island, Maine", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Sky and Sand is a song by German electronic music producers Paul Kalkbrenner and who?", "answer": "Fritz Kalkbrenner", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which band has more members, The Border Surrender or Morphine?", "answer": "The Border Surrender", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Dezadeash Lake is located in the territory that has what capital?", "answer": "Whitehorse", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What city was JaMarcus Russell's college football team stadium located?", "answer": "Baton Rouge", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "The animated Christmas television special that included the song \"Christmas Time Is Here\" is based on what comic strip?", "answer": "Peanuts", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Charlie Simpson and Yang Seung-ho are both in musical groups consistiing entirely of which sex?", "answer": "male", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "The first African-American woman to be elected a diocesan bishop succeeded a woman who annouced her retirement during what convention?", "answer": "2015 Diocesan Convention", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "he breakfast roll (Irish: \"roll\u00f3g bhricfeasta\" ) is a bread roll filled with elements of which breakfast meal that typically includes bacon, sausages, eggs, other cooked foods and a beverage such as coffee or tea?", "answer": "full breakfast", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What was the city, in which Kiyoyuki Yanada born, formerly known as?", "answer": "Edo", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Who was one of the most important producers-directors of the German silent cinema, Maya Deren or Frederic Zelnik ?", "answer": "Frederic Zelnik", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Anderson Silva has been lauded by the current president of what organization?", "answer": "Ultimate Fighting Championship", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "In what city did Isaac Merritt Singer's company use offices in 120 S. State St?", "answer": "Chicago, Illinois", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What type of alcoholic beverage is served at the brewery established in 1634 during the annual festival at Nockherberg ?", "answer": "German beer", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What is the parent company of the non-British airline company for which William Mathew Walsh is CEO? ", "answer": "International Airlines Group (IAG)", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Did writers Milan Kundera and John Berger both live in France?", "answer": "yes", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "AKS Lytham was formed from the merger of King Edwards VII and Queen Mary School and which independent school in Blackpool, Lancashire, England?", "answer": "Arnold School", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "At what age did Natalie Toro debut at the Apollo Theater?", "answer": "five", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Ghazn\u012b, also historically known as Ghazn\u012bn, or Ghazna, is a city in Afghanistan with a population of nearly 150,000 people, it is linked by which 2,200 kilometre two-lane road network circulating inside Afghanistan, connecting the following major cities (clockwise): Kabul, Maidan Shar, Ghazni, Kandahar, Delaram, Herat, Sheberghan, Mazari Sharif, and Puli Khumri?", "answer": "Highway 1", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which member of the Bee Gees Line up was born on 22 December 1949 ?", "answer": "Maurice Gibb", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Spencer List, is an American teen actor, and he made a guest appearance on Bunk'd, an American sitcom that premiered on the Disney Channel, on which date?", "answer": "July 31, 2015", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What actor who played roles in both \"The Manchurian Candidate\" and \"Barney Miller\" also featured in American anthology series \"Police Story\"?", "answer": "James Gregory", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What type of category does Cassiope and Pediocactus have in common?", "answer": "genus", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "How many Bombardier Dash 8's does the airline that operates flights to other communities in Finnmark from Honningsv\u00e5g Airport, Valan have?", "answer": "41", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "The 66th Primetime Emmy Awards were hosted by someone who was born in what year?", "answer": "1973", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What's the NASDAQ ticker symbol of Hostess Brands, maker of the Twinkie cake?", "answer": "TWNK", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "\"Two Dozen and One Greyhounds\" was written by Mike Scully and guest starred Frank Welker as a pet greyhound who was introduced in a special called what?", "answer": "Simpsons Roasting on an Open Fire", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "The song \"9 Piece\" performed by rapper Rick Ross was on the soundtrack of which movie written, directed and produced by Sofia Coppola?", "answer": "The Bling Ring", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What is the name of the site on the largest of the Dodecanese islands in terms of land area and also the island group's historical capital, which has an area of 178.900 km?", "answer": "Lindos", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Gyp Rosetti worked for the boss of which New York Crime Family?", "answer": "Genovese", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "the National Film Award (Silver Lotus Award) for Best Male Playback singer