o worked with Ernest Walton?", "answer": "John Cockcroft", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "How many Academy Awards did the actor, who featured in the film, Stand By for Action win ?", "answer": "three", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "John Campbell, 5th Duke of Argyll retired to a castle located on the shore of what loch?", "answer": "Loch Fyne", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "The 2000 United States Senate election winner later resigned amid what investigation?", "answer": "Senate Ethics Committee investigation", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which  American stand-up comedian featured in Fort Night ", "answer": "Sarah Kate Silverman", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Stark Raving Mad stars which actor who plays Barney Stinson on \"How I Met Your Mother\"?", "answer": "Neil Patrick Harris", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "When did the man overthrown in the Libyan Crisis become the leader of Libya?", "answer": "1969", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which HBO series features an actor who made a movie in 1981 with George A. Romero?", "answer": "Westworld", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What British department store chain is an anchor store in the Mercat Shopping Center in Fife, Scottland?", "answer": "British Home Stores", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What aerospace, defense company produces the Selectable Lightweight Attack Munition?", "answer": "Alliant Techsystems", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "The actress who portrayed Luna Lovegood also starred in an unfinished independent thriller drama based on the true story of who?", "answer": "Archibald Hall", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Where was the Belmont Mast and Skelton Transmitting Station based?", "answer": "Penrith", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Whose orchestra accompanied the First Lady of Song and other singers in a 1967 television special?", "answer": "Nelson Riddle", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What horror film, typically involving a violent psychopath stalking and murdering several people, was Caitlin Gerard in? ", "answer": "Smiley", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Are Mike Ness and Marc Bolan both guitarists?", "answer": "yes", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Are Buckinghamia and Aronia both a genus of shrubs?", "answer": "no", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "How much is spent on the type of whiskey that 1792 Whiskey is in the United States?", "answer": "about $2.7 billion", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Ohrid Summer Festival has a musician who was born 8 December 1974. What is their name?", "answer": "Julian Rachlin", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "In what year was the rapper whose fifth studio album was \"Welcome To Haiti: Creole 101\" born?", "answer": "1969", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Who has the highest scope of profession in Paul Rodgers or Bill Kaulitz", "answer": "Bill Kaulitz", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "The director of Biutiful was born in what year?", "answer": "1963", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Who was born first, Kristina Mladenovic or Lleyton Hewitt?", "answer": "Lleyton Glynn Hewitt", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "In what state does the documentary Brick City take place?", "answer": "New Jersey", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Dead Reign, a zombie apocalypse role-playing game, was published by which publisher who perhaps is best known for its popular, expansive \"Rifts\" series (1990-present)?", "answer": "Palladium Books", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Were the The Incredibles and Beauty and the Beast directed by the same person?", "answer": "no", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Who was born first Karel Reisz or Ralph Nelson ?", "answer": "Ralph Nelson", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Alex Orbison and Roy Orbison Jr are co-presidents of which publishing company?", "answer": "Still Working Music Group", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which newspaper is located in the city known as the \"nest of snakes\"?", "answer": "Novedades", "type": "bridge"}, {"question":