ar?", "answer": "1957", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Who wrote The Unauthorised Biography of David Cameron and a politician?", "answer": "Michael Ashcroft", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "\"The Homecoming of Beorhtnoth Beorhthelm's Son\" takes place during the aftermath of a battle that took place beside what river?", "answer": "River Blackwater", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "A. V. Anand worked for what singer whose first public performance was in 1904?", "answer": "Chembai", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Effingham is a large semi-rural and rural English village in the Borough of Guildford in Surrey, the village has been chosen as the home of notable figures, such as Sir Barnes Wallis who was buried here and who?", "answer": "Toni Mascolo", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Who helped cowrite the song \"Dirt on My Boots\"  and is based out of Nashville, Tennessee?", "answer": "Ashley Gorley", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Garth Fundis produced albums for the country singer who was inducted into the Country Music Hall of Fame in what year?", "answer": "2010", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Academy for Advanced Academics is located in a Florida school district founded in what year?", "answer": "1885", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Balthazar Getty is a member of the family that was heavily involved in what industry?", "answer": "petroleum", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What remembrance day held on April 25 features a riderless horse leading the march?", "answer": "Anzac Day", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What band from Salford has Stephen John \"Steve\" Osborne worked with?", "answer": "Happy Mondays", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Rick Leach and Yaroslava Shvedova played in what sport?", "answer": "tennis", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "The 2014 NCAA Division I Women's Soccer Championship, was the 33rd edition of the tournament, the first round of the tournament began on November 14 and concluded with the College Cup final match a