s the Scottish author died who wrote the novel  Fear Is the Key?", "answer": "2 February 1987", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What was the final race ran by the man won the the men's Great North Run in 2015?", "answer": "2017 IAAF Diamond League 5000 metres", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Luck of the Corpse has cover art from the film directed by whom?", "answer": "Mario Bava", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Joel Meyerowitz taught photography at what privately funded college located in Cooper Square in the East Village neighborhood of Manhattan?", "answer": "Cooper Union", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "The first airline before Empires Airlines was absorbed into Delta Air Lines and was the largest airline in the world until what year?", "answer": "2013", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "How was famous first Hampar Kelikian or Manvel Gamburyan?", "answer": "Hampar Kelikian", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "In Oklahoma, which football team is one of the most successful program since World War ll?", "answer": "The Oklahoma Sooners football program", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "In what city is the headquarters for the company which displayed the Tat Elagante as a concept car in 2007?  ", "answer": "Mumbai", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Who chaired the 27th C\u00e9sar Awards ceremony in which a film written by Jeunet with Guillaume Laurant won the award for the Best Film?", "answer": "Nathalie Baye", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "In what region was a city founded as a polis in 497 BC by colonists from an ancient Greek city on the western coast of Anatolia?", "answer": "Edonis", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Jagmo, born Nels Jacobson, is a US artist and poster art historian born in Chicago in 1949, he has designed posters for live-music venues such as Jimmie Dale Gilmore, an American country singer, songwriter, actor, recording artist and producer, currently living where?", "answer": "Austin, Texas", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Who has had more band members, Babes in Toyland or Something Corporate?", "answer": "Babes in Toyland", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Trent Garrett had a recurring role as Bowie in a series created by who ?", "answer": "Terri Minsky", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which of the following writers was a professor at the College de France from 1981 to 1993: Yves Bonnefoy or James Agee?", "answer": "Yves Jean Bonnefoy", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Stoked and 6teen creators also produced which series?", "answer": "Total Drama", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Buffalo Bill was a 1944 film with the film actress of what nationality in a supporting role?", "answer": "American", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Who is the director of the film for which Roschdy Zem shared the award for Best Actor at the 2006 Cannes Film Festival?", "answer": "Rachid Bouchareb", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "After the \"Anschluss\" with Nazi Germany, the right-wing paramilitary group in Austria, Ostm\u00e4rkische Sturmscharen, was replaced in Nazi Propaganda by which name? Answer: Ostmark", "answer": "Ostmark", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "James R. Matthews was the running mate of a politician who was a wide receiver for what NFL team?", "answer": "Pittsburgh Steelers", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which NBA head coach hold the record for the most championships won by an athlete in North America?", "answer": "Bill Russell", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which artist is known for the 1989 album Flowers in the Dirt which featured the song My Brave Face?", "answer": "Paul McCartney", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "The composer of the original music score of The Handmaid's Tale was born in what year?", "answer": "1952", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Who has composed the scores for four feature-length films, including 2014's American romantic drama film directed by Josh Boone, based on the novel of the same name by John Green ?", "answer": "Nathaniel Clifford \"Nate\" Wa