ks on cookery appeared in the first series of Market Kitchen?", "answer": "Tana Ramsay", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which is more widespread in nature, Utricularia or Franklinia?", "answer": "Utricularia", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Mikkey Ekko's first-charting material was released on which of Rihanna's albums?", "answer": "Unapologetic", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "The 2015\u201316 Charlotte 49ers women's basketball team represents represents the University located where? ", "answer": "Charlotte, North Carolina, United States", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What year was the star of Proximity, The Outsiders and St Elmo's Fire born in?", "answer": "1964", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which board game was created in Finland, King Oil or Inkan aarre?", "answer": "Inkan aarre", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Between Soundgarden and Flight of the Conchords, which group has more members?", "answer": "Soundgarden", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Which movie stars Jeffrey Byron, The London Connection or The Light in the Forest?", "answer": "The London Connection", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Are Strangers in Paradise and Half Japanese both from the United States?", "answer": "no", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Patrick Miller of Dalswinton, just north of Dumfries, was a Scottish banker, shareholder in the Carron Company engineering works and inventor, he is buried in a tomb against the southern wall of Greyfriars Kirkyard in Edinburgh, in which country?", "answer": "Scotland", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which queen, crowned in 1952 bestowed Caritas Lawrence the recipient of the Order of the British Empire?", "answer": "Elizabeth II", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "This 1992 game for the Atari Lynx that let you play a casino game named after the French word meaning what?", "answer": "little wheel", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What proportion of California residents supported creation of a bioregion and proposed country in western region of North America.", "answer": "One-third", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What job title did both Miranda Hart and some of the actors in Rush Hour have in common?", "answer": "comedian", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which university is a private university, Massachusetts Institute of Technology or University of Missouri System?", "answer": "The Massachusetts Institute of Technology (MIT) is a private research university in Cambridge, Massachusetts.", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Forman Christian College and Rice University, have which university type in common?", "answer": "research", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Anti-Semitism in the 21st Century: The Resurgence and Wrath of Gods, is which genre film?", "answer": "documentary", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "What year did the father of Konstantin Raikin die?", "answer": "1987", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "As of 2011, Rena Effendi is based in a city titled as what ?", "answer": "the city of a thousand minarets", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What does the Challenger 2 have in common with the Challenger 1?", "answer": "British main battle tank", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What is the name of the castle on the coast of Kirkoswald parich that Christina Bruce was born at?", "answer": "Turnberry Castle", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "On what date did the he Maryland 400 repeatedly charge a numerically superior British force?", "answer": "August 27, 1776", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What staff college is located on Aquidneck Island?", "answer": "Naval War College", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Strictly Come Dancing returned for its twelfth series beginning from 7 September 2014, judges include Craig Revel Horwood, an Australian-British dancer, choreographer and theatre director, in which country?", "answer": "United Kingdom", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Warren East is the chief executive officer of a company established in which year ?", "answer": "1904", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Felix Airways Limited, also known as Al Saeeda, is a low-cost airline based in Sana'a, Yemen, it was established in 2008 as a subsidiary of which flag carrier, it  operates scheduled domestic and international passenger flights to destinations in Africa and the Middle East, as well as to Asia and Europe?", "answer": "Yemenia", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What year did the actress and dancer noted as an iconic symbol of the flapper star in a Mal St. Clair film?", "answer": "1926", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Where does the hotel and casino located which launched Mansfield's revue \"The House of Love\"?", "answer": "Paradise, Nevada", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Where is the builder of The V/Line RTL class headquartered?", "answer": "Portland, Oregon", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "When did the marque of brand that the Scion Fuse is part of start?", "answer": "2003", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Who voiced the character of the person who helped Ned Flanders spread the religious belief of creationism in the episode The Monkey Suit ?", "answer": "Harry Shearer,", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which modern day states were a part of the 14th century Turco-Mongol empire?", "answer": "Iran, the Caucasus, Mesopotamia, Afghanistan, much of Central Asia, as well as parts of contemporary Pakistan, Syria, and Turkey", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Who is the vocalist on Skintight and started as a vocalist for Theatre of Tragedy?", "answer": "Liv Kristine", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Of the magazines The Weekly Standard and Viltis which is the lighter read?", "answer": "Viltis", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Scott Kosar is a screenwriter who updated the horror film that was originally released in what year?", "answer": "1979", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What was the seating capacity for the venue in which the 2016 LNB All-Star Game was played?", "answer": "7,000 to 20,300", "ty