n Mulgrave Road and Cairns is a city in the Cairns Region, Queensland are located in what country?", "answer": "Australian", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "I Prevail gained popularity for posting a cover of a Taylor Swift song that is off which of her Albums?", "answer": "1989", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What was the nickname of the Jazz player who retired following the 1990\u201391 Utah Jazz season ?", "answer": "Dr. Dunkenstein", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Lowe has been compared favorably to which English rock band formed in 1980?", "answer": "New Order", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which Canal was constructed during World War II, Middlesex Canal or Cape May Canal?", "answer": "Cape May Canal", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Charles Blake was part of a regiment that was raised in what year?", "answer": "1702", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which of these is a French composer Claude Debussy or Giovanni Paisiello", "answer": "Claude Debussy", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "What is the population of the county in which Jamesburg Park, New Jersey lies?", "answer": "837,073", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "did Walt Disney produce both the The Parent Trap and The Light in the Forest?", "answer": "yes", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "The College of Engineering at the University of Illinois at Urbana\u2013Champaign was first established in 1868,  Engineering at Illinois consistently ranks amongst the top five such engineering colleges in the United States by which American media company that publishes news, opinion, consumer advice, rankings, and analysis, founded as a newsweekly magazine in 1933?", "answer": "U.S. News & World Report", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Do Cara Black and Marin \u010cili\u0107 share the same nationality?", "answer": "no", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "What comedian who died in 1971 appeared in Reaching for the Sun?", "answer": "Billy Gilbert", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Kubilay \"Kubi\