ices such as accepting deposits, making business loans, and offering basic investment products, was established in which city?", "answer": "Tehran", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Who directed the 2015 film starring an American professional poker player?", "answer": "Steven C. Miller", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which cinema at The Centre at Salisbury opened in the space formerly occupied by the defunct mail order and department store retailer, Montgomery Ward?", "answer": "Regal Cinemas", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "The actress that plays  Dr. Allison Cameron in series \"House\" also stars with Matthew Davis in a 2000 slasher film that is a sequel to what movie?", "answer": "\"Urban Legend\"", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Zoya Ivanovna Voskresenskaya, was a Soviet diplomat, NKVD foreign office secret agent and, in the 1960s and 70s, a popular author of books for children, he was born in the Tula what, an administrative division of a country?", "answer": "governorate", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Where was a Belgian variety of hop cultivated, it is used for a type of beer brewed in the Pajottenland region of Belgium southwest of Brussels and in Brussels itself at the Cantillon Brewery?", "answer": "Flemish Aalst-Asse", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What Monteverdi ballet was first performed in Lombardy, Italy? ", "answer": "Il ballo delle ingrate", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Who gave the formal recommendation to recognize Cosimo I of Florence, the second duke, after he defeated a hastily organized army of those wishing to restore the Republic of Florence?", "answer": "Emperor Charles V", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Who composed music for Bombay the Hard Way: Guns, Cars and Sitars and is the recipient of the civilian honour of Padma Shri?", "answer": "Anandji Virji Shah", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which battle, occurring 100 days after the Second Battle of the Marne, went into effect on November 11, 1918 and marked the victory for the Allies?", "answer": "Armistice of 11 November 1918", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which Bengali Indian music director provided assistance in the composition of music to the film Karodpati?", "answer": "Pankaj Mullick", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Who directed more films, Jean Epstein or Felix Basch?", "answer": "Epstein directed three dozen films and was an influential critic of literature and film from the early 1920s through the late 1940s.", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Who did the 2007 Music Broadcaster of the Year host a radio show on BBC Radio 1 with?", "answer": "Edith Bowman", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Esad T. Ribi\u0107, is a Croatian comic book artist, known for his work on various titles for which organization, including \"Loki\", a fictional character appearing in American comic books?", "answer": "Marvel Comics", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which great American architect was the mentor of Carter Manny, creator of many public buildings around Chicago?", "answer": "Frank Lloyd Wright", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Hayley Williams and Ian MacKaye, have which occupations in common?", "answer": "singer, songwriter and musician", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "What was an altercation on November 19, 2004, at The Palace of Auburn Hills in Auburn Hills, Michigan two years before the one between the New York Knicks and Denver Nuggets at Madison Square Garden?", "answer": "Pacers\u2013Pistons brawl", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What is the third-smallest stadium in Major League baseball first housing a Florida team for their 20th season in the MLB/", "answer": "Marlins Park", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "In what specific part of the state is the village that us 1 km north of the gateway to the Southern Highlands?", "answer": "Wingecarribee Shire", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Typhoon Joan was the 25th named storm of a season that had what ACE rating?", "answer": "594.11", "type": "bridge"}, {"question