 is a division record shared with which British former professional boxer who competed from 1986 to 2005?", "answer": "Johnny Nelson", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which star of \"The Man with the Golden Arm\" also starred in the film \"A Christmas Story\"?", "answer": "Darren McGavin", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What famous document of the United States reflects the contributions to classical republicanism and liberal theory of the author of A Letter Concerning Toleration?", "answer": "Declaration of Independence", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which star of the movie \"Home Fries\" has also appeared in \"E.T. the Extra-Terrestrial\"?", "answer": "Drew Barrymore", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Who founded the largest classical ballet company in Australia for which Roma Egan was notably a senior soloist?", "answer": "J. C. Williamson Theatres Ltd. and the Australian Elizabethan Theatre Trust", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What tv show did Sarah Price direct that Will Finn did not?", "answer": "The Carrie Diaries", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "In which city is this university located for which Quincy Acy of the Brooklyn Nets of the National Basketball Association (NBA) played college basketball?", "answer": "Waco, Texas", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "In what comic book did the fictional husband of Sue Dibny, who was murdered by Jean Loring, first appear?", "answer": "\"The Flash\"", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Adam Schmalholz, who performs as IN-Q and IN-Question, contributed to this track for Selena Gomez & the Scene released in which year?", "answer": "2011", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "During the 2015-16 S.S.C. Napoli season, a player of what nationality set a Serie A goal record?", "answer": "Argentine", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Who is older, Dexter Holland or Mark Shaw?", "answer": "Mark Shaw", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "In what region did the Sika deer that are now found on the Tibradden Mountain originate?", "answer": "East Asia", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which English actor, born in 1957 and considered a method actor, starred in the 2009 musical drama film \"Nine.\"", "answer": "Daniel Day-Lewis", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Mordecai Lincoln was the son of Captain Abraham Lincoln, the grandfather of the U.S. president, Abraham Lincoln, and a pioneer settler of what state?", "answer": "Kentucky", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Policital leadership of athens was passed to a decendant of what powerful and historically influential family?", "answer": "Alcmaeonid family", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Who was born first, Kiyoshi Kurosawa or Tom DiCillo", "answer": "Thomas A. \"Tom\" DiCillo (born August 14, 1953) is an American film director, screenwriter and cinematographer.", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "What actress in Innocence was nominated for a Laurence Olivier Award for Best Actress of 2003?", "answer": "Kelly Reilly", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "The church at the north end of the village of Skenfrith, Monmouthshire, Wales is named for what patron saint of Ireland?", "answer": "Saint Brigid of Kildare", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "ORiNOCO was the brand name of wireless networking technology by Proxim Wireless, which was previously an American multinational telecommunications equipment company that was headquartered in Murray Hill, New Jersey, and was established on what date?", "answer": "September 30, 1996", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What is the shared occupation of Donald Cammell and Leopold Wharton?", "answer": "film director", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Where are Psychiatric Institute of Washington and Children's National Medical Center located?", "answer": "Washington, D.C.", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Which Gujarati city is known to be the 3rd \"cleanest city of India\"?  ", "answer": "Surat", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Nevelsk (Russian: \u041d\u0435\u0301\u0432\u0435\u043b\u044c\u044