wer": "Thor", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Independents Day features the rapper and actor from what city?", "answer": "Detroit", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Are the genuses Cyanotis and Syzygium both found in Africa?", "answer": "yes", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "What genre of music was played by the band, formed in 2007, Austin Carlile was lead vocalist for?", "answer": "metalcore", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "The Most Valuable Player of the 2007 Anaheim Classic was drafted in 2008 by which NBA team?", "answer": "Minnesota Timberwolves", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What Dutchman was born in 1585 and had a lunar crater Jansen named after him?", "answer": "Zacharias Janssen", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Where is the club that beat Port Adelaide in 1909 located?", "answer": "Richmond", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which book was the basis for the film which had Dancing in the Dark on its soundtrack ?", "answer": "\"The True Meaning of Smekday", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Cacareco inspired which party in Canada that lasted from the 1960s to the 1990s?", "answer": "Rhinoceros Party of Canada", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Arjay L. Smith is best known for his teenage role on a television series that aired when?", "answer": "1997 to 2000", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Are both Stan Moore and Benjamin Stoloff American?", "answer": "yes", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Kim Eui-sung is a south korean actor who starred in the film Office directed by who?", "answer": "film directed by Hong Won-chan", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "The Kranji War Memorial was dedicated to the men and women who died defending against the invading forces during a war that involved how many people?", "answer": "100 million", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which type of sports car was introduced by Mitsubishi in 1969 and was later imported by Chrysler in the ninties?", "answer": "Mitsubishi GTO", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "The Antioch Mission Baptist Church of Miami Gardens is a Baptist megachurch in a neighborhood that had how many inhabitants in the 2010 census ?", "answer": "61,233", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "what college footaball team played at soldier field for their home games and still went 9-0 for one season", "answer": "University of Notre Dame", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Who directed the first installment in the \"Disney Fairies\" franchise?", "answer": "Bradley Raymond", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Are Petra Kvitov\u00e1 and Oliver Marach of the same nationality?", "answer": "no", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "The city containing the Jinwan District is called what name, being one of China's premier tourist destinations?", "answer": "the Chinese Riviera", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "The town of Riverhead rests on the mouth of which river that drains an area between the Harbor Hill and Ronkonkoma terminal moraines?", "answer": "Peconic River", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What was the name of the nighttime event that ran from 2010-2012 located at a theme park located in Anaheim, California, owned by The Walt Disney Company? ", "answer": "ElecTRONica", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Radiohalos or pleochroic halos are microscopic, spherical shells of discolouration within minerals such as biotite that occur in granite and other igneous rocks, wider interest has been prompted by the claims of a creationist, by Robert V. Gentry, an American young Earth creationist and nuclear physicist, known for his claims that radiohalos provide evidence for a young age of what?", "answer": "Earth", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Evan Buliung played the role of Aragorn in the Toronto production of the most prominent of several theatre adaptations of what kind of book series?", "answer": "epic high fantasy", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "The bassist for Marianas Trench and Alice in Chains share what common first name?", "answer": "Mike", "type": "comparison"}, {