": "Are Lee Daniels and Robert Zemeckis both directors ?", "answer": "yes", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Soviet serial killer, Andrei Chikatilo, nicknamed the Butcher of Rostov, the Red Ripper, and the Rostov Ripper, was depicted in what movie in 1995?", "answer": "Citizen X", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Whitney Avalon released her first parody as the send-up of the CeeLo Green song that was released on what date?", "answer": "August 19, 2010", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What brewery is located in a Trappist monastery and makes a special \"patersbeir.\"", "answer": "Chimay Brewery", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": " One Communications provides Telecommunications services to commercial entities in Burlington, Massachusetts, a town located in what county?", "answer": "Middlesex", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What label released the soundtrack to John Curan's 2006 drama film?", "answer": "Deutsche Grammophon", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What two occupations did Park Subin and Tony Sly have in common?", "answer": "singer, songwriter", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Romeo Brown was a British comic strip published from 1954 to 1962, on which British national daily tabloid newspaper founded in 1903?", "answer": "Daily Mirror", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Jo In-sung stars in the 2017 political crime thriller released in what country?", "answer": "South Korea", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Day of the Dead was written and directed by which American-Canadian filmmaker?", "answer": "George Andrew Romero", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Donald K. Peterson was the former CFO of a multinational telecommunications equipment company headquartered in what state?", "answer": "New Jersey", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What is commonly known as Paris 2024 and were elected during the 131st IOC Session on September 13, 2017?", "answer": "2024 Summer Olympics", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What football club based in Accrington, Lancashire has its home ground at Crown Ground?", "answer": "Accrington Stanley Football Club", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What artist is best known for his design of the former estate of John Shaffer Phipps, heir to the U.S. Steel fortune?", "answer": "George Abraham Crawley", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Kick-Ass is portrayed by which English actor in the feature film adaptations of the same name?", "answer": "Aaron Taylor-Johnson", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What song on the fifth full-length album of the band Voodoo Glow Skulls was originally released in 1973 by The Wailers?", "answer": "I Shot the Sheriff", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which breed of hunting dog can also be used as a water dog, the East Siberian Laika or the Mountain Cur?", "answer": "Mountain Cur", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Which studio album by Malcom McLaren introduced a highly stylized, modern house dance in the late 1980s?", "answer": "Waltz Darling", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": " ROH 13th Anniversary Show took place at a hotel and casino owned by what company?", "answer": "Boyd Gaming", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Benjamin Wallfisch composed the score for a science fiction psychological horror from what year?", "answer": "2016", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "How far did the highway depicted in Bob Waldmire's artwork originally cover?", "answer": "2448 mi", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which state was the 2011 ISAF Sailing World Championships - Star held in?", "answer": "Western Australia", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "what does Jack Horner and Jack and the Beanstalk have in common?", "answer": "Jack", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Frank Little was succeeded as the Archbishop of Melbourne by a former player for which Aussie Rules Football team?", "answer": "Richmond Football Club", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Who wrote the 1986 novel that the 2017 horror movie is based on that features the actor from Hemlock Grove? ", "answer": "Stephen King", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which film starring Ben Kingsley gained Tom Smith his 1982 Academy Award nomination?", "answer": "Gandhi", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Port Adelaide is an electoral district of the House of Assembly, in the Australian state of South Australia,Besides the bulk of the suburb of Port Adelaide, which is shared with Cheltenham, it includes the suburbs of which location, that's a mostly industrial suburb north of Adelaide, containing significant wetlands and a substantial area formerly devoted to salt crystallisation pans, managed by Ridley Corporation, which plans to redevelop the site for housing?", "answer": "Dry Creek", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "The Big Blue is between Sydney FC and another team that competed in the AFC how many times ?", "answer": "on five occasions", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "The 1986 South Antrim by-election included a candidate from which Northern Irish unionist party?", "answer": "Democratic Unionist Party", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What is the new name of the individual who's bags are carried on Ebags.com?", "answer": "Kate Valentine", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What is the area of the country for which Facinet Keita was the flag bearer for the 2012 Summer Olympics?", "answer": "245,860 km2", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Bronco was a program that starred an officer who met which American outlaw in one episodes?", "answer": "Myra Maybelle Shirley Reed Starr", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which alternative/punk band from Moscow has a track called \"The Time of X\"? ", "answer": "Louna", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "When did an American politician and senior United States Senator from Kentucky create an endowed institution?", "answer": "1991", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Riley Jack Tufte was drafted in the first round, 25th overall of a draft held from June 24\u201325, 2016 at what center?", "answer": "First Niagara Center", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Who