", "answer": "Consignment", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Nicolette Ella Fraillon, is an Australian conductor, since 2003, has been Chief Conductor of the Australian Ballet, the largest classical ballet company in Australia, founded in which year?", "answer": "1962", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Oebares was a Persian officer of Cyrus II of Persia, commonly known as Cyrus the Great\u2009 and also called Cyrus the Elder by the Greeks, was the founder of which Empire?", "answer": "menid Empi", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Introduced in the Broadway musical starring Fred and Adele Astaire, the song Oh, Lady Be Good! was written by whom?", "answer": "George and Ira Gershwin", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Blue Picardy Spaniel and Alpine Dachsbracke, are a breed of what?", "answer": "dog", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Satoru Nakamura was a Japanese educator and Scouting leader during what record period of economic growth between post-World War II era to the end of Cold War in Japan?", "answer": "Japanese economic miracle", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "United States Army post, Fort Elliott, was named for a casualty of the Battle of Washita River, which occurred on what day?", "answer": "November 27, 1868", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Jackson Ramsay, is a professional Australian rules football player at the Collingwood Football Club in the Australian Football League (AFL), after the match he was mentioned as one of the outstanding younger players of the team by the coach,  Nathan Charles Buckley, is a former professional Australian rules football player, commentator and coach, best known for his time as captain of the Collingwood Football Club, in which organization?", "answer": "Australian Football League (AFL)", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "The Derry Citizen's Defense Association was organized in response to which police force known as the most dangerous police force in the world?", "answer": "Royal Ulster Constabulary", "type": "bridge"