, "answer": "Harry Dean Stanton", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "The 3s Cable Car was developed by a company in which canton in Switzerland?", "answer": "Bern", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which kind of plant is native to more locations, Chelidonium or Kirengeshoma?", "answer": "Chelidonium", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "At what address did Final Battle 2012: Doomsday take place?", "answer": "311 West 34th Street", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "The town in which the Suncook Lakes is located had a population of what at the 2010 census?", "answer": "4,593", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which large intracratonic sedimentary basin in eastern Montana that uses north dakota pipeline company system to collect oil from its fields?", "answer": "Williston Basin", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Lake Mary Jane is located north of a city in what Florida county?", "answer": "Highlands County", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Wrecking Everything \u2013 An Evening in Asbury Park is a 2002 live DVD by a band that has a notable skeleltal bat mascot named what?", "answer": "Chaly", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What type of profession does Jim Reese and Mary Fallin have in common?", "answer": "politician", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Botanica is a New York based band featured in Greg Pritikin's film \"Dummy\" staring an American actor who won an Academy Award for what 2002 film?", "answer": "The Pianist", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Where did Wayne Simmonds play hockey when he was on his junior team?", "answer": "Brockville, Ontario, Canada", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Kris Tompkins husband gifted land to governments in which continent?", "answer": "South America", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "The 2015 Toronto International Film Festival, the 40th annual Toronto International Film Festival was held from 10 to 20 September 2015, which 2015 drama film directed by Jean-Marc Vall\u00e9e and written by Bryan Sipe, and starring Jake Gyllenhaal?", "answer": "Demolition", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Xavier University ( ) is a co-educational Jesuit, Catholic university in Cincinnati, Ohio, United States. ", "answer": "a co-educational Jesuit, Catholic university in Cincinnati, Ohio, United States.", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "The U.S. Navy admiral nicknamed \"Slew\" married who in 1965?", "answer": "Carol Shepp", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Disappearance of Renee MacRae, Britain's longest running missing persons case, is as notorious as the murder cases of this serial killer involved with how many people? ", "answer": "three", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Mike Edison was the editor-in-chief of which weekly pornographic tabloid newspaper published in the United States aimed at heterosexual men; according to a statement on the cover, it offered \"Jerk-Off Entertainment for Men?", "answer": "Screw", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Buck Rogers: Countdown to Doomsday is a role-playing video game released by Strategic Simulations in 1990 , set in which game setting created by TSR, Inc. in the late 1980s?", "answer": "Buck Rogers XXVC", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Amen is an American sitcom produced by Carson Productions that aired on NBC from 1986, to 1991, set in Sherman Hemsley's real-life hometown of Philadelphia, Hemsley was an American comic actor best known for his role as George Jefferson on which CBS television series, that Hemsley was nominated for a Golden Globe Award and an Emmy Award?", "answer": "The Jeffersons", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What author objects to the name Predator Cities Quartet or the Hungry City Chronicles for the  fourth and final novel in the \"Mortal Engines Quartet\" series?", "answer": "Philip Reeve", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Yang Sze collaborated with Van Damme in a movie directed by who?", "answer": "Sheldon Lettich", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Eileen Sheridan is a perceived associate to a gang in East London known for the murders of what two men?", "answer": "Jack \"the Hat\" McVitie and George Cornell", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Are OneRepublic and Air Traffic both bands from America?", "answer": "no", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Between the Irish Red and White Setter and American Foxhound, which bread of dog is considered to hunt foxes by scent?", "answer": "American Foxhound", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Name Eirik Blod\u00f8ks's wife's name?", "answer": "Gunnhild", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What is the name of the Roller Coaster that shares an area with the Kali River Rapids and is about the Yeti protecting the Forbidden Mountain next to Mount Everest?", "answer": "Expedition Everest", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "The American singer who recorded the 2013 song \"Love More\" signed with what record company in 2004?", "answer": "Jive Records", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What is a professional baseball team in the Negro American League who had a member nicknamed \"Hammer\" who  is a retired American Major League Baseball right fielder who is currently the senior vice president of the Atlanta Braves ?", "answer": "Indianapolis Clowns", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What Soviet-born Dutch-British physicist wrote a paper that described devices that contained just one, two, or three atomic layers?", "answer": "Andre Konstantin Geim", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Are Terence Rattigan and Andr\u00e9 Malraux both writers?", "answer": "yes", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "What is the name of the game written and directed by David Cage, published in February 2010 by Sony Computer Entertainment?", "answer": "Heavy Rain", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "HMAS \"Platypus\" was a submarine depot ship and base ship operated by the Royal Australian Navy (RAN), ordered prior to World War I to support the Australian submarines originally known as just AE1, HMAS \"AE1, was an \"E\"-class submarine of which organization?", "answer": "Royal Australian Navy (RAN)", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which song recorded by the Canadian musician did critics noted First Kiss inspiration came from ", "answer": "\"Summer of '69\"", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Are both Sussex Spaniel and Lakeland Terrier native to England?", "answer": "yes", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Mitchellville, Maryland's Freeway Airport has a collection of planes that includes what type of single-engine plane built by Piper Aircraft?", "answer": "Piper PA-28 Cherokee", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Time's Up! and Crokinole, are which type of entertainment?", "answer": "game", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Which band received a five-album deal with Sony BMG, Bullet for My Valentine or The Life and Times?", "answer": "Bullet for My Valentine", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "When did English rock band New Order record their live album \"Live at Bestival 2012?", "answer": "September 2012", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Katharine McPhee gained fame from working with Susan Marshall in what season of American Idol?", "answer": "fifth season", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What flavor are the puffed cornmeal snacks that is in the line of products put out by Matutano Snack Ventures?", "answer": "cheese-flavored", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "In what year was Josph Campbell's widow born?", "answer": "1916", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What was the 2017 population of the area in which Highgate is located?", "answer": "1.94 million", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Alain Sailhac worked as a chef in a restaurant founded by Sirio Maccioni in what city?", "answer": "New York City", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which novelist was from the US, Randall Jarrell or Louis-Ferdinand C\u00e9line?", "answer": "Randall Jarrell", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "David Lane of The Order encourages white nationalists to move to which 5 states?", "answer": "Washington, Oregon, Idaho, Wyoming, and Western Montana", "type": "bri