le to the third single of an ablum named what?", "answer": "Rated R", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which magazine-Women's Health or Parents- is an international company?", "answer": "Women's Health", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Menahem Golan and John Rawlins, have which mutual occupation?", "answer": "director", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Karma is closely associated with the idea that an aspect of a living being starts a new life in a different physical body or form after each biological what?", "answer": "death", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Roxanne \"Roxie\" Hart is a fictional character originally from the 1927 play \"Chicago\", the playwright, reporter Maurine Dallas Watkins, was inspired by the real-life 1924 murder trials of Beulah Annan,  an American suspected murderer, that died on which date?", "answer": "March 10, 1928", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "The book Diseases of Canaries was written by a man incarcerated at Alcatraz between what years?", "answer": "1942 to 1959", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Komikku Yuri Hime published work from which female manga artist born in Tokyo, Japan?", "answer": "Milk Morinaga", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Pasco County, incorporating Jasmine Estates and the county seat Dade City, is in which U.S. state?", "answer": "Florida", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What was the profession of the man who called Log College's structure very plain in his journal?", "answer": "cleric", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What American novelist born in 1947 has published at least 81 novels?", "answer": "Danielle Steel", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Tula Paulina \"Tulisa\" Contostavlos was a judge on a show created by who?", "answer": "Simon Cowell", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "The winner of the 2014 Macau Open Grand Prix Gold was also the first Indian to win what badminton series?", "answer": "Korea Open Super Series", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which Toronto group share writing credits for \"Lust\", a track on Kendrick Lamar's DAMN album?", "answer": "BadBadNotGood", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What kind of group does Madmen and DC Comics have in common?", "answer": "team", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Who published a book most recently, William Gaddis or Lyudmila Ulitskaya?", "answer": "Lyudmila Evgenyevna Ulitskaya", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Martin Holtzhey died in a city in the southwest of what country?", "answer": "Netherlands", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "American actress Sarah Wright, of the movie American Made, recently co-starred in what NBC sitcom?", "answer": "\"Marry Me\"", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Sumner, New Zealand was named in 1849 in honour of an Archbishop born in which year?", "answer": "1780", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which is an herb, Goldenseal or Afgekia?", "answer": "Goldenseal", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "What year was the first production of the car on which the Megane Renault Sport is based?", "answer": "1995", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "what year was the 2008 electee for a Cheshire constituency represented in the UK Parliament born?", "answer": "1973", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "John \"Jocko\" Willink (September 8, 1971) is an American podcaster, author, martial artist and retired United States Navy SEAL, other notable members of Task Unit Bruiser included which United States Navy SEAL, and  the first SEAL to lose his life in Operation Iraqi Freedom?", "answer": "Marc Alan Lee", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "When was the game starring Altair released for Playstation 3?", "answer": "November 2007", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What state did the winner of the 2008 Utah Democratic Primary represent in the Senate?", "answer": "Illinois", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What is Ofsted outstanding further and higher education college and has the highest number of HE in FE student numbers?", "answer": "Blackpool and the Fylde College", "type": "bridge