, "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What year was the namesake of The Roberto Clemente Museum inducted into the Hall of Fame?", "answer": "1973", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What number album of 8Ball & MJG features Christopher Lee Rios", "answer": "seventh", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Joyce Carman Barkhouse, was a children's writer, of which nationality, best known for writing historical fiction, and is the aunt of Margaret Atwood, a Canadian poet, novelist, literary critic, essayist, inventor, and environmental activist?", "answer": "Canadian", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "At the end of the 2003\u201304 Spanish football season, Rafael Benitez was replaced as manager of Valencia by a manager born in which year ?", "answer": "1951", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Staffordshire helmet was similar to which helmet found during a 1939 excavation?", "answer": "Sutton Hoo helmet", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Bear Paw Ski Bowl is a ski area that draws people from a recreaton area of what tribe? ", "answer": "Chippewa-Cree Tribe", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "The song, \"What the World Needs,\" was written by American singer, songwriter, and producer, Brett James, and cowritten by who else?", "answer": "Holly Lamar.", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which university, Seattle University or California State University, Dominguez Hills, is a Jesuit Catholic university in the northwestern United States?", "answer": "Seattle University", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "What center was founded by the Turkish physicist who hosted one of the winners of the 1961 Nobel Prize in Physics at the University of Miami?", "answer": "Center for Theoretical Studies", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "The daughter of what  actor is an American actress and adult film performer, who is the niece of  an American actor, comedian, singer, dancer, writer, and producer?", "answer": "Jerry Van Dyke", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "In which Parish was the property know as the 'Monk's Garden' located?", "answer": "Kilwinning", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which film was based on adult life events of the composer Giuseppe Verdi, and released theatrically in the USA as The Life and Music of Giuseppe Verdi and on video as Verdi, the King of Melody, is a 1953 Italian biographical film starring Pierre Cressoy and directed by Raffaello Matarazzo?", "answer": "Giuseppe Verdi", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Are Jean M. Auel and No\u00ebl Coward both playwrights?", "answer": "no", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "What year did the third film installment in the series based on a 1990 novel by Michael Crichton release?", "answer": "2001", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Dane DeHaan plays James Dean in Anton Corbijn's biographical drama film written by whom?", "answer": "Luke Davies", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Are both punk rock musicians, Spike Slawson and Greig Nori, from Canada? ", "answer": "no", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "What year was the author of \"On the Basis of Morality\" born?", "answer": "1788", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What is the name of the second book released by Bridget Marquardt's costar in The Telling?", "answer": "The Vegas Diaries: Romance, Rolling the Dice, and the Road to Reinvention", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which man born in Dalmatia ordered Genesius of Rome to denounce Christianity", "answer": "Diocletian", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What country is Dancing on Ice's third listed original HD broadcaster based in?", "answer": "Northern Ireland", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Thomas Jackson Calvert was educated at the school in what English county?", "answer": "Lancashire", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "how is Solenostemon and Pseudocydonia connected?", "answer": "flowers", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "In what year was the actress born who played Melinda Gordon on Ghost Whisperer?", "answer": "1979", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Zhongwei and Nyingchi are both claimed by what country?", "answer": "People's Republic of China", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Fort Wentworth in the southwestern New Hampshire town Northumberland is located at the junction of what two rivers?", "answer": "Upper Ammonoosuc River and Connecticut River", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What is the name of an English rock band who released a song which was a rock opera about a deaf, dumb, and blind boy?", "answer": "The Who", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What city and state was the 1973 film, which starred Gary Kurtz, set?", "answer": "Modesto, California", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "The 1993\u201394 NBA season was the 6th season for the Charlotte Hornets in which organization, the team would soon struggle as Larry Johnson injured his back?", "answer": "National Basketball Association", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "When was the American journalist who investigated  one of those that investigated the current state of our planet  born? ", "answer": "June 3, 1967", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "A crime forum aka internet forum works on what type of fraud?", "answer": "Internet fraud", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Jung Ji-hoon, better known as Rain, starred in which movie directed by Kim Dong-won?", "answer": "R2B: Return to Base", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "The No Taxpayer Funding for Abortion Act bill was introduce by Dan Lipinski and a politician that represents which congressional district?", "answer": "New Jersey 's 4 congressional district", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Were Menno Oosting and Liezel Huber both professional tennis players?", "answer": "yes", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Were the films \"King of the Grizzlies\" and \"Enchanted\" released in the same year?", "answer": "no", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Which band was formed first, Counting Crows or Belle and Sebastian?", "answer": "Counting Crows", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Alan Bock wrote regular columns for which opinion site and news aggregator and fringe site?", "answer": "WorldNetDaily", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Boyle Travers Finniss, John Baker (for only 12 days) and Sir Robert Torrens were the first three Premiers of which Antipodean colony?", "answer": "South Australia", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "The Brink's robbery of 1981 was an armed robbery and three related murders committed on October 20, 1981, which were carried out by six Black Liberation Army members, including Mutulu Shakur, he was a close friend of who?", "answer": "Geronimo Pratt", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What is the name of the animated film co-directed by a Danish Animator who formerly worked at Sullivan Bluth Studios that is based off a graphic novel?", "answer": "Asterix and the Vikings", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What mythology worships the deities/gods: K\u016b, Kanaloa, K\u0101ne, and Lono?", "answer": "Hawaiian mythology", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Do the genera Helianthemum and Magnolia share the same family?", "answer": "no", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "What medium of communication does Oliver Queen and Stephen Amell have in common?", "answer": "television", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "The 11th Hour and City of Water, are which type of film?", "answer": "documentary", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Who are Queens of the Stone Age?", "answer": "American rock band", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which band was formed first, Papa Roach or McFly?", "answer": "Papa Roach", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "When was the company owned by the entrepreneur born on February 24, 1962 founded?", "answer": "January 2001", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which documentary was produced first, The Mouth of the Wolf or Fahrenheit 9/11?", "answer": "Fahrenheit 9/11", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Eccles is a constituency that is in what part of England?", "answer": "Greater Manchester", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Who has received attention from from literary critics in recent years, Shirley Jackson or Edwidge Danticat?", "answer": "Shirley Hardie Jackson", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Which 2015 Chinese comedy film is a remake of Miss Granny and stars the winner of Outstanding New Actress at the Huabiao Awards?", "answer": "20 Once Again", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which singer-songwriter wrote songs influenced by alternative rock as well as country for her album released in 2012?", "answer": "Taylor Swift", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Who was the director of the 2002 motion picture drama which featured John Hiatt's \"Slow Turning\"?", "answer": "John Lee Hancock", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What is the name of this independent municipality that has an area less than 9 km and has the street of Vesterbrogade running through it?", "answer": "Frederiksberg", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What Shin Tae-ra directed film featured former musical theatre actor Kang Ji-hwan?", "answer": "My Girlfriend Is An Agent", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Collegium Hosianum was a center of the Catholic Revival that began with what event in 1545?", "answer": "Council of Trent", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "The soundtrack Movin' with Nancy includes the hit single \"Some Velvet Morning\", a song composed by which American country and pop singer, songwriter, and record producer?", "answer": "Lee Hazlewood", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What top 40 hit was written by the noted \"The Moonshiner\" performer and was covered by many artists including Robert Plant and Johnny Cash?", "answer": "If I Were a Carpenter", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Who directed the 1988 film in which the exterior of the abandoned W.S. Kelly gas station and general store in Cogar can be seen?", "answer": "Barry Levinson", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "John Hughes, was an American film director, producer, and screenwriter, he directed and/or scripted some of the most successful comedy films, including the coming-of-age comedy-drama \"The Breakfast Club\", released in which year, an American coming-of-age comedy-drama film written, produced, and directed by Hughes?", "answer": "1985", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "The Green Corn Rebellion was an act that tried to stop enforcement of enlistement during what war?", "answer": "World War I", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Lew Baker was a close friend of the mob boss who went by what nickname?", "answer": "Old Smoke", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Are Capriccio and La finta giardiniera both operas?", "answer": "yes", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "What year was the action comedy film released in which the voice of the actor known for playing Cousin Oliver in \"The Brady Bunch\" is used one of the four title characters?", "answer": "1990", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "The Bentley Continental Flying Spur shares its platform with a car described by Volkswagen as what ?", "answer": "their \"premium class\" vehicle", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "In which town of Long Island is Rocky Point High School located?", "answer": "Town of Brookhaven", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Who wrote Alambama's Ordinance of Secession after the March 1861 election of Abraham Lincoln? ", "answer": "William Lowndes Yancey", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What fusion genre combining elements of heavy metal and hardcore punk is Noxious Enjoyment a part of?", "answer": "Metalcore", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Are both Jimmie Ross and Jang Hyun-seung Americans?", "answer": "no", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Rose Mary Woods and Harry Robbins \"Bob\" Haldeman both had ties to President Richard Nixon, how long did Rose Mary Woods work for him?", "answer": "was Richard Nixon's secretary from his days in Congress in 1951, through the end of his political career.", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Indian film director AR Murugadoss won Best Director for his film \"Kaththi\", starring which actor in dual roles? ", "answer": "Vijay", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Who won more Drama Desk awards, Ivan Tors or Brothers Quay?", "answer": "Brothers Quay", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Lynn Whitfield played a French Resistance agent in a biographical film in what year?", "answer": "1991", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "When did the coach of the Karachi Kings play South African domestic cricket?", "answer": "1986 to 2001", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "are Rhoicissus and Commidendrum different genus", "answer": "yes", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "James Rhodes is a Marvel Comics character that has appeared in comics related to a fictional superhero created by who?", "answer": "Stan Lee", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "In what Super Bowl game did John Jett win a Super Bowl ring at the Sun Devil Stadium? ", "answer": "Super Bowl XXX", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What job title was held by the person the Rindge communication center was named after?", "answer": "White House Press Secretary", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Who directed the film in which Talitha Bateman played the character \"Teacup\"?", "answer": "J Blakeson", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Question: What is the name of Queen Elizabeth's ll father? answer: King George Vl", "answer": "King George VI", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": " In computing, the FLEX language was developed by a scientist born in which year ?", "answer": "1940", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "The Rangers won the 2003 Scottish League Cup Final thanks to goals from Peter L\u00f8venkrands and an Argentien footballer who was known for what?", "answer": "his speed as a player", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which musician or musical group became popular after appearing on a talent reality show, Vanessa Petruo or Clap Your Hands Say Yeah?", "answer": "Vanessa Anneliese Petruo", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Which artist went by a stage name when preforming Beth Ditto or Ben Jorgensen?", "answer": "Beth Ditto", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "What is the birth date of the actress who costarred in \"King\" with Arjan Bajwa and Nagarjuna Akkineni?", "answer": "4 May 1983", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What short and violent movement in 20th century art is attributed to photographer Friedl Kubelka?", "answer": "Viennese Actionism", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "The Portsmouth Herald covers what area that had a population of 6,204 at the 2010 census?", "answer": "Eliot", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Silent Movie is a 1976 American satirical comedy film co-written, directed by, and starring an American actor, writer, producer, director, comedian, and composer who began his career as a comic and writer for what early TV variety show?", "answer": "Your Show of Shows", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Pet Shop Boys recorded a cover of the Brenda Lee track that was written by whom?", "answer": "Johnny Christopher, Mark James and Wayne Carson", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What clinical study during 1932 and 1972 involving African-American males was documented in a play that won 4 Emmy awards", "answer": "Tuskegee syphilis experiment", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "The Edge of Evolution is by this American biochemist, author, and intelligent design (ID) advocate born in what year", "answer": "1952", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which one of Canada's three Maritime provinces is The Back Bay Formation  a geologic formation in", "answer": "New Brunswick", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "In what year was the pianist that released the album \"Historicity\" born?", "answer": "1971", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "The person who hosted the 2nd IIFA Utsavam Awards Show with Nani received the National Film Award for co-producing \"Bommalata \u2013 A Bellyful of Dreams\" in what year?", "answer": "2006", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which Won Shin-yun film inspired the Sanjay Gupta directed film Jazbaa?", "answer": "Seven Days", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Song for Someone is from what 2014 U2 studio album?", "answer": "Songs of Innocence", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "On February 25, 2017 he lost to Jarrett Hurd for the International Boxing Federation light middleweight world title, the  fight was originally supposed to be a title eliminator for the right to fight Jermall Charlo, an American professional boxer who held the IBF light middleweight title from which year, to 2017?", "answer": "2015", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "The Australian women's national soccer team represents Australia in international women's soccer at the senior level, the team's official nickname is the Matildas, their  best-known bush ballad, that has been described as the country's \"unofficial national anthem\", is titled?", "answer": "Waltzing Matilda", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which magazine was published first, Arthur's Lady's Home Magazine or The Lady?", "answer": "Arthur's Home Magazine", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Hamish & Andy is an Australian comedo duo formed in part by the person whp also won what award for the Most Popular Personality on Australian Television?", "answer": "Gold Logie Award", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What actor played Doug Wilson on the series \"Weeds\" and starred in the television film \"Principal Takes a Holiday\"?", "answer": "Kevin Nealon", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "A Dush-toh is a hair ornament traditionally worn by people of which nation that is a confederacy of several Southeastern Native American tribes?", "answer": "Caddo", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What BET award did the rapper who had a song appear in the video games \"Need For Speed Underground 2\", \"Def Jam Rapstar\" and \"The Hip Hop Dance Experience\" win multiple times?", "answer": "Best Female Hip-Hop Artist", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "When was the band formed with which Erik Ronalso worked with and it's debut album released on 2005?", "answer": "2004", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "The Almost Human game Legend of Grimrock is based on a 1987 video game developed by which company?", "answer": "FTL Games", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Who is the host of the reality television cooking competition where the prize is a head chef position at Pub & Grill? ", "answer": "Gordon Ramsay", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which city is the metropolitan area that contains the Independent School League centered on?", "answer": "Washington, D.C.", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Ashley Riches and Roberto Alagna are what types of operatic singers, respectively?", "answer": "operatic", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Mystery Mansion is a 1983 family film starring an American actor with extensive work as what?", "answer": "a voice actor", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which Georgia city has State Route 317 running through it?", "answer": "Suwanee", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "English actor, Bill Stewart, starred in a 1996 American live-action comedy adventure film based on what? ", "answer": "Walt Disney's animated 1961 movie adaptation of Dodie Smith's 1956 novel \"The Hundred and One Dalmatians.\"", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What film did Aja direct and Desmond Askew star in?", "answer": "The Hills Have Eyes", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Iru Mugan stars the actress who has won which two awards for her work?", "answer": "Filmfare Awards", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Stephen Milne held the record for most games played by a player originaly drafted via the Rookie Draft which was surpassed in 2014 by someone who plays for who?", "answer": "West Coast Eagles", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Leeland Road station is a Virginia Railway Express station located at 275 Leeland Road in Stafford, Virginia, the station serves the Fredericksburg Line and shares the right-of-way with the Northeast Regional, a higher-speed rail service operated by who, in the Northeastern and Mid-Atlantic United States?", "answer": "Amtrak", "type": "bridge"}, {"q