ompany that creates the types of knives that were first used after what period?", "answer": "World War II", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": " I Stole a Million is a 1939 film written by an American author, screenwriter and what?", "answer": "satirist", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What island is represented by the breed of dog that killed Diane Alexis Whipple?", "answer": "the island of Gran Canaria", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What was the population in 2015 of the town nearest to the West Burton power stations ?", "answer": "22,117", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What is the name of the individual who introduces us to a scientist who is credited with the invention of the first capacitor in 1746?", "answer": "Al-Khalili", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Evans Notch and Pinkham Notch, are which type of location?", "answer": "mountain pass", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "During which Chinese dynasty did this Chinese general, statesman and warlord had great influence, who was suspected of spreading rumours about infant-kidnapping by westerners in the late 19th century Korea?", "answer": "Qing dynasty", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "The political magazine, in which David Weigel was a former journalist for, is based in what city?", "answer": "New York City", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "In which city was this group formed that has the musician Patrick Keeler whose unreleased tracks were included in Acoustic Recordings 1998\u20132016?", "answer": "Detroit, Michigan", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "The first single from \"Break Up\", a collaborative album between Pete Yorn and Scarlett Johansson, samples lyrics from a song by the English rock band the Beatles that was written by who?", "answer": "Paul McCartney", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which of the following, Coiba or Nalanda, was an acclaimed \"Mahavihara\", a large Buddhist monastery in the ancient kingdom of Magadha ?", "answer": "Nalanda", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "On which network did Paul Dellegatto get his broadcast meteorology start?", "answer": "CBS", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Do Barbarea and Conradina originate from different countries?", "answer": "yes", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Which  research university did  Josephine Ulrick Poetry Prize moved to from 2001 to 2003 ", "answer": "The University of Queensland", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "what is the nationality of the composer of String Quartet No. 7 ?", "answer": "Czech", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which film starring Emily Watson had its soundtrack shaped by Peter Raeburn?", "answer": "Breaking the Waves", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Who completed Prokofiev's Cello Concertino with a Russian composer born in 1904?", "answer": "Mstislav Rostropovich", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Are Adim Williams and Elio Petri from the same country?", "answer": "no", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "What province is King Saud Medical City in Saudi Arabia in?", "answer": "Riyadh Province", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Were Monte Melkonian and Tatev Abrahamyan both chess players?", "answer": "no", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "What private railway company is based in an Italian city that had a population of 326,799 as of 2015?", "answer": "Ferrotramviaria", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "William Frederick Truax was traded by the Los Angeles Rams to the Dallas Cowboys for a wide receiver who played college football at what university?", "answer": "University of Oklahoma", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "As well as directing, who also had a career as an actor, Michael Dolan or William K. Howard?", "answer": "Michael Dolan", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Which Fox game show did the actor who played the taxi driver hostage from the film collateral go on to host?", "answer": "Fox game show \"Beat Shazam\"", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What is the alcohol content of a beer named after a city in Australia 4 km east of the Inn river?", "answer": "4.9%", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Lynda Bird Johnson Robb\u2019s predessor as the oldest living child of a U.S. President was an ambassador to which county?", "answer": "Belgium", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What is the commonly known name of a German football player who provided the inspiration for a nickname of Fl\u00e1vio S\u00e9rgio Viana?", "answer": "Toni Schumacher", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What is the musical which has \"The Rain in Spain\" based on?", "answer": "Pygmalion", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What year was the rock supergroup formed that included the American guitarist, singer, songwriter, and performer born in 1953?", "answer": "1989", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "The Klansman starred what American singer, dancer, and actress, who was born in 1942?", "answer": "Loletha Elayne Falana", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "  \"There She Goes Again\" is a song by The Velvet Underground which first appeared on their 1967 debut album, \"The Velvet Underground & Nico\", recorded in what year while the group were featured on Andy Warhol's Exploding Plastic Inevitable multimedia event tour?", "answer": "1966", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What is the name of the Finch Family's famous relative who was the senior officer of the Royal Household in the United Kingdom?", "answer": "Lord Chamberlain", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What 1988 American film is directed by Roger Donaldson and casts Elisabeth Shue?", "answer": "Cocktail", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What was the release year of the sequel to the novel that T2 Trainspotting was based on?", "answer": "2002", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which American real-estate holding company that rents out U.S. shopping malls is controlled by the family who have purchased an interest in Manchester United?", "answer": "First Allied Corporation", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Who besides Led Zeppelin has performed at Bath Festival of Blues and Progressive Music?", "answer": "Pink Floyd", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "When was the building that has an American trumpeter whose nickname is Satchmo, Satch or Pops as a featured performer built?", "answer": "1923", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "The author of \"Empress Bianca\" also wrote a 1992 New York Times best selling biography of what princess?", "answer": "Diana, Princess of Wales", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What is the North Indian equivalent to Kapi?", "answer": "Pilu", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What is the birthdate of this decorated American combat soldier of WWII, receiving the Meadl of Honor for valor and who starred in The Cimarron Kid?", "answer": "20 June 1925", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Nickerson Mountain is a mountain located in Carroll County, New Hampshire, in which location of mountains, just south of the White Mountains of New Hampshire, United States?", "answer": "Ossipee Mountains", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Who was the former chairman of a Venezuela-owned American refiner?", "answer": "Nettie Marie Jones", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": " What American mathematician who made fundamental contributions to game theory, differential geometry, and the study of partial differential equations, had a film based on his the life called, A Beautiful Mind?", "answer": "John Forbes Nash Jr.", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which court case took place first, Graham v. Florida or United States v. Windsor?", "answer": "Graham v. Florida", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Abdelhamid Abou Zeid in 2012 took control of an ancient city in Mali, situated 20 km north of what river?", "answer": "Niger River", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which British fortification was a post of passage during a war launched in 1763 by a loose confederation of elements of Native American tribes, primarily from the Great Lakes region?", "answer": "Fort Ligonier", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "While both are musicians; which artist is also a dancer, actor and model, Yang Seung-ho or David Vincent?", "answer": "Yang Seung-ho", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "What female author whose works are known to interpret, critique and comment upon the British landed gentry at the end of the 18th century is related to Eliza, Comtesse de Feuillide?", "answer": "Jane Austen", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "The star of Splatter in also the lead singer for what rock band?", "answer": "Truth Movement", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What is the name of the Pizza chain in Maine, Pat's Pizza or Discovery Zone?", "answer": "Pat's Pizza", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Janis Paige, the actress who starred alongside Wayne Morris in the 1949 film \"The House Across the Street\", was born in what year?", "answer": "1922", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which United States Marine Corps aviator preceded United States Navy Commander Scott Carpenter as one of the first Americans in space?", "answer": "John Glenn", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What other well known movie has the star of Gerald been in?", "answer": "My Big Fat Greek Wedding", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Aurelio's Pizza and Cottage Inn Pizza, are which type restaurant?", "answer": "pizza", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "A Room with a View takes place in what period of British history, that covers the brief reign of King Edward VII?", "answer": "Edwardian era", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "\"UnIndian\" stars an Australian cricketer whose quickest delivery, recorded in a test match, was how fast?", "answer": "161.8 km/h", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What was the name of the professional wrestling tag team composed of Glenn Gilbertti and Alex Wright?", "answer": "The Dancing Fools", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which species of flowering plant is named after a Greek philosopher, Mutisia or Aristotelia?", "answer": "Aristotelia", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "H\u00e1ry J\u00e1nos and Fedora, are which type of dramatic play?