 Streak", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "New Street, a principal thoroughfare and shopping street, and Grand Central shopping centre, are located in what town?", "answer": "Birmingham, England", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What city is home to both Vytenis Jasikevi\u010dius and the National Basketball League?", "answer": "Lithuania", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "in what year did one of the stars of Legal Entanglement win Miss Asia?", "answer": "1990", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Oksana Grishuk had a partnership with an ice dancer who won at the Olympics how many times?", "answer": "two-time", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What collection of papers by a Russian-British social and political theorist appeared in 1969?", "answer": "\"Four Essays on Liberty\"", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What song was released as the lead song of tje black eyed6 peas fith album the e.n.d. and was number 1 in the Billboard hot 100?", "answer": "Boom Boom Pow", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Baknaffek samples a song by the impresario who was of what nationality?", "answer": "English", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Is the Taigan or the Estonian Hound considered a scent hound?", "answer": "Estonian Hound", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Dan in Real Life stars a British-American actor who also played what character on \"Frasier\"?", "answer": "Martin Crane", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Silver Lining was recorded for the film directed by whom?", "answer": "David O. Russell", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Li Fanghua is an editor of what peer reviewed journal of physics?", "answer": "Chinese Journal of Physics", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which musician is older, Wil Francis or Billy Idol?", "answer": "Billy Idol", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Which other name is the crime The Black Mafia is accused of that involves a form of illegal gambling?", "answer": "the numbers racket", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Beady Eye and Minutemen, have