ginal 1995 movie for the film franchise on which Lego Toy Story was based on?", "answer": "Pixar Animation Studios", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Could Cult, the experimental indie rock band from Minnesota released their 10th album in 2010 entitled what?", "answer": "Light Chasers", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What animated creatures were the title characters of the film which was based one of the most frequently performed plays written by William Shakespeare early in his career?", "answer": "seals", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which documentary film was released first, Soldier Girls or The 11th Hour?", "answer": "Soldier Girls", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "A Faust Symphony in three character pictures, was written by Hungarian composer Franz Liszt and was inspired by Johann Wolfgang von Goethe's drama, \"Faust\", a tragic play in how many parts?", "answer": "two", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "P\u0113teris Dzelz\u012btis fought for the Latvian partisans during which armed struggle against Soviet rule that spanned for 1944 until the mid-1950s?", "answer": "Guerrilla war in the Baltic states", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "The head coach of a football team that plays their home games at Gibbs Stadium represents a college with an enrollment of how may students?", "answer": "1,550", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Both The Rubens and Royal Blood produced what type of music?", "answer": "rock", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "When was the English actor who featured in Girls At Sea born ", "answer": "14 January 1926", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "In what American film did Scott Shepherd appear in which starred Jude Law and Catherine Zeta-Jones co-star as psychiatrists?", "answer": "Side Effects", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "The Youth in Music championship is held in the stadium that was built on the site of what former stadium?", "answer": "Hubert H. Humphrey Metrodome", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "McKayla Maroney was part 