s KMRB and KAZN broadcast from?", "answer": "Pasadena", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "The Trip to Italy is a 2014 British comedy film, written and directed by Michael Winterbottom, and is the sequel of Winterbottom's TV series, which 2010 British television sitcom series, starring Steve Coogan and Rob Brydon as fictionalised versions of themselves on a restaurant tour of northern England?", "answer": "The Trip", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": " Lady Augusta Gordon was the fourth illegitimate daughter of a man who was born when?", "answer": "21 August 1765", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Victoria Rooms, Bristol includes a bronze statue of which King of the United Kingdom?", "answer": "Edward VII", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Edward Maya had a international hit based which refrain composed by Azerbaijani musician Eldar Mansurov?", "answer": "Bayat\u0131lar", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What is the 2001 population of the village  where Aquilo hails from? ", "answer": "1,545", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Burt Styler wrote scripts for the CBS television show that was eventually followed by what sequel?", "answer": "Archie Bunker's Place", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Clair Francis Bee, was an American basketball coach, who led the team at which private institution of higher education located in Brooklyn, New York City?", "answer": "LIU Brooklyn", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which Italian composer who wrote 39 operas has the 1833 version of the \"Stabat mater\"", "answer": "Gioachino Antonio Rossini", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Najwan Halimi served as special officer to the founder of which party in Malaysia?", "answer": "People's Justice Party", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which Indian politician served as a Chairperson for the National Advisory Council and is also a widow of a former Prime Minister?", "answer": "Sonia Gandhi", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What is the full name of the artist who recorded Me Enamore?", "answer": "Jos\u00e9 Montserrate Feliciano Garc\u00eda", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "In The Right Stuff, Levon Helm is the narrator, and co-stars as an aeronautical engineer who was highly respected among fellow test pilots, including who?", "answer": "Chuck Yeager", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What film genre are Werner Herzog's Wheel of Time and Dave Chappelle's Block Party an example of?", "answer": "documentary", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Was At Night, They Dance or A Diary for Timothy released first?", "answer": "A Diary for Timothy", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Which Bulgarian-Canadian actress appeared in the drama series \"The Vampire Diaries\" and in the 2007 Canadian drama film \"The Poet?\" ", "answer": "Nina Dobrev", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What Irish businessman and shipbuilder was the managing director and head of the shipbuilding company that built the majority of the ships intended for the White Star Line?", "answer": "Thomas Andrews", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Are The Black Keys and Saint Motel both pop bands?", "answer": "no", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Trevor George Smith Jr., is better known by his stage name Busta Rhymes, is an American rapper, actor, record producer and record executive, Chuck D of which group, gave him his moniker?", "answer": "Public Enemy", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "The Stewart Manor station is one of five stations of the Long Island Rail Road that serve the village of Garden City, New York, Stewart Manor is a village in Nassau County, New York in which country?", "answer": "United States", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What movie starring Park Sang-myun started a trilogy of films about a female gang boss?", "answer": "My Wife Is a Gangster", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Viktor Selyavin is best known for his interpretation of Lensky in  an opera composed by who?", "answer": "Pyotr Ilyich Tchaikovsky", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Irvin Willat and Rowland V. Lee, have which mutual occupation?", "answer": "film director", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Diya Aur Baati Hum was replaced by a romantic drama series that premiered on what date?", "answer": "12 September 2016", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": " Ian Crawford has been a guitarist for the American rock band from what Nevada city?", "answer": "Las Vegas", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "How many acts are there in the opera in which Fran\u00e7ois Le Roux portrayed Pell\u00e9as ?", "answer": "five", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Are either Jean Vigo or Richard Williams American professionals?", "answer": "no", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Who directed a 1944 film starring an actress born June 30, 1917", "answer": "Irving Pichel", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which Northern Irish footballer, who last played for Lisburn Distillery, also played for the club currently managed by David Jeffrey?", "answer": "Aaron Callaghan", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "When was the composer, who remarked on Den Pobedy that \"the song seemed to have turned back the time,\" born?", "answer": "born 12 December 1925", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Z\u00e9 Ramalho Canta Bob Dylan pays homage with which song that was for the soundtrack of the 1973 film \"Pat Garrett and Billy the Kid\"?", "answer": "Knockin' on Heaven's Door", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "By whom is the University where Jerry Wilkerson got his BS accredited?", "answer": "Southern Association of Colleges and Schools.", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Who has more scope of profession, Brandon Wood or Lonnie Wilson?", "answer": "Lonnie Wilson", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "The largest United Methodist congregation in the United States is associated with which school of theology?", "answer": "Saint Paul School of Theology", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "John Hughes, an American film director, producer, and screenwriter, wrote which screenplay, based on his short story \"Vacation '58\"?", 