rey office block that houses a tabloid newspaper that was founded as a successor to what?", "answer": "Daily Herald", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Between P. J. Castellaneta and Oscar Micheaux, who directed more films?", "answer": "Micheaux", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "What other show did co-creator of and actor in Coppertop flop shop win an award for Leading Young Actor?", "answer": "He has won two Young Artist Awards in the Leading Young Actor category for his performances in the comedy film \"National Lampoon's Thanksgiving Family Reunion\" (2003)", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What Shakespearean play is the ABC drama \"Still Star-Crossed\" based on?", "answer": "Romeo and Juliet", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Wang Xuejun is a choreographer for what New York-based entertainment company performing classical Chinese dance?", "answer": "Shen Yun Performing Arts", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What are Bearno's and Gino's East both famous for serving?", "answer": "pizza", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "What is the nationality of the company that sells Disney Dollars ?", "answer": "American", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Ludwig K\u00f6gl was in which 1987 football match held at Prater Stadium?", "answer": "1987 European Cup Final", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which band includes singers Roody Woomble and Rod Jones: Idlewild or Voxtrot?", "answer": "Idlewild", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Who was born on November 23, 1978, and is a member of the American Rock group called The Dead Weather?", "answer": "Alison Mosshart", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What era was the show, in which Peter Sellers co-starred with a French actress, popular during?", "answer": "1960s", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which plant has more species, Barklya or Ajuga?", "answer": "Ajuga", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "How many drafts were included in the year that the Pistons moved to Detroit?", "answer": "14", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "The Parades Commission is composed of seven members, all of whom are appointed by a Minister of the Crown that is accountable to who? ", "answer": "Parliament of the United Kingdom", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "The actor that stars as Joe Proctor on the series \"Power\" also played a character on \"Entourage\" that has what last name?", "answer": "Assante", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "In what year was the band behind the Evil Empire Tour nominated for a Grammy Award for Best Rock Album?", "answer": "2001", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which song from the band with the debut album \"It's About Time\" was the first to be released by a new record label?", "answer": "\"Pom Poms\"", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "In what year was the band whose version of \"Friggin' In The Riggin\" was used as the theme song for Captain Butler formed?", "answer": "1975", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What is the name of former Washington Bullets player Harvey Grant's identical twin brother?", "answer": "Horace Grant", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What was the population in the county as of 2010 census where the Long Beach city located in?", "answer": "187,105", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Anders Morgenthaler and Max Neufeld are both what?", "answer": "film director", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "What year saw the premiere of the television series where Tom McGowan plays a disgruntled fan?", "answer": "2000", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Levance E. Fields played college basketball at the University of Pittsburgh a state-related research university located in what state?", "answer": "Pennsylvania", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Do Razorlight and Joywave play the same genre of music?", "answer": "yes", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Suzuki F10D engine is an inline 4-cylinder 1061cc engine that was developed in India by a manufacturer headquartered in which city ?", "answer": "New Delhi", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "After the execution of which individual did Conneticut repeal capital punishment in 2012?", "answer": "Michael Bruce Ross", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Bruce Van De Velde served as Director of Athletics at which university in Louisiana?", "answer": "Louisiana Tech University", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which retired Danish striker gained fame playing for Vanl\u00f8se IF?", "answer": "Preben Elkj\u00e6r", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Were Walter Lippmann and H. P. Lovecraft both authors?", "answer": "yes", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Who plays a stockbroker in a film that Claire Simpson was an editor for?", "answer": "Charlie Sheen", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "When did the person who was jointly named man of the match with  Gauhar Ali make his One Day debut?", "answer": "13 November 2015", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Were John Derek and Emilio Fern\u00e1ndez both actors and directors?", "answer": "yes", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Collins & Harlan sang songs that presented a stereotyped image of who?", "answer": "Blacks", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "EntropiK is a duo influenced by an English rock band consisting of Guy Garvey, Craig Potter, Mark Potter and Pete Turner who have played together since when?", "answer": "1990", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which novelist was born first, William Golding or Noah Gordon?", "answer": "Sir William Gerald Golding", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "In which country Corporation Street located?", "answer": "England", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Both the songs U.F.O. and Princess of China are on the album Mylo Xyloto from which British rock band?", "answer": "Coldplay", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Are both Name Taken and Jars of Clay American rock bands?", "answer": "yes", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Which genus has more species, Echium or Ptilotus?", "answer": "Ptilotus", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Who has authored mroe books, Stephen King or Clive Cussler?"