"}, {"question": "Where is the plant, which manufactured the British Army's standard rifle from 1895 to 1957, located?", "answer": "Maltby, South Yorkshire", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Sky Track Cycling was a team that included which British jockey and track cyclist?", "answer": "Victoria Louise Pendleton", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which Mexican beer brand is produced by the Modelo brewery, and was the title sponsor for the football stadium at Torre\u00f3n?", "answer": "Corona", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What is the capital where Ahafo Ano South is located?", "answer": "Mankranso", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Who is older, Mark Lanegan or Eric Dover", "answer": "Mark William Lanegan", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "A Snowball and a Caesar are both what type of beverage?", "answer": "cocktail", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": " Jerez de los Caballeros is a town of south-western Spain, also the birthplace of the explorers Hernando de Soto and who?", "answer": "Vasco N\u00fa\u00f1ez de Balboa", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Louise Wener and Deni Hines, are both of which musical occupation?", "answer": "singer", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Who was Taylor Swift addressing in the song \"Should've Said No\"?", "answer": "her former lover", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Estonian Philharmonic Chamber Choir won the grammy Award for Best Choral Performance for two songs by a composer born in what year ?", "answer": "1935", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Aerial skier Li Nina won silver medals and the 2006 Winter Olympics and another Winter Olympics held in what country?", "answer": "Canada", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "The George Bray Neighborhood Center reopened in a ceremony that featured an NBA player who last played for what team?", "answer": "Sacramento Kings", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Who build the ship that sank in the Atlantic Ocean on April 15, 1912?", "answer": "Harland & Wolff shipyard", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Are singers Peter Steele and Sonny Sandoval both lead vocalist of a band?", "answer": "yes", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "In what year did the writer of \"Inescapable\" rise to prominence?", "answer": "1983", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which skyscraper stands taller, 126 Madison Avenue or Empire State Building?", "answer": "The Empire State Building", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Which is a port city on the coast of China in northeastern Hebei province, Xinmi or Qinhuangdao?", "answer": "Qinhuangdao", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Which western Penobscot County town with a population of only 1,246 in 2010 was home to a republican state senator?", "answer": "Etna is a town in Penobscot County, Maine", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": " State Route 96 connects to SR 27 in a town with a population at the 2010 census of what?", "answer": "2,165", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which major mid-20th century film director lived longer, Philip Ford or Julien Duvivier?", "answer": "Philip Ford", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Which band was formed first, Grizzly Bear or Jesus Jones?", "answer": "Jesus Jones", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "What was the nationality of the star of \"Bob\"?", "answer": "American", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Who produced the film in which \"The Borrowers\" lost to at the 1998 Best British Film at the BAFTA awards?", "answer": "Douglas Urbanski and Luc Besson", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Harry James Byart, better known by his former stage name, is what, is an English singer, rapper, songwriter and record producer, and has been favourably received by BBC Radio One's Nick Grimshaw, an English television and radio presenter?", "answer": "Fugative", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What experimental architectural community project based at The Park, in Moray, Scotland is home to thousands of residents from 40 countries?", "answer": "Findhorn Ecovillage", "type": "bridge"}, {"que