ormerly which organization, that is an American Christian music band?", "answer": "News from Verona", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "M. Caldwell Butler is a native of an independent city in Virginia, that is located in the Roanoke Valley, and had what population in the 2010 census?", "answer": "97,032", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Who lived earlier, Ibn Khaldun or Muhammad Baqir Yazdi?", "answer": "Ibn Khaldun", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Which sort of sun was the god that Imhotep was the high priest for associated with?", "answer": "the noon sun", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Lake of Fire is a 2006 documentary film directed by Tony Kaye features, among others, Norma McCorvey, better known by what legal pseudonym? ", "answer": "\"Jane Roe\"", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What position does the winner of the 2010 South American Footballer of the Year play?", "answer": "attacking midfielder", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "In 1701, Jean-Baptiste  was named engraver to what king who reigned for 72 years and 110 days?", "answer": "Louis XIV", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Bill Tung was a Hong Kong actor who played in what crime-action film series directed by Jackie Chan, Stanley Tong, Benny Chan and Ding Sheng?", "answer": "Police Story", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What American sitcom, billed as a spin-off of \"Maude\", shared an actor with \"The Jeffersons\"?", "answer": "Good Times", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Konni was a female black Labrador Retriever belonging to a Russian president born in what year?", "answer": "1952", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Who produced the album that \"My Apocalypse\" is a single on?", "answer": "Rick Rubin", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What year did a French cabaret singer star in a Marcel Blist\u00e8ne film?", "answer": "1946", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "The 2011 Speedwat Grand Prix of Great Britain took place in a stadium that is home to what team? ", "answer": "Wales national rugby union team", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Ed is an NBC television program co-produced by an American television comedian, writer, and producer who hosted a late night television talk show for how long?", "answer": "33 years", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which award was won in 1990, by the scorer of the tying run in game 7 of the 1992 National League Championship ?", "answer": "Rookie of the Year Award", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Question: The opera sometimes called La favola d'Orfeo's original name is L'Orfeo or La scala di seta?", "answer": "L'Orfeo", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Which writer illustrated a Japanese Manga Series which spent 18 weeks at the top of the New York Times Manga Best Sellers list of 2009?", "answer": "Masashi Kishimoto", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "\"The Carpet Crawlers\" is a song from a concept album released by which record label ?", "answer": "Charisma Records", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Who was born first, Antonio Machado or Stella Gibbons?", "answer": "Antonio Machado", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "The song Love Is All I Got was relased by a band who's second album was released in May 2013, what was their second album called?", "answer": "\"Cave Rave\"", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which magazine was founded first, Glamour or Vogue?", "answer": "Vogue", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "What other book did the author of \"Rita Hayworth and Shawshank Redemption\" publish?", "answer": "Skeleton Crew", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Who is known more for their biographical novels, Irving Stone or Elinor Lipman?", "answer": "Irving Stone", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": " Lisa Smith-Batchen was the first American to win  Marathon des Sables a six day marathon that spans how long of a distance?", "answer": "251 km ultramarathon", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which of Jamill Kelly's students ranks as the sixth best pound-for-pound fighter in the UFC? ", "answer": "Daniel Co