 ) (Scottish Gaelic: \"Caisteal Tioram\" , meaning \"dry castle\") is a ruined castle that sits on which tidal island in Loch Moidart, Lochaber, Highland, Scotland?", "answer": "Eilean Tioram", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Who was the actress that overcame breast cancer and played a part in I Know Why the Caged Bird Sings?", "answer": "Diahann Carroll", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Where was theater which The State Theatre is part of located ", "answer": "Victoria, Australia", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What genre of music are Fred Durst and Steven Page a part of?", "answer": "music group", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Which breed was developed in South Africa, Rhodesian Ridgeback or Canadian Eskimo Dog.?", "answer": "The Rhodesian ridgeback", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "On what day aired the last episode of a children's Indian television series starring the Indian actor Keval Vora on SAB TV?", "answer": "4 November 2016", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What is the name of Barbara Tausia footballer husband?", "answer": "Nicolas Anelka", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What was the name of the Osbournes Reloaded host who also is the voice of Hildy Gloom in \"The 7D\"?", "answer": "Kelly Lee Osbourne", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "When did the person that rebuilt the Temple of Minerva Chalcidica rule Rome?", "answer": "from 81 to 96", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which Professor at the University of Hertfordshire in the United Kingdom has written several best-selling popular psychology books and has supervised other British psychologists such as Ciar\u00e1n James O'Keeffe?", "answer": "Richard Wiseman", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "The Renault R.S.16 was driven by the McLaren driver of what nationality?", "answer": "Danish", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Are both the Miniature Pinscher and the Tibetan Mastiff dog breeds which originally come from Europe?", "answer": "no", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "What year w