ich British-American musical screwball comedy horror film did Susan Margaret makes costume design for ", "answer": "The Rocky Horror Picture", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "The single  \"Dangerous Game\" was produced by a man that has sold approximately how many singles in the United Kingdom?", "answer": "21 million", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What country does Kentucky Route 97 and Mayfield, Kentuck have in common?", "answer": "United States", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Who was part of more bands, Kurt Cobain or Keith Buckley?", "answer": "Keith Buckley", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "When was the Emperor of Austria and King of Hungary died who proclaimed December Constitution?", "answer": "21 November 1916", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which film director was born in Utrecht, Jan Kounen or Edgar Reitz?", "answer": "Jan Kounen", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Are two rock bands, Green on Red and The Zolas, both American bands?", "answer": "no", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Rock'n Rollers were shell shaped crisps made by a British company that has been a wholly owned subsidiary of what company since 2006?", "answer": "Tayto", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Do Alexis Ohanian and Naz Edwards work in different fields?", "answer": "yes", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "The Pathfinder Badge is awarded to soldiers who successfully complete pathfinder school at a United States Army base that supports more than how many people on a daily basis?", "answer": "120,000", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": " Deerfoot City has an anchor store that has a headquarters in what Ontario city?", "answer": "Mississauga", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "In what year did the monarch whose flagship was called Griffen become king of Norway ?", "answer": "1483", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What is the name of the 350m high hill and Gustav Arthur Graser and his brother Karl Graser co-founded a social reform settlement?", "answer": "Monte Verit\u00e0", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What mockumentary comedy film featured the original host of \"The Daily Show\"?", "answer": "Pittsburgh", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Are both Pauline Kael and Christa Wolf from critics of artistic works?", "answer": "yes", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "What drummer from the band that sung \"Kryptonite\" was on the album \"All the Right Reasons\"? ", "answer": "Daniel Adair", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What Biblical and Quranic figure was the center of the 2007 Yemen tourist attacks?", "answer": "Queen of Sheba", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "When did the shopping center that's a part of Linacre open?", "answer": "1968", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Wilhelm Wiegand is best known for and his publications involving a man that was King of Prussia beginning in what year?", "answer": "1740", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What NCAA division are the Hartford Hawks in?", "answer": "Division I", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Armando Pontone is an Italian motorcycle racer that races motorcycles, other categories of racing include what?", "answer": "hill climbs, drag racing and land speed record trials", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which leader led the party that abolished Control Council Law No 22 and invaded Poland?", "answer": "Adolf Hitler", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What American actress, singer, songwriter, television personality, starred in \"The Cosby Show\" and has a single called \"Backflip\"?", "answer": "Raven-Symon\u00e9", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What was the population in the 2010 census of the County in which the city of Hogansville is located ?", "answer": "67,044", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "USS \"Elrod\" (FFG-55), an \"Oliver Hazard Perry\"-class frigate, is a ship of the United States Navy named after which Marine, born on September 27, 1905, from Turner County, Georgia?", "answer": "Henry T. Elrod", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Getting Married is a 1978