idge"}, {"question": "Snehaseema was a retelling of the story by the Poet Laureate of which country?", "answer": "Great Britain and Ireland", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "John Williams was a political advisor to a King born in what year ?", "answer": "1566", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Professor Bruce S. Grant is a defender of the teaching of evolution and has criticized creationist Jonathan Wells, an American molecular biologist, author and advocate of the pseudoscientific argument of  what?", "answer": "intelligent design", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Summer Breeze is the fourth album by which American soft rock band?", "answer": "Seals and Crofts", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Straight Arrow Press publishes the entertainment magazine founded in what year by the New York Times Company?", "answer": "1977", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": " Park Hae-jin is best known for his supporting roles in which 2014 South Korean television series?", "answer": "Doctor Stranger", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Who is the brother of the creator, director, and choreographer of the 1986 Broadway play \"Uptown... It's Hot!?\"", "answer": "Gregory Hines", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Are both Peter Bogdanovich and Bob Clark American actors?", "answer": "yes", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "The Franco-Spanish reconquest of Menorca (historically called \"Minorca\" by the British) from its British invaders in February 1782, after the Siege of Fort St. Philip lasting over five months, was an important step in the achievement of Spain's aims in its alliance with France against Britain during the American Revolutionary War, the ultimate result was the devolution of the island to Spain in which treaty, signed in Paris by representatives of King George III of Great Britain and representatives of the United States of America on which date, ended the American Revolutionary War?", "answer": "September 3, 1783", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Roland Riese (born 29 July 1960 in Neuenhaus, Lower Saxony) is a German politician for the Free Democratic Party, FDP, is a liberal and classical liberal political party in Germany, FDP is led by who?", "answer": "Christian Lindner", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which studio produced the 1944 film of the play in which Donna Kane made her Broadway debut ?", "answer": "Metro-Goldwyn-Mayer", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "One of several Elizabethan-themed summits in the area of the Southgate River is named for an English gentleman who is well known for popularising what in Englad?", "answer": "tobacco", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "John Spence was an American diver enlisted in a clandestine group operated by a general whose statue now stands in the lobby of what building?", "answer": "CIA headquarters", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Of the documentary films A Brony Tale and Are the Kids Alright? Which film focuses on the decline of available mental health services?", "answer": "Are the Kids Alright?", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "What actress from The Big Bang Theory wrote The Bronze?", "answer": "Melissa Rauch", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "This American football coach who is partnered with John Lynch and whose father was head coach of Los Angeles Raiders is a part of which Football League?", "answer": "National Football League", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which documentary came first, 10 Questions for the Dalai Lama or Bougainville \u2013 Our Island Our Fight?", "answer": "Bougainville \u2013 Our Island Our Fight", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "The actor that played Peagreen Clock in \"The Borrowers\" also stars with Tom Wilkinson and Miranda Richardson in a 2013 British film directed by who?", "answer": "Amma Asante", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Obama Eksklusif RCTI Bersama Putra Nababan was filmed in what city?", "answer": "Washington, D.C.", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What is the name of the market town in the Metropolitan Borough of Bury that was added to the Rossendale constituency in 1950?", "answer": "Ramsbottom", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Before 2012, who were the Baylor Bears sports rival?", "answer": "Texas A&M Aggies", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which actress played a role in both Half Moon Street and Ghostbusters?", "answer": "Sigourney Weaver", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What religion does Doyle Dykes and Amazing Grace have in common?", "answer": "Christian", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What bands was the producer of Yes Please! with Tina Weymouth the drummer for?", "answer": "Talking Heads and the Tom Tom Club", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Were Dmitri Anosov and Mikhail Kravchuk both mathematician?", "answer": "yes", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "The History of Eric Clapton features him performing with what English rock band that was formed in London in 1963?", "answer": "The Yardbirds", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What year did the movie that starred Sterling Jerins as Judy Warren come out?", "answer": "2013", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "When was the political party, of which David Lewis was national secretary, founded ?", "answer": "1932", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which 2005 horror movie staring Steffany Huckabee was filmed at a closed sanatorium located in southwestern Louisville/Jefferson County, Kentucky?", "answer": "Death Tunnel", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What McMOnagle, Perri & McHugh attorney is notable for representing a hip hop artist with a stage name from a street in South Philadelphia", "answer": "Fortunato Natale Perri Jr.", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which person who had a cameo on Caesar's Hour was born Lucille Fay LeSueur?", "answer": "Joan Crawford", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Who was the blind music director for the film \"Ram Teri Ganga Maili\"?", "answer": "Ravindra Jain", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What were the two fields of study engaged in by a biochemist who taught at a university 