ed in what country?", "answer": "United Kingdom", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Wells Cathedral School is a co-educational independent school located in Wells, Somerset, England, the school is one of the five specialist musical schools for school-age children in the United Kingdom, includes which specialist music school for children, located in the town of Bushey, in which south location?", "answer": "Hertfordshire", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "In between Lydia Zimmermann and William Keighley who was an American stage actor and Hollywood film director?", "answer": "William Jackson Keighley", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Two versions of the song \"Feelin' Alright\" were featured in the 2012 film directed by the director who came to public attention after which 1984 movie?", "answer": "Romancing the Stone", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Have Mark Hennessy and John Corabi both performed with Motley Crue?", "answer": "no", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "A boyar was a member of a system that flourished in medieval Europe between what centuries?", "answer": "9th and 15th", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Who directed the film in which Peter Cornell portrayed Vakidis?", "answer": "Kent Alterman", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "From which country does MTV Africa Music Awards 2014 nominee Diamond Platnumz hail?", "answer": "Tanzania", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "The Australian Department of Education was a department of the Government of Australia charged with the responsibility for national policies and programs to help Australians access quality and affordable childcare; early childhood education, school education, post-school, higher education, international education and academic research, the Minister for Education was which Australian politician who has been the Liberal member for the House of Representatives seat of Sturt since the 1993 election?", "answer": "Christopher Maurice Pyne", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Who is the American professional basketball player that was traded to the Atlanta Hawks?", "answer": "Mookie Blaylock", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "For which team does the professional footballer Alexander Hleb, whose country gained independence in 1991 and whose most popular sport is football closely followed by ice hockey, currently play?", "answer": "BATE Borisov", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What man do both the social-democratic political party in Italy and the Shadow Cabinet of Italy have in common?", "answer": "Walter Veltroni", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Alpheoidea is part of the relative level of a group of organisms that contains what families?", "answer": "families Alpheidae, Barbouriidae, Hippolytidae and Ogyrididae", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What Austrian-born British concert pianist co-founded the Leeds International Piano Competition?", "answer": "Marion Stein", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "The 1956 Sugar Bowl featured the 7th ranked team which was a combination of all intercollegiate athletic teams that play for what school?", "answer": "Georgia Institute of Technology", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "How many Golden Globes did the actress who played Isabelle Wright in episode 3 of season 4 of Glee win for other roles ?", "answer": "four", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "The United States Bullion Depository, often known as Fort Knox, is a fortified vault building located the United States Army post of Fort Knox, in Kentucky south of Louisville and north of where?", "answer": "Elizabethtown", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Have Dean Koontz and Bernhard Schlink both written at least one novel?", "answer": "yes", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "What do The Wild Country and The Greatest Game Ever Played have in common? ", "answer": "film", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Which sovereign state in the Lesser Antilles has a capital of Port Elizabeth? ", "answer": "Saint Vincent and the Grenadines", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "