m that plays its home games at the arena that opened on what date?", "answer": "17 September 1981", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "In what state is the public university whose football team won the 1957 NAIA championship?", "answer": "Kansas", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Are Florian Gallenberger and Jackie Chan both actors?", "answer": "no", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "The castle of John Vaux is located in what country?", "answer": "Scotland", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "This Album Featured the song Shattered and has how many copies sold as of the year 2000?", "answer": "six million", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Lucian Truscott a light infantry division based at which state ?", "answer": "Georgia", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "How many schools does the university where Dan W. Reicher is the Executive Director of the Steyer-Taylor Center have?  ", "answer": "seven", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "In what year was the author of \"Omnipotent Government: The Rise of the Total State and Total War\" born?", "answer": "1881", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "According to the 2010 census, which city has a larger population, Yushu City, Qinghai or Nanping?", "answer": "Nanping", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "The winner of season 11 of the US \"The Voice\" received how much as a cash prize?", "answer": "US$100,000", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What United States military branch prevailed in the battle after which the Midway Glacier is named?", "answer": "Navy", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": " \"Fat Tony\" D'Amico hires Bart to work as bartender in what animated sitcom?", "answer": "The Simpsons", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Khabur ware was named after the region in which what British archaeologist found a large quantity of it?", "answer": "Sir Max Edgar Lucien Mallowan", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Trump Steaks were initially sold through QVC and a brand whose licensing is owned by what company?", "answer": "ThreeSixty Group, Inc", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Dialogues of the Carmelites was an opera that had a libretto by which French composer and pianist?", "answer": "Francis Jean Marcel Poulenc", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Leon Plantinga is the brother of which analytic philosopher?", "answer": "Alvin Plantinga", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What is the nationality of the author of \"Island\"?", "answer": "English", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": " \"Mother Knows Best\" is a musical theatre-inspired pop and jazz ballad performed a singer born in which year ?", "answer": "1959", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "In what year did Luke Greenfield produce an American romantic comedy film about a high school senior who falls in love for the first time with the firl next door?", "answer": "2004", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "B&H most commonly refers to which organization, founded in 1973, and the largest photo and video equipment store in the United States?", "answer": "B&H Photo Video", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What movie did the actress best known for being one of the most popular child film stars of the 1930s star in?", "answer": "Danger Street", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Who sings for their main band, Anette Olzon or Brian Welch?", "answer": "Brian Philip Welch", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "The Case for Democracy is a foreign policy manifesto written by one-time Soviet political prisoner and former Israeli Member of the Knesset, Natan Sharansky and co-authored by what former Isreali ambassador to the United States?", "answer": "Ron Dermer", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which of John David Marks's song was first recorded by Berry in 1958 and released as a single on Chess Records?", "answer": "Run Rudolph Run", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which war hero starred in Gunsmoke along with Susan Cabot?", "answer": "Audie Murphy", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "The Secret Garden was written by which keyboardist for the 1970s band Heatwav