le", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Nike Hypervenom is endorsed/worn by a professional footballer who plays for the Algeria national team, and what Premier League club?", "answer": "Leicester City", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What was the nationality of the person who wrote Variations on a Theme by Tchaikovsky?", "answer": "Russian", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "The birth city of Temoer Terry was named after what Union general?", "answer": "James Birdseye McPherson", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Both Deschampsia and Wigandia are what classification level?", "answer": "genus", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Where is the supermarket chain started by Joseph E. Grosberg now headquartered?", "answer": "Downtown Schenectady", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which was a documentary film distributed by HBO, Thin or Congo River, Beyond Darkness?", "answer": "Thin", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Who developed a first-person shooter sports video game for the PlayStation 4 console and its virtual reality head-mounted display  known by the codename Project Morpheus during development?", "answer": "Guerrilla Cambridge", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What did Pseudo-Ingulf write that is an important primary source for English medieval history, particularly the late 15th century?", "answer": "Croyland Chronicle", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which English novelist published an anthology in 1981?", "answer": "Kingsley Amis", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "White Dwarf is a publication that advertises which producer of Warhammer 40,000 game products?", "answer": "Citadel Miniatures", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Who directed more films, Guy Hamilton or Ulli Lommel?", "answer": "Ulli Lommel", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "The Cheeseburger song \"Comin' Home\" was used as the theme song for a tv series that first aired on what date? ", "answer": "May 13, 2007", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Bhagat Ram Talwar was a comrade of the natio