": "Greece", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What was the previous name of the newspaper that Poynter Institute owns?", "answer": "St. Petersburg Times", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which alternative rock band, The Cinematics or Cloud Control has released more albums?", "answer": "The Cinematics", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "The person who presented Mary Queen of Shops television series was appointed by who to lead a review into the future of Britain's high streets?", "answer": "David Cameron", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Shubhendra Shankar, also known as Shubho Shankar, was a graphic artist, musician and composer, he was the son and the eldest child of renowned musicians Ravi Shankar and Annapurna Devi, an Indian surbahar (bass sitar) player of which type of music?", "answer": "Hindustani Classical Music", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which has more varieties of beverages, Schweppes or Duke and Sons?", "answer": "Duke and Sons", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "What is Dean Martin's birth name?", "answer": "Dino Paul Crocetti", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What horror film directed by Breck Eisner did Radha Mitchell act in?", "answer": "The Crazies", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which operation was conducted at a test site which began with a 1-kiloton-of-TNT (4.2 TJ) bomb dropped on Frenchman Flat on 27 January 1951?", "answer": "Operation Teapot", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What building located in Saint Paul, Minnesota is listed on the National Register of Historic Places and is the largest, most costly, and most elaborate movie palace in the Upper Midwest?", "answer": "The Hamm Building", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which movie has more producers, Laura's Star or 9?", "answer": "9", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "How many athletes competed in the event the Samsun Golf Course was made for?", "answer": "3,148", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What is the name of the stadium where Mark Mangino coached football prior to being on the coaching staff at Iowa State University?", "answer": "Memorial Stadium", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which actor that appeared in Old Spice commercials was born on July 30, 1968", "answer": "Terry Crews", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Who did a star of This Is My Life play in Star Wars?", "answer": "Princess Leia", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "The park in which Naval Medical Center San Diego is located consists of how many acres?", "answer": "1200", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What game was created by Klaus Teuber and published by Kosmos in German and Mayfair Games in English, The Kids of Catan or Scattergories?", "answer": "The Kids of Catan", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Did Thomas Schlamme and Hobart Henley share the same nationality?", "answer": "yes", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "In which medium published by Rodale Inc. was Clarence Bass mentioned in 2017?", "answer": "Men's Health", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Who directed the romantic comedy written by Habib Faisal?", "answer": "Maneesh Sharma", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Alain Dorval  is best known as the official dub-over artist of an American actor and filmmaker well known for his Hollywood action roles, including what title character of the \"Rocky\" series?", "answer": "Rocky Balboa", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "David A. Goodman is an American writer and producer and a graduate of the University of Chicago, and is the writer for the film based on the Fred Figglehorn YouTube series, released in which year.?", "answer": "2010", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Rose Byrne starred in what 2010 black comedy film?", "answer": "Get Him to the Greek", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "In the season where the Raptors recruit the shortest player to ever play in the NBA, what place did the team finish in the Central Division?", "answer": "third", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What film adaptation did a performer in a 1985 American epic romantic