nd Final for the 2010 AFL finals series which had to replayed after St Kilda and Collingwood drew the match?", "answer": "Yarra Park", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Who was the brother of Tostig Godwinson that overthrew Gruffydd, Rhiwallon, and Bleddyn?", "answer": "King Harold Godwinson", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Team2015 was an initiative set up by the Conservative Party politician who is the current MP for which constituency?", "answer": "Welwyn Hatfield", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Durring what war did an American restaurateur and the owner/operator of a landmark museum and restaurant in New York City, situated at 54 Pearl Street at the corner of Broad Street provide for prisoners held during the seven-year British occupation of New York City ?", "answer": "Revolutionary War", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Who did the 2015 coach of the New York Liberty play most of his NBA career for?", "answer": "the Detroit Pistons", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "The single storey shed mill operated by the Lancashire Cotton Corporation in the 1930s is located in which town in  Greater Manchester, England, on the River Douglas near Bolton and Warrington?", "answer": "Wigan", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "When was the Jewish American mobster died based on who's prosecution Tight Spot movie story was made?", "answer": "June 20, 1947", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "In between Sorry! and Aladdin's Dragons which is a reimplementation of his 1998 game \"Keydom\"?", "answer": "Aladdin's Dragons", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "When was the American actor starred in The Chairman born? ", "answer": "April 5, 1916", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What recorder of I Saw Mommy Kissing Santa Claus starred in The Two Little Bears?", "answer": "Jimmy Boyd", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": " World Wide What? indludes a cameo from this American best known as the co-founder and former chief executive officer and chairman of America Online (AOL) who retired in what year", "answer": "2003", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which mission was completed first, Cos-B or Uhuru?", "answer": "Uhuru", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Which short film was directed by John Sanford and Elaine Bogan for the How to Train Your Dragon franchise?", "answer": "Dawn of the Dragon Racers", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What American actor and comedian, best known for his role as Oscar Madison in The Odd Couple, had an original interview in the program,  Jack Lemmon - A Twist of Lemmon?", "answer": "Walter Matthau", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Who died first Richard Strauss or Pietro Mascagni?", "answer": "Pietro Antonio Stefano Mascagni", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Feinstein's/54 Below has hosted shows by which famous singer who stared in \"Candide\" (1956)?", "answer": "Barbara Cook", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which writer was of German descent, Herbert Achternbusch or Pedro Sienna?", "answer": "Herbert Achternbusch", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Watford Rural is a civil parish in which local government based in Rickmansworth, Hertfordshire, in southern England?", "answer": "Three Rivers District", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which Jeepers Creepers 2 producer is known as a central figure in the New Hollywood wave of filmmaking?", "answer": "Francis Ford Coppola", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which of the Hindi films in which Vijay Prakash gave his voice was directed by Satish Kaushik?", "answer": "Tere Naam", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Does the population of the city of Shangzhi exceed that of Chengde?  ", "answer": "no", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Michael Stich and Chanda Rubin, have which occupation in common?", "answer": "tennis player", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Who published the comics featuring the hero named Baron Mordo, created by Stan Lee?", "answer": "Marvel Comics", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Between Beware of Darkness and Volcano Suns which band was 