ration consoles?", "answer": "Nintendo", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Kim Hyun-seok, is a South Korean film director and screenwriter, she wrote and directed C'est si bon, a South Korean musical drama film, released on February 5, 2015?", "answer": "2015", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which two artists are also featured in the Jay-Z song in which Jeff Bhasker won a Grammy Award for producing?", "answer": "Kanye West and Rihanna", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Are Charlottesville\u2013Albemarle Airport and Tri-Cities Airport located in the same state?", "answer": "no", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Kyle Balda worked on a film part of the \"Desipicable Me\" franchise produced by who?", "answer": "Illumination Entertainment for Universal Pictures", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Can Lachenalia and Saintpaulia be found on the same continent?", "answer": "yes", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Which show premiered first The Living Planet or Life After People?", "answer": "The Living Planet", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Jeju Air is a founding member of the air alliance formed in what month?", "answer": "May 2016", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Did the Valens Aqueduct ever transport water to the city where Kabata\u015f Erkek Lisesi is?", "answer": "yes", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Which airline shares its main base at Kuwait International Airport with Kuwait Airways and Wataniya Airways?", "answer": "Jazeera Airways", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What was Bill Ford's football team nicknamed?", "answer": "Tigers", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Suzy starred the actress who was a sex symbol of what decade?", "answer": "1930s", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Pennsylvania Route 213 (PA 213) is a 6.95 mi state highway in Bucks County, Pennsylvania, it ends in Middletown Township, near the Oxford Valley Mall, a two-story shopping mall, managed and 65%-owned, by which company?", "answer": "Simon Property Group", "type": "bridg