arl Rantzau?", "answer": "Johann Friedrich Struensee", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Dev Negi's latest song is from a film released on what date?", "answer": "29 September 2017", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "The fantasy film \"The Holy Mountain\" was produced by a man that died in what year?", "answer": "2009", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What 4-time NBA MVP announced he was signing with Miami Heat in a live ESPN television special?", "answer": "LeBron James", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Pixie Geldof's mother died of what cause?", "answer": "a heroin overdose", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "In between Chusquea and Bolax which one is endemic to temperate South America?", "answer": "Bolax", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "What state was the author of \"To Die For\" born?", "answer": "Alabama", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "The Lintong District included the sculptures that depicted the armies of which first Chinese emperor?", "answer": "Qin Shi Huang", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "In which format did this type of music retail outlet, such as Bull Moose Music, sell music?", "answer": "gramophone records", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Who directed Rock-a-Doodle and An American Tail animated movies?", "answer": "Don Bluth", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Who founded the predominantly African-American Methodist denomination based in the United States, located at 32 West 123rd Street in Harlem?", "answer": "Rev. Richard Allen", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "The municipality Barbara Borsinger was from had a population of what in 2010?", "answer": "over 18,000", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which album was produced by a topless model as well as one of the most photographed British women of the 1980s?", "answer": "Angel with an Attitude", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Operation Plowshare occurred in what US state?", "answer": "Nevada", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Sha'Keela Saunders was a champion in the event that has been an Olympic event for women since what year?", "answer": "1948", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What year was the opening ceremony flag bearer for the Czech Republic at the 2010 Winter Olympics born?", "answer": "1972", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Ry\u016bichi Hiroki and Yash Chopra, have which mutual occupation?", "answer": "film director", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Pandikona and Alpine Mastiff are both what?", "answer": "dog", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Which American rock band from Newark, New Jersey, active from 2001 to 2013 has James Dewees been involved in?", "answer": "My Chemical Romance", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which band was formed in England, Vib Gyor or Evanescence?", "answer": "Vib Gyor", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Which province or subdivision has a higher population, Ordos City or Deyang?", "answer": "Deyang", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "What McComb, Mississippi-born singer is the subject of the 169th episode of South Park?", "answer": "Britney Spears", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "The Cardinal Knox Centre, is a modernist church associated building located on 383 Albert Street, East Melbourne, Victoria, it is situated next to colloquially known as St Patrick\u2019s Cathedral, officially The Cathedral Church and Minor Basilica of Saint Patrick,  is the cathedral church of the Roman Catholic Archdiocese of Melbourne in Victoria, which country?", "answer": "Australia", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What were the annual revenues of the computer company for which COBOL ReSource is a development and production environment for Unix?", "answer": "$3 billion", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Of which house is this monarch usually considered the last king during whose reign a single coin had the Horndon mint?", "answer": "House of Wessex", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which writer of the BBC sitcom \"Whites\" , also played in the sitcom \"Peep Show\"?", "answer": "Matt King", "type": "bridge"}, 