ison"}, {"question": "Who was a Jewish American mobster that was known as one of the most \"infamous and feared gangsters of his day\" and was also an associate and childhood friend of Harry Schachter or Harry \"Big Greenie\" Greenberg and ended up murdering him along with Whitey Krakow?", "answer": "Bugsy Siegel", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What is the name of this forest on the northwestern flank of Japan's Mount Fuji near Fuji Five Lakes that is known to provide visitors with a sense of solitude?", "answer": "Aokigahara Jukai Forest", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Ercheia subsignata is a species of what of the Erebidae family, it is found in the Republic of Congo, the Democratic Republic of Congo and Gabonese Republic, a sovereign state on the west coast of Central Africa?", "answer": "moth", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Dogspot sells products from brands such as one with undertakes research into the nutritonal requirements of what?", "answer": "dogs and cats", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "The inaugural Daily Sports Women's Tag Team Championship included which MMA fighter on the losing team?", "answer": "Yumiko Hotta", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": " \"ATLiens\" is a song by a hip-hop group formed in which year ?", "answer": "1991", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Unser Mund sei voll Lachens is a church cantata by a composer born in what year?", "answer": "1685", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What frozen food products are sold by the subsidiaries of the National Dairy Development Board in India?", "answer": "frozen vegetables", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What courthouse was built in 1913 in a town established in 1876?", "answer": "Rosebud County Courthouse", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What was the catchphrase of the presenter of the first two episodes for the Eastern Cabaret?", "answer": "Pin back your lugholes", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What is the engine type of the plane in service in AirTran JetConnect?", "answer": "twin-engine", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Judas Kiss is a 1998 American crime thriller film that starred Alan Rickman, and which British actress and screenwriter, and is known for her portrayals of reticent women, often in period dramas and literary adaptations, and playing haughty or matronly characters with a sense of irony?", "answer": "Emma Thompson", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Alpnachstad railway station is the lower terminus of the mountain railway in what country?", "answer": "Switzerland", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "The head coach of The Longhorns in the 1932\u201333 Texas Longhorns men's basketball season was born on what date?", "answer": "February 12, 1904", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Monk starred Tony Shalhoub, Traylor Howard, Jason Gray-Stanford and what American actor born in 1957", "answer": "Ted Levine", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Gunnar Andersson is considered as one of Olympique de Marseille's best strikers, along with a former French professional football player who was named European football of the year when?", "answer": "1991", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Desert Rock Airport is in a town north of what route? ", "answer": "U.S. Route 95", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which disease outbreak of 2002/3 caused 774 reported deaths, the majority being in Hong Kong, as reported by Andrew Brown for CNN?", "answer": "SARS", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "How did the surfer die, who was a member of the Kahanamoku Surf Team, and who was best known for surfing in areas such as one Hawaiian bay who's name means \"reddish water\"?", "answer": "alcohol-related illness", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "In the 19th century, Rhea Springs was inundated when the completion of Watts Bar Dam by the Tennessee Valley Authority, a federally owned corporation in the United States created by congressional charter on May 18, 1933 to provide navigation, flood control, electricity generation, fertilizer manufacturing, and economic development to the Tennessee Valley, a region particularly affected by what historical event?", "answer": "the Great Depression", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which artist-in-residence at the Walt Disney Concert Hall has also worked with Guy Sigsworth?", "answer": "Eric Whitacre", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Who directed the 2006 film in which Sam Jones III played Willie Worsley?", "answer": "James Gartner", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "The Kingdom starred the American actress who had her debut in what 2000 comedy?", "answer": "Dude, Where's My Car", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which non-Swedish actress also starred in The Light Between Oceans?", "answer": "Rachel Weisz", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Was the George W. Bush administration's foreign policy in the Arab world an example of totalitarianism? ", "answer": "the spread of democracy in the Arab world, while highly difficult and involving a long struggle, is a fundamentally just cause, and he writes in support of the George W. Bush administration's foreign policies", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which film was from Britain, Scandalous John or The Watcher in the Woods?", "answer": "The Watcher in the Woods", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Cus D'Amato who developed Peek-a-Boo boxing trained boxers who eventually became members of which Hall of Fame?", "answer": "International Boxing Hall of Fame", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Snowball is a character in what film released in 1999 by Hallmark Films and was shown on TNT?", "answer": "Animal Farm", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Woman's Era and Alt for Damerne, are magazines for which genre?", "answer": "women", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "What year did the film by Jenuse Mohamed starring a winner of 2 Filmfare Awards come out?", "answer": "2015", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "In which century was this colonial province established where Anthony Colve served as Dutch naval captain and the Director-General?", "answer": "