rring an American actor who also starred in what trilogy of horror films?", "answer": "Scream", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Flash - Der Fotoreporter is a 1993 German television series, about a press photographer named Flash, it stars Oliver Tobias Freitag, known professionally as Oliver Tobias, is a Swiss-born film, stage, and television actor and director, based in which location?", "answer": "UK-based", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "The winner of the 1998 Compaq Grand Slam Cup \u2013 Women's Singles was born in what year?", "answer": "1980", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Once Ian Crozier was infected with Ebola Virus Disease, what was his chance or survival?", "answer": "about 50 percent", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Who is the publisher of the American magazine who published a series of comical parodies by Marshall Brickman?", "answer": "Cond\u00e9 Nast", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What year was the song \"Go Now\" released by an early Moody Blues artist?", "answer": "1964", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Akira Kurosawa and Alan Alda, have which occupation in common?", "answer": "screenwriter", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "\"La Folie\" is a 1981 song by The Stranglers, the song makes allusions to Japanese necrophiliac murderer and cannibal Issei Sagawa, also known as Pang, is a Japanese criminal who in which year, while in Paris, murdered and cannibalized a Dutch woman?", "answer": "1981", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Hillary Rodham Clinton served as a United States Senator from New York from 2001, to 2009, she won which United States Senate election in New York was held November 7, 2006?", "answer": "United States Senate election in New York, 2006", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "A Christmas Carol and Otra Pel\u00edcula de Huevos y un Pollo are what kind/ type of movies?", "answer": "animated", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Black Forest, South Australia is bounded by the railway line that is a commuter line in what city?", "answer": "Adelaide", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which artists are responsible for the sculpture permanently installed northwest of Valentine, Texas and about 26 miles northwest of a city in the high desert of the Trans-Pecos, located between the Davis Mountains and Big Bend National Park?", "answer": "Elmgreen and Dragset", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Take All My Loves: 9 Shakespeare Sonnets is a studio album by Rufus Wainwright, features a guest appearance, by which Canadian-American folk-rock singer?", "answer": "Martha Wainwright", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Samuel de Champlain (born on or before August 13, 1574 \u2013 December 25, 1635), \"The Father of New France\", was a French navigator, cartographer, draftsman, soldier, explorer, geographer, ethnologist, diplomat, and chronicler, he founded New France and Quebec City on which date, when  arrived on the ship Don de Dieu, or \"Gift of God\"?", "answer": "July 3, 1608", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "In which air combat did this aviator after whom Sioux Falls Regional Airport was named serve and receive the Medal of Honor for?", "answer": "the Guadalcanal Campaign", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Who did an American lawyer and Democratic Party politician from Helena, Montana run against in an election in Montana that took place on November 4, 1930 ?", "answer": "Albert J. Galen", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What is the birthdate of this American sports interviewer who works for ESPN and hosts Football Sunday on ESPN Radio?", "answer": "August 12, 1972", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Who was the author of a production in which John Fielder voiced the character Piglet?", "answer": "A. A. Milne", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Are both Robert Plant and Klaus Meine a musician?", "answer": "yes", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Durolevum was a Roman settlement in which country, the only surviving mention of it from antiquity appears in the Antonine Itinerary, where it forms part of the Roman equivalent of Watling Street, a route in England and Wales that began as an ancient trackway first used by the Britons, mainly between the areas of modern Canterbury and St Albans using a natural ford near Westminster?", "answer": "Britain", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which supporting cast member of Jiminy Glick in Lalawood was best known for her work on \"Saturday Night Live\"?", "answer": "Jan Hooks", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Who was the English film director, Doug Langway or Ken Russell?", "answer": "Henry Kenneth Alfred", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Which is native to Western China, Petrocosmea or Onoclea?", "answer": "Petrocosmea", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Which university has the most campuses, Southern New Hampshire University or University of Detroit Mercy?", "answer": "University of Detroit Mercy", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "What former leader of the Gracie Humait\u00e1 school in Rio de Janeiro, Brazil, with the help of his father, demonstrated the Ashi-Hishigi in several medias?", "answer": "Royler Gracie", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What Nobel Prize winning British writer who was born in Trinidad, wrote \"A Writer's People: Ways of Looking and Feeling\"?", "answer": "V. S. Naipaul", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "In which prominent Pixar Animation Studios film did James Albert Varney Jr. provide voice acting?", "answer": "Toy Story", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which of the following musicians is known for his falsetto vocals: Thom Yorke or Sa\u00fal Hern\u00e1ndez?", "answer": "Thomas Edward Yorke", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Inc. and Coronet are both what type of publication?", "answer": "magazine", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "On what street that was once home to the Royal Geographical Society, could you one find the Burlington Fine Arts Club?", "answer": "Savile Row", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Songs of the Season is the second Christmas album by an American singer who, since 1985, has recorded 20 studio albums, and charted more than how many singles on the Billboard Hot Country Songs charts?", "answer": "50", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Phil Thornalley is best known for co-writing the song recorded first by which Danish singer?", "answer": "Lis S\u00f8rensen", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What profession do Eric Ambler and Yevgeny Zamyatin have in common?", "answer": "author", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Which Himalayan peak has greater prominence, Sunanda Devi or Gyachung Kang?", "answer": "Gyachung Kang", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "In what year did the sports film that starred Tessa Thompson as Bianca come out?", "answer": "2015", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "\"Unholy Confessions\" is a song by Avenged Sevenfold, from their second album, Waking the Fallen, released on August 26, 2003, by who?", "answer": "Hopeless Records", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "The Mothers of Plaza de Mayo, is a 1985 Argentine documentary film, about which association of Argentine mothers whose children \"disappeared\" during the state terrorism of the military dictatorship, between 1976 and 1983?", "answer": "Mothers of the Plaza de Mayo", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What Bayern Munich player is a team captain and scored during the final 2009-10 DFB-Pokal game?", "answer": "Arjen Robben", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What job do Tod Browning and Norman Tokar have in common?", "answer": "director", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Emma Rigby plays the role of Hannah Ashworth in which long-tunning soap opera?", "answer": "Hollyoaks", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Blanding is a small railroad junction in Illinois, located north of an army depot that was opened in what year?", "answer": "1917", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which actor from the 1973 American film The World's Greatest Athlete also appeared in \"The Mary Tyler Moore Show\" and \"Roots\"?", "answer": "John Amos", "type":