an who began his music career as Mudfoot in The Whooliganz?  ", "answer": "June 18, 2013", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which famous comic book movie universe features the voice of an Irish-American actor who previously did work on \"Agents of S.H.I.E.L.D\"?", "answer": "DC", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Joint Innovation Lab is a venture that includes the state-owned telecom company that is listed on what two stock exchanges?", "answer": "NYSE and the Hong Kong Stock Exchange", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "When was the father of the 6th overall draft for the ClevelandCavaliers in the 2002 NBA draft born? ", "answer": "February 20, 1963", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "How many members are there in the athletic conference that includes the Georgia Bulldogs football team?", "answer": "fourteen", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Pennsylvania Route 51 (PA 51) is a major state highway in Western Pennsylvania, Century III Mall is located on this road, an ailing enclosed shopping mall located in the southern Pittsburgh suburb of West Mifflin, in Pennsylvania, opened in what year?", "answer": "1979", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What city was Camino Palmero inspired by, and The Calling found in?", "answer": "Los Angeles, California", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Colin Hicks & The Cabin Boys were a British rock and roll band, led by Colin Hicks, the younger brother of which English entertainer, regarded as Britain's first teen idol and rock and roll star?", "answer": "Tommy Steele", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Warragamba Power Station is located at the dam that creates what lake?", "answer": "Lake Burragorang", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "University of Washington and Stevens Institute of Technology, are located in which country?", "answer": "United States", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "What year was the route that is a length of about 5320 km, and has the North Wales Expressway as a designated part to it ,extended?", "answer": "2002", 