west game that uses the game system that Alshard uses?", "answer": "\"Full Metal Panic! RPG\"", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "The confucian academy, Dosan Seowan, located in the East Asian country bordered by China to the northwest and Russia to the northeast, was founded by two prominant Confucian scholars, one being known as Yi Yulgok. What was the \"pen\" name of the other founding scholar?", "answer": "Yi Hwang is often referred to by his pen name Toegye (\"Retreating Creek\").", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Marc Zwiebler and Jan \u00d8. J\u00f8rgensen both are players for which sport?", "answer": "Badminton", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Bertha \"Beatrice\" Alexander Behrman, known as Madame Alexander, was an American dollmaker, among her notable creations were which doll of a fictional character and the main protagonist in Margaret Mitchell's 1936 novel \"Gone with the Wind\" and in the later film of the same name?", "answer": "Scarlett O'Hara", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Who was born first, John Corabi or Jason Schwartzman?", "answer": "John Corabi", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Onry Ozzborn has collaborated with a hip hop artist born in 1981 in which state?", "answer": "Minnesota", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which Italian composer was from the earliest time period, Giovanni Battista Pergolesi or Giacomo Puccini?", "answer": "Giovanni Battista Pergolesi", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "What was fifth studio album of Kid Rock with Lonely Road of Faith as the second single?", "answer": "Cocky", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Who art name was a Chinese general and martial artist best known for countering the \"wokou\" pirates during the reign of the then known  Empire of the Great Ming?", "answer": "Xujiang", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "To what does the name of the musical genre which Stan Kenton produces in refer to?", "answer": "development and growth by accumulation", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What Disney Channel show is Chynna Phillips' half-sister known for?", "answer": "So Weird", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Who created the television series in which Madison Wolfe made her television debut ?", "answer": "Nic Pizzolatto", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Who directed the 1963 horror film that starred the man who played Doc Holliday on the TV series \"Maverick\"?", "answer": "Herbert L. Strock", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Patricia Lamond Lawman, was born in Sydney in 1932, she has starred in which Australian program, Graham Cyril Kennedy, an Australian entertainer and variety performer, as well as a personality and star of radio, theatre, television and film?", "answer": "\"In Melbourne Tonight\"", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which hospital, St. Elizabeths Hospital or Howard University Hospital, opened in 1855 as the first federally operated psychiatric hospital in the United States?", "answer": "St. Elizabeths Hospital", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "In the 2001 Pixar Animation film, which Monster is the best friend to top scarer \"James P. Sullivan\", as voiced by Billy Crystal?", "answer": "Mike Wazowski.", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": " Who Jorge Zorreguieta's daughter marry?", "answer": "King Willem-Alexander", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which lake, Lake Mamry or Suraj Tal, is the second largest lake in Poland?", "answer": "Mamry", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Oskar Kokoschka used what style in his painting that features a female Viennese-born composer, author, editor and socialite?", "answer": "oil on canvas", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Who portrayed Barbara Zeisl Schoenberg in \"Woman in Gold\" and who's son lodged claims against the collective body that exercises executive powers in the Republic of Austria?", "answer": "Frances Fisher", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Does the Hokkaido or Segugio Italiano breed of dog come in both short haired and wire haired varieties?", "answer": "Segugio Italiano", "type": "comp