hat Peggy Robertson's 1948 movie is based on?", "answer": "Helen Simpson", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Cari Roccaro is a soccer player from the CDP in what New York county?", "answer": "Suffolk", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Tod James Murphy played for which Oakland, California basketball team?", "answer": "Golden State Warriors", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Byelka was devoped for an aircraft which was a product of what?", "answer": "PAK FA", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which of the Khans of Bollywood was awarded the Padma Shri in 2003?", "answer": "Aamir Khan", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Fuelled by the earlier conflicts of Matthias Corvinus king of Hungary battled which empire during the Battle of Leitzersdorf?", "answer": "Holy Roman Empire", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "On what date did Atco Records release the album where Pantera introduced a groove metal sound?", "answer": "July 24, 1990", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Afterplay is a 2002 one-act play by Brian Friel, it centres on two characters from Chekhov (Sonya from \"Uncle Vanya\" and Andrey from which play by the Russian author and playwright, Anton Chekhov?", "answer": "Three Sisters", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Gerard Way and Raimund Marasigan explored their musical talents in various ways, but did they both write comic books? ", "answer": "no", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "The group that took responsibility for a mass shooting that happened in 1993 blamed it on an event carried out by who?", "answer": "Provisional Irish Republican Army", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "The indigenous peoples group that John H. Kilbuck was a member of live in what two countries?", "answer": "Canada and the United States", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Krasdale Foods is an independent grocery wholesaler which supplies more than how many products to food retailers, including C-Town Supermarkets, a chain of independently owned and operated supermarkets operating in the nort