ow Chow or Lakeland Terrier? ", "answer": "Chow Chow", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Dan Bilzerian was born the same month that Extraction was released. What month was it?", "answer": "December", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which opera, if any,  Venus and Adonis or Bluebeard's Castle has more acts ?", "answer": "Venus and Adonis", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "The head office of the corporation which has formerly been McGraw Hill Financial, Inc. is located in what city?", "answer": "New York City", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What Canadian documentary is about the hobby where participants wear costumes to represent a specific character?", "answer": "Fanboy Confessional", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "In which Indiana town is there a urban planned worker community designed by American architect Howard Van Doren Shaw?", "answer": "East Chicago", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which British film features extra Shane Hart?", "answer": "Hummingbird", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What movie does the Queen of Kollywood and Prabhas star in together? ", "answer": "Chakram", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which game was released first out of Stonehenge and Pictionary?", "answer": "Pictionary", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "In what year was the man that bought a sports franchise from members of the Bruce Norris family in 1982 born?", "answer": "1929", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Who was the subject of the film featured on Python Night, shown on BBC2 on 9 October 1999?", "answer": "Brian Cohen", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Q: What transit system has been open since 1904 and comes to an intersection at Beach 36th Street and Rockaway Freeway in Edgemere, Queens?", "answer": "New York City Subway", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which director is best known for working with film, Charles Crichton or Kinka Usher?", "answer": "Charles Ainslie Crichton", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "How many Grand Slam titles did the winner of the 1980 Avon Championships of Houston win ? ", "answer": "39", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "The Seventh Date of Blashyrkh is black metal band, and which black metal band from Bergen, Norway, founded in 1991 by frontman and bassist Abbath Doom Occulta (Olve Eikemo), first live DVD?", "answer": "Immortal", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What genre of films were the films The Devil Came on Horseback and Comic Book Confidential?", "answer": "documentary film", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Which of the 2016 Georgia Bulldogs football team coach was born in December 23, 1975? ", "answer": "Kirby Smart", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What popular single by Sammy Hagar promoted his nightclub in Cabo San Lucas, BCS, Mexico?", "answer": "Mas Tequila", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Are Encelia and Gleditsia from the same family?", "answer": "no", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "What does the perennial rainforest shrub containing an active alkaloid also found in Voacanga africana and Tabernaemontana undulata induce in large doses?", "answer": "visions", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What influenced the song, written by Ne-Yo, from Rihanna's second studio album?", "answer": "Caribbean roots", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Who plays for Palmeiras and achieves representation from Juan Figer Svirski's organisation?", "answer": "Z\u00e9 Roberto", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Sue-Ann Levy, is a Canadian writer, and was hired by the \"Toronto Sun\", an English-language daily tabloid newspaper published in Toronto, Ontario, in which country?", "answer": "Canada", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What profession does Izu Ojukwu and Fred Savage have in common?", "answer": "director", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Are Anne Rice and V. S. Naipaul both authors?", "answer": "yes", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "The director of a 2015 film based on Austro-Bavarian folklore has collaborated with which screenwriter?", "answer": "Dan Harris", 