d?", "answer": "Gabriel Eduardo \"Gabe\" Saporta", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "In what city was The Making of Me shown?", "answer": "Lake Buena Vista, Florida", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What Scottish singer covered \"The Man Who Sold the World\"?", "answer": "Lulu", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "The Portsmouth Gaseous Diffusion Plant is located in a town that was originally called what?", "answer": "Jefferson", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Who directed the 1991 Australian romantic comedy, starring the daughter of actors Barry and Lindsay Otto?", "answer": "Kathy Mueller", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "The Whip featured what American film actor that appeared in some 250 movies during a 36-year career", "answer": "Wallace Beery", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which magazine had a greater number of founders, Honey or Girlfriends?", "answer": "Girlfriends", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Which Italian sculptor created the sculpture \"Aeneas, Anchises, and Ascanius\" and was also a well known architect and city planner?", "answer": "Gian Lorenzo Bernini", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Calais ( , traditionally ; ] ; Picard: \"Cal\u00e9s\" ; Dutch: \"Kales\" ) is a town and major ferry port in northern France in the department of Pas-de-Calais, of which administrative division of a country that is below prefecture or province?", "answer": "Subprefecture", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Iuty was an ancient Egyptian vizier presumably of the Late New Kingdom whose family tomb made up of bricks was discovered in December 1964 by the Egyptian archaeologist Shafik Farid, in the so-called \"Cemetery of the Nobles\" of Bubastis (Tell Basta), A calcite canopic jar (representing Duamutef) belonging to Iuty\u2019s son, the high-priest of which ,  goddess in ancient Egyptian religion, worshiped as early as the 2nd Dynasty (2890 BCE)?", "answer": "Bastet", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "The man who did the film score for \"Silver Streak\" won 