 (born 20 September 1944) is a former television news presenter, who lived in Adelaide, South Australia?", "answer": "2007", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": " Ruud Janssen is a Dutch Fluxus and mail artist currently living in Breda in the Netherlands, also known informally as what?", "answer": "Holland", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "who was head coach for 2002\u201303 Connecticut Huskies men's basketball team and was inducted into the Basketball Hall of Fame? ", "answer": "Jim Calhoun", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Who is an American supermodel and actress who hosted Project Runway All Stars?", "answer": "Angela Lindvall", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Is Bob Mould or Kendall Schmidt better known for their television career?", "answer": "Kendall Francis Schmidt", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Stock Ticker and Colt Express are what type of games?", "answer": "board game", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Where did the namesake of the Kilby International Awards take part in the realization of the integrated circuit at?", "answer": "Texas Instruments", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Sean O'Neal played Sam Anders in a television show created by which person?", "answer": "Mitchell Kriegman", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Bradshaw Leigh is known for habing recorded for a man who is the child of who? ", "answer": "John Lennon", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What role in the creation of music is filled by both Frank Sinatra and Ed Robertson?", "answer": "singer", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Did Margaret Mead get her PhD at the university Jamaica Kincaid teaches at?", "answer": "no", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "What is the name of the British romantic war drama film shown at The Scoop in June 2008?", "answer": "Atonement", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Are Croton and Chasmanthium in the same family?", "answer": "no", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Which genus has the most species of trees, Mesquite or Ceanothus", "answer": "Ceanothus", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "The man featured in the documentary The Man Who Predicted 9/11 led hundreds out of which tower before its collapse?", "answer": "the South Tower", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Who is an American film director, producer, and writer, Herk Harvey or Sean S. Cunningham ?", "answer": "Sean Sexton Cunningham", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Nuvvila is a film that features music by the director of what nationality?", "answer": "Indian", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "what position did \u00d6mer Toprak play for Borussia Dortmund", "answer": "centre back", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What song by The Les Claypool Frog Brigade appeared as the theme song for a season of an American animated television series plagued by controversy when the Halloween episode depicted \"The Crocodile Hunter's\" Steve Irwin with a stingray lodged in his chest getting thrown out of Satan's Halloween party?", "answer": "\"Whamola\"", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Gunhilda of Denmark is a member of a ruling royal house in Middle Age Scandinavia and England whose most famous king was who?", "answer": "Cnut the Great", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Linghai and Pingdu, are from which country?", "answer": "China", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Which American composer wrote Symphony No. 4, based on the album Heroes by David Bowie?", "answer": "Philip Glass", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which prehistoric period of Mesopotamia were the majority of the remains from found in Tell al-Ubaid?", "answer": "Ubaid period", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What are the German initials of the party that included K\u00e4the Leichter in its rolls?", "answer": "SP\u00d6", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which American author has sold over 600 million copies one of which had a television special of it in 1971?", "answer": "Theodor Seuss Geisel", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Mankiller is a 2017 documentary film directed by Valerie Red-Horse Mohl, concerning the life of Wilma Mankiller, was a community organizer and the first woman elected to serve as chief of which organization?", "answer": "Cherokee Nation", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "WHat job do both  Jake Kasdan and Boris Barnet have?", "answer": "film director", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "The Sleaford, England brewery founded in 1777, now owned by The Bass Maltings, had an annual output of how many barrels by 1877?", "answer": "one million", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Shatner's Raw Nerve has had an appearance by the model and actress who had what nickname?", "answer": "The Queen of Porn", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": " In which film did Miley Cyrus appear with the actor who played Gale Hawthorne in The Hunger Games", "answer": "The Last Song", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What was the nationality of the person being paid tribute to in the single \"Skeptic\"?", "answer": "American", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Who was an  intellectual and diplomat, he held various academic posts and served as a Goodwill Ambassador for UNICEF and President of the World Federalist Movement, Billy Bob Thornton or Peter Ustinov?", "answer": "Sir Peter Ustinov", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Both North Rock and Machias Seal Island are nearest to which U.S. State?", "answer": "Maine", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "John Shakespeare was the son of the husbandman who lived in what Warwickshire town?", "answer": "Snitterfield", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What 2012 sports-drama film directed by Robert Lorenz, and starring Clint Eastwood, which revolves around an aging baseball scout whose daughter joins him on a scouting trip features a real life father-son appearance?", "answer": "Trouble with the Curve", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Bruce Rowland wrote the film score for which 1989 live-action film?", "answer": "Cheetah", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Treviso is a city and \"comune\" that is home to an Italian brand of shoe and clothing manufactured with what?", "answer": "waterproof/breathable fabrics.", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which cemetery in Suffolk County, New York, is the permanent resting place of more 18th and 19th century sea captains that in any other Long Island cemetery?", "answer": "Oakland Cemetery", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "British actor Christian Bale has starred in various films, as well as advertisements and a video game, Bale had a minor role in which 1989 British historical drama film adapted for the screen and directed by Kenneth Branagh, based on William Shakespeare's play of the same name about King Henry V of England?", "answer": "Henry V", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Who directed the documentary that features an American rapper of Korean descent by the name of Jonathan Park?", "answer": "Salima Koroma", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Graham Christopher Stack (born 26 September 1981) is a professional footballer who plays as a goalkeeper for National League club Eastleigh, hehas featured for which professional football club in Bermondsey, South East London, England?  ", "answer": "Millwall Football Club", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What is the title of this 2013 American 3D computer-animated comedy film produced by Pixar Animation Studios that Robert Kondo and Daisuke Tsutsumi were involved with when they opened the project \"The Dam Keeper?\"", "answer": "Monsters University", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "In what political role did the politican who Alistair Beaton worked as a speechwriter for, serve in the Blair Government? ", "answer": "Chancellor of the Exchequer", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Cumbernauld House is on the site of what former edifice in the Park in Cumbernauld?", "answer": "Cumbernauld Castle", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Who was born earlier, John Wetton or Anders Nystr\u00f6m?", "answer": "John Kenneth Wetton", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "The album that 808s & Sax Breaks is a jazz interpretation of was released in what year?", "answer": "2008", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "A Casino pit is an area of a casino, which typically contains tables for games, which casino game is named after the French word meaning, \"little wheel\"?", "answer": "Roulette", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Thin Black Duke is a studio album by which San Francisco-based rock band?", "answer": "Oxbow", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What alternative rock band, Madrugada or Helium, released two full-length albums in 5 years? ", "answer": "Helium", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "What city were the murders committed by the person played by Maxim Gaudette in?", "answer": "Montreal", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What is the birth date of the composer of First Suite in E-flat for Military Band?", "answer": "21 September 1874", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Harrah's & The Linq station is an island platform located between The Linq and a hotel and casino on the Las Vegas Strip that has over 1200 slot machines, and is owned and operated by who?", "answer": "Caesars Entertainment Corporation", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Per Mertesacker plays as a centre back for a professional football club in HIghbury, London, England, that has won how many league titles?", "answer": "13", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Are both Jack Evans and Chester Bennington songwriters?", "answer": "yes", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Which son of George V attended the 1932 Isle of Man race?", "answer": "Prince George, Duke of Kent", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "In what year did the inventor of the mass driver propose a design for a space settlement?", "answer": "1976", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What country did Frederic Thesiger, 1st Viscount Chelmsford serve in from 1909 to 1913?", "answer": "Australia", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Who did Manchester City beat on the day that Swansea City beat Liverpool 1-0 in the 2011-12 season ?", "answer": "Queens Park Rangers", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Who directed this 1986 British biopic starring Gary Oldman and Chloe Webb, which was parodied in The Simpsons episode \"Love Springfieldian Style?\"", "answer": "Alex Cox", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What US state is the KeyArena located in where the Ultimate Fighting Championship holds events?", "answer": "Washington", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What city was founded by a Greek hero and is located on the Mediterranean Sea? ", "answer": "Tyre", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Eat, Pray, Love was turned into a film that was co-written and directed by whom?", "answer": "Ryan Murphy", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "The Big Apple Coaster is located in what state? ", "answer": "Nevada", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Highest Duty: My Search for What Really Matters is a memoir written by a pilot who retired after how many years of commercial service?", "answer": "30", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "The 1991\u201392 Indiana Hoosiers men's basketball team represented Indiana University, their head coach was Bobby Knight, Robert Montgomery Knight, a retired American basketball coach, who was in his which year?", "answer": "21st", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What date did brothers, Peter \"Goosey\" Gusenberg and Frank Gusenberg die?", "answer": "February 14, 1929", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What was the name of the 1985 formed band, Fu Manchu's debut album?", "answer": "No One Rides for Free", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Stuss or Jewish Faro is a card game, a variant of which late 17th-century, French gambling card game?", "answer": "Faro", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Rosie Fellner has starred alonside an actor who won what? ", "answer": "\"Triple Crown of Acting\"", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What other Disney film did the writer of the song performed by singer Idina Menzel in her vocal role as Queen Elsa contribute to?", "answer": "\"Winnie the Pooh\"", "type": "bridge"}, {