ague?", "answer": "Doomsday", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "New York Times Co. v. Sullivan and Strauder v. West Virginia, cases with which organization?", "answer": "United States Supreme Court", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "What country hosted the World Cup that Hussain Ghuloum played in?", "answer": "Italy", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which actor in \"Inherent Vice\" was also in \"Star 80\"?", "answer": "Eric Roberts", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "How many counties are in the named part of Maryland on which the Choptank people historically lived?", "answer": "nine counties", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Icons.com sells merchandise signed by a professional footballer that won UEFA Club Footballer of the Year in 2005 and what other award?", "answer": "Ballon d'Or Bronze Award", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What is the name of this Mexican public company and major retailer in Mexico that competes mainly with H-E-B grocery, along with Walmart Mexico, S-Mart, Chedraui, and Casa Ley?", "answer": "Soriana", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Are Arctotis and Polyscias both types of plants?", "answer": "yes", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "What is the name of the ancient people first described by a Roman historian in his treatise that is adjacent to Prussia?", "answer": "Aesti", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "St James's Palace held the first playing of the wedding anthem of Princess Anne, and though no longer the the principle residence of the monarch, it is still the ceremonial meeting place of what group?", "answer": "the Accession Council", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "L\u00e9o Delibes and Igor Stravinsky, both had which musical occupation?", "answer": "composer", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Which college offers more majors, Western Institute of Technology or University of Maryland, College Park?", "answer": "University of Maryland, College Park", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "In which city was this English new wave and synth-pop band that released the studio album \"Liberty\" formed?", "answer": "Birmingham", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Dansranbilegiin Dogsom was from a country located between which two countries ?", "answer": "China to the south and Russia to the north", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which case was ruled on first Selle v. Gibb or Edwards v. Aguillard ?", "answer": "Selle v. Gibb", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Ngonidzashe Makusha is a sprinter and long jumper who won double at the NCAA championships, what other athlete, born July 1, 1961, also won doublein 1981?", "answer": "Carl Lewis", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Where is the main building of the rebuilt structure that was the subject of the Impending Death located in?", "answer": "Lower Manhattan, New York City", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "The 2006 film directed by Nick Broomfield, known as Ghosts is named in reference to which Cantonese slang term for Westerners or \"ghost man\"?", "answer": "Gweilo", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Are Kim Jong-hyun and Ace Frehley European?", "answer": "no", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": " PartyCasino is an online casino first launched in 1997 under the name Starluck Casino before relaunching again in 2006, the casino offers over 500 games, like which comparing card game between usually several players and a dealer, where each player in turn competes against the dealer, also known as twenty-one?", "answer": "Blackjack", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "One of the stars of the Hunchback of Notre Dame also starred in \"Murphy Brown\" as which character?", "answer": "Jim Dial", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "The Carleton Knights are the sports team of a college that enrolled how many students in Fall 2015?", "answer": "2,014 undergraduate students", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "The song \"Gashina\" was recorded by a South Korea singer that was a member of what group in 2007?", "answer": "Wonder Girls", "type": "bridge"}, {"question"