swer": "Leningrad", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which breed was originally from Brittany, a historical kingdom of France, Old English Terrier or Basset Fauve de Bretagne?", "answer": "Basset Fauve de Bretagne", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "In what country is the university where Frances Andrews is a professor?", "answer": "Scotland", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": " Are the Comx-35 and Sharp MZ both personal types of computers?", "answer": "yes", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "How many rooms does the Rockefeller house that is above the town of Pocantico Hills have?", "answer": "40-room", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "The Mountains-to-Sea Trail (MST) is a long-distance trail, for hiking and backpacking, that runs across North Carolina from the Great Smoky Mountains to the Outer Banks, the trail's western endpoint is at Clingman's Dome, where it connects to the Appalachian National Scenic Trail, generally known as the Appalachian Trail or simply the A.T., is a marked hiking trail in which location?", "answer": "Eastern United States", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which documentary film was released first, Target for Tonight or Greetings from Out Here?", "answer": "Target for Tonight", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Payment on Demand stars an American actress who is regarded as one of the greatest actresses in Hollywood history, and who comes from what ancestry?", "answer": "Welsh", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Who was behind the largest private share sale on record in the initial flotation of a supermarket chain owned by Jardine Matheson Holdings via its Dairy Farm International Holdings subsidiary?", "answer": "Ian Macgregor", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "In what year did the movie for which Laura Weissbecker win the Chinese Huading award for \"best new actress\" released?", "answer": "2012", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Donald Curry, Baron Curry of Kirkharle, served as a chair of this UK registered mutual insurance composite that is based in which region?", "answer": "Warwickshire", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Refugee Boy is a novel written by a British writer born in which year ?", "answer": "1958", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "In what state has both Victoria Williams and Sugarcult resided in?", "answer": "California", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Who received two National Film Awards in Kalankini Kankabati?", "answer": "Sharmila Tagore", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which American Sitcom that aired on CBS featured music created by Adam Merrin?", "answer": "How I Met Your Mother", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which 2005 historical novel deals with a top secret Nazi scientific technological device?", "answer": "The Black Sun", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Rapper Sadat X is named for the third President of Egypt, who was?", "answer": "Anwar Sadat", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which film, The Incredibles or Anaganaga O Dheerudu, is a computer-animated film?", "answer": "The Incredibles", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "The Family of Imran Khan, belongs to a Pashtun tribe which originated where?", "answer": "eastern Afghanistan and northwestern Pakistan", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Umbarra was the Aboriginal elder of  what town in Australia in the Bega Valley Shire?", "answer": "Bermagui", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which American Formula One World Drivers' Champion raced for the Ferrari team at the 1962 Monaco Grand Prix?", "answer": "Phil Hill", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What 19th-century transportation route through central North America did William Bent and his brothers establish a trade buisness along?", "answer": "The Santa Fe Trail", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Family Circle and Avantages, are which forms of publication?", "answer": "magazine", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "An American film and television writer is known for a 1983 British American swashbuckler film that was directed by Peter Yates, and was produced by who?", "answer": "Ron Silverman", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Thomas Warren Muecke, Jr., was an American football quarterback who played seven seasons in the Canadian Football League (CFL), and played college football at Baylor University (BU), a private Baptist university in Waco, in which US state?", "answer": "Texas", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Camp Merritt was named after a Brevet Major General who was the first American Military Governor of which country?", "answer": "Philippines", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "For which 1988 French film directed by Jean-Jacques Annaud, did No\u00eblle Boisson win great recognition?", "answer": "The Bear", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Who wrote the song \"Nothing but Your Love Matters\" and was a part of a trio with his brothers Steve and Rudy?", "answer": "Larry Gatlin", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Joe Pesci played a character based on the nephew of what man known for being a crime Boss?", "answer": "Frank DeSimone", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Hospital Daher is located in the capital of Brazil and seat of government of what area?", "answer": "Federal District", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Who is an american novelist who created The Keep?", "answer": "Jennifer Egan", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "In the year 2016, how many passengers used the airport adjacent to the Kansas City Overhaul Base?", "answer": "11.04 million", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "The English football manager and former player, Teddy Sheringham, is the head coach of this team, which is based in what city?", "answer": "Kolkata", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which magazine covers B movies, Herald, or Castle of Frankenstein?", "answer": "Castle of Frankenstein", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Ibou Touray plays for Which Football Club based in the Kersal area of Salford, Greater Manchester, England?", "answer": "Salford City", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which happened first, the Battle of the Ch'o