ge"}, {"question": "In what country is the priory that Roger de Birthorpe was imprisoned for trespass after a raid on? ", "answer": "England", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What is the difference between the Podenco Canario and the Great Pyrenees?", "answer": "livestock guardian dog", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "What American football defensive tackle for the Tampa Bay Buccaneers who played college football at Oklahoma, was third overall pick in the club's 35th season as a franchise in the NFL?", "answer": "Gerald Keith McCoy Jr.", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "The book Outliers: the story of success, mentions what man who's IQ is between 190 and 210?", "answer": "Christopher Langan", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which island in Germany is home to the seaside resort named Trassenheide?", "answer": "Usedom", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Panthera youngi is known from Choukoutien, northeastern China and Japan, and lived about 350,000 years ago in the Pleistocene epoch, Harington, 1969 suggested that the American lion, the Eurasian cave lion and the large Chinese \"Panthera youngi\" are conspecific, The American lion (\"Panthera leo atrox\" or \"P. atrox\" ) \u2013 also known as the North American lion, Naegele\u2019s giant jaguar or American cave lion \u2013 is an extinct lion of the family Felidae, endemic to which location during the Pleistocene epoch?", "answer": "North America", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What town is considered to be the start of colonization that included the Americas, as well as Upper Canada and Lower Canada?", "answer": "Jamestown, Virginia", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Paranoia 1.0 includes an actor who began acting as what character in \"My Little Girl\"?", "answer": "Arthur", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Who founded a utopian experiment which was inspired by the ideals of a philosophical movement developed in the late 1820s and 1830s?", "answer": "George Ripley", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Enderal: