ove", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Are Laurence Olivier and Aleksandr Ivanovsky both directors?", "answer": "yes", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "What Class II freight railroad line does the Orford Express operate on seasonally? ", "answer": "Montreal, Maine and Atlantic Railway", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Jean Tassy was born on this island?", "answer": "Hispaniola", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Chinese poles are vertical poles on which circus performers climb, slide down and hold poses, a few Chinese pole tricks have been incorporated with pole dancing, Pole dance combines dance and acrobatics centered on which type of pole?", "answer": "vertical", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Are Hoobastank and Julien-K both electronic bands?", "answer": "no", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "When was the tank that The Panzerkampfwagen VII was dropped in favor of completed?", "answer": "late 1944", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What is the nationality of the director of What Happened to Monday?", "answer": "Norwegian", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "USNS \"Lone Jack\" was a Type T2-SE-A1 tanker delivered to a company that its American headquarters in what area?", "answer": "Energy Corridor area", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Ennio Morricone won the BAFTA Award for Best Film Music for two consecutive years. For the second, who is the period-correct music by?", "answer": "Duke Ellington", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What number president was the father of Michael Gerald Ford?", "answer": "38th", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "In which West African capital city is the Invincible Eleven and Majestic Sports Association Inc located?", "answer": "Monrovia", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which \"Please Give\" actress also starred in \"The L Word'?", "answer": "Elizabeth Keener", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Are Haicheng, Liaoning and Nantong in the same country?", "answer": "yes", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "The owner of the rad