ng Griffon?", "answer": "The Wirehaired Pointing Griffon", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "When was the album that \"Wildest Dreams\" was on released?", "answer": "October 27, 2014", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Was either the Tet Offensive or Western Allied invasion of Germany started on a holiday?", "answer": "yes", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "\"Everybody's on the Run\" is a song from an album that was the first studio release since it's frontman departed from Oasis in what year?", "answer": "2009", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "The Cirrus SR22 aircraft was built by a company founded in what year?", "answer": "1984", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which of the following was founded by the Society of Jesus: Ateneo de Manila University or Washington State University?", "answer": "Ateneo de Manila University", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Arrhenius equation was proposed by this  Nobel-Prize winning Swedish scientist who is one of the founders of the science of what?", "answer": "physical chemistry", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "\"Woman Don't You Cry For Me\" was released in what month?", "answer": "November", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Where is the mobile company named Tecno Mobile, who created HiOS, located?", "answer": "Hong Kong", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What fruit, often soaked in a suspension of food coloring, is found on top of a Manchester tart?", "answer": "Maraschino cherry", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "The Apples in Stereo and SafetySuit are both what?", "answer": "rock band", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Which Republican House Representative was defeated by Thad Cochran for a Senate Chair in 2014?", "answer": "Chris McDaniel", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "When did the TV series which showed the episode Nepotism start on NBC ? ", "answer": "March 24, 2005,", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "The New York City Airport that is associated with Shuttle America is located on which New York bays?",