nected to that has 22 episodes in the season she is in?", "answer": "\"Once Upon a Time\"", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "KIM-1 was produced by a semiconductor design and fabrication company that is based in what city in Pennsylvania?", "answer": "Norristown", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which Baltimore Colts defensive end joined Alan Ameche to start the fast-food restaurant chain Gino's Hamburgers?", "answer": "Gino Marchetti", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What political term was coined by a co-owner of the winner of the 1889 Epsom Oaks ?", "answer": "Tory Democracy.", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Are both Lushan City and Qionghai in China?", "answer": "yes", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Danny Brown\u2019s latest studio album is primarily produced by whom?", "answer": "Paul White", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What is the mission of the humanitarian aid and development agency of which Michelle Nunn is the president?", "answer": "fighting global poverty", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Who is the actor in the play Face Value who has had roles on Oz, Awake, and the first Jurassic Park film?", "answer": "B. D. Wong", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "In addition to \"A Minute with Stan Hooper,\" what other tv series was Norm Macdonald known for? ", "answer": "Saturday Night Live", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What is the name of the football team that defeated the Stanford Cardinal 31\u201327 on December 31, 2009 at the Sun Bowl?", "answer": "Oklahoma Sooners", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Name the 2004 telenovela from Mexico that stars Maite Perroni who released a solo album in 2013 titled Eclipse de Luna? ", "answer": "Rebelde", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which university is a land-grant university, Mississippi State University or Quaid-i-Azam University?", "answer": "Mississippi State University", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Rob & Big follows Rob Dyrdek and his best friend with what nickname?", "answer": "Big Blac