nger\", had an English-speaking role in which 2012 film directed by the Wachowski siblings?", "answer": "\"Cloud Atlas\"", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What is Matka?", "answer": "Indian", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Timo Kotipelto and John Waite, are Finnish?", "answer": "no", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Which network aired the American psychological horror drama television series Mike Vogel appeared in?", "answer": "A&E", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "In what country did a popular actress play a role in a film about coming of age?", "answer": "South Indian cinema", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which plant consists of more species and is native to over 7 different countries, Arachnis or Callistephus?", "answer": "Arachnis", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "The american actress Ann Wedgeworth starred in a film originally titled Dragonfly, what was the name changed to? ", "answer": "One Summer Love", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Who directed the comedy film which was written by Tina Fey and based on a book by American parenting educator Rosalind Wiseman?", "answer": "Mark Waters", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Murder on the Waterfront stars an American model and stage and film actress whose brother was what bohemian surrealist?", "answer": "Charles Henri Ford", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Long Hard Road Out of Hell was used in the trailer for which 2001 American film?", "answer": "From Hell", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Of Scott Treleaven and Kelly Reichardt which is American?", "answer": "Kelly Reichardt", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Where is the church in which T. D. Jakes is the bishop located?", "answer": "Dallas, Texas", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "In what year was the man after whom the Reynolds crater on Mars was named born?", "answer": "1842", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What British multinational confectionery company wholly owned by Mondelez International (originally Kraft Foods) since 2010, a