rayed by a 1980-born actor in Criminal Minds?", "answer": "187", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "what does John Huston and The African Queen have in common?", "answer": "film", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "This musician born in 1972, who is a member of the English rock band Beady Eye formed in 2009, first rose to fame in which rock band?", "answer": "Oasis", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Legalize LA was a campaign that centered on a city what an estimated population of what in 2016?", "answer": "3,976,322", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What is the birth date of the actor who reprised his role and acted as a sequel to the original trilogy \"Evil Dead?\"", "answer": "June 22, 1958", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What role did Eugene Mirman play on Delocated?", "answer": "Yvgeny Mirminsky", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Justin Alfond  was elected to replace the Democratic state senator who was born on October 19,1967 in what year?", "answer": "2008", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Where did the team that beat the Penn State Nittany Lions in the 2015 TaxSlayer bowl play their home games?", "answer": "Sanford Stadium", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Were novelists Alfred D\u00f6blin and Nevil Shute both doctors?", "answer": "no", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Who of Karen Carpenter and Alexi Laiho is from farther west?", "answer": "Karen Anne Carpenter", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "What type of curriculum does the high school Lauren J. Fuchs teach for grades nine through twelve ?", "answer": "a college preparatory curriculum", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Were John Bush and Annie Haslam both lead singers?", "answer": "yes", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Which world leader commanded the rebel force that ended the 1994 Rwandan Genocide, and today sponsors the CECAFA Club Cup?", "answer": "Paul Kagame", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Who reversed the Sixth Circuit's decision, paving the way for same-sex marriage to become legal in places like Ohio?", "answer": "U.S. Supreme Court", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Are both Jean Genet and Nicola Black of European decent?", "answer": "yes", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Who directed Soviet biopic film The great Glinka about Russian composer Mikhail Ivanovich Glinka?", "answer": "Lev Arnshtam", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What ski racer won more consecutive World Cup Championships and also won a 1976 Winter Olympic gold medal?", "answer": "Franz Klammer", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "The North Pacific albatross are the most tropical of the albatrosses with two species one of which primarily lives in the Northwestern Hawaiian Islands with an estimated population of how many?", "answer": "2.5 million", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What was the birth date of a wide receiver who played for the 1933-founded football team based in Pennsylvania and who played for the Buccaneers for a total of nine seasons?", "answer": "December 21, 1953", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Did Lloyd Corrigan or Percy Adlon begin working in films first?", "answer": "Lloyd Corrigan", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Don Orsillo is the sports commentator play-by-play announcer for the San Diego Padres on Fox Sports San Diego, Orsillo was the television voice of the Boston Red Sox  from 2001 to 2015, on the NESN (New England Sports Network) is an American regional sports cable and satellite television network, that is owned by a joint venture of which organization?", "answer": "Fenway Sports Group", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "At which market town in England did Boulton's Siding, Sheffield and Lincolnshire Railway all situated in the 1800s?", "answer": "Ashton-under-Lyne", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which Brittish rock band is responsible for the recording of So Far Away and Brothers in Arms?", "answer": "Dire Straits.", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Streets is watching features music from the album, \"Reasonable Doubt\", which is written by which famous rapper?  ", "answer": "Jay-Z", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Both Dariush Mehrjui and Paul W. S. Anderson are members of the Iranian Academy of the Arts?", "answer": "no", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "The actress providing the voice of Eliza Thornberry also stars in a holiday film ranking within The New York Times' Top 5 Holiday TV movies that is directed by whom? ", "answer": "David Winning", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Beyond Einstein is a book by a theoretical physicist who has authored how many \"New York Times\" best sellers?", "answer": "three", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which city was named after the Union Army colonel and the president of the Cape Fear Building Company?", "answer": "Abbottsburg", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Where is the company based that owns and operates Rio Secco Golf Club?", "answer": "Paradise, Nevada", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which state is the state park, which is named after the network of trails used by Native Americans to navigate through the Great Appalachian Valley, located?", "answer": "Pennsylvania", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "In what region of Central and East Africa is the company which manages teh Fanisi Venture Capital Fund located?", "answer": "African Great Lakes region", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Were both Tian Zhuangzhuang and Marcel Varnel a chinese film director and producer? ", "answer": "no", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "What award was given to the Norwegian-born American physical chemist which Bruria Kaufman used applied spinor analysis to rederive the result of on the partition function of the two-dimensional Ising Model", "answer": "Nobel Prize in Chemistry", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Roger Avary and Basil Dearden both shared what role in the film industry?", "answer": "director", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "What type of grand fir is found in Washington State and Northern California?", "answer": "Abies grandis", "t