e of consent", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "In what county is the mosque that Husham Al-Husainy works at?", "answer": "Wayne County", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Ursula Reith is best known for her role as Mrs. Gloop in a 1971 American musical fantasy film that was directed by Mel Stuart, and starred who?", "answer": "Gene Wilder", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "In what year were both UCLA football players Chris Markey and Maurice Jones-Drew born?", "answer": "1985", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "How was the Republic of Kawait formed?", "answer": "the aftermath of the invasion of Kuwait by Ba'athist Iraq during the early stages of the Persian Gulf War.", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Are Grigori Perelman and Valery Goppa Swedish mathematicians?", "answer": "no", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Who produced Kelis most well-known song?", "answer": "The Neptunes", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "The writer of National Lampoon has also written for what animated television series created by Arlene Klasky, G\u00e1bor Csup\u00f3 and Paul Germain for Nickelodeon?", "answer": "Rugrats", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Kilcoy Castle and Dalcross Castle are both in what country?", "answer": "Scotland", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "University of Houston was defeated 84\u201375 by Georgetown who was led by a basketball player who played most of his career with what team?", "answer": "New York Knicks", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What nationality was the star of Orson Welles \"The Trial\", Anthony Perkins?", "answer": "American", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Saratoga Springs is a train station owned by a public benefit corporation that runs the day-to-day management of what other Amtrak station in the Capital region?", "answer": "Albany-Rensselaer", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "The pop bands Dodgy from the UK and Kane from Holland are both known for their pop rock fusion with the former being described as power pop rock and the latter being