at team was Shaun Livingston drafted by in the 2004 NBA draft that was held at The Theater at Madison Square Garden in New York City and broadcast live on ESPN?", "answer": "Los Angeles Clippers", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Prior to the Chinese Student Protection Act of 1992 (CSPA), the Act\u2019s main sponsors were which American politician who currently serves as the Minority Leader of the United States House of Representatives, representing California's 12th congressional district?", "answer": "Nancy Pelosi", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "George Juskalian was the MACV inspector general under the leader who served as Chief of Staff for the Army during what span?", "answer": "1968 to 1972", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Q1: Who has operations in more countries, Jackson National Life or Prudential Financial? A1: Prudential Financial. Q2: Who provides more services, Jackson National Life or Prudent Financial? A2: Prudent Financial.", "answer": "Prudential Financial.", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "The sole goal-scorer in the 2015-16 Coppa Italia championship game plays what position for Chelsea's team?", "answer": "striker", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "When was the  American businessman who founded  Red Swoosh born ", "answer": "August 6, 1976", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What star of a popular Pakastani sitcom drama series is a rapper, actor and rock music keyboardist?", "answer": "Ahmad Ali Butt", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Many loanwords in Hawaiian Pidgin (or Hawaiian Creole English) derive from the Japanese language, the linguistic influences of the Japanese in Hawaii, began with the first immigrants from Japan in what year?", "answer": "1868", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which genre do the movies You've got mail and Sano Sansar have in common?", "answer": "romantic comedy", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What are both Al-Nayrizi and Abu'l-Hasan al-Uqlidisi?", "answer": "mathematician", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "