er, radio contributor, and actress, who stareed in Punching Henry?", "answer": "Tig Notaro", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Wild and Woolly starred the American actor who was also a professional in what other discipline?", "answer": "dog breeder", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Karl Paley Cohen workd within a group that included an American physicist who won the Nobel Price in Physics for his discovery of what?", "answer": "nuclear magnetic resonance", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "When was the writer of Hyperspace born?", "answer": "born on January 24, 1947", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "When was the writer of the thirteenth episode of \"30 Rock\" born?", "answer": "May 18, 1970", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What university did an individual born in 1946 and currently in charge of Us Weekly drop out of?  ", "answer": "University of California, Berkeley", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Peace Internation School, a private institution in the Western Part of Ghana, is loacted in the hometown of whose father? ", "answer": "Kwame Nkrumah's father", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which 20th century battleship featured artillery with a specially reinforced barrel and steam turbine propulsion?", "answer": "Dreadnought", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which tennis player won a major tennis championship in singles, Juan Mart\u00edn del Potro or Bob Bryan?", "answer": "Juan Mart\u00edn del Potro", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Which St. Louis Rams head coach worked with Phil Towle?", "answer": "Dick Vermeil", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Who was born first out of Sidney Franklin and M. Night Shyamalan?", "answer": "Sidney Arnold Franklin", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Who directed the 2014 film that was a knock-off of the 2012 film directed by Jung Byung-gil?", "answer": "Jean Markose", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Cifte hammam, is a hammam in the Old Bazaar,  a bazaar located in Skopje, situated on the eastern bank of the Vardar River, stretching from the Stone Bridge to the Bit-Pazar and from the Skopje Fortress to the Serava river, in which country?", "answer": "Macedonia", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Domhnall Gleeson is the son of the recipient of three IFTA Awards who has been nominated for a Golden Globe Award how many times?", "answer": "three", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What is the estimated market capitalisation as of March 2011 of the company that owns Uttar Pradesh Wizards ? ", "answer": "25.94 billion", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "what is the nickname of the sea monster that lives at TenMile Point, British Columbia?", "answer": "Caddy", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which novelist was also a short story writer, Jo\u00e3o Guimar\u00e3es Rosa or Philip Pullman?", "answer": "Jo\u00e3o Guimar\u00e3es Rosa", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Who directed the 1983 American crime film, a remake of the film based on Armitage Trail's best known work?", "answer": "Brian De Palma", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": " Boston Market Corporation is a chain of American fast casual restaurants headquartered in a municipality founded on 16 June 1859 during what?", "answer": "the Pike's Peak Gold Rush", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which dog breed is larger, Whippets or Jack Russell Terriers?", "answer": "Whippets", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "How many engines does the plane the \"Texas Raiders\" fly have?", "answer": "four-engine", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Cha Seung-won achieved stardom, in part through a horror-comedy film, which sold how many tickets the year it was released?", "answer": "2,890,000", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Skandar Keynes had a starring role in the series of fantasy films released by what company?", "answer": "Walden Media", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "The Nemean games honored what mythology concerning, Pronax?", "answer": "Greek", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "The Armored Medical Research Laboratory was located at the Ar