out two young star-crossed lovers?", "answer": "Carlo Vanzina", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "When did Frank Sinatra's career begin to lag?  Frank Sinatra lived in a walled compound with some of his best friends.  Who were they?", "answer": "His career was reborn in 1953 with the success of \"From Here to Eternity\", with his performance subsequently", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What movement did the writer of The Great Shark hunt found?", "answer": "gonzo journalism movement", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "When did the movement exist that Richard Moore was a part of?", "answer": "1838 to 1857", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Janez Lapajne and Tony Scott, have which mutual occupations?", "answer": "film director and producer", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "The person who wrote the musical score for \"Onde Roopa Eradu Guna\" is affectionately called what by his admirers?", "answer": "\"Salilda\"", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What type of media does Final Score and Wordplay have in common?", "answer": "film", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Are Calocedrus and Lycaste both genii of plants?", "answer": "yes", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "What controversial dating service did Singapore's Media Development Authority censor?", "answer": "Ashley Madison", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "The writer of \"I Am Joaquin\" convened the first-ever Chicano youth conference in what year?", "answer": "1969", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which American actor starred in Surrogates ", "answer": "James Oliver Cromwell", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Jumbo the Elephant is a concrete and reinforced steel statue by Canadian artist Winston Bronnum, the city funded the $70,000 sculpture in part with the sale of Indiana Jones-style hats and commemorative coins, Dr. Henry Walton \"Indiana\" Jones Jr. is a title character and protagonist of the \"Indiana Jones\" franchise, who created the character in homage to the action heroes of 1930s film serial