, are which type of entertainment?", "answer": "game", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Egmont Key State Park lies southwest of what park that is operated by Pinellas County on five offshore keys?", "answer": "Fort De Soto Park", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What is a United Kingdom-based company which holds the licence to operate the two main vehicle rental brands of Avis Budget Group one being an American car rental company that was founded in 1958 in Los Angeles, California by Morris Mirkin ?", "answer": "Avis Europe", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "WASP-17b is located in a constellation identified by which astronomer?", "answer": "identified by the Greek astronomer Ptolemy", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What campaigning publishing organisation for freedom of expression employed Elena Oznobkina as an editor for one of its publications?", "answer": "Index on Censorship", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "The city where the Anubis Shrine was found was known to the ancient Egyptians as what?", "answer": "Waset", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which American minimalist composer created the symphony Na\u00efve and Sentimental Music, first performed in 1999?", "answer": "John Adams", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What show starred Canadian actor born on February 4, 1923, alongside Gary Coleman and Todd Bridges?", "answer": "Diff'rent Strokes", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "When was the Russian former figure skater who often skated to the music of Edvin Marton born?", "answer": "3 November 1982", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "The Birmingham bid for the 2022 Commonwealth Games", "answer": "The Birmingham bid for the 2022 Commonwealth Games", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "The super is the last film to feature what actor who portrayed Det. Frank Ochoa in Death Wish?", "answer": "Vincent Gardenia", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Are Hattiesburg\u2013Laurel Regional Airport and The Eastern Iowa Airport located in different US states?", "answer": 