ured heavily in the fomation of colonial policy on what historical island?", "answer": "Dutch Formosa", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Poetry Translation Centre has had work championed by the poet of what nationality?", "answer": "Northern Irish", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What nationality was the composer of Drei Lieder?", "answer": "German", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What is the name of the famous director of Marnie, a psychological thriller, for which a book about his relationship with Evan Hunter and their ill fated collaboration was written?", "answer": "Alfred Hitchcock", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Ameesha Patel made her acting debut in a 2000 film directed by who?", "answer": "Rakesh Roshan", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "The Sudbury Reservoir, is an emergency backup Boston metropolitan water reservoir located in Framingham, a town in the Commonwealth of Massachusetts, in which country?", "answer": "United States", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What director, known for 2000 film \"Girlfight\" also directed the 2009 supernatural horror black comedy film starring Megan Fox?", "answer": "Karyn Kusama", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "American Kim Wilson and Englishman Baz Warne are both accomplished musicians, but are they both singers?", "answer": "yes", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "What American animated sitcom mystery comedy series was produced by the director of the TV series \"Recess\"?", "answer": "What's New, Scooby-Doo?", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Colonel Chabert, released in which year, is a French drama film directed by Ren\u00e9 Le H\u00e9naff, the film is based on the novel \"Colonel Chabert\" by Honor\u00e9 de Balzac?", "answer": "1943", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What year was the Nobel Laureate American economist, who studied under Frank Knight, born?", "answer": "1912", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which voice actor sang \"Born to be Wild\" as Miss Piggy on the 1994 Kermit Unplugged?", "answer