ers?", "answer": "yes", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "What is the name of this music genre that originated in the mid 1960s when African American musicians created a rhytmic, danceable new form of music though a mix of soul, jazz, and R&B, the genre of the band Gotcha!?", "answer": "Funk", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Shenzhou 9, was the fourth manned spacecraft flight of China's Shenzhou program, launched on 16 June 2012, the mission's crew included which first Chinese female astronaut, and pilot?", "answer": "Liu Yang", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which Australian rules football club, nicknamed the Crows, was coached in an interim capacity by Scott Camporeale after the death of head coack Phil Walsh?", "answer": "Adelaide Football Club", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "who had more success as singles, Travis Parrott or Pierre-Hugues Herbert", "answer": "Pierre-Hugues Herbert", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Who stars in the film based on a short story by Daphne du Maurier with cinematography by Anthony B. Richmond?", "answer": "Julie Christie and Donald Sutherland", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Who played a cunning an opportunistic pirate that had been quartermastered under the notorious Captain Flint?", "answer": "Charles Ogle", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "When was the American comedian and vaudevillian died who introduced \"Thanks for the Memory\" (1938) in the film \"The Big Broadcast of 1938\"?", "answer": "July 27, 2003", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "When was the University of which the Whiting School of Engineering, is part, founded ?", "answer": "1876", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Fantasy film The Witcher about witcher Geralt of Rivia and A Time of Contempt was written by what author?", "answer": "Andrzej Sapkowski", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Name the British-American musical fantasy film produced by Walt Disney Productions based upon the book 'How to Become a Witch in Ten Easy Lessons' which features the frau