ed in the movie The Ghost and the Darkness?", "answer": "construction workers", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "\u201cSuicide Solution\u201d is a song from an album released on which date ?", "answer": "20 September 1980", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What is the middle name of the man who developed MegaMemory?", "answer": "Mark", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which of the following directors is known for his work on \"I, Robot\": Marcus Stokes or Mel Brooks?", "answer": "Marcus Stokes", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Which Victorian stage actor had children named Laurence and Elizabeth Irving?", "answer": "Henry Irving", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What is the birthdate of this American mixed martial artist, currently fighting in the welterweight division for the World Series of Fighting and who met up with Frank Gomez at San Francisco State College?", "answer": "January 9, 1979", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Sports Illustrated Kids and Popular Photography are considered to be what kind of production?", "answer": "magazine", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "What influence did works based on the Faust such as Damn Yankees have over time?", "answer": "inspired artistic and cultural works", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which creator of The Bugle is known for his use of extended pun runs?", "answer": "Andy Zaltzman", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Peter Webber directed which fifth film of the Hannibal Lecter franchise?", "answer": "Hannibal Rising", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Sechskies is a six member South Korean boy band that includes what South Korean rapper whose first solo single was \"A-Ha\"?", "answer": "Eun Ji-won", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "The Anti-Pamela; or Feign\u2019d Innocence Detected is a 1741 novel written by Eliza Haywood as a satire of of a novel that was criticized for what ?", "answer": "for its perceived licentiousness", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Are the Madera Canal and the Dismal Swamp Canal 