estion": "The show where Mira Furlan played a scientist who was shipwrecked on a island went on for how many episodes?", "answer": "121", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What anthology are the graphic novels upon which the role-playing game designed by Luke Crane a part of?", "answer": "Negative Burn", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What was Grace Mugabe's title after she married the former chairman of the Zimbabwe African National Union?", "answer": "First Lady of Zimbabwe", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What was the population of the town that is near Butcher Hills in 2010?", "answer": "332", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "in 2014 the Baylor Bears football team relocated after 64 years at the Floyd Casey Stadium, to which Waco, Texas arena?", "answer": "McLane Stadium", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Who managed the team that placed the first during the Pittsburgh Pirates season in the 1940s when the Pirates placed the fourth?", "answer": "Leo Durocher", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which actor who starred in \"The Matrix\" wrote, directed and starred in the film \"Once in a Lifetime\"?", "answer": "Laurence Fishburne", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What neighborhood on the west side of Lower Manhattan, New York City, did Harry Peter Traum become a musical scene stalwart in the 1960s of?", "answer": "Greenwich Village", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What American film and television actor was featured in, Heat, a 1995 American crime film written, produced and directed by Michael Mann?", "answer": "Dennis Dexter Haysbert", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What town has a  24.8 mi tributary of Schoharie Creek in Schoharie and Albany counties in the U.S. state of New York, and was named after governor Silas Wright?", "answer": "Wright", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which reality TV series did Andre Thysse's opponent in his IBF Australasian super middleweight title fight, win?", "answer": "The Contender", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "The Me