": "comparison"}, {"question": "What borough is the high school that the person who committed the largest financial fraud in US history went to?", "answer": "Queens", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What does KO Magazine and Analog Science Fiction and Fact have in common?", "answer": "magazine", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "What was Reece Daniel Thompson called at the beginning of his acting career?", "answer": "child actor", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "the Bengali musician who inspired George Harrison's song \"Bengla Desh\" was a composer of what kind of music>", "answer": "Hindustani classical music", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "The Washington Valor play their home games at the arena formerly known as what?", "answer": "MCI Center and Verizon Center", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What do these peoples of many nations and tribal affiliations, whom global maritime and naval historian Barry M. Gough had good relations with, believe as a resource and spiritual symbol?", "answer": "centrality of salmon", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What are both Commodore 64 and Memotech MTX?", "answer": "computer", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Which director was born first, James Mangold or Kostas Andritsos?", "answer": "Kostas Andritsos", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Selaginella and Desfontainia, are what kind of item?", "answer": "plants", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "In 2008, the fourth Malaysian player to achieve the #1 ranking also won a silver medal at the 2008 Olympics in which respective sport?", "answer": "badminton", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Who has been in more bands, Shifty Shellshock or Richard Z. Kruspe?", "answer": "Richard Zven Kruspe", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "An animal carcass tha twashed ashore on a beach under the Brooklyn Bridge has been compared to another animal carcass that washed ashore on a beach near Montauk, New York, in what year?", "answer": "2008", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "when does Plum Island Light built which has the same design as Great Captain Island Lighthouse?", "answer": "1869", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What part of the world do the Viezenbeek and Lindemans Brewery hale from?", "answer": "Brussels", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which rock band was formed more recently Said the Whale or Butthole Surfers?", "answer": "Butthole Surfers", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "What do King Roger and La donna del lago have in common?", "answer": "opera", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "What year was the novel featuring the fictional firm Roark Capital Group written?", "answer": "1943", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "The Expected utility hypothesis was initiated by which Swiss mathematician in 1738?", "answer": "Daniel Bernoulli", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which film genre do the films \"Crazy English\" and \"Capturing the Friedmans\" belong to?", "answer": "documentary", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "What is the name of the American actress that starred in Extraction?", "answer": "Gina Carano", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "This annual publication listed RMIT School of Art as the top art school in which country for 2016?", "answer": "Australia", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Was Apsley Cherry-Garrard a zoologist?", "answer": "It was originally named Cherry Glacier by the British Antarctic Expedition, 1910\u201313, for Apsley Cherry-Garrard, zoologist with the expedition.", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which has more acts Faust or Die schweigsame Frau?", "answer": "Faust", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "What was the population in 2000 of the community where Allegiant Travel Company has its headquarters ?", "answer": "59,000", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "In what year was the band of the keyboard player who did \"Flame\" with Tim Bowness formed?", "answer": "1987", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which mosquito-borne infectious disease was deadly to many new arrivals, especially in the Southern colonies", "answer": "Malaria", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which \"Australia's Next Top Model\" co-host appeared in John Wick: Chapter 2?", "answer": "Ruby Rose Langenheim", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What Texas Tech All-American was on the cover of Electronic Arts NCAA Football 10?", "answer": "Michael Crabtree", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which team  did professional basketball player Tom Van Arsdale play for that began during the 1962-63 NBA season?", "answer": "NBA All-Rookie Team", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Are Jeff Scott Soto and Petri Lindroos both members of Ensiferum?", "answer": "no", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "What professional footballer who plays as a midfielder for Aston Villa and for England U21 has played in the HKFC Soccer Sevens?", "answer": "Jack Grealish", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "The Festning Tunnel runs under what type of structure?", "answer": "a medieval castle", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Spoon and The Datsuns, are bands of which shared genre?", "answer": "rock", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Which character from the twelfth episode of \"The Simpsons\" second season was created and designed by cartoonist Matt Groening?", "answer": "Marge\" Simpson", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": " Budapest Resonance contained a cover of the song that was first released on what date?", "answer": "28 August 1989", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What was the date of a a Premier League matched played by a Dutch man born 1 July 1976?", "answer": "24 October 2004", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Bailey Hall was built by the same architect as that who created the building that goes by which other name?", "answer": "Kansas Statehouse", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Who directed the 2008 American political satire is Emmanuelle Chriqui known for her performance on", "answer": "Dennis Dugan", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "In what year was the man who scored the winning goal in the 2009 DFB-P