ul or the Walled Obelisk?", "answer": "The Grand Bazaar", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Escape from the Studio '06 was a tour that took place before the release of which Metallica album?", "answer": "Death Magnetic", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "what is the slogan of the airline that has one of its hubs in Sir Captain Charles Kirkconnell International Airport ?", "answer": "Those who fly us love us", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What year was A Turtle's Tale: Sammy's Adventures featuring the voice of Robert Sheehan, an Irish actor, released? ", "answer": "2010", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What Mexican drug lord know as \"El M\u00e1s Loco\" (English: \"The Craziest One\") preached his organization's divine right to eliminate their enemies?", "answer": "Nazario Moreno Gonz\u00e1lez", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Are Gareth Edwards and Michael Lembeck both film directors?", "answer": "yes", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Columbia Edgewater Country Club is west of whichmilitary airport?", "answer": "Portland International Airport", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Who is the lead vocalist, rhythm guitarist, and occasional pianist for the American rock band, REO Speedwagon, Kevin Cronin or Derek Hough?", "answer": "Kevin Patrick Cronin", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Russian Dolls, is a 2005 French-British film, the sequel to \"L'Auberge Espagnole\", a 2002 French-Spanish film, directed and written by who?", "answer": "C\u00e9dric Klapisch", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "John Ida is best known for the vocalist and guitarist in which band?", "answer": "Yardbirds", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": " \"Girl\" was the last complete song recorded for an album that was release in what month of 1965?", "answer": "December", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Who was born first, Mrinal Sen or Terry Jones?", "answer": "Mrinal Sen", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "The band Salem had a song featured in a 2012 film directed by whom?", "answer": "Derek Cianfrance", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "The station MGM Grand station is a station on is how many miles long?", "answer": "3.9", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which game was published or manufactured first, Hanabi or Cluedo?", "answer": "Cluedo", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Are both Jesse Michaels and Dan Swan\u00f6 a musician?", "answer": "yes", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "What Family Guy actress also played in That 70's Show?", "answer": "\"Mila\" Kunis", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which was an animated film, Coco or Secretariat?", "answer": "Coco", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "What is the county seat of Neosho County, Kansas where Shaw is also a part of?", "answer": "Erie", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What member of even-toed ungulate species lives in an African game reserve?", "answer": "Antelope", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What day was the Jay-Z album featuring FuckWithMeYouKnowIGotIt released for retail sale?", "answer": "July 8, 2013", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which 2016 French comedy film also starred the actress who play Henrietta of England in \"Versailles?\" ", "answer": "Radin!", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What was Jack Buck's younger brother's job?", "answer": "sportscaster", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What type of compilation does Chris Harris and Into the Labyrinth have in common?", "answer": "television series", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Anna Riva (1922\u20132003) was the pen name of who, a well-known American occult author and manufacturer of Hoodoo spiritual supplies, a traditional African American folk spirituality that developed from a number of West African spiritual traditions and beliefs? ", "answer": "Dorothy Spencer", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "American Ride is the thirteenth studio album by American country music artist Toby Keith and includes a tribute song to an American basketball player ho was elected into what?", "answer": "National Collegiate Basketball Hall of Fame", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Batman Begins is a 2005 superhero film that was co-written by what screenwriter and director who is one of the highest-grossing directors in history?", "answer": "Christopher Edward Nolan", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "The bec de corbin and Lucerne hammer were both popular in medieval Europe, but the Lucerne hammer was particularly popular in what European country during the 15th to 17th centuries?", "answer": "Switzerland", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Where is the oil corporation located that is a direct descendant if the \"wealthiest American of all time's\" oil company?", "answer": "Irving, Texas", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which American football quarterback has played for Detroit Lions, Oakland Raiders, Miami Dolphins, Carolina Panthers, Hartford Colonials, San Francisco 49ers, Chicago Bears, Tampa Bay Buccaneers, Cleveland Browns and New York Jets, and has and is the younger brother of a former quarterback for Texas A&M and the Houston Marshals of the Spring Football League?", "answer": "Joshua Treadwell McCown", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Who was a lead composer for the \"bel canto\" opera style, Gustave Charpentier or Gaetano Donizetti?", "answer": "Donizetti was a leading composer of the \"bel canto\" opera style during the first half of the nineteenth century.", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "What identical process will take place for gubernatorial elections and United States Congress elections if vacancies arise?", "answer": "special elections", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What sporting event happened in the summer of  1924 where Australia competed.", "answer": "Summer Olympic Games", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Kim Sung-oh, is a South Korean actor, he is best known for his supporting roles in which South Korean action-thriller film starring Won Bin and written and directed by Lee Jeong-beom? ", "answer": "The Man from Nowhere", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Bill Nye hosted a self-titled show, which was predecessor to \"The Eyes of Nye\"; what was the final air date of that predecessor show?", "answer": "March 1, 1999", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Do both the Kintamani and Alpine Mastiff still exist?", "answer": "no", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Who is older, Jessica Jung or Steve Augeri?", "answer": "Steve Augeri", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Are Jiangyin and Beipiao both in China?", "answer": "yes", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Which hamlet in Suffolk County, New York is part of District 3?", "answer": "Coram", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What position did Michael Platt Jr originally hold working for the politician representing Tennessee's 7 congressional district?", "answer": "chief of staff", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Have Alejandro Gonz\u00e1lez I\u00f1\u00e1rritu and Sydney Pollack both been nominated for an Academy Award?", "answer": "yes", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Brachypodium and Kohleria, are types of what?", "answer": "plants", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Who is the director of the film in which Colin Edward Quinn had a part as Amy Schumer's father ?", "answer": "Judd Apatow", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which of the two players who scored in the 2010-11 league cup final was born in 1984 ?", "answer": "Obafemi Martins", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Who established himself as the acclaimed host of televisions show and was in a Austrian-West German musical comedy film?", "answer": "Peter Alexander", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "In 2015, Matt Stone listed this episode of South Park as his third favorite that used a screen-capturing program for what operating system?", "answer": "macOS", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Eric Weisbard founded the Pop Conference which is hosted annually by a nonprofit museum founded by who?", "answer": "Paul Allen", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What is the home stadium of the University where Roy Finch played college football ?", "answer": "Gaylord Family Oklahoma Memorial Stadium", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "If 6 Was 9 is featured in the soundtrack of a 1991 film directed by whom?", "answer": "Kathryn Bigelow", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What is the release date of this song recorded by Taylor Swift for which she released a music video?", "answer": "June 19, 2006", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What school did Denzel Ramirez run track for that was established in 1964?", "answer": "Colby Community College", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "The Port of Eden is a small seaport situated in Twofold Bay, adjacent to the town of Eden, a coastal town in the South Coast region of New South Wales, in which country?", "answer": "Australia", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "John Hamilton-Leslie, 9th Earl of Rothes was a Scottish nobleman who fought on the side of a king of Great Britain that died in this year?", "answer": "1727", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Who founded the American investment management firm that managed Numerai's investment group?", "answer": "James Simons", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Colin and Edith was hosted by Edith Bowman and another radio personality who won what award at the 2007 Sony Radio Academy Awards?", "answer": "'Music Broadcaster of the Year'", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Lakshminath Bezbaroa, (1864\u20131938) was a great Assamese personality and celebrated pioneer of modern Assamese literature, he was one of the literary stalwarts of the era, named after which Assamese language magazine published from Calcutta in 1889?", "answer": "Jonaki", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which movie Vinessa Shaw was in was based on a novella by Arthur Schnitzler?", "answer": "Eyes Wide Shut", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Who began his career in film as a visual effects artist at George Lucas's Industrial Light and Magic, Willard Huyck or Marcus Stokes?", "answer": "Marcus Stokes", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "The man that invented Zone melting was a political supporter of what?", "answer": "Communism", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "The Texas Theatre is a movie theater and Dallas Landmark located in the Oak Cliff neighborhood of Dallas, Texas, it gained historical significance on November 22, 1963 as the location of Lee Harvey Oswald's arrest, and the killing of which Dallas police officer, who was an 11-year veteran with the Dallas Police Department, and died on November 22, 1963?", "answer": "J.D. Tippit", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which film featuring Kelly Rohrbach was relased in 2017 and directed by Seth Gordon?", "answer": "Baywatch", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Tripel beer was first introduced in 1956, by which Belgian abbey brewery?", "answer": "Westmalle Brewery", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "In addition to Matthew Macfadyen and the actor who played Richard Winters in Band of Brothers, what other actor starred in Warriors?", "answer": "Ioan Gruffudd", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "President's Choice Financial is a financial service division to a supermarket chain with how many regional and market segment banners?", "answer": "22", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Whos home country is farther north, Ivan Perestiani or Valie Export?", "answer": "Valie Export", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Bedroom at Arles is a painting based on which Van Gogh series of three works?", "answer": "Bedroom in Arles", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "X, is the second studio album by English singer-songwriter, Ed Sheeran, which song single did he record?", "answer": "Don't", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Evolution: A Theory in Crisis is a 1985 book by a biochemist and Senior fellow at Discovery Institute's Center for what?", "answer": "Science and Culture", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What nationality is the host of Mr. Romance?", "answer": "Italian-American", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "7/7 Ripple Effect is a 57-minute homemade film produced and narrated under the pseudonym \"Muad'Dib\", the film disputes the official account of the 7 July 2005 London bombings (also known as 7/7), a terrorist attack on public transport in Central London, by four suicide bombers, including Germaine Maurice Lindsay, also known as Abdullah Shaheed Jamal, was one of the four terrorists who detonated bombs, on how many trains?", "answer": "three", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which UK chart topping single came first, John Newman's \"Blame\" featuring Calvin Harris or \"I'm Not Alone\" by Calvin Harris?", "answer": "\"I'm Not Alone\"", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Are Volcanic Sprint and For the Bible Tells Me So both films in the same genre?", "answer": "yes", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Are Mate Pavi\u0107 and Raffaella Reggi from the same country? ", "answer": "no", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Which 7th place finisher on the third season of American Idol recorded the song Giving Myself?", "answer": "Jennifer Hudson", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Joseph Kitchen is an English footballer who played for what club that was founded in 1904, and plays in the second tier of English football?", "answer": "Hull City Association Football Club", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Andrew Card was White House Chief of Staff under a president that was previously governor of what state?", "answer": "Texas", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which singer is Dutch, Floor Jansen or Aaron Lewis?", "answer": "Floor Jansen", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "What do Mariqueen Maandig and Peter Furler have in common?", "answer": "musician", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "After Brown v. Board of Education, the Florida legislature opened Hampton Junior College in which city as one of 11 black community colleges to show that the education system was separate but equal?", "answer": "Ocala, Florida", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which person won the Nobel Prize in Literature in 1961, Ivo Andri\u0107 or Nicholas Pileggi?", "answer": "Ivo Andri\u0107", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "The 2001 FIBA European Championship, commonly called FIBA EuroBasket 2001, was the 32nd FIBA EuroBasket regional basketball championship held by FIBA Europe, which also served as Europe qualifier for the 2002 FIBA World Championship,Yugoslavia's Predrag Stojakovi\u0107  Serbian professional basketball executive and former player, and voted the tournament's what?", "answer": "MVP", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Jimmy Duncanson played striker for a football club in Glasgow, Scotland whose home ground has what name?", "answer": "Ibrox Stadium", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What band did Joe Long play bass guitarist for?", "answer": "The Four Seasons", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What is the nickname of the public figure who's attorney used a Chewbacca defense in his murder trial?", "answer": "The Juice", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "How old is the currently active shield volcano located in the Ka\u02bb \u016b Desert?", "answer": "between 300,000 and 600,000 years", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "In between Michael Vartan and Vartan Gregorian who is is a French-American actor?", "answer": "Michael S. Vartan", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "What record did Jacues Piccard's father break?", "answer": "hot air balloon flights", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which Japanese mixed martial artist is the former DREAM Openweight Grand Prix Champion was once defeated by Kiyoshi Tamura?", "answer": "Ikuhisa Minowa", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What romantic thriller film, directed by Roman Polanski, did Vangelis witness filming while producing The City album?", "answer": "Bitter Moon", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "In what year was the man who named the First Battle of Kharkov born?", "answer": "1882", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What did residents claim to encounter one evening in 1955 on US 41 at Kelly, Kentucky, leading to an annual festival of Little Green Men?", "answer": "alien", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Sinhala Hound and German Shepherd, are breeds of which animal?", "answer": "dog", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "When was the president born that Ed Callahan served under as Chairman of the NCUA?", "answer": "February 6, 1911", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "The Rural Landless Employment Guarantee Programme (RLEGP) was launched on which date, by Prime Minister of India Indira Gandhi during which the Indian economy was premised on the concept of planning, the Five-Year Plans, developed, executed, and monitored by the Planning Commission (1951 - 2014)?", "answer": "15 August 1983", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "The Olympics Hassan Al-Absi competed in took place in what city?", "answer": "Los Angeles, California, United States", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Musicality features covers of songs from a jukebox musical written by who?", "answer": "Catherine Johnson", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Both Zan-e Rooz and Glamour are magazines catered to which biological sex.?", "answer": "women", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "What does Paul Georgescu and Ion Antonescu have in common? ", "answer": "was a Romanian", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Live  is a song that was covered by which Los Angeles-based pop-rock band?", "answer": "The Bangles", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Hudson's bay trading became involved in fur trading with this individual born in riviere-Ouelle", "answer": "Horace B\u00e9langer", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "The 17th Premier of Nova Scotia and leader of the federal Progressive Conservative Party of Canada Robert Stanfield fought a few times and lost in general elections against which politician who is currently one of the longest-serving Prime Minister in Canadian history?", "answer": "Pierre Trudeau", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which UFC weight division did Chris Leben and Anderson Silva compete in?", "answer": "Middleweight", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": 