3 and included the Operation Torch?", "answer": "North African Campaign", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Does Leucothoe or Pileostegia have more species?", "answer": "Leucothoe", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Which genus has more species, Itea or Anthriscus", "answer": "Anthriscus", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Are Myoporum and Jacquemontia both types of trees or shrubs?", "answer": "no", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "The village of Lissington, the districts of Lindsey and town on Wragby are all in which English county?", "answer": "Lincolnshire", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What acress starred in both \"Third Person\" and \"From Here to Eternity\"?", "answer": "Kim Basinger", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What hit song, sung by Rihanna was featured on her fifth studio album \"Loud\" and reached number one on the US Billboard Hot 100?", "answer": "\"What's My Name?\"", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "To which American football team was the wide receiver Pete Mills drafted in the twelfth round of the 1965 AFL draft and who first enrolled at the Coffeyville Community College in Kansas?", "answer": "Buffalo Bills", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "In what year was the art critic which The Old Masters is about born?", "answer": "1865", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Who met a singer that has released twelve regular studio albums, mostly through Virgin Records, while attending Pitzer College in Claremont, California?", "answer": "Tom Freund", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Who distributed Park Jung-woo's third feature?", "answer": "CJ E&M", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "The bomber stopped by Candice DeLong used his crimes to advance what type of anarchism?", "answer": "nature-centered", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "World News Tonight included which neo-conservative founder of The Weekly Standard?", "answer": "William \"Bill\" Kristol", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "XXX stars the actor known for playing which character in The