wer": "pressure from his probation officer", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Able Seaman Colin Grazier, GC was posthumously awarded what, for \"bravery and steadfast devotion to duty\", he displayed on 30 October 1942 in action in the eastern Mediterranean when capturing codebooks vital for the breaking of the German naval \"Shark\" Enigma cipher from the sinking, the Enigma machines were a series of electro-mechanical rotor cipher machines developed and used in the early- to mid-20th century to protect commercial, diplomatic and military communication?", "answer": "George Cross", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What TV show did the singer of Stunnah become prominent for?", "answer": "\"The Simple Life\"", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Fetteresso Castle is a 14th-century towerhouse, rebuilt in 1761 as a Scottish gothic style Palladian manor, with clear evidence of prehistoric use of the site, other notable historic fortified houses or castles in this region, include which ruined fortress in Aberdeenshire, Scotland?", "answer": "Cowie Castle", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "When was the attack occured which destroyed a builiding neary by the the Irish Hunger Memorial in Manhattan in New York City?", "answer": "September 11 attacks in 2001", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "When was the American actor and, producer, who hosted the 23rd People's Choice Awards born", "answer": "December 15, 1949", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which singer has been part of more bands, Richard Ashcroft or James Bourne?", "answer": "James Elliot Bourne", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Who was the starring basketball player in the movie that Ryan Woodward worked on that was about basketball?", "answer": "Michael Jordan", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What architectural style is used for the building that houses the museum directed by Fr. Timothy Verdon?", "answer": "Gothic", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "When was the independent music and dramatic arts school  founded