 is larger, Pingxiang or Shijiazhuang?  ", "answer": "Shijiazhuang ( ; ), formerly romanized Shihkiachwang, is the capital and largest city of North China's Hebei Province", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Igor Matvienko and Fabrika, are both Russian musicians, from which city?", "answer": "Moscow", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "In which city is the headquarters of the restaurant operator of The Capital Grille located?", "answer": "Orlando", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "James Fleet is famous for his role as Tom in what film that was directed by Mike Newell and featured Hugh Grant?", "answer": "Four Weddings and a Funeral", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Who was the father of the racer who died in an accident similar to Markus Hottinger?", "answer": "John Surtees", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "In what country is the castle associated with the line of pottery called Wemyss Ware located?", "answer": "Scotland", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "The Witches of Eastwick was a film based on a book by the author who won what prize more than once?", "answer": "Pulitzer Prize for Fiction", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "The World's Funniest was hosted by an American sportscaster who also hosted The NFL Today, and what other show on CBS Sports?", "answer": "Thursday Night Football", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which film director is best known for the movie \"Alvin Purple\", Mark Robson or Tim Burstall?", "answer": "Timothy \"Tim\" Burstall AM", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Which style of house, located in The Old Town Historic District, is usually no more than 12 feet wide?", "answer": "shotgun house", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Who directed the film in which Monica Keena made her film debut?", "answer": "Jon Turteltaub", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What kind of objects did the astronomer who discovered NGC 369 find?", "answer": "New General Catalogue objects", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Benjamin Russell Hanby was an American 