 genus of plants in the amaranth family, and Tolpis in the dandelion tribe flowering plants?", "answer": "yes", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Which band has more members, Mando Diao or Sloan?", "answer": "Mando Diao", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Who wrote the Dragon King the third of the four music dramas?", "answer": "Richard Wagner", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which Breakthrough film director was based in Dallas, Texas?", "answer": "David Lowery", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Henry Chichester Hart edited Elizabethan plays for Methuen's Standard Library's scholarly editions of plays and poems that is named after what forest? ", "answer": "Forest of Arden", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "The film Nandha whose music was scored by Indian singer-songwriter Yuvan Sahnkar Raja, was released in what year?", "answer": "2001", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Who is the Chicago recording artist's mixtape \"They Forgot\" by?", "answer": "Lil Durk", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Vincent Cirelli worked on what film centered on the development of the 1964 film \"Mary Poppins\"?", "answer": "Saving Mr. Banks", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What is the capital of the country in which Lokovina is located?", "answer": "Ljubljana", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which was founded earlier, The Week or New Scientist?", "answer": "New Scientist", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Who was born first, Tom Green or Ford Beebe?", "answer": "Ford Beebe", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "What activity are both  Roman White and Kelsea Ballerini known for?", "answer": "music", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which private university was founded first, Northeastern University or Lawrence Technological University?", "answer": "Northeastern University", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "H\u00e9lio Gracie A patriarch of the Gracie family, he was the father of a UFC Hall of Famer considered by UFC fans to be the most influential figure in the history of what?", "answer": "modern MMA", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What Italian former professional footballer and manager scored the winning shot in the 1999-2000 FA Cup?", "answer": "Roberto Di Matteo", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What were the main subjects of photographs taken by William Clarridge in a medium-sized historic market town close to the western boundary of Hertfordshire, England?", "answer": "young girls", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "The Lake Koocanusa Scenic Byway begins in what county?", "answer": "Lincoln County", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Who wrote the book that was made into the film adaption that was the first movie Ridley Scott and Giannina Facio were partners during?", "answer": "Thomas Harris", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What records released the album that has \"Big Time Sensuality\" as fourth single?", "answer": "One Little Indian and Elektra Records", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Ray Shaw (born 27 April 1954) is a former Australian rules footballer who played for Collingwood in the Victorian Football League (VFL), his two sons also played for Collingwood, one son is Heath Shaw,   a professional Australian rules footballer playing for the Greater Western Sydney Giants in which organization? ", "answer": "Australian Football League (AFL)", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "For which state was the 44th Vice President of the United States a state senator?", "answer": "Indiana", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What is the nationality of the media escort of Myla Goldberg ?", "answer": "American", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Today's Pulse shares staff and resources with it's sister publication, that is a daily newspaper formed in 2013 from a merger between the Hamilton JournalNews and what other newspaper?", "answer": "The Middletown Journal", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "When was the player whom the Los Angeles Rams traded William Frederick Traux for born?", "answer": "October 14, 1943", "type": "bridge"}, {"