t\" did Judi Dench play?", "answer": "Ophelia", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "In which journal was the novel, from which the lyrics of Crystal Castle's \"Air War\" are from, first serialised?", "answer": "The Little Review", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Who is older, the band Kings of Leon or the artist Hozier?", "answer": "Andrew Hozier-Byrne", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Which poet was born first, A. E. Housman or Jaroslav Seifert ?", "answer": "A. E. Housman", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Vincent Angelo LaRusso s best known for playing the character of \"Adam Banks\" in a trilogy released by which company ?", "answer": "Walt Disney Pictures", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What musical was based on the 2003 film directed by Jon Favreau?", "answer": "Elf", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "UCLA Campus Events Commission had a film pre-screening for this 2014 American 3D computer-animated superhero-comedy film produced by who", "answer": "Walt Disney Animation Studios", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What overall number is the episode \"Go Fund Yourself\" of South Park?", "answer": "248th", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Atomic Skis, an Austrian ski company, is founded by who?", "answer": "Alois Rohrmoser (July 11, 1932 in Grossarl, Austria, \u2020 4, 2005 in Wagrain, Austria) is an Austrian Entrepreneurial leadership, and founder of Atomic Skis, in Altenmarkt im Pongau.", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "The head coach of the 2011 Indiana Hoosiers football team is the current offensive coordinator at what university?", "answer": "Ohio State University", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Sydney bus route L90 is operated by the agency that reports to whom?", "answer": "Andrew Constance", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Pampa Almir\u00f3n is a village and municipality in which province in north-eastern Argentina?", "answer": "Chaco Province", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What is the birth city of this Soviet and Russian actress and singer, who voiced Cheburashka in a 1966 story by Eduard Uspensky?", "answer": "Leningrad", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "The Vee Cliffs are located between The Terror Glaciar and this location that also shares a name with a spectacular light show often found in the higher lattitudes of the Arctic and Antarctica", "answer": "Aurora", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "In what year was the actor who was starred in \"Intrepid\" with James Coburn and Finola Hughes born?", "answer": "1965", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "The person Ed Zschau lost to in 1986 served as a United States Senator from California between what years?", "answer": "1969 to 1993", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What battle took place during an offensive that pushed the Germans out of France, forcing them to retreat beyond the Hindenburg Line?", "answer": "Battle of the Scarpe", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What hosted a radio show from 1995 to 2014 alongside hosts born in 1961 and 1968?", "answer": "Gregg \"Opie\" Hughes", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "When was the British Conservative politician died who's health never fully recovered after the botched operation on Foreign Minister in 1953?", "answer": "14 January 1977", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "State the birth date of one of Dil-e-Beqara's stars ?", "answer": "24 December 1989", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which band was formed first, The Pretenders or All Time Low?", "answer": "The Pretenders", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "In what state did the election of the governor and a member of senate get elected on November 4th, 2014?", "answer": "Kansas", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Who directed the cult horror film Holeg Spies made music for?", "answer": "Tom Six", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Peter Kohn worked with the Men's Lacrosse Team at this college founded in what year?", "answer": "1800", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "The LIGO Scientific Collaboration (LSC) is a scientific collaboration of international physics institutes and research groups dedicated to the search for gravitational waves, the LSC was established in 1997, under the leadership of Barry Barish, an American experimental physicist, he is a Linde Professor of Physics, emeritus at which institution?", "answer": "California Institute of Technology", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Who owns a 2,640-room hotel, casino and shopping promenade on the Las Vegas Strip that has a casino located within it that includes beer pong tables, a stage, a dance floor and a pit with games including blackjack, roulette, and craps?", "answer": "Caesars Entertainment Corporation", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Where was Mary Hill Fulstone born?", "answer": "Eureka County, Nevada, United States", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": " An english singer, songwriter and record producer has worked with a prominent rapper from what city?", "answer": "Chicago", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What profession does Andrew Murray and Ike Quartey have in common?", "answer": "boxer", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What fictional character featured in \"SpongeBob SquarePants\" first appeared in the episode \"Tea at the Treedome\"?", "answer": "Sandy Cheeks", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "The Xar file format is the fully specified vector graphics file format of  UK-based software company founded in what year?", "answer": "1981", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Larry Johnson is the father of which player, drafted by the Kansas City Chiefs in 2003?", "answer": "Larry Alphonso Johnson Jr.", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "BALR. is a brand co-founded by which \u0130stanbul Ba\u015fak\u015fehir winger?", "answer": "Eljero George Rinaldo Elia", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "The first Korean student movement begun in 1919, when students took part in the Sam-il Movement of 1 March to call for the end of Japanese colonization, after the Gwangju massacre in May 1980, the student movement got a clear vision, partly based on which form of socioeconomic analysis that explores class relations and societal conflict using a materialist interpretation of historical development and a dialectical view of social transformation \u2013 it originates from the mid-to-late 19th century works of the German philosopher Karl Marx?", "answer": "Marxism", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What is the other name  for a huge area of heavy fighting across Europe with the Soviet Union having occupied and annexed several countries effectively handed over by Nazi Germany?", "answer": "Second European War", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Who produced the third feature film that Park Jung-woo directed ?", "answer": "Lim Ji-young and Oz One Film", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What is the name of the complex where Aldrich Hazen Ames is serving a life sentence?", "answer": "Terre Haute Federal Correctional Complex", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "In which region was this prominent Indian singer who sang the Hindi song \"Mera Naam Chin Chin Chu\" born?", "answer": "Faridpur", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Sara Jane Moore, is an American citizen best known for attempting to assassinate US President Gerald Ford in 1975, Moore and Lynette \"Squeaky\" Fromme are the only two women to have attempted to assassinate an American president, \"Squeaky\" Fromme (born October 22, 1948) is an American would-be assassin, a member of which infamous family, she was sentenced to life imprisonment?", "answer": "Manson", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Results May Vary is the fourth studio album by a band whose vocalist was born on what day ?", "answer": "August 20, 1970", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What type of combat is specialized in the style of kung fu for which the character portrayed by Bryan Leung in Warriors Two is well known? ", "answer": "close range combat", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which singer is from the US, Jesse Michaels or Daryl Braithwaite?", "answer": "Jesse Michaels", "type": "comparison"}, {"question"