oen brothers on films such as which 1994 comedy film co-written, produced, and directed by Joel and Ethan Coen?", "answer": "The Hudsucker Proxy", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "For which state did this American politician serve as senator whose logo morphing from the apple logo was featured in \"Hillary 1984?\"", "answer": "Illinois", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Dreschhoff Peak is named after a physicist at a university that is one of how many members of the Association of American Universities?", "answer": "62", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Who is the artist in which James Abrahart has worked with and who rose to prominence after being featured on \"Hot Right Now?\" ", "answer": "Rita Sahat\u00e7iu Ora", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Multekrem and Kransekake are both traditional Norwegian desserts commonly eaten together during what winter holiday?", "answer": "Christmas", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Konarka Technologies was a spin off from the college located how far northwest of Boston?", "answer": "25 miles", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "which  lower chamber of the United States Congress is  Jim McGovern a  member?", "answer": "House of Representatives", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Yaroslava Shvedova and Lucie Hradeck\u00e1 both share what occupation?", "answer": "tennis player", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Who did Honora Edgeworth decline the hand of, even as she had a romantic engagement with a British Army officer hanged as a spy by the Continental Army?", "answer": "Thomas Day", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Who was loaned out by the \"Les Blues?\"", "answer": "Kurt Happy Zouma", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "How many senators represent the state where Vicki Schmidt is a Republic member?", "answer": "40 senators", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What religion does Hank Johnson practice and is on the Georgia's 4th congressional district?", "answer": "Buddhists", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Nathan Crowley (born 1966) is an English production designer and a former art director nominated for an Academy Award for Best Production Design for \"The Prestige\", a 2006 British-American mystery thriller film directed by who?", "answer": "Christopher Nolan", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Park Min-ha has appeared in the 2013 South Korean disaster film directed by whom?", "answer": "Kim Sung-su", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Who Shot Ya?, is a controversial hip-hop song by The Notorious B.I.G., the track was later released on the posthumous album \"Born Again\", the remastered edition of which debut studio album by American rapper The Notorious B.I.G.; it was released on September 13, 1994?", "answer": "Ready to Die", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which director was from Chile, L\u00e1szl\u00f3 Benedek or Ra\u00fal Ruiz?", "answer": "Ra\u00fal Ernesto Ruiz Pino", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Who was born first, Doro or Park Subin?", "answer": "Dorothee Pesch", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Which 2-time All-American from Louisville was inducted into the Naismith Memorial Basketball Hall of Fame in 1988?", "answer": "Wes Unseld", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What American novelist born in the Allegheny West neighborhood of Pittsburgh is also mentioned in a Scottish rock band song?", "answer": "Gertrude Stein", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What university did the defendant in a 2015 case who was tried by a Santa Clara county judge attend?", "answer": "Stanford University", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What kind of musical influences are found in the fifth single from the EP Christmas Kisses?", "answer": "R&B", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What type of media does Octane and Mischa Barton  have in common?", "answer": "film", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "In which year did a national football team featuring a striker for Premier League club Swansea City win the Africa Cup of Nations?", "answer": "1992", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "what album that had honky talk women on it and was the last week to feature Steven Tylor?", "answer": "Let It Bleed", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Were Camille Saint-Sa\u00ebns and Giacomo Puccini from the same country?", "answer": "no", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Who wrote the ballet, \"Romeo and Juliet\" which is regularly performed by the Joffrey Ballet?", "answer": "Sergei Prokofiev", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which musical revue directed by Richard Maltby Jr. is named after a song by Fats Waller?", "answer": "Ain't Misbehavin'", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Gil Duran is the former Press Secretary of a governor who is a member of which party ?", "answer": "the Democratic Party", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What genre of music were the band Noir D\u00e9sir and the band fronted by Adam Gontier known for?", "answer": "rock", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Who is the first season winner of the US version of the UK series \"Strictly Come Dancing\"?", "answer": "Kelly Marie Monaco", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Dime Magazine and McCall's, are which form of publication?", "answer": "magazine", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "What is the nationality of the director of a film that premiered at the Sundance Film Festival?", "answer": "American", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Who was the president that went into office after the assassination of the previous president and gave his State the Union Address when the American Civil War had ended?", "answer": "Andrew Johnson", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What company introduced a digital music workstation in 1992 and is the world's largest piano manufacturing company? A: Yamaha Corporation ", "answer": "Yamaha Corporation", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "When was the national park next to Ghost Town Village chartered by Congress?", "answer": "1934", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Who produced the series in which Nicholas Brendon played Kevin Lynch?", "answer": "The Mark Gordon Company", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Hollies Sing Hollies is the ninth studio album released by an English pop/roc group best known for their pioneering and distinctive what?", "answer": "three-part vocal harmony style", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What day month and year did rick lazio become well known for running against and losing to hilary clinton for the u.s senate?", "answer": "November 7, 2000", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What magazine has a strong emphasis on photojournalism, Life or New Era?", "answer": "and launched a major weekly news magazine with a strong emphasis on photojournalism.", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "When was the person who wrote \"Affirmative Action Around the World: An Empirical Study\" born?", "answer": "June 30, 1930", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What state has a historic town site for Overhill Cherokee, a term used by 18th-century European traders and explorers from British colonies along the Atlantic coast?", "answer": "Tennessee", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Who stared in the 1999 Italian movie Lucignolo and was born on 18 December 1971?", "answer": "Claudia Gerini", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What was the 1920's stage name of the actress who starred with Ernst Reicher and Johannes Riemann  in The Armoured Vault ?", "answer": "Imogene \"Bubbles\" Wilson.", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "How many Academy Awards did Walter Brennan win before the year that he starred in The North Star?", "answer": "three", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "The Magic Keyboard (Apple Magic Keyboard), is the current computer keyboard produced by Apple Inc. as the successor to the Apple Wireless Keyboard, manufactured in association with which multinational electronics contract manufacturing company headquartered in Tucheng, New Taipei, Taiwan, trading as what?", "answer": "Foxconn Technology Group", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What is the middle name of the American singer songwriter who has been pushing the boundaries of lyrical content and visual imagery and who has worked with Tessa Watts, the English music video and film producer at Virgin Records and MTV?", "answer": "Louise", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What is the name of the grange that was populated by the people who were affiliated with Whalley Abbey?", "answer": "Marland Grange", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What part of the Cahill Expressway is nicknamed \"The Coathanger\"?", "answer": "The Sydney Harbour Bridge", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "The Return of the Living Dead starred the actor and director who played what role on The Tall Man?", "answer": "William H. Bonney", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "In the Battle of G\u0142og\u00f3w  the Imperial forces were under command of Holy Roman Emperor and the fourth and last ruler of the what dynasty?", "answer": "Salian", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "When did the magazine that Dr. Eugene B. Habecker is the chairman of get founded?", "answer": "1956", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "how is Juliet Ibrahim and 4 Play connected?", "answer": "Ghanaian", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "NASA Astronaut Group 5 includes the last living pilot of which North American test flight program?", "answer": "X-15", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What battle tank was acquired from Germany by the Polish army, developed by Krauss-Maffei?", "answer": "Leopard 2", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Who directed the film in which Zach Tyler Eisen played Lucas Nickle?", "answer": "John A. Davis", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Diagonal Norte is located near what Plaza?", "answer": "Plaza de la Rep\u00fablica", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "The coach for whom Orlando Brown played in college was born in what year?", "answer": "1937", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "MyAllSearch gives results from which search engine that emphasizes searchers' privacy?", "answer": "DuckDuckGo", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "MxO was billed as an official continuation of the storyline of a franshise created by film directors formerly known as what?", "answer": "The Wachowski Brothers", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which actor stars in the Hong Kong television drama Men With No Shadows and has also starred in \"Vigilante Force\", \"Twin of Brothers\", \"Dicey Business\", \"Heart of Greed\", \"Moonlight Resonance\", \"Beyond the Realm of Conscience\", \"The Mysteries of Love\", \"The Other Truth\", \"The Hippocratic Crush\", and \"Silver Spoon, Sterling Shackles\"?", "answer": "Tavia Yeung", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Maki Nomiya and Max Carl, share which mutual occupation?", "answer": "singer", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Are Charles Burnett and Frank R. Strayer both African-Americans?", "answer": "no", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Foul papers are often used in the study of the plays of the poet who created approximately how many plays?", "answer": "38", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which NBC sitcom is star of the second and final season of ''\" now playing the afterlife \"architect\" Michael?", "answer": "\"The Good Place.", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Where is the company based that acquired MetCare  in 2012 ?", "answer": "Louisville, Kentucky.", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "\"Bring Out the Bottles\" is a song by American singer, dancer, DJ and rapper Redfoo, also known for being half of the duo LMFAO,  an American electronic dance music duo consisting of Redfoo and SkyBlu. Who are related to each other how?", "answer": "uncle and nephew", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Who built the resort that Kathy Griffin recorded Look at My Butt Crack at?", "answer": "developer Steve Wynn", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "what \"eighth wonder of the world location hosted a boxing match between Ali amd Mathis?", "answer": "The Astrodome", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which footballer shares a hometown with the Egyptian who plays for Liverpool and the Egypt national team?", "answer": "Ahmed Elmohamady", "type":