roducer?", "answer": "Armin van Buuren", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "The cover for the video game \"NHL 11\" features a player born in what year?", "answer": "1988", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which party did both David Soares and Paul Clyne belong to when they first ran against each other in September 2004?", "answer": "the Democratic Party", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "How far southeast of Xalapa is the city at the east end of Mexican Federal Highway 150?", "answer": "90 km", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "The Complex Rock Tour Live DVD by Blue Man Group features a cover of a song by The Who that was released in what year?", "answer": "1971", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "When was the man that studied Transcendental Meditation with Harrison  when he wrote \"Circles\" born? ", "answer": "12 January 1918", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "how is SoHo, Hong Kong and Lan Kwai Fong related?", "answer": "Central", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What was a notable difference between the Apple IIc and the Newbear 77-68?", "answer": "The Newbear 77-68 was a kit of parts", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Who is the director of the upcoming film based on the real-life cases of Ed and Lorraine Warren?", "answer": "Corin Hardy", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Root Beer Guy is an episode of a serieis which was officially premiered when?", "answer": "April 5, 2010", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What rock band was the mentor of Jimmy McCulloch the lead guitarist for?", "answer": "the Who", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "When did Coop, the owner of the largest supermarket chain in Italy, launch CoopVoce?", "answer": "June 1, 2007", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Who composed the music for the 2007 comedy film in which Emma de Caunes played Sabine?", "answer": "Howard Goodall", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which railway station was Windermere Hotel located near ", "answer": "Windermere railway station", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Emas