ember 1963?", "answer": "Caroline Aherne", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Christian Kane stared in a 2003 romantic comedy film that was produced by who?", "answer": "Robert Simonds", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "BusyBox software has been compared to a mutli-tool pocket knife manufactured by what company?", "answer": "Victorinox AG", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "The 2010\u201311 season was Birmingham City Football Club' s seventh season in the Premier League and their 57th in the top tier of English football,  won the League Cup, their first major trophy since 1963, by beating favourites Arsenal 2\u20131 in the final with goals from Nikola \u017digi\u0107 and Obafemi Akinwunmi Martins (born 28 October 1984) is a Nigerian footballer who plays as a forward for which team? ", "answer": "Shanghai Greenland Shenhua", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "the 2012 production Empire charting the rise of the British Empire from the trading companies of India was co-produced by BBC and which research university?", "answer": "Open University", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Who is a founding member of Joy Division, Peter Cox or Bernard Sumner?", "answer": "Bernard Sumner", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Walter Mart is home to which leader of the largest healthcare and beauty store chain in Asia?", "answer": "Watsons", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "In what film does Jake Gyllenhaal play a coal miner's son, who gets inspired by the 1957 launch of \"Sputnik 1\", to take up rocketry?", "answer": "October Sky", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which musician was born first, George Michael or Tom Petty?", "answer": "Thomas Earl Petty", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Of which company was a Domestic Television which was one of the producer of \"On the Red Carpet\"  a division?", "answer": "The Walt Disney Company", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "In which city is the conference, where Texas Longhorns women's volleyball competes, headquartered?", "answer": "Irving", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Who was an adivisor to the eighth leader of the Soviet Union who died in 2006? ", "answer": "Vadim Valentinovich Zagladin", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which was established first, Case Western Reserve University or Grinnell College?", "answer": "Grinnell College", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Dark Ages was developed by which South Koream online gaming company?", "answer": "Nexon", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Who is the Mexican-American bassist that plays for the band Big Sir?", "answer": "Juan Alderete", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Christopher Isherwood and Charles Reznikoff, have which mutual nationality?", "answer": "American", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Daniel Dromm is a council member from the district that includes which northwestern Queens neighborhood?", "answer": "Jackson Heights", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "The Professional DJ Clue?'s debut studio album features which artist?", "answer": "Nas", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which was a civil rights judgment, Garner v. Louisiana or Canterbury v. Spence?", "answer": "Garner v. Louisiana", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Matt Walsh starred in a 2014 disaster movie about tornadoes striking which city ?", "answer": "Silverton, Oklahoma", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "The ruler who the Welser were financiers for when they rose to great prominence in international high finance was born on what date? ", "answer": "24 February 1500", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Who wrote the hymn that was reworked into a song concerning the death, funeral, and mourning of the narrator's mother, by an American musician and founding member of The Carter Family, one of the most notable acts in the history of country music?", "answer": "Ada R. Habershon and Charles H. Gabriel", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What is the name of the program funded by a national network of 33 Sea Grant Colleges and universities involved in scientific research, education, training, and extension projects geared toward the conservation and practical use of the coasts, Great Lakes, and other marine areas?", "answer": "Wisconsin Sea Grant", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which pharmaceutical company has its headquarters in McKesson Plaza?", "answer": "McKesson Corporation", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which is a genus native to more areas of the world, Ailanthus or Leonotis? ", "answer": "Leonotis", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Who was a Civil Rights leader that was born into slavery?", "answer": "Harriet Tubman", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Who co-invented the refrigerator that had it's manufacturing rights sold to an American manufacturer founded in 1922?", "answer": "Carl Munters", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Lee Yong-soo was a woman who worked in the industry that was instigated by what group?", "answer": "Imperial Japanese Army", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Natalie Venetia Belcon stars in which broadway musical?", "answer": "Avenue Q", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Are Nikolai Rimsky-Korsakov and Giovanni Paisiello both composers?", "answer": "yes", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "The city where Derrick Spencer was born was officially recognised as one of the New7Wonders Cities in what year?", "answer": "2015", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "\"High Maintenance\" is a song that features the lead vocalist of a band that has sold 9.2 million what?", "answer": "albums in the US", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "How many acres is the Disney's Animal Kingdom themed area featuring the Na'vi River Journey?", "answer": "12 acres", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Gotta Have You is a song from the soundtrack of a film set in what city?", "answer": "New York City", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which Linkin Park album takes its title from the Doomsday clock and helped to earn the band a Grammy nomination?", "answer": "Minutes to Midnight", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which of the following is a quarterly journal of folk music: Country Living or Sing Out!?", "answer": "Sing Out!", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Causeway Lane is a street that runs between Little Collins Street and Bourke Street, the latter of which is a core feature of what?", "answer": "Hoddle Grid", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Elwood worked with MCA, who was the founding member of what hip hop group?", "answer": "Beastie Boys", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What is the nationality of the actor who voices Nathan Drake in the Uncharted video game series ?", "answer": "American", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What silent film adapted from the novel \"The Clamsman\" did Elmer Clifton appear in?", "answer": "The Birth of a Nation", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which band was formed first Blue October or The Sugarcubes ?", "answer": "The Sugarcubes", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "The new Movie, \"Rampage,\" stars what actress who also stared in the critically acclaimed film \"Moonlight\"?", "answer": "Naomie Harris", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "By whom was Zaladane, the fictional character created by Marvel Comics, written?", "answer": "Arnold Drake and Jim Steranko", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which college team went 7-5 under the coach who is now the head coach of the Detroit Lions of the National Football League (NFL)?", "answer": "Wake Forest Demon Deacons", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": " The Places in Between is a travel narrative by a British diplomat, politician, writer and former chair of what?", "answer": "House of Commons Defence Select Committee", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Was Giant Drag or Cracker formed first?", "answer": "Cracker", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Princess Victoria Louise of Prussia was the great-granddaughter of a Queen of Great Britian and Ireland that adopted what additional title in 1876?", "answer": "Empress of India", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What was stage debut for the actress that voic