n a Northern Irish professional footballer who won the European Cup with Manchester United, and was named the European Footballer of the Year and FWA Footballer of the Year, who was this football player?", "answer": "George Best", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "This song mentioned above is sung in what language? ", "answer": "English", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "How did the winner of the 1967 Pau Grand Prix die?", "answer": "he was killed during practice", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Who composed lyrics for the rock musical by Andrew Lloyd Webber that has the love duet \"Only You?\"", "answer": "Richard Stilgoe", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Jonathan Clark is the older brother to a fellow soldier who was what? ", "answer": "surveyor, soldier, and militia officer", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What was the Italian general who's theories strong opponent was Amedeo Mecozz's \"Attack air force\" doctrine?", "answer": "air power theorist", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Are both Lydia Zimmermann and Miranda July Canadian film directors?", "answer": "no", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Nivdung is a drama film by which music composer from India?", "answer": "Hridaynath Mangeshkar", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Mauricio \"Baboo\" Da Silva, is a Brazilian kyokushin kaikan full contact karate practitioner and former professional kickboxer and mixed martial artist, he's aprofessional coach and trainer of K-1 and MMA (Mixed Martial Arts), who has trained a number of world class fighters including which American-Samoan kickboxer, boxer and mixed martial artist of Samoan heritage who competes in the Heavyweight division, often billed as who? ", "answer": "Mighty Mo", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Montesquieu and which English philosopher and physician believed in liberalism?", "answer": "John Locke", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Who is the actress from the 1963 comedy film \"My Six Loves\" (1963) that also appeared in \"Three Little Words\"