r": "mini-marts", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What Canadian folk singer and songwriter performed with Jack Nissenson in The Mountain City Four?", "answer": "Anna McGarrigle", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Encyclopedia of Afghan Jihad was a manual found in the residence of which Egyptian cleric?", "answer": "Abu Hamza al-Masri", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which of these two pizzerias has had the same owners for longer, Regina Pizzeria or Pietro's Pizza?", "answer": "Regina Pizzeria", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Dane DeHaan played the title character in which 2017 3D film written by Luc Besson?", "answer": "Valerian and the City of a Thousand Planets", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What is the birthday of the lead vocalist of the band that released \"Live in Manila\"?", "answer": "September 5, 1967", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What is the birthday of the actress who starred in \"I Love Lucy\", and Yours, Mine, and Ours?", "answer": "August 6, 1911", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which of these was a French lawyer, Nathalie Sarraute or Robert Olmstead?", "answer": "Nathalie Sarraute", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Who was born first, Mike Shinoda or Nam Woo-hyun?  ", "answer": "Michael Kenji Shinoda", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "What is the highest mountain in Germany, ahead of the Hochwanner the highest peak on the main ridge of the Wetterstein, lying south of the town of Garmisch-Partenkirchen?", "answer": "Zugspitze", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Sheldon Thomas played for what team that was based in the Los Angeles suburb of Carson, California?", "answer": "LA Galaxy", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Both Zixing and Baotou are cities in what Asian country?", "answer": "China", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Did authors Sigrid de Lima and Irving Stone both live at least part of their lives in California?", "answer": "yes", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Are Hayley Williams of the band Paramore and Preston of the band The Ordinary Boys both lead singers?", "answer": "yes", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": " Donald Corren is an American Broadway and film actor and screenwriter who created the role of Cosm\u00e9 McMoon opposite Judy Kaye's Florence Foster Jenkins,  an American socialite and amateur soprano who was known and mocked for her flamboyant performance costumes and what poor ability?", "answer": "singing", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What was the 2011 net worth of the executive producer of \"I'm Bad\"", "answer": "$340 million", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What was the name of the best selling book about serial killers that was written by a former chief reporter of national red top newspaper published in the United Kingdom?", "answer": "Inside 25 Cromwell Street", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "As of 2011, what is the population of the parish that lies to the west of Temple Bruer with Temple High Grange?", "answer": "356", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Who released the Sia album that featured Sean Paul?", "answer": "Inertia, Monkey Puzzle and RCA Records", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "what movie title is in both paragraphs", "answer": "Back to the Future is a 1985 American science-fiction adventure comedy film", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "When was the chair of The Nineteenth Canadian Ministry born?", "answer": "23 April 1897", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "do  Roupen Altiparmakian and John Matoian work in the same industry? ", "answer": "no", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Who is older, Rose McDowall or Paul Roberts?", "answer": "Rose McDowall", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Joe Darone was in the punk bank The Fiendz and another band known for what subgenre of punk?", "answer": "horror punk", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "In 1989 what acclamation was given to the director of the film The Overcoat ?", "answer": "a Hero of Socialist Labour", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "\"Whenever God Shines His Light\" is 