her that had what last name?", "answer": "Gormsson", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "The birthplace of Valerie Brisco-Hooks is located in which county?", "answer": "Leflore County", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What big cat is Venghai named for?", "answer": "Jaguar", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What political party predated the party shared by Abdul Hai Neamati and Ismail Khan", "answer": "United National Front party.", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What British show is a Jewish comedian created Russian sketch show based on?", "answer": "Little Britain", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What was the common abbreviation for the railroad by which the Cricket Tunnel and Crest Tunnel were built?", "answer": "MoPac", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What reed instrument was played by Indian musician S. R. D. Vaidyanathan?", "answer": "the Nadhaswara", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Return of the Living Dead: Necropolis stars what actress known for a role on \"One Tree Hill\"?", "answer": "Jana Kramer", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What year was the first broadcast of the show which is similar to \"Night of a Thousand Boyfreinds\"?", "answer": "1998", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "In which U.S. state is the city which was served by the Floridian train, affectionately known as \"The River City\"?", "answer": "the State of Alabama", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Kansas's 1st congressional district is a congressional district in the U.S. state of Kansas, Huelskamp was re-elected twice in 2012 and 2014, but lost the 2016 Republican primary for a fourth term to which obstetrician, and an American politician?", "answer": "Roger Marshall", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which film was released first The Odd Life of Timothy Green or  James and the Giant Peach ?", "answer": "James and the Giant Peach", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "How many caps has the father of a Finnish footballer who plays as a striker for Dynamo Dresden, on loan from AIK, has