s the  American singer, songwriter born who's live album is Wanda Live! at Third Man Records?", "answer": "October 20, 1937", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Live at Bell's was an album the band that has a home base at the brewing company in what city?", "answer": "Kalamazoo,", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Who is the co-executive producer of the film in which Dean Edwards voiced a robot?", "answer": "Christy Karacas", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which university is a public research university, Ashesi University or National Autonomous University of Mexico?", "answer": "National Autonomous University of Mexico", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Who founded the record label that Strange Pleasures released their second full-length album with?", "answer": "Bruce Pavitt", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "The Association for Contemporary Music's leading members include what Russian composer of the early Soviet era, best known for his early futurist piano sonatas, orchestral episodes, and vocal music?", "answer": "Alexander Vasilyevich Mosolov", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "How many BAFTA TV Awards have been won by the DJ that premiered the song \"That's the Truth\" on British Radio?", "answer": "five-time", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What is the name of this region of Italy, referring to the medieval March of Ancona and nearby marches of Camerino and Fermo, where the comune Pollenza is located?", "answer": "Marche", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What 2010 prize did the writer of the lyrics for Making Tracks win?", "answer": "Pulitzer Prize for Drama", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What year was the film released that features a United States Navy \"Iowa\"-class battleship?", "answer": "1992", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Who wrote the screenplay for a 1959 American Southern Gothic Mystery in which English stage designer, Oliver Messel did the production design?", "answer": "Gore Vidal", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Who passed away first, Jack Gilbert or Tom Clancy ?", "answer": "Jack Gilbert", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Eleanor's Secret and Up are what type of films?", "answer": "animated feature film", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "What former Italian footballer is the manager of the Milan team which claimed its first league title for five seasons", "answer": "Carlo Ancelotti", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Who directed secretprojectrevolution with the American singer and songwriter born in 1958?", "answer": "Steven Klein", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What is the name of the future head coach of the University of Pittsburgh football team whom Dick Jauron replaced as head coach of the Chicago Bears on January 24, 1999?", "answer": "Dave Wannstedt", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "James Redfield and James A. Michener, share which mutual occupation?", "answer": "author", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Which university has more students enrolled, Saint Louis University or the University of Missouri System?", "answer": "University of Missouri System", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": " David Victor Canter is a psychologist that helped police on a case involving two serial killers who attacked numerous women and children in the south of what?", "answer": "England", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "In what year was the football player featured in The Blind Side drafted into the NFL?", "answer": "2009", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Do the pizza stores Your Pie and The Pizza Studio offer numerous customization options?", "answer": "yes", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Tanedra Howard, who played Simone Bethson in the 2009 American horror film \"Saw VI\", was the winner of which reality show?", "answer": "Scream Queens", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which German actress starred as Senora Fourneau?", "answer": "Lilli Palmer", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which plant is found in more southern regions of the world, Dendrocalamus or Chamaedaphne", "answer":