hem to the Final Four NCAA Basketball Tournament, what was his name?", "answer": "Jerry Tarkanian", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "The director of In the Sun also worked with what other famous artists?", "answer": "Depeche Mode and U2", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "J. Searle Dawley and Genndy Tartakovsky, have which mutual occupations?", "answer": "director and screenwriter", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "When did the construction begin for the former home of the Houston Livestock Show and Rodeo?", "answer": "1962", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "The One and Only... is a British entertainment show was presented by a man who claims to be the only O'Connor who ever had a what?", "answer": "Bar Mitzvah", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Who did Andre Agassi lose to when competing in the2000 Legg Mason Tennis Classic \u2013 Singles", "answer": "\u00c0lex Corretja", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Milo Murphy's Law (previously titled Mikey Murphy's Law) is an American animated television series from the creators of \"Phineas and Ferb\", the series revolves around the title character, Milo Murphy, who is a descendant of Edward A. Murphy Jr., was an American aerospace engineer who worked on safety-critical systems, and the namesake of which term,?", "answer": "Murphy's law", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What is the name of the American singer songwriter and television personality whose identity was used in an off-Broadway musical based on 'American Idol' where contestants dream of winning a spot as the opening act for this celebrities new tour?", "answer": "Clay Aiken", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "B. Dalton was founded by the same family that also founded what Minneapolis-based store chain?", "answer": "Dayton's", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Jason Ballantine was nominated for an award for what 2005 Australian horror film?", "answer": "Wolf Creek", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Who does Wim Jonk manage Cruyff Football with?", "answer": "Jord