n  October 12, 1992?", "answer": "Josh Hutcherson", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Prato Rio was the home of a general who served in the Polish army under what king?", "answer": "King Stanislaus II", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which actor known for his roles on the television shows \"Party of Five\" and \"7th Heaven\" also stared in a 2001 film based off of William Shakespeare's \"Othello\"?", "answer": "Andrew Keegan", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Heliopsis and Cosmos are both genuses for which family of flowering plants?", "answer": "sunflower", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Lakeland, New York derived its name from the lake located northwest of what major city?", "answer": "Syracuse", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "In what year was the transgender actress who purchased Mexico y Barra Restaurant with Ryan Allen Carrillo born?", "answer": "1971", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which position did this American actress, singer, dancer, businesswoman, and diplomat who resigned from the San Francisco International Film Festival over the Swedish movie entry \"Night Games\" in 1966 serve abroad as an adult?", "answer": "United States ambassador", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What governor-general of the Philippines in the 18th century had the same last name as a Spanish autonomous city on the north coast of Africa?", "answer": "Pedro Manuel de Arand\u00eda Santisteban", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "The Frogman Corps is the maritime special operations force of the unified armed forces of what kingdom?", "answer": "Kingdom of Denmark", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "The 2009 Minneapolis mayoral election was held on November 3, 2009 to elect the Mayor of Minneapolis for a four-year term, incumbent R. T. Rybak won re-election for a third term, Rybak is an American politician, journalist, businessperson, and activist who served as which number mayor of Minneapolis?", "answer": "46th", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which store served by Connoisseur's Bakery is actually a symbol group of independent retailers? ", "answer": "Nisa", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "The inventor of the Graphophone also founded what company in 1885?", "answer": "American Telephone and Telegraph Company", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What is the year of the event that occured first, Poleconomy was published, or Take It Easy was published?", "answer": "1980", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "What industry did both John Grierson and Sam Raimi work in?", "answer": "film", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Rob Nilsson and Ted Demme, are in which mutual industry?", "answer": "film", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Which film director is older, Pavel Ruminov or Harry Lachman?", "answer": "Harry B. Lachman", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "This school founded in 1906 as a land grant college is only a few blocks away from the Georgia Southern Botanical Garden", "answer": "Georgia Southern University", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What Forward from the Premier League club Arsenal scored a goal in the Major League Soccer All-Star Game, on July 27, 2011?", "answer": "Danny Welbeck", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "The 51st Governor of Alabama won the election on 3 November 1998 against which Republican candidate?", "answer": "Fob James", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Who is older, Steve Dildarian or Ian Bremmer?", "answer": "Steve Dildarian", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Who are the parents of the god who has a temple in Esanai?", "answer": "Shiva and Mohini", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What Canadian thrash metal band released a compilation album as a free download in 2010?", "answer": "Annihilator", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "808s & Heartbreak is an album by whom?", "answer": "Kanye West.", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Between Sidney Sheldon and Allegra Goodman, who had a more diverse career?", "answer": "Sidney Sheldon", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Fulda Cathedral is the burial place of the leading figure in what?", "answer": "Anglo-Saxon mission", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "The Equatorial Convention Centre is located in what city in Maldives that consists of the inhabited islands of the southernmost atoll of the archipelago?", "answer": "Addu City", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Are Niagara and Twister produced by the same company?", "answer": "no", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "What artist does Love and Loyalty have in common?", "answer": "Kendrick Lamar", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What year was the Labour Party politician representing Warrington South Mayor of Warrington?", "answer": "2016", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Armond White has had work published in which neoconservative religious journal?", "answer": "First Things", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "How many islands are in the island group where Steven Raymond Christian was born ?", "answer": "four", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Parsley and Nandina, are a species of what?", "answer": "flowering plant", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Which genus is in the family Brassicaceae, Aethionema or Dionysia?", "answer": "Aethionema", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Edoardo Ponti is the brother of which Italian orchestral conductor?", "answer": "Carlo Ponti Jr.", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "In what year was Tony Johnson's older brother born?", "answer": "1979", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Elena Duggan was the winnder of a 2016 series that airs on what network?", "answer": "Network Ten", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "In what year did Lee Eun-woo both star in the intially banned film Mobius and get nominate for Best New Actress at the 34th Blue Dragon Film Awards?", "answer": "2013", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which was released first, Gunner Palace or War/Dance?", "answer": "Gunner Palace", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Which state is the maker of Turbo Drop located in?", "answer": "Utah", "type": "bridge"}, {"questio