ation of the Firearms Act 1995?", "answer": "The \u00c9cole Polytechnique massacre", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What mode allows users to play The Last of us with other individuals in partnership, competition, or rivalry?", "answer": "online multiplayer", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "When was the 2016 Oregon Rebulican primary held?", "answer": "May 17", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which 1999 book was written by the creator and host of \"Dreamland?\"", "answer": "The Coming Global Superstorm", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Are Gloria Naylor and Dorothy L. Sayers both nationals of the same country ?", "answer": "no", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "D1  was closed when this agency, created in 1916, petitioned to allow climbing", "answer": "National Park Service", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Yukshin Gardan Sar and Gyachung Kang, are record breaking mountain what?", "answer": "peak", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "The German word Kreis and the Thai word Monthon both translate to what?", "answer": "circle", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Retired Soviet freestyle swimmer Vladimir Valeryevich Bure is the fater of Russian-American former ice hockey right winger Valeri Vladimirovich \"Val\" Bure  and what other retiered NHL player?", "answer": "Pavel", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Cheick Guillaume Ouedraogo holds notable wins over a mixed martial artist who is known particularly for his what?", "answer": "low kicks.", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which executive producer also played Deandra Reynold in \"It's Always Sunny in Philadelphia?\"", "answer": "Kaitlin Olson", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which city is the university that Tim Tadlock coaches baseball for located in?", "answer": "Lubbock, Texas", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Local boys was what starring an American actor whos roles include the title role in the 2003 live action film \"Peter Pan\"?", "answer": "2002 American coming of age drama film", "type": "bridge"}