g a 2015 romantic comedy staring Amy Schumer?", "answer": "John Russell Houser", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "The Quest of Erebor was published by the third son of which novelist?", "answer": "J. R. R. Tolkien", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What group primarily wrote and conducted an album that features a singer/songwriter from the South Korean Chinese boy group EXO?", "answer": "Far East Movement", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Are Harris Corporation and Darden Restaurants both American companies?", "answer": "yes", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "What team finished third in the AFC South during the 88th regular NFL season?", "answer": "Jacksonville Jaguars", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Yang Seung-Pil, is a South Korean actor, he has two supporting roles in the historical television series \"Maids\" (2015), in English language literature sageuk usually refers to historical films and television series, of which location?", "answer": "South Korea", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which German-born comedian played in the movie Bad Boys?", "answer": "Martin Lawrence", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "A video game where contestants race through off-road environments was made popular first by which famous off road racer from the late 80's and early 90's?", "answer": "Ivan Stewart", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What street named after a British parliamentarian and social reformist runs to the west of Rundle Mall?", "answer": "Hindley Street", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What national park in Virginia does the Hughes River run through?", "answer": "Shenandoah National Park", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Who directed the movie in 1988 featuring the actress who starred in Gidget and the Flying nun?", "answer": "David Seltzer", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Who played the composer of \"The Liberty Bell\" in Stars and Stripes Forever? ", "answer": "Clifton Webb", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Matthew Casey is a fictional character portrayed by actor Jesse Spencer on which American drama tv show that debuted in 2012?", "answer": "\"Chicago Fire\"", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which province does this Australian Senator and media personality represent, with whom Alyson Best appeared in a famous photo in \"Playboy?\"", "answer": "Victoria", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What American rubber company bought Crosley Motors, Incorporated?", "answer": "General Tire", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What is Monica's former fianc\u00e9's real name?", "answer": "Rodney Ramone Hill, Jr.", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What Disney sitcom premiered on February 27,2012 and featured Tyrel Jackson Williams?", "answer": "Lab Rats", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What band formed first, Shinedown or The dB's?", "answer": "The dB's", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Strawberry Jam Comics published a successful comic involcing Turles, one writer was born January 27 and known as what?", "answer": "Peter Laird", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": " Narinder Kumar Mehra is the founding head of the department of transplant immunology and immunogenetics at a college established in what year?", "answer": "1956", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Jim Dziura is an American film director, cinematographer, and editor, in 2001, Jim directed a feature-length documentary about Swedish musician Moneybrother for Red Bull, an energy drink sold by Austrian company Red Bull GmbH, created in which year?", "answer": "1987", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "The 1979 play \"Bent\" takes place during and after a purge that took place in Nazi Germany in what year?", "answer": "1934", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Julie Halard-Decugis and Fabrice Santoro, have which mutual ocuppation?", "answer": "professional tennis player", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Caesarea Golf Club was established by the family who were integral in which German industry?", "answer": "banking", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Frank Augustus Miller owned an Inn that is the a member of what official program of the National Trust for Historic Preservation?", "answer": "Historic Hotels of America", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "David Whatton QPM, a retired British senior police officer, was the Chief Constable of a territorial police force responsible for policing the English unitary authorities of Cheshire East, Cheshire West and Chester, Halton (including Runcorn, and Widnes) and what other authority?", "answer": "Warrington", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "How many games did Mel Tucker replace Jack Del Rio for?", "answer": "five games", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Who was born first Conor Oberst or Jesse Leach?", "answer": "Jesse David Leach", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Walkinshaw Racing is an Australian motor racing team based in the Melbourne suburb of Clayton, Victoria, which at the 2011 Census, had a population of what?", "answer": "15,543", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Harris Yulin appeared in this 1983 movie about which Cuban refugee?", "answer": "Tony Montana", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Just Dance Kids is a video game for which console released by Nintendo on November 19, 2006?", "answer": "Wii", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "The Frazer (1946\u20131951) was the flagship line of upper-medium priced American luxury automobiles built by which organization, the result of a partnership between automobile executive Joseph W. Frazer and industrialist Henry J. Kaiser?", "answer": "Kaiser-Frazer Corporation", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Who has been the host of ITV game shows Cash Trapped and Spin Star?", "answer": "Bradley Walsh", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which uncompleted opera was written by the composer of Croquefer, ou Le dernier des paladins?", "answer": "The Tales of Hoffmann", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "The founder of which american rock band, formed in the late 90s in California, is responsible for composition of the score for the 2003 drama directed by Ed Solomon and filmed in Montreal, Canada? ", "answer": "Eels", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What was the birth date of an English actor known for his boisterous roles who played in a film set in a futuristic mining site on an unspecific moon?", "answer": "13 June 1943", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Are both 500 Years Later and Fig Trees documentaries?", "answer": "yes", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Pussy Cat Doll's producer Jimmy lovine co founded what record company?", "answer": "Interscope Records", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What Evangelical Christian leader who founded Prison Fellowship, Prison Fellowship International, and BreakPoint was a hatchet man for  President Richard Nixon?", "answer": "Charles Colson", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "North is a 1994 American comedy drama adventure film, which American actress made her film debut in the fantasy comedy?", "answer": "Scarlett Johansson", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Sir Neil was a founding member of the Order of the Garter, established by a king whose reign was how long?", "answer": "50 years", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Land of Silence and Darkness and Gates of Heaven, are films of which genre?", "answer": "documentary", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "What nationality was the person whose music inspired the Folias Flute and Guitar Duo ?", "answer": "Argentine", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "The Unknown Known, is a 2013 American documentary film about the political career of former U.S. Secretary of Defense and congressman Donald Rumsfeld, an American retired politician and businessman, heserved as the 13th Secretary of Defense from 1975 to 1977 under which President?  ", "answer": "Gerald Ford", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Dan Wilson and Bert McCracken, have which mutual occupations?", "answer": "singer and songwriter", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Who has more scope of profession, Victor Hugo Halperin or Aleksander Ford?", "answer": "Victor 