rthur and the Revenge of Maltazard", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Who is older, Danan Januzaj or David Moyes?", "answer": "David Moyes", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What German born racing driver raced against lost the 1970 International Gold Cup to John Surtees and later dies during a practice for the Italian Grand Prix?", "answer": "Jochen Rindt", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "John Stuart Anderson was a Professor of Chemistry at a university that was founded in what year?", "answer": "1853", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "The 2016 City of Onkaparinga ATP Challenger took place in a metropolitan suburb how far south of the Central Business District of Adelaide?", "answer": "20 km", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which one of the five Cricketers of the Century has their cricket bat on display at the Museum of Antigua and Barbuda?", "answer": "Viv Richards", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "When was the game after Zork Zero published?", "answer": "1980", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Where was the castle located in which is related to William Douglas and Margaret Hay?", "answer": "Gifford in East Lothian, Scotland", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "In which competition held in Buenos Aires, Argentina did Stanly Stanczyk win a gold medal?", "answer": "The 1951 Pan American Games", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What film starring Matthew Broderick also became the third-longest-running musical in Broadway history, garnering six Tony Awards including Best Musical? ", "answer": "The Lion King", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Harry Prout was a former captain at a college in what city?", "answer": "Melbourne", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What British company that operates the John Lewis department stores was founded by William Crabtree?", "answer": "John Lewis Partnership", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Shepherd Gate Clock was probably the first to display the solar time at which location in London?", "answer": "Royal Observatory", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Q1.)Who has majority ownership of an Icelandic-based airline WOW air, headquarted in Reykajavik and is based at the Keflavik International Airport?  A1.)Sk\u00fali Mogensen", "answer": "Sk\u00fali Mogensen", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "This actor starred in the BBC series \"Sherlock\" and was named Best Supporting Actor in 2012 for his performance in Nick Perry's radio play \"Referee\"?", "answer": "Andrew Scott", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What male actor starred in a 2014 superhero sequel alongside the actor who shot Brandon Lee in \"The Crow?\"", "answer": "Andrew Garfield", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "MGM Records produced a 1954 revival of an off-Broadway musical; what is the name of opera this musical was adapted from?", "answer": "\"The Beggar's Opera\"", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": " Sarah Dunn a television writer is known for novels and the ABC sitcom \"American Housewife\", starring an actress who was born in what year? ", "answer": "1981", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "The Bellerose Village Municipal Complex is located in what county?", "answer": "Nassau County", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Who did the box cover art for Keith Martin to make Night Below?", "answer": "Jeff Easley", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Did F. Gary Gray and Nicola Black both direct the movie \"Friday\"?", "answer": "no", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "\"The Sponge Who Could Fly\" was the name of an episode for a show that aired on what network?", "answer": "Nickelodeon", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which channel featured a show with Joe Tracini and laucnhed in 2000?", "answer": "Boomerang", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Muraba\u1e25ah is a term for a sales contract where the buyer and seller agree on the markup (profit) or \"cost-plus\" price for the item(s) being sold, which covers the cost of what?", "answer": "doing business", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What magazine was Dr. Mehemed Fehmy Agha associated with