ny?", "answer": "Apple Records", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What hotel did Carl Cohen  manage that operated from 1952 to 1996?", "answer": "Sands Hotel and Casino", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Margarete Berta \"Gretl\" Braun, was one of the two sisters of Eva Braun, raun married who, which was a high-ranking commander in the Waffen-SS of Nazi Germany, and a liaison officer on Hitler's staff, on 3 June 1944?", "answer": "Hermann Fegelein", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What professional wrestler that is currently part of the Killer Elite Squad shares a first name with a member of the Rock 'n' Rave infection?", "answer": "Lance Hoyt", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "The 2005 KNVB Cup Final included a goal by which now-manager of PSV?", "answer": "Phillip John-William Cocu", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "The Division of Angas was named for the founder of which colony on the continent of Australia? ", "answer": "the Colony of South Australia", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Where was the decree issued that Antoine Galland  was called upon, with two other experts, to make  lithographic copies of in Cairo ?", "answer": "Memphis, Egypt", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What was the 2010 population of the city Frank Lautenberg is from?", "answer": "146,199", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What is the name of the 2011 $1,000,000 winner of the reality show \"Survivor\" who appeared in \"The Amazing Race\"  with Amber Joy Mariano?", "answer": "Rob Mariano", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which of the following directors was a friend of Max Reinhardt: Marco Bellocchio or F. W. Murnau?", "answer": "Friedrich Wilhelm \"F. W.\" Murnau", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Elijah Connor, an American pop singer, is best known for his roll on an American reality television dating game show that was a spin-off of what series?", "answer": "The Apprentice", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Cloudburst is a famous composition by what American composer?", "answer": "Eric Whitacre", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "The Battle of Nuremberg, is the nickname of a football match played in the Round of 16 of the 2006 FIFA World Cup between Portugal and the Netherlands at the Frankenstadion, which stadium in Nuremberg, Germany, which was opened in 1928. [4] It is located next to Zeppelinfeld. [5] It also neighbors the Nuremberg Arena?", "answer": "Max-Morlock-Stadion", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": " Dan Barreiro is a sports radio talk-show host on a radio station owned by which company ?", "answer": "iHeartMedia", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What was the middle name of the owner of the Clermont Club?", "answer": "Victor", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Marc Cantin played for the Coventry Blaze in a league located where?", "answer": "United Kingdom", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Who was a politician, Gene Wilder or Cheick Oumar Sissoko?", "answer": "Cheick Oumar Sissoko", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Who, Henri Bergson or David Edgar, is a British playwright and writer who has had more than sixty of his plays published and performed on stage, radio and television around the world, making him one of the most prolific dramatists of the post-1960s generation in Great Britain?", "answer": "David Edgar", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "The song Tell Me Why on the album Maya is recorded by what English artist?", "answer": "M.I.A.", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Dan Seymour appeared in a 1948 film by what director?", "answer": "John Huston", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Are both Penstemon and Cicerbita native to the same continents?", "answer": "no", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Prior to reestablishing the Deputy Chair of the Democratic National Committee in  February 2017, Tom Perez served in what position from 2009 to 2013? ", "answer": "Assistant Attorney General for Civil Rights", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Beside the one at Magic Kingdom Walt Disney World, what other theme park would one