ty Airport?", "answer": "Portland International Jetport", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Guideposts is different from Meatpaper how?", "answer": "Guideposts is a faith-based non-profit organization", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "What is this British multinational banking and financial services company that operates a network of over 1,000 branches across dozens of countries that was formed in 1969 after merging of a few companies?", "answer": "Standard Chartered", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What state is part of Tornado Alley and where Mike McShaffry graduated college?", "answer": "Texas", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Neil LaBute wrote and directed the 2006 horror film starring whom?", "answer": "Nicolas Cage", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which is known as a educational music institution and had Maria Szraiber as pianist teacher?", "answer": "Moscow Conservatory", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "The Doomsday Flight is a film written by a screenwriter known as the what of Hollywood?", "answer": "\"angry young man\"", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "The Sinai and Palestine Campaign was led by Philip Chetwode during World War I in March of what year?", "answer": "1917", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Massachusetts rapper Joyner Lucas repeased her mixtape 508-507-2209 in 2017 produced by which recording label?", "answer": "Atlantic Records", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Gert Korthof reviewed the intelligent design book published by Free Press in what year?", "answer": "2007", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "McDull, Prince de la Bun, is a 2004 animated Hong Kong film directed by who, and starring the voice of Anthony Wong, a Hong Kong actor, and is perhaps best known in the West for his roles in the 1992 action film \"Hard Boiled\"?", "answer": "Toe Yuen", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": " Belinda Jane Charteris played in the Silver Ferns team that won a silver medal at a multi-sport event with how many sports featured?", "answer": "