re Show?", "answer": "Georgia Engel", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "In what neighborhood of Manhattan is the museum Jacqueline Nesti Joseph had an art exhbition at?", "answer": "Upper East Side", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Bellerophon and the Son of Zeus and Alcmene were known as what?", "answer": "heroes", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which Australian group played an extreme metal fusion genre?", "answer": "Slice The Cake", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "In which film does a compiler of an Under the Influence album play a cameo role?", "answer": "Harry Potter and the Prisoner of Azkaban", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Maryanne Demasi worked for a decade at a hospital that provided services to what region of Australia?", "answer": "South Australia", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Where is the author of \"Justice: What's the Right Thing to Do?\" a professor?", "answer": "Harvard University", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which musical act was active first, APB or Hozier?", "answer": "APB", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "What American rapper, singer, songwriter, record producer and actor born in 1971 has worked with Axident?", "answer": "Snoop Dogg", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "False Dawn is a short story by this English journalist born in what year?", "answer": "1865", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which singer who recorded the song \"In the Misty Moonlight\" was known as \"Gentleman Jim\"?", "answer": "James Travis Reeves", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Who was the county named after that Drexell R. Davis was born in?", "answer": "Isaac Shelby", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "The surf reef break which Joel Parkinson surfed on in the ASP World Championship Tour Surfing Title on 14 December 2012 is located in what state?", "answer": "Hawaii", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Besides the Shard, where can other major works of Severfield Plc be found?", "answer": "United Kingdom", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Who is the artist that sings both \"Fading\" and \"Take a Bow\"?", "answer": "Rihanna", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "On Chesil Beach stars an actress that received a Best Supporting Actress nomination for what 2007 movie?", "answer": "Atonement", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Gut Symmetries is a 1997 novel by a writer born in which year ?", "answer": "1959", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What city boosts a daily newspaper which was also selected to choose the best American Football League players in 1961?", "answer": "New York City", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Name the dominant tree species located in Virginia's largest state forest, who's Ancient Greek name is genus Carya.", "answer": "Hickory", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Who is the actor in \"Rings\", \"Roseanne\", and \"The Big Bang Theory\"?", "answer": "Johnny Galecki", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "A Director of Biological Sciences at what college served as an advisor to a United States Department of Energy national laboratory in New York?", "answer": "Yale", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Tales of Pain and Wonder have a the influence of which American writer born on August 6, 1874?", "answer": "Charles Fort", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What house did the director of \"On the Trail of the Bremen Town Musicians\" frequent?", "answer": "Livanov house", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What five-time NBA champion makes up half of San Antonio Spurs Twin Towers?", "answer": "Tim Duncan", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "While Philadelphus is a genus of about 60 species of shrubs, what genus is the Pachyphytum?", "answer": "a small genus of succulents in the Crassulaceae family", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Both Jay Elmer and a current Attorney General are politicians in which state?", "answer": "Kansas", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Are Fran\u00e7ois Truffaut and Tarsem Singh of the same nationality?", "answer": "no", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Did singer Julian Casablancas a