ich competed from 1977 to 1997 and won titles in five weight divisions, are from what city in Maryland?", "answer": "Palmer Park", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Dream High starred which South Korean rapper, singer, songwriter, actor and entrepreneur?", "answer": "Ok Taec-yeon", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "The death of alexander the great occurred during the Hellenistic period in the palace of who?", "answer": "Nebuchadnezzar II in Babylon", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Kathleen Harrison starred as Mrs Dilber in a movie directed by who ?", "answer": "Brian Desmond Hurst", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which magazine has been published since 1899: Teen or Stanford Chaparral? ", "answer": "Stanford Chaparral", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "What famous family summered where Walter S. Franklin died?", "answer": "Rockefeller family", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Lord of Souls is an English Fantasy novel by Greg Keyes and is the second of two planned books based on \"The Elder Scrolls\" , a series of action role-playing open world fantasy video games primarily developed by what studios?", "answer": "Bethesda Game Studios", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Where did the reigning champion of The Champions League of Darts move to in 1993?", "answer": "Vienna", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which genus is a small group of flowering plant species, Sapindus, Artanema, or both?", "answer": "Artanema", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Neal Stephenson and Peter Benchley, are of which nationality?", "answer": "American", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "What 1962 French romantic drama film, directed, produced and written by Fran\u00e7ois Truffaut, included an Austrian stage and cinema actor whose prominent roles include two 1965 films, \"The Spy Who Came in from the Cold\" and \"Ship of Fools\"?", "answer": "Jules and Jim", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which studio is responsible for the release of the 2010 country pop song 'Fearless' which w