in that has been in continuous operation since what year?", "answer": "1939", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which opera has more acts, Der Zwerg or Billy Budd?", "answer": "Billy Budd, Op. 50, is an opera by Benjamin Britten to a libretto by the English novelist E. M. Forster and Eric Crozier, based on the short novel \"Billy Budd\" by Herman Melville. Originally in four acts, it was first performed at the Royal Opera House, London, on 1 December 1951; it was later revised as a two-act opera with a prologue and an epilogue.", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Are Born into Brothels and Touching the Void both films?", "answer": "yes", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Solar Crisis is a 1990 Japanese-American science fiction film, the cast featured which American actor, as Arnold Teague?", "answer": "Peter Lawrence Boyle", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Johnathan Rice is a songwriter who frequently collaborates with the actress who was the lead singer for what indie band?", "answer": "Rilo Kiley", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Who designed the guns used in the \"Limited Class\" and \"Open Class\" pistols offered by A & B?", "answer": "John Browning", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Are Qixia, Shandong and Wuchuan, Guangdong in the same country?", "answer": "yes", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Who directed the 2017 animated science fiction comedy that starred a cast member in Dumb & Dumber To?", "answer": "Tony Leondis", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What actress born in June 1924 starred in the 1983 American horror thriller The Dead Zone?", "answer": "Colleen Dewhurst", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "what do Suor Angelica and Louise have in common?", "answer": "opera", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Who wrote the novel \"The First Bad Man\", Peter Sasdy or Miranda July?", "answer": "Miranda July", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "In which year did this American poet, librettist, and translator who co-wrote \"The Rake's Progress\" born?", "answer": "1921", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What city in Texas contains North East mall and, in the past, also hosted North Hills mall?", "answer": "Dallas/Fort Worth metro area.", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Are Rusty Nail and French Connection both cocktails?", "answer": "yes", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Which singer sang for more bands, Jesse Leach or Steve Strange ?", "answer": "Jesse David Leach", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Howard Carter discovered the tomb of Tutankhamun which was located in what valley?", "answer": "Valley of the Kings", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What nationality are both Live It Up and 360?", "answer": "Australian", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What is the current work of the British cyclist who was one of the Team Halfords Bikehut?", "answer": "environmental consultant", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "NED University of Engineering and Technology in urban Karachi and Ege University in Turkey are both considered the oldest type of what in their respective countries?", "answer": "institution", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "When was the killer of Nicola Huges born?", "answer": "6 June 1983", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What is an international magazine for Linux software enthusiasts and professionals, Dine or  Linux Magazine ?", "answer": "Linux Magazine", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Pippa Middleton married married the heir to the title of what?", "answer": "Laird of Glen Affric", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "The captain of the Karachi Kings in 2016 also played for what team in the Indian Premier League?", "answer": "Kings XI Punjab", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What American romantic drama film directed by Drake Doremus stars an English actress who started her professional acting career as a child, appearing at age 12 in \"The Treasure Seekers\"?", "answer": "Like Crazy", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which group is from Nova Scotia, The Trews or Dodgy?", "ans