ison"}, {"question": "What was the name of the severe dust storm that occurred on April 14, 1935 as part of the era known as the Dirty Thirties, which was partially caused by failure to apply the correct dryland farming methods along with a severe drought?", "answer": "Black Sunday", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What country of origin does Roberto Vittori and Maurizio Cheli have in common?", "answer": "Italian", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Who wrote the coming-of-age novel, set in the Canadian Prairies, that has a strong affiliation with the genre that expresses a primarily realistic view of the real world while also adding or revealing magical elements?", "answer": "Thomas King", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Chappaquiddick is an upcoming American drama film starring an Australian film and television actor known for playing Tommy Caffee on what television series?", "answer": "Brotherhood", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Are both Athlete and Fatherson name of Scottish bands?", "answer": "no", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Who served as the first president of the organization at which a partner of the architectural firm McKim, Mead & White was a founding member?", "answer": "John Quincy Adams Ward", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What is the birth date of this Congolese progessional footballer, who was on the top scoring charts of the domestic top division in the 2007-08 Standard Liege season?", "answer": "22 November 1985", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Bar Hopping is a film that starred what \"Saturday Night Live\" cast member?", "answer": "Kevin Nealon", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Kai Bird and Martin Sherwin wrote a book about the father of what?", "answer": "the atomic bomb", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "The Art of Noise was a short-lived radio program that starred a musician that produced how many number-one hits in the US?", "answer": "23", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What English guitarist worked on \"Out of My Mind