o specializes in seamless matte painting effects, while at Industrial Light & Magic, or Matte World Digital, he worked on, or supervised the crews of more than a hundred films, including which 1995 American epic crime drama film ?", "answer": "Casino", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What American actor was grandson of American actress and poet Dorothy Bridges?", "answer": "Jordan Bridges", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What was the original capital of the British colony that included Georgetown?", "answer": "St. Mary's City", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Walter Brit was a follower of which scholastic philosopher?", "answer": "John Wycliffe", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Javed Afridi is the CEO of the company established in what year?", "answer": "2000", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Woolworths.co.uk was replaced by which online retailer with headquarters in Speke?", "answer": "Very", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Who was the founder of the party of which Vydas Gedvilas is a member?", "answer": "Viktor Uspaskich", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "A roller coaster is a type of amusement ride that employs a form of elevated railroad track designed with tight turns, steep slopes, and sometimes inversions, LaMarcus Adna Thompson obtained one of the first known patents for a roller coaster design in 1885, related to the Switchback Railway, at which location, and was the first roller coaster designed as an amusement ride in America?", "answer": "Coney Island", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which seinen manga featuring Kei Kurono, and Masaru Kato, did Hiroya Oku write?", "answer": "Hen", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which Irish symbol used in heraldry to denote the Irish province of Ulster is included in Flag of Ulster?", "answer": "The Red Hand of Ulster", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Before becoming known as Noul, what was known as the second costliest United States Disaster in 2002?", "answer": "Typhoon Pongsona", "type": "bridge"}, {"questi