en supported by a Turkish-American businessman's Foundation?", "answer": "Cleveland", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "The 2015 Ulster Club Senior Football Championship had reigning champions of which Gaelic club?", "answer": "Robert Emmet's Gaelic Athletic Club Slaughtneil", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What powers the 300 East?", "answer": "electricity", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "The team that featired Dirk Nowitzki was from which conference?", "answer": "Western Conference", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Do War and Peace and Mireille have the same number of acts?", "answer": "yes", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "What 1986 film directed by Russell Mulcahy has a fictional character named Juan Sanchez Villa-Lobos Ramirez?", "answer": "Highlander", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Berlin's \"Love Life\" included the band's first Top 40 single. Which of their songs made it to number 1?", "answer": "\"Take My Breath Away\"", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What Hong Kong actor pops up as a major supporting role in To Catch the Uncatchable?", "answer": "Michael Tong Man-lung", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Cake Man Raven was said to \"turn Dixieland dessert red velvet cake into a Brooklyn thing.\" by a news paper that was founded in which year ?", "answer": "1919", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "How is the name of this princess, who has a brother named Semyon Vorontsov, and who was a  major figure of the Russian Enlightenment, often spelled in English?", "answer": "Princess Dashkov", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What is the name of the controversial environmental book written by the editor of Global Crises, Global Solutions?", "answer": "The Skeptical Environmentalist", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What psychedelic rock band recorded their second album in the town that is home to Cadillac Mountain?", "answer": "Coke Weed", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What is the correct spelling of honorable in Irish English ?", "answer": "honourable", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Atsuko Tanaka voices Bayonetta in a game developed by PlatinumGames and produced by whom?", "answer": "Atsushi Inaba and Hitoshi Yamagami", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Who has more scope of proffesion, Hideo Gosha or Dallas M. Fitzgerald?", "answer": "Dallas M. Fitzgerald", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "On which album did the song that was ahead of \"Where the Stars and Stripes and the Eagle Fly\" on the Billboard Hot Country Singles & Tracks chart appear?", "answer": "Drive", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What position does the basketball player, who appears in the cover of the German version of NBA 2K16, play ?", "answer": "point guard", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Was Elektor TV Games Computer or Exidy Sorcerer sold first?", "answer": "Sorcerer", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Are authors David Eddings and Nicholas Christopher both American?", "answer": "yes", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "What is the primary instrument played by the artist responsible for Waitin for the Sun?", "answer": "mandolin", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What American Idol star's singing competition did BoybandPH win?", "answer": "Simon Phillip Cowell", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Beiliu and Qingzhou are both located in what country?", "answer": "China", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Which coastal city is the second largest in Wales and home to the blues band The Electric Revelators? ", "answer": "Swansea", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What stadium is the football club a member of which is located in Cheshire, England, and in which Neil Young was a manager at one time?", "answer": "Deva Stadium", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which long-running magazine was founded first: Belgian publication Femmes d\u2019Aujourd\u2019hui, or Better Homes and Gardens, from the USA?", "answer": "Better Homes and Gardens", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": " Israelite School of Universal Practical Knowledge and Southern Poverty Law Center are both located in what country?", "answer": "United States", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Salvador included the actress in a starring role who was of which heritage?", "answer": "Mexican and American", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Eugene Vidal, father of Gore, worked with Amelia Earhart on pioneering projects in what fledgling industry?", "answer": "aviation", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Are Lincoln Airport and Unalaska Airport public use?", "answer": "yes", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "In what year was the magazine first published that was the source of the stories for the anthology Hell Hath Fury ?", "answer": "1939", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What Argentinian singer sang Volver\u00e9?", "answer": "Diego Verdaguer", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "\"Get Out\" is 2017 American horror film was written, co-produced, and directed by this man who is best known for starring in which Comedy Central sketch series?", "answer": "Key & Peele", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Are both Archie Mayo and Shinya Tsukamoto film directors?", "answer": "yes", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Mois\u00e9s Solana Was a Race car driver from Mexico who also played this sport that is a variation of what? To fund his racing career?", "answer": "Basque pelota", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What is the capital city of the least populous nation where Himalayan Butterfly Bush grows?", "answer": "Thimphu", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Trent Jordan \"T. J.\" Watt, is an American football outside linebacker for the Pittsburgh Steelers of the National Football League (NFL), and is the younger brother of professional football players, J. J. Watt and who?", "answer": "Derek Watt", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Do both Bidens and Pimelea have poisonous species in them?", "answer": "no", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "The 2014 Australian federal budget was presented to the House of Representatives by a man that is the curren