ed on what date?", "answer": "June 27, 1966", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Mate Pavi\u0107 and Andrea Jaeger are both what?", "answer": "professional tennis player", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Which metal band from Melbourne, Victoria released their debut studio album through Volkanik Music on November 13, 2012?", "answer": "Twelve Foot Ninja", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What major company produced the film \"Fun and Fancy Free\", an American live-action animated movie in 1947 and \"Roving Mars\", an IMAX documentary about the Mars Exploration Rovers years later?", "answer": "Disney", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Which NFL team drafted the senior quarterback of the 2002 Texas Longhorns?", "answer": "Tampa Bay Buccaneers", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What was the English publication name of the architecture treatise written by the Roman author commonly known as Vitruvius?", "answer": "Ten Books on Architecture", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "what bands Lead singer Nicholas Petricca started the band in 2006, The Kooks or Walk the Moon ?", "answer": "Walk The Moon", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Yoad Nevo is an English producer/mixer known for his work with Jem, Pet Shop Boys, Bryan Adams, and Goldfrapp, Goldfrapp is an English electronic duo from London, formed in which year?", "answer": "1999", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What is the country of origin of Janeane Garofalo and the comedy film entitled 200 Cigarettes?", "answer": "American", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Who was the head coach of the team that defeated the the 2011\u201312 Kansas Jayhawks men's basketball team on April 2?", "answer": "John Calipari", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "William Thomas Seawell was the head of what company that was the largest international airport carrier until 1991?", "answer": "Pan American World Airways", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "In \"The Brotherhood\" Anthony Marciona played the godson of an an actor that had his