ter Telescope", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "When was the album of the song \"Good Life\" released?", "answer": "September 11, 2007", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which country's team swept all their assignments en route to their 5th title in the men's tournament at the Asian Games in the same year  Allan Caidic and Alvin Patrimonio played for the Philippines men's national basketball team?", "answer": "China", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "A Girl like Me was a collaboration with Ne-Yo who wrote which song produced by StarGate?", "answer": "Unfaithful", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What award did Susan Lynch win as a result of her role in Beautiful Creatures?", "answer": "British Independent Film Award", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which film is more recent, Michael or 3096?", "answer": "3096", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Whiting is an unincorporated community in Mississippi County, in the U.S. state of Missouri, a U.S. state is a constituent political entity of which entity?", "answer": "United States of America", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What position does alexis sanchez play and is speed a factor?", "answer": "Alexis, is a Chilean professional footballer who plays as a forward", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What position does the captain of the Washington Capitals who previously tucked in his  Jersey play?", "answer": "winger", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Who created the official portrait of the 38th President of the United States?", "answer": "Everett Raymond Kinstler", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "An American stand-up comedian, actor, and author performed in Broaway shows such as West Side Story and in 1976 he enjoyed a two-year run starring in what NBC television sitcom?", "answer": "C.P.O. Sharkey", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Droga5 has created ad campaigns for the brown ale now brewed by which company?", "answer": "Heineken", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What hydroelectric dam located on the Little Tennessee River in Swain and Graham counties, North Carolina, United States is home to MINIs on the Dragon is an annual gathering of MINI Coopers in Robbinsville, North Carolina? ", "answer": "Fontana Dam", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Between Hana Mandl\u00edkov\u00e1 and Johan Kriek, who won more Grand Slam singles at the French Open?", "answer": "Hana Mandl\u00edkov\u00e1", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Gina Philips was in which 2001 American-German film?", "answer": "Jeepers Creepers", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Sid Haig and Mark Hoplamazian, have which mutual nationality?", "answer": "American", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Who created the first alternative education program in a city in southern Otsego County, with a nickname of \"City of the Hills.\"?", "answer": "Mike Newell and principal Mark Rathbun", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which documentary film, \"That's Dancing!\" or \"V-Day: Until the Violence Stops\", was filmed first?", "answer": "That's Dancing!", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Superjail!, is an American animated television series produced by Augenblick Studios in its first season, the series was the creation of Christy Karacas, who was a member of the band Cheeseburger, and also directed \"Robotomy\" for which TV station?", "answer": "Cartoon Network", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Who issued the first predecessor of the currency that is awarded to the winner of the Indira Gandhi Prize?", "answer": "Sultan Sher Shah Suri", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "In what year was the most prized player from the 2002\u201303 Olympique de Marseille season born?", "answer": "1978", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Are Hans Weingartner and Mario Bava both directors?", "answer": "yes", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "What profession does Alice Hoffman and Marguerite Duras have in common?", "answer": "novelist", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Arthur Firth started his career at a daily newspaper first published in what year?", "answer": "1886", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which breed was recognized first, the Swedish Vallhund or the Ratonero Bodeguero Andaluz?", "answer": "Swedish Vallhund", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Clockwork Orange, is the name of the secret British security services project, which was alleged to have involved a right-wing smear campaign against British politicians, it took its name from which 1971 dystopian crime film by Stanley Kubrick?", "answer": "A Clockwork Orange", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What is the name of the convention center in which the first prototype models of the BluOnyx were first demonstrated? ", "answer": "Las Vegas Convention Center", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Thomas Joseph Papa provided some voiceover work for a spin-off of what Pixar franchise?", "answer": "Cars", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Do the genuses Thalictrum and Rumex contain roughly the same number of species?", "answer": "yes", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "What are the call letters of the sports radio station, also known as \"The Fan\" that broadcasts from the same building as sister station WNNX, a mainstream rock station?", "answer": "WCNN", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Thorpe Camp was a barracks 2.5 mi south-east from a former Royal Air Force station located where?", "answer": "2 mi north of Coningsby", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Who produced the song that plays during the credits of the american martial arts/buddy action comedy film released on August 10, 2007?", "answer": "Salaam Remi", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which Italian Prime Minister who was born in 1883, had a government which included Giuseppe Cobolli Gigli as the Minister for Public Works?", "answer": "Benito Mussolini", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "The person who appointed Ahmad Khatami as Tehran\u2019s substitute Friday prayer leader was born in what year?", "answer": "1939", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": " Eve Beglarian was born in a city