, "answer": "Seventeen", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Which 1976 American suspense-thriller film is spoofed by Hot Shots!?", "answer": "Marathon Man", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "which American sports media has Tim Marchman previously written for?", "answer": "Sports Illustrated", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What are the languages of the two albums released by the boy band which calls Pledis Entertainment its home?", "answer": "one Korean and one Japanese", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which hospital has more beds, Children's National Medical Center or Providence Hospital?", "answer": "Providence Hospital", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Are Daytona Beach International Airport and El Paso International Airport both located in the United States ?", "answer": "yes", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "What 1994 American Christmas fantasy film starred James Remar as Jack Duff?", "answer": "Miracle on 34th Street", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Who starred in both \"Dunkirk\" and a 2017 British-American mystery drama film directed by Ritesh Batra and written by Nick Payne?", "answer": "Billy Howle", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What TNT American fantasy-adventure did Christian Kane star on?", "answer": "The Librarians", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which rebellion which began on 10 May 1857 did  Frederick Haines  served in India during the period", "answer": "The Indian Rebellion of 1857", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Are Linhai and Wugang, Hunan located in the same province?", "answer": "no", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Which fictional character created by William Dozier, Julius Schwartz and Carmine Infatino portrays a transgender woman?", "answer": "Barbara Gordon", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Who directed the German war film that had studio props reused in the film \"Sinking of the Lusitania: Terror at Sea\"?", "answer": "Wolfgang Petersen", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Of Charles de Gaulle and Georges Pompidou, what year was the longer lived born?", "answer": "1890", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "How many inhabitants are in the city where Club Alianza Viedma is from?", "answer": "47,246", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Tumble included trainers who once trained which retired British artistic gymnast?", "answer": "Elizabeth \"Beth\" Kimberly Tweddle MBE", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "since what has the conference that has the North Texas Mean Green football team been affiliated with the NCAA's Division I?", "answer": "since 1976", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Who did Stephanie Moore play in the 2007 American-Canadian horror thriller film directed by Franck Khalfoun?", "answer": "Lorraine", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which town was razed for the creation of the airforce base known as \"The Cradle of Naval Aviation\"?", "answer": "Woolsey", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Who is older Charlie Papazian or John Matoian?", "answer": "John Matoian", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Johan Kriek's most memorable wins include victory over a tennis player who has been cited as one of the most what?", "answer": "charismatic players in history", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Mpulungu District is in a country located in which part of Africa ?", "answer": "Southern Africa", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "The Holy Cross Crusaders baseball team is a varsity intercollegiate athletic team of a college founded in which year ?", "answer": "1843", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "The March to the Drina was dedicated to a commander who had fought during a battle in the early stages of what war?", "answer": "First World War", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "In what city did the game event that debuted NetherRealm Studio's May 2017 fighting video game for PlayStation 4 and Xbox One take place?", "answer": "St. Charles, Illinois", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Lindley Miller Garrison, was a New Jersey lawyer who served as Secretary of War under U.S. President 