ience fiction comedy horror film, and stared an actor who  is a distinguished professor in musical theater at Western Carolina University in Cullowhee, North Carolina?", "answer": "Rupert Harvey", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Who won the 1977 Grand Prix and was a British racing driver in the One world championship?", "answer": "James Hunt", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Enoch Bolles' most widely reproduced advertising illustration is for a manufacturing company located where?", "answer": "Bradford, Pennsylvania, United States of America", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which railroad did Chessie System own that was formed in the mid 1800s in Virginia?", "answer": "Chesapeake and Ohio Railway", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What presenter on the Full Irish radio breakfast show also was a pioneering member of the Twitterati? ", "answer": "Ryan Tubridy", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Who produced the film which was Omung Kumar's directorial debut?", "answer": "Sanjay Leela Bhansali", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "In what year did the guest wrestling coach for person that many consider to be the greatest mixed martial artists of all time win a silver medal a the Summer Olympics?", "answer": "2004", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Who wrote the song with which Critics compared Fading?", "answer": "Erik Hermansen", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Who voiced Kermit the Frog in the Muppets television series that aired from 1984 to 1991 on CBS?", "answer": "Frank Welker", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "The Futures Wheel was invented at which graduate school in New Hampshire?", "answer": "Antioch University New England", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Epidendrum and Platycodon, are genus of which species?", "answer": "plant", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "this town with its population of 1,152 at the 2000 census is the terminus for mailboat ferry service to an island town which at the 2010 census had a population of what?", "answer": "73", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "The Mills River flows into what other river, located in Transylvania County, North Carolina? ", "answer": "The French Broad River", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Is a Kumquat a member of the Tetracentron genus?", "answer": "no", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Which Romanian former football striker who scored 4 goals in the 1994 World Cup also played for AS Monaco?", "answer": "Florin R\u0103ducioiu", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "In which province is the city, where the company that premiered Conversations on a Homecoming, is based ?", "answer": "Connacht", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What Spanish retired footballer who played during the 1980s and 1990s, helped Barcelona win The 1989 European Cup Winners' Cup Final?", "answer": "Julio Salinas", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which Magazine came out first, Yankee or The Christian Science Monitor ?", "answer": "The Christian Science Monitor", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Which retired Canadian professional ice hockey player did Mike Barnett make contract for ", "answer": "Owen Liam Nolan", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "To which profession do both Bill Leeb and Bernie Leadon belong?", "answer": "musician", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Shahzad Nawaz has been an advisor to which subsidiary of the Dubai based holding company founded by Haji Abdul Razzak Yaqoob ", "answer": "ARY Digital Network", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "having previously served as the creative director at Gucci and Yves Saint Laurent this American fashion designer directed a film based on what novel?", "answer": "Tony and Susan", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Who wrote and directed the 2009 film in which Audrey Giacomini played Jeanne?", "answer": "Jaco Van Dormael", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Who is the American professional basketball player and four-time NBA All-Star in a basketball simulation video game developed by Visual Concepts and published by 2K Sports?", "answer": "Paul George", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Are both Harry Daghlian and Mark Krikorian work at the Center for Immigration Studies?", "answer": "no", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Azurik: Rise of Perathia features a score by game composer born in which US state ?", "answer": "Iowa", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "what does The Prospect of Whitby in Wapping a district in London Docklands lay claim to being the oldest of?  ", "answer": "riverside tavern", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which nationality is the performer of the song 'Ghetto Cowboy'?", "answer": "American", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Brown Hill Creek is part of the river that is located in what Australian state?", "answer": "South Australia", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "The 21 Irrefutable Laws of Leadership: Follow Them and People Will Follow You is a 1998 book written by John C. Maxwell, professional basketball player Harrison Barnes read and spoke positively of the book, Harrison Bryce Jordan Barnes (born May 30, 1992) is an American professional basketball player for the which city's team, of the National Basketball Association (NBA)?", "answer": "Dallas Mavericks", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "KKJZ broadcasts from a college campus located in what California neighborhood?", "answer": "Los Altos", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Magda's Funny Bits starred which Australian film actress and comedian?", "answer": "Magdalene Mary \"Magda\" Szubanski", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which singer is part of a band with a shorter name, Rivers Cuomo or Max Bemis?", "answer": "Rivers Cuomo", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "What star of Submergence made his acting debut in The Near Room?", "answer": "James McAvoy", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which American Magazine was printed first, Baltimore or Woman's Day?", "answer": "Baltimore", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "What was the birth date of a British actor and director that directed a 2001 American romantic comedy film written by Marc Klein?", "answer": "20 April 1956", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "A railway constructed along aqueducts in north west England from Heywood to Rawtenstall was built in response to the growing population of what time period?", "answer": "Industrial Revolution", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Physics for Future Presidents: The Science Behind the Headlines is a 2008 book by an American physicist who founded an independent 501(c)(3) non-profit with his daughter named what?", "answer": "Berkeley Earth", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Who is older, Aretha Franklin or Hahm Eun-jung?", "answer": "Aretha Louise Franklin", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "This basketball team who lost the 2011 Big 12 Men's Basketball Tournament quarterfinals played itshome games at an arena briefly known as what?", "answer": "Paige Sports Arena", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which of these tennis players is from Germany, Mike Bryan or Michael Stich?", "answer": "Michael Detlef Stich", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "What type of film is \"Cat People\"?", "answer": "horror film", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What is the title of this satirical realistic fiction comedy novel for children and teenagers by the author who created \"Poptropica?\"", "answer": "Diary of a Wimpy Kid", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What type of club was the Hasty Pudding Club, founded by Charles Macomb Flandrau?", "answer": "a social club", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Robert Benton and Tom Walls both worked which role in the making of a movie?", "answer": "director", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "How many places are Ahmad A'zam's ethnic group found?", "answer": "Afghanistan, Tajikistan, Kyrgyzstan, Kazakhstan, Turkmenistan, Russia and China", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "\"Wearing and Tearing\" is a song by English rock group Led Zeppelin, it's the eighth and final track on their final studio album, \"Coda\", the ninth and final studio album by the English rock band Led Zeppelin, released in what year?", "answer": "1982", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Are Joe Walsh and Mark Hoppus both songwriters as well as vocalists in their various bands?", "answer": "yes", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "The Swedish, alternative rock band ALPHA 60 was named in reference to the computer in the 1965 French science fiction film Alphaville, which debuted in what year?", "answer": "1965", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "A Very Potter Musical (originally titled Harry Potter: The Musical and often shortened to AVPM) is a musical with music and lyrics by Darren Criss and A. J. Holmes, the story is a parody, based on several of the \"Harry Potter\" novels, including Harry Potter and the Goblet of Fire, the which number novel?", "answer": "fourth", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Where was the birth place of the novelist who was the father of Sue Taylor Grafton?", "answer": "China", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "When was trhe Maxican actress born who wasa star during the 1940s and 1950s with Pedro Armend\u00e1riz and one of the most beautiful faces of the cinema in her time?", "answer": "August 3, 1904", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which book series from Rick Riordan do both the fantasy novel The Hidden Oracle and the Camp Half-Blood-Chronicles have in common?", "answer": "Percy Jackson & the Olympians", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Pride & Joy featured the American actor and producer known as Ari Gold on which comedy series?", "answer": "Entourage", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Independent Citizens' Initiative Save Austria, or Save Austria,  is an anti-EU movement in Austria which was founded by former presidential candidate and pro-neutrality activist Karl Walter Nowak, in the Austrian legislative election, 2008 they received 0.73% of the vote and no seats, it was held on which date?", "answer": "28 September 2008", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What year was the play, directed by Frith Banbury and starring the man best known for his role of King Lear, released? ", "answer": "1968", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Caldera de Taburiente National Park and Picos de Europa National Park are located in what country?", "answer": "Spain", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Which actress born Yang Sung-yoon stared in the South Korean film Traces of Love?", "answer": "Kim Ji-soo", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What month do  Legion of French Volunteers Against Bolshevism and Philippe P\u00e9tain have in common?", "answer": "July", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Are The Devil Came on Horseback and The California Reich both documentary?", "answer": "yes", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Caythorpe, Lincolnshire is located in the district that covers what towns?", "answer": "Grantham, Stamford, Bourne and Market Deeping", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Buddy's Buddy was a tribute album to what American singer, songwriter, and guitarist, who died in a plane crash with Buddy Holly and The Big Bopper?", "answer": "Ritchie Valens", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which university did Brook Lopez and his brother Robin Lopez attend and play basketball for?", "answer": "Stanford", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which genus was described first, Ixiolirion or Allosyncarpia?", "answer": "Ixiolirion", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": " Krzysztof Zimnoch once defeated the current heavyweight boxing champion, who has held his title since what year?", "answer": "2015", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Greatest Hits is a compilation album of recordings by a band founded by guitarist Chris Stein and a singer named what?", "answer": "Debbie Harry", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "The Pro\u2013Wailing Wall Committee was established by a professor that was the chief redactor of what encyclopedia?", "answer": "\"Encyclopedia Hebraica\"", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which family occupied the place where the Robert Burns World Federation literary society met?", "answer": "Boyd Family", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Collective Soul and Catfish and the Bottlemen are both what?", "answer": "rock band", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "What is the title of the 13th episode of the American fantasy drama television series that premiered on October 23, 2011, on ABC?", "answer": "What Happened to Frederick", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which woman is a talk show host on the WIBC radio station in Indianapolis and also very active in the National Rifle Association?", "answer": "Dana Loesch", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Where is the college located that owns and operates WURC (88.1 FM)?", "answer": "Located approximately 35 miles southeast of Memphis, Tennessee", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Jeannette-Th\u00e9r\u00e8se Obstoj is known for writing what song for Mary Isobel Catherine Bernadette O'Brien?", "answer": "Arrested by You", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Giselle Cossard Binon Omindarewa was also known as what?", "answer": "Yemoja", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What operation was thwarted by a brigade of about 40 members?", "answer": "Operation Conservation", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What country does Cangzhou and Miquan have in common?", "answer": "China", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "What kind of English is colloquially referred too the language of all people descended from enslaved Black Africans?", "answer": "African American Vernacular English", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "The 1965 Giro d'Italia started in the country with an area of how many square kilometers?", "answer": "61 sqkm", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What kind of person does Ian Johns and World Series of Poker have in common?", "answer": "player", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Hesperantha and Echeveria, are types of which genus?", "answer": "flowering plants", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "From 1966 to 1973 Edward Staley was the chairman of a company founded by who?", "answer": "William Thomas Grant", "type": "b