e?", "answer": "Wombeyan Karst Conservation Reserve", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "In the movie about an icon painter, who did Irma Raush play?", "answer": "Durochka", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "In what year was the son of Tariq Alam who is a Pakistani cricketer born?", "answer": "1985", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What is the Scottish Gaelic word for the city in which the Craigentinny Traction Maintenance Depot is located?", "answer": "D\u00f9n \u00c8ideann", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Who won the Palme d'Or at the 1993 Cannes Film Festival, Tonya Suzanne Holly or Chen Kaige?", "answer": "Chen Kaige", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "What roller coaster in Mumbai, India features five track turns that put riders upside-down? ", "answer": "Nitro", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "How many years was the man who was the new head coach of the St. Louis Rams in 2006, a college assistant coach ?", "answer": "13 seasons.", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Who was a Jewish businessman responsible for starting a company dealing with medial equipment after leaving Germany sometime between 1933-1945?", "answer": "Rolf Schild", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "According to the 2011 census, what was the population of the municipality in which Erjon Dollapi was born?", "answer": "20,517", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Musical Sources was directed by what French historian who was a Western convert to Shaivite Hinduism?", "answer": "Alain Dani\u00e9lou", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which star of the Karate Kid was born on July 8, 1998 ?", "answer": "Jaden Smith", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "When was the  Australian cricketer born who made his Test debut in the first match, scoring 151 in the first innings?", "answer": "2 April 1981", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "East Siberian Laika and Rastreador Brasileiro, are which kind of animal?", "answer": "dog", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "What is the style of art that combine modernist styles with fine craftsmanship and rich materials that autoportrait was most known for?", "answer": "Art Deco", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Between the two Spanish national parks, Garajonay National Park and Monfrag\u00fce, which is known for its bird-life?", "answer": "Monfrag\u00fce", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Girlfriendis a song by British rock band The Darkness, released as the third and final single from their second studio album, the music video for the song is inspired from which 1983 American romantic drama film?", "answer": "Flashdance", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Joe Kristosik, is a former American football player, after graduating from which Roman Catholic, private, preparatory school located in Summerlin, Nevada, he entered the working world as a door-to-door salesman and a valet before enrolling at the University of Nevada?", "answer": "Bishop Gorman High School", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Who directed the christmas film starring an actress who studied at Chicago's Second City and ImprovOlympic in the early 1990s?", "answer": "Sofia Coppola", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Who directed the 2012 documentary film about the Welsh artist best known for his work with Hunter S. Thompson?", "answer": "Charlie Paul", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What was the video game mentioned in a Nintendo news and strategy magazine scheduled for USA release but canceled?", "answer": "Lost Mission", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What computer did the female designer of Monaco work on?", "answer": "the Apple Macintosh", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What is the name of the American subsidiary of the French production company that Germaine Dulac spent the last decade of her life working on newsreels for?", "answer": "Gaumont International Television", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Are Manfred Noa and Brad Anderson both film directors?", "answer": "yes", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Are Xerophyllum and Arthrocereus both plants?", 