 the Alcohol\" for a series made by fox, and directed by Kevin Tancharoen?", "answer": "fourteenth", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which airport is closer to west Nebraska, Unalaska Airport or Central Nebraska Regional Airport?", "answer": "Central Nebraska Regional Airport", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Which of the following magazines converted to solely online resource, Premiere or Film Threat?", "answer": "Film Threat", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "The Christ the Redeemer of the Andes statue stands at an altitude of 3832 metres, reachable by road only in summer, on the border between which countries?", "answer": "Argentina and Chile", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Typhoon Amy originated near what land mass that is part of the Republic of Marshall Islands?", "answer": "Amy developed from an area of low pressure near the Kwajalein Atoll", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which film was released first, Miracle of the White Stallions or Cool Runnings?", "answer": "Miracle of the White Stallions", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "When did the mountain building period that created the Taconic unconformity end?", "answer": "440 million years ago", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What is the permanent seating capacity of the stadium in which the 2006 USC Trojans football team played its home games?", "answer": "93,607", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "The Sapling Foundation is a non-profit organization that owns what media organization which posts talks online for free distribution, under the slogan \"ideas worth spreading\"?", "answer": "TED", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Iron Man 3 stars a British-American actress who made her first onscreen appearance at age 10 in the 1992 television adaptation of what?", "answer": "The Camomile Lawn", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "In which year did this Saxon noble woman whose daughter gave birth to Gisela and Charles the Bald was born?", "answer": "778", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which member of the group of seven astronauts announced by NASA in 1959 had Leroy as his given first name?", "answer": "Gordon Cooper", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Peter Jackson and Pam Veasey, have which mutual occupations?", "answer": "writer, producer and director", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "What year did Michael Foster's band win the award for Favorite Heavy Metal/Hard Rock New Artist at the American Music Awards?", "answer": "1992", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "The conference that the 2012-13 Hartford Hawks men's basketball team were members of was named what between 1988 and 1996? ", "answer": "North Atlantic Conference", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Gentle Giant stars an actor born on November 21, 1920 who died in what year?", "answer": "1988", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "S\u00f4nia Maria Campos Braga appeared int 1988 American comedy-drama film, The Milagro Beanfield War and won a BAFTA award nomination in 1981 for what film?", "answer": "\"Dona Flor and Her Two Husbands\"", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Are Sparta and Sister Hazel both from the same state?", "answer": "no", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Which current Strictly Come Dancing female judge was born in 1960?", "answer": "Shirley Ballas", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What musician who released the single \"Swag It Out\" stars in The Greatest Showman?", "answer": "Zendaya", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "ARA Sarand\u00ed is the fourth and last ship of what class of warships built in Germany", "answer": "MEKO 360H2 type", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Where was the author of the 2011 novel Inheritance born?", "answer": "Los Angeles, California", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Of the bothers featured in the 2014 American true crime sports drama film produced by Bennett Miller, which was a seven-time World and Olympic medalist?", "answer": "David Leslie \"Dave\" Schultz", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "The winner of the 1993 Miss USA contest had a minor role in a 2003 romantic comedy starring LL Cool J that was inspired by what Shakespeare play?", "answer": "\"The Taming of the Shrew\"", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What mostly decommissioned nuclear production complex operated by the United States is overlooked by Rattlesnake Mountain?", "answer": "Hanford Site", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Under which king of England, Scotland and Ireland who was deposed in Scotland in 1651 did Earl of Middleton, Charles, serve?", "answer": "Charles II", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which Japanese-born American cinematogrpher is known for his photography in the 2009 supernatural horror film Jennifer's Body?", "answer": "David Mullen", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Who is the recorder of \"I Will Go to You Like the First Snow\" signed to in South Korea?", "answer": "YMC Entertainment", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Texas Country Weekend is a syndicated radio program that plays which rapidly growing subgenre of American country music?", "answer": "Texas country music", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What month was the female cast member of the King of the mountain born?", "answer": "August", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "The Amazing Spider-Man 2 stars this actor born in Los Angeles in what year?", "answer": "1983", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Les Vacances de Monsieur Hulot showcases the character also in what 1967 French comedy film?", "answer": "Playtime", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What phenomenon said to be often seen on the mekong river and was included in the 2002 Thai comedu-drama, Mekhong Full Moon Party?", "answer": "Naga fireball", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which is native to Africa, Cylindropuntia or Encephalartos?", "answer": "Encephalartos", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Finest Worksong is a single from an R.E.M. album released in what year?", "answer": "1987", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Were Allure and Today's Housewife founded in the same century?", "answer": "yes", "ty