om Germany?", "answer": "Albert Einstein", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "What's the name of the group that  Bacharach worked hands-on with, when rock and pop acts from Britain became popular in the United States", "answer": "Manfred Mann", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Strawberry Saroyan and Hrayr Shahinian, have a relationship with which mutual location?", "answer": "California", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": " Climate for Killing  is a 1991 American thriller-drama film starring an actress who won a Golden Globe for what 1976 film?", "answer": "Voyage of the Damned", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Clotel; or, The President's Daughter is an 1853 novel by United States author and playwright who was a prominent African-American abolitionist lecturer, novelist, playwright, and historian, about Clotel and her sister, fictional slave daughters of Thomas Jefferson,?", "answer": "William Wells Brown", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Do both Kaiyuan, Liaoning and Runan County border Jilin?", "answer": "no", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "What is the middle name of the youngest ever Curtis Cup player as of 2004", "answer": "Sung", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Super Bowl XXXVIII was played at the stadium with a seating capacity of how many people?", "answer": "71,795", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What song that Jake Sinclair worked on was performed by Taylor Swift?", "answer": "Everything Has Changed", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which of the following operas was written by Gioachino Rossini: Il turco in Italia or La Calisto?", "answer": "Il turco in Italia", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "How many residential states is the town, located near Orford and Cinnamon Brow, divided into?", "answer": "three", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Made in England is the twenty-fifth studio album by English singer-songwriter Elton John, released in 1995, it was the last album to feature which regular English virtuoso percussionist, born on 19 September 1947?", "answer": "Raymond Thomas \"Ray\" Cooper", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Nikolay Surov was a Russian rower who competed at the summer Olympic games against athletes from all over the world in what year?", "answer": "1968", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "How long was the marriage of the couple who starred in the movie  Steel Dawn?", "answer": "34 years", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Who directed the 2011 film in which Svetlana Ivanova starred ?", "answer": "Dzhanik Fayziev.", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which minor league team that plays its home games at Ogren Park did Tetsuya Yamaguchi play for before he was drafted by the Giants?", "answer": "The Missoula Osprey", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What game can have more players, Ouija or Onyx?", "answer": "Ouija", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Who has played in more bands, Max Green or Nadine Coyle?", "answer": "Max Green", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Who is older, Gary Numan or Denise Pearson?", "answer": "Gary Numan", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Which Disney film was released first, Eight Below or Pocahontas?", "answer": "Pocahontas", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "What was the name of the group in which one half of the duo Toheart debuted, the other being Woohyun from Infinite?", "answer": "Shinee", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Man Caves is hosted by a former National Football League defensive tackle who spent 12 season with the Indianapolis Colts and what other team?", "answer": "Baltimore Ravens", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What 2005 film did the co-founder of fashion label Marchesa appear in?", "answer": "The Business", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Who was the director of the film in which the actor who played Harry Osborn in \"Spider-Man\" debuted?", "answer": "Raja Gosnell", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "KFAN and its rebroadcasted sister station KFXN-FM broadcast what format?", "answer": "sports talk", "type": "bridge"}, {"questi