ision station in the 1980s?", "answer": "MTV", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Tal-Borg Battery was an artillery battery near  Southern European island country consisting of an archipelago in what sea?", "answer": "Mediterranean Sea", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Sayeret Matkal Is based off of which army unit that was founded in 1941?", "answer": "Special Air Service", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which American band produced the album 'Hot Streets' and whose founding member is praised for his Ray Charles-influenced vocal style?  ", "answer": "Chicago", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Dome Mine and Catcha Lake are both located in what country?", "answer": "Canada", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Faerie Stories is the second album by Scottish Celtic fusion group Peatbog Faeries, released in 2001 on Greentrax Recordings, influences of electronic genres such as electronica, house, dubtronica and trip hop, in addition to even dub music and African music can be heard on the album fused with traditional Scottish music of which type, that's a broad grouping of music genres that evolved out of the folk music traditions of the Celtic people of Western Europe?", "answer": "Celtic music", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What company released a game in 2006 which included a real life mission where six armed men stormed the Iranian embassy in South Kensington, London in 1980?", "answer": "Konami", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Who licensed a game for the player that received AL's Most Valuable Player in 1993?", "answer": "Major League Baseball Players Association", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What age did one of the actress that stars in Brain on Fire begin her acting career?", "answer": "seven", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What role-playing game centers on the conventions of mecha anime and science fiction and was authored by Mike Pondsmith?", "answer": "Mekton", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "An Irish Actor who died in 2010 starred in a 2009 French-Belgian-Irish film which premiered when?", "answer": "8 February 2009", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "The actor that played the starring role in a 1996 historical biopic about the Civil War also played the starring role in what 1993 Oscar winner?", "answer": "Schindler's List", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which Swedish NHL player is the cover athlete on Backyard Hockey?", "answer": "Nicklas Lidstr\u00f6m", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "The producer for the 2014 Russian drama film Leviathan was born in what year?", "answer": "1961", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What country of origin does Robert Langdon and Inferno have in common?", "answer": "American", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Who was the person who founded CNN & helped created the TV program Captain Planet and the Planeteers ? ", "answer": "Ted Turner", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "The director of Jack the Giant Slayer is the founder of what production company?", "answer": "Bad Hat Harry Productions", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Who was the producer of the 2002 British action horror film written and directed by Neil Marshall, and starring Kevin McKidd, Sean Pertwee and Liam Cunningham?", "answer": "Christopher Figg", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Where is the basketball court named after Norman Eugene \"Norm\" Stewart (born January 20, 1935) is a retired American college basketball coach located", "answer": "the University of Missouri in Columbia", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Clayton S. Rose succeeded an official as president of Bowdoin College who was born in what year?", "answer": "1950", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Hana Mandl\u00edkov\u00e1 and Robert Seguso, have which occupation?", "answer": "former professional tennis player", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "George Washington Gibbs Jr. (November 7, 1916 \u2013 November 7, 2000), a sailor in the United States Navy, became the first African American to set foot on the continent of Antarctica, Gibbs worked i