n 1962?", "answer": "first American to orbit the Earth", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "The Hindu Yuva Vahini was founded by an Indian priest and Hindu nationalist polition who is the current Chief Minister of who?", "answer": "Uttar Pradesh", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Name the Danish professional football club based in Herning and Ikast, in midwestern Jutland whose chairman Rasmus Ankersen is also one of the Directors at Brentford FC?", "answer": "FC Midtjylland", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "This song, which got heavy rotation on MTV was written by Sebastian Bach, Rachel Bolan and a rock guitarist in what kind of band?", "answer": "heavy metal band", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Telenor, who sponsored the 3rd Hum Awards ceremony, is mostly owned by which country?", "answer": "Norwegian", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Where was Unico National established after Sacco and Vanzetti were sentenced to death?", "answer": "Waterbury, Connecticut", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Jennifer Capriati and Scott Draper, have which shared occupation?", "answer": "professional tennis player", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Who manages the birdwatching site found south of the dam originally known as the Boulder Dam?", "answer": "US Fish and Wildlife Service", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Who performed with Carla Fracci and is a Danish danseur?", "answer": "Erik Bruhn", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "In what country does baechu originate?", "answer": "China", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which 1991 American action gangster film based upon an original story is co-produced by George Jackson?", "answer": "New Jack City", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What is the popular martial arts technique associated with Wing Chun Kung Fu with the abbreviation JKD?", "answer": "Jeet Kune Do", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which genus, Cymbopogon or Amherstia, has a larger native habitat?", "answer": "Cymbopogon", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Which