ve the same nationality ?", "answer": "no", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "\u00c6thelgeard was likely an official of a king usually called by what nickname?", "answer": "the All-Fair", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "In what city did the children's magazine featuring Goous and Gallant begin?", "answer": "Honesdale, Pennsylvania", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "The F Word is an American competitive cooking reality show based on a British show that aired on which channel ?", "answer": "Channel 4", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Marina Raquel Riofr\u00edo, is an Argentine Justicialist Party politician, and was born in San Juan, the capital city of the Argentine province of San Juan in which region?", "answer": "Cuyo", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which documentary featured cameos by musicians, Go Further or The True Glory?", "answer": "Dave Matthews, Natalie Merchant, Ken Kesey, Bob Weir (of the Grateful Dead), Michael Franti (of Spearhead), Anthony Kiedis (of Red Hot Chili Peppers), Rob Heydon, Medeski Martin & Wood, and The String Cheese Incident", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Kuch Kuch Locha Hai starred the Canadian-born Indian American actress who worked in what capacity previously?", "answer": "pornstar", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Julia Donaldson's illustrated children's books include Room on the Broom, Stick Man and which story that has sold 13 million copies?", "answer": "The Gruffalo", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Are both  Panzhou and Tianchang in China?", "answer": "yes", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "What mobile payment and digital wallet service is overseen by Eddy Cue?", "answer": "Apple Pay", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Patrick Reynolds is an American music executive, record producer and songwriter noted for working with prominent artists such as an American rapper and actor from where?", "answer": "Queens, New York", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Essie Davis has the role of Elizabeth woodville in a British