onal historian Diedrich Knickerbocker?", "answer": "Washington Irving", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Who played more instruments in their respective bands, Heidi Newfield or Roger Waters?", "answer": "Heidi Newfield", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "What is the year of the person who was born first, Jessie Fauset or Claude McKay?", "answer": "1882", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which fourth highest scoring ace in aviation history flew with the \"Jagdgeschwader\" 54?", "answer": "Otto Kittel", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What book about swine was written by the author of Pacala?", "answer": "The Story of the Pig", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Who starred in a 2013 film which inspired by events in council house in England from 1977 to 1979?", "answer": "Patrick Wilson and Vera Farmiga", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Are Cyrtanthus and Fouquieria plants in the same family?", "answer": "no", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "What nationality is the actressKang Hye-jung, star of Welcome to Dongmakgol?", "answer": "South Korean", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What American sitcom that ran on CBS starred Casey Sander? ", "answer": "Rules of Engagement", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Yewbarrow is a fell in the English lake district that lies immediately north of the head of what lake that is almost 3 miles long and more than 1/3 mile wide? ", "answer": "Wast Water", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which national beauty pageant crowned Rachita Kumar the winner in 1981 and is organized by The Times Group?", "answer": "Femina Miss India", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Who was the South African anti-apartheid activist that Mthuli ka Shezi's writings reflect?", "answer": "Steve Biko", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What state was the man that Atchison County was named after from?", "answer": "Missouri", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "On which album was Eminem and Rihanna's second collaborative song featured?", "answer": "Loud", "type": "