rained at the National Youth Center in Great Britain?", "answer": "Idris Elba", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Simon & Garfunkel were an American folk rock duo consisting of singer-songwriter Paul Simon and singer Art Garfunkel, their biggest hits\u2014including \"Bridge over Troubled Water\" is a song by American music duo Simon & Garfunkel, produced  by the duo and who?", "answer": "Roy Halee", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What movie had Legos based off of it and was written by Steve Kloves?", "answer": "Harry Potter and the Philosopher's Stone", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "\"Love the Way You Lie (Part II)\" and \"Only Girl\" are both singles from which of Rihanna's albums?", "answer": "Loud", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "The M62 has 7 miles that are shared with which Manchester orbital motorway?", "answer": "M60", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which South Korean singer born in 1986 appeares as a guest to the Seoul Concert?", "answer": "Lee Sung-min", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What is the middle name of the lead singer on the song \"Wasted Time\"?", "answer": "Philip", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which mathematician joined Yale in 1991, Grigory Margulis or Boris Galerkin?", "answer": "Gregori Aleksandrovich Margulis", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Zulema Castro de Pe\u00f1a was a member of what organization that began to march in 1977 at the Plaza de Mayo in Buenos Aires?", "answer": "Mothers of the Plaza de Mayo", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What American astronaut from Hawaii has a United States Air force Test Pilot Scool award named after him?", "answer": "Ellison Onizuka", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Are \"Prince Among Slaves\" and \"Marlene\" both documentaries?", "answer": "yes", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "The creator Ed Edd n Eddy also created the title screen opening for what program?", "answer": "Cartoon Sushi", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "The Belle Ayr mine is a coal mine located 18 miles southeast of Gillette, Wyoming currently owned and operated by Alpha Natural Resources, a large American producer of metallurgical coal for the industrial production of steel and iron and low-sulfur thermal coal to fuel steam boilers for the production of what type of power?", "answer": "electrical", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What is the address of the building that houses the Chicago Sports Museum?", "answer": "835 North Michigan Avenue", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Who directed the film that Charlie Cox played Jonathan Hellyer Jones in?", "answer": "James Marsh", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "which county has the highest border Jishou: or Acheng District", "answer": "Acheng District", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Which band was formed first The Servants or The Calling?", "answer": "The Servants", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "What band was formed by Savannah Buist and Katie Larson, The Dead Weather or The Accidentals?", "answer": "The Accidentals", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Where did The Road to Oz characters, sky princess Polychrome and Dorothy Gale meet?", "answer": "on an Enchanted Road", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What mountainous topography spans the French-Italian border?", "answer": "Mont Blanc", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Who plays Dutch Schultz in a film with an Australian Actress who has won two Primetime Emmy Awards?", "answer": "Dustin Hoffman", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Are Edmund Wilson and Arthur Koestler both writers?", "answer": "yes", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Which college football league was the team from that was defeated by the 2007 Georgia Bulldogs in the 2008 Sugar Bowl?", "answer": "2007 NCAA Division I-Bowl Subdivision", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Who was born first, Jon Anderson or Sonny Sandoval?", "answer": "Jon Anderson", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Sir Cyril Osborne served as Member of Parliament for a county constituency that was abolished in which year ?", "answer": "1983", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Fred Mundee, an American football center, attended a public high school in Youngstown, Ohio that closed following which school year?", "answer": "1992\u20131993", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "The Helicon Home Colony was an experimental community formed by author Upton Sinclair using proceeds from what novel that portrayed the harsh conditions and exploited lives of immigrants in the United States in Chicago and similar industrialized cities? ", "answer": "The Jungle", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "The original seven schools established, or re-endowed and renamed, by King Henry VIII in 1541, to pray for his soul, during which titled event, the set of administrative and legal processes between 1536 and 1541 by which Henry VIII disbanded monasteries, priories, convents and friaries in England, Wales and Ireland, appropriated their income, disposed of their assets, and provided for their former personnel and functions?", "answer": "Dissolution of the Monasteries", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which president, who was a businessman, has Doug Overbey as a nominee?", "answer": "Donald Trump", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Who is older, Buster Bloodvessel or Barney Greenway?", "answer": "Buster Bloodvessel", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Which of the people that wore Basil Soda's designs played in \"Boudica (Warrior Queen)\"?", "answer": "Emily Blunt", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Who is the playwright who wrote the play that Sakura no Sono's story focuses on?", "answer": "Anton Chekhov", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "One of Belron's brands in the United States is Safelite, based in what state?", "answer": "Ohio", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "The textbook \"Of Pandas and People\" was published by an organization based in what city and state?", "answer": "Richardson, Texas", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Fantastic Beasts and Where to Find Them is a 2016 fantasy film, the film stars Ez