ormer Australian rules football player, who appeared in a humorous TV advertising campaign by Meat and Livestock Australia mentioning the word \"un-Australian,\" born?", "answer": "1950", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What was the occupation of both Marguerite Radclyffe Hall and Charles Bukowski?", "answer": "poet", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Killer Be Killed is the debut studio album from the supergroup Killer Be Killed, included what Brazilian heavy metal band from Belo Horizonte?", "answer": "Sepultura", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "what University did the Dimensions of Culture author work for?", "answer": "Maastricht University", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Robert Hampton \"Robbie\" Rogers III, is an American professional soccer player who plays for LA Galaxy in Major League Soccer, in February 2013, Rogers came out as gay, becoming the second male soccer player in Britain to do so after Justin Fashanu in which year?", "answer": "1990", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What is the given name of the Jackson, Mississippi mayor succeeded by Tony Yarber?", "answer": "Edwin Finley Taliaferro", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Jeremy Rea Jackson, is a former American mixed martial artist from where, he is known as one of two men (along with K.J. Noons) to have finished Nick Diaz in mixed martial arts competition?", "answer": "California", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which film came out first, Olympia or Greetings from Out Here ?", "answer": "Olympia", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Zora Neale Hurston Museum of Fine Arts is located in which Florida county?", "answer": "Orange", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Timothy Upham rescued a brigadier general of what military branch ?", "answer": "United States Army", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What is the population of the city six miles north of Octagon City?", "answer": "1,953", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "which Four Diamond luxury hotel  hold The 2012 Evolution Championship Series fighting game event ", "answer": "Caesars Palace", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "The Portland Pilots women's basketball team are members of an athletic converence with member schools across what states?  ", "answer": "California, Oregon, Utah and Washington", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "The English man who influenced Zbigniew Brzezinski had what occupations?", "answer": "English geographer, academic, politician, the first Principal", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which brand sponsored the competition that Reggina Calcio was re-promoted to?", "answer": "TIM", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Yahya Abdul-Mateen II starred in an upcoming American superhero film that is being directed by James Wan, with a screenplay by who?", "answer": "Will Beall", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Semyon Aranovich Gershgorin and Vladimir Berkovich, have which occupation?", "answer": "mathematician", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Brian Hayes was born in a city whose name means what in Irish?", "answer": "marsh", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Yin Jian, also known as Dongshan, was an early member of the Communist Party of China(CPC) is the founding and ruling political party of which country?", "answer": "People's Republic of China", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "O\u00f9 est la maison de fromage is the debut album by an English performance poet that was born in what month?", "answer": "January", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "John, was the Count of Auxonne and Chalon-sur-Sa\u00f4ne in his own right, was a French nobleman, in contemporary documents, he was sometimes called \"Count of Burgundy\", in 1251, by which King?", "answer": "William II of Holland", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which film was released first, The Living Desert or Angels in the Outfield?", "answer": "The Living Desert", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Which comedian appeared in both Charlie Brooker's Weekly Wipe and Live at the Electric?", "answer": "Diane Morgan", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "The term \"Five Civilized Tribes\" derives from the colonial and early federal period in the history of the United States, and it refers to how many Native American nations, one being the Muscogee, also known as the Creek and the Creek Confederacy, are a closely related group of native North American tribes or Indigenous peoples of the Southeastern Woodlands?", "answer": "five", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which computer was released first, the Orao or the Mattel Aquarius?", "answer": "Aquarius", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "what airline did the presenter of the Stelios Award found? ", "answer": "easyJet", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Are Tom Araya and Danny Worsnop of the same nationality?", "answer": "no", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Who is the subject of the Springheel Saga and was said to have been first sighted in 1837?", "answer": "Spring-heeled Jack", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Who played a lead role in the television series based on Sir Arthur Conan Doyle's detective stories?", "answer": "Kang Soo-jin", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "One of the actor's from Harm's way received his most praised role as a war veteran Fred Derry.  What was the name of the movie Fred Derry is from?", "answer": "The Best Years of Our Lives", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What is the title of the 1978 play by this Nobel Prize-winning English playwright, screenwriter, director and actor who provided the standard for distinguishing between just talking and really communicating through silence in Western literature?", "answer": "Betrayal", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Guy Mezger holds wins over which former Dutch kickboxer?", "answer": "Semmy Schilt", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What large city is located near the McCrae Homestead? ", "answer": "Melbourne, Australia", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Barb Honchak holds a victory against someone born August 17, 1982 who currently competes in what?", "answer": "Ultimate Fighting Championship", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What American rock band from Tallahassee, Florida have showcased alternative rock bands along with many other groups?", "answer": "Mayday Parade", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": " Kim Sang-bum is best known for his role as So Yi-jung in \"Boys Over Flowers\", a South Korean television series, which aired in what year?", "answer": "2009", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "An example of a hidden asset is a frequent flier program that was chosen for a combined airline in what year?", "answer": "2011", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Who was regarded as the greatest switch hitter in baseball history and married to Merlyn Mantle?", "answer": "Mickey Mantle", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "You're No Good: was covered in a charting version by which soul singer and pianist?", "answer": "Betty Everett", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which American rapper co-wrote a song featured on the album unfold?", "answer": "Jay-Z", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What country hosts the rally that is similar to the Paris\u2013Dakar Rally, that takes place by pyramids?", "answer": "Egypt", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "In what year was the album that \"Watching the Wheels\" was on released?", "answer": "1980", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What national park housed a quasi-commune that arose in California in the late 1960s?", "answer": "Death Valley National Park", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which documentary came out first The Birth of Sak\u00e9 or Roam Sweet Home ?", "answer": "Roam Sweet Home", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Steyr M\u00e4nnlicher was originally part of what conglomerate?", "answer": "Steyr-Daimler-Puch", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Bill Monroe's bluegrass song Blue Moon of Kentucky was released by Elvis Presley on the B-side of his first ever single. What was that song? ", "answer": "That's All Right", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which slave's story inspired the novel that beings the \"trilogy\" that, according to Toni Morrison, Paradise completes?", "answer": "Margaret Garner", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What is the middle name of the composer of the \"American Beauty: Original Motion Picture Score\"?", "answer": "Montgomery", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "David Campbell was a leader for what unrecognized territory in what is now eastern Tennessee, United States?", "answer": "State of Franklin", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which \"The Playboy Club\" star is best  known for his performance in the romantic drama \"Latter Days\" ?", "answer": "Wes Ramsey", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Was Tom Forman or John Michael Crichton an American actor in the 1920s?", "answer": "Tom Forman", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Which musician is known for their baritone vocals, Eddie Vedder or Bruce Dickinson?", "answer": "Eddie Vedder", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Who founded the record company that Hopsin was signed to in 2007?", "answer": "Eazy-E and Dr.Dre", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Ted Strehlow married his first wife in a suburb of this city in South Australia?", "answer": "Adelaide", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Patricia van der Kammen served as a member of the European Parliament for what Dutch nationalist and right-wing populist political party in the Netherlands?", "answer": "The Party for Freedom", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Giuseppe Motta was a member of a council that has how many members ?", "answer": "seven-member", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which one of the founding members of deep purple referred to the studio album 'The Battle Rages On' as \"The cattle grazes on\"?", "answer": "Ritchie Blackmore", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Qubilah Shabazz is the daugther of the woman also known by what name?.", "answer": "Betty X", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "An American animator and film director known for co-directing \"The Lorax\", and also directed a 2015 American computer-animated comedy film that was a spinoff of what?", "answer": "Despicable Me", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Between Jerry Belson and James Broughton, who had a more diverse career?", "answer": "Jerry Belson", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Who has more locations, Fox's Pizza Den or Snappy Tomato Pizza?", "answer": "Fox's Pizza Den", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Which singer and songwriter worked with Mark S. Berry and was the lead singer of the Brit Award-Winning pop band Culture Club?", "answer": "Boy George", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "WHAT FILM STARRING KEITH LONEKER, DIRECTED BY STEVEN SODERBERGH AND WRITTEN BY SCOTT FRANK?", "answer": "Out of Sight", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which president of the United States first appointed a graduate of UC Berkeley School of Law as Secretary of State of the United States ?", "answer": "John F. Kennedy", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What contest did the composer of \"Into a Fantasy\" win in 2009?", "answer": "Eurovision Song Contest", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What 2017 biographical sports film was written by Simon Beaufoy and directed by husband and wife, Jonathan Dayton and Valerie Faris?", "answer": "Battle of the Sexes", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What year was the rock musical, in which Michael Greif was the stage director, released?", "answer": "2008", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which American chef known for wearing a fleece vest and orange crocs was featured in the PBS series \"Spain\u2026 on the road Again?\"", "answer": "Mario Batali", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which 2012 film was written by the screenwriter who also wrote Armageddon?", "answer": "Savages", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What type of animal is the Alaskan husky and Small M\u00fcnsterl\u00e4nder?", "answer": "dog", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Brison D. Gooch was an authority on which President of France from 1848 to 1852?", "answer": "Louis-Napol\u00e9on Bonaparte", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What is the birth date of this professional Italian racing driver, who was bested by 35.5 points to lose the 2008 Formula 3 Euro Series championship?", "answer": "12 January 1987", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Catch a Christmas Star is a 2013 Hallmark Channel film starring Shannon Elizabeth, is an American actress and former fashion model, born in which year?", "answer": "1973", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Westmoreland County, Pennsylvania is located west of a mountain range that runs for about how many miles?", "answer": "400", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Out of the Darkness was a film about a serial killer known as what?", "answer": "Son of Sam and the .44 Caliber Killer", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Western culture depicts cockroaches as vile pests and was popularized by a traditional folk song from which country?", "answer": "Mexico", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which mine was established earlier, Murray Brook Mine or Temagami-Lorrain Mine?", "answer": "Temagami-Lorrain Mine", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "The actor that played Dr. Sam Loomis in \"Halloween\" also stars with Gary Bond in a 1971 thriller film directed by who?", "answer": "Ted Kotcheff", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Collen Kay Hutchins won the crown for Miss America 1952, what is the city it was held in known for?", "answer": "known for its casinos, boardwalks, and beaches.", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "How many air combat victories did Ferdinand von Richthofen's pilot nephew have?", "answer": "80", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Are Tom DiCillo and Elem Klimov both directors?", "answer": "yes", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "What was the original name of the liberal arts college in Waterville, Maine that sponsors The Associated Kyoto Program?", "answer": "the Maine Literary and Theological Institution", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which road located on the St. Zacharie, Maine - St. Zacharie, Quebec border stretches 96 miles and was built by the Great Northern Paper Company? ", "answer": "Golden Road", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "The songs on Cover your tracks are named after movies from an American actor and producer who has been nominated for how many academy awards?", "answer": "three", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which Indian singer sang a wedding-themed Punjabi dance song based on the classic folk song \"Chitta Kukkad Banere Te\" and also featured on the reality show, Indian Idol?", "answer": "Neha Kakkar", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Chris Daughtry and Bobby Fuller, are which nationality?", "answer": "American", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Do Georg Trakl and Angela Carter share the same nationality?", "answer": "no", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Lex Luger, who handled production in Brake Lights, is also a retired what?", "answer": "professional wrestler", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Oscar Torre was in what 2013 American comedy film produced by Legendary Pictures?", "answer": "The Hangover Part III", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Who is a graphic designer best known for designing the \"swoosh\" logo for an American multinational corporation that is engaged in the design, development, manufacturing, and worldwide marketing and sales of footwear, apparel, equipment, accessories, and services ?", "answer": "Carolyn Davidson", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Dekh Magar Pyaar Say starred what Pakistani actress and model who appears in Pakistani and what other films and serials?", "answer": "Bollywood", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Park Holme a southern suburb of Adelaide in the City of Marion, South Australia is adjacent to Ascot Park, Edwardstown, South Plympton, Mitchell Park, Clovelly Park, Glengowrie, Morphettville and Oaklands Park whose major feature is what? ", "answer": "The Marion Shopping Centre", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Lous Marson has played for the Philadelphia Phillies and another MLB team that was established in what year?", "answer": "1901", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Scottish term and quarter days are the four divisions of the legal year, historically used as the days when contracts and leases would begin and end, servants would be hired or dismissed, and rent, interest on loans, and ministers' stipends would become due, Lammas is one of the Quarter Days, Lammas Day (Anglo-Saxon \"hlaf-mas\", \"loaf-mass\"), is a holiday celebrated in some English-speaking countries in the Northern Hemisphere, usually between 1 August and 1 of which month?", "answer": "September", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which Montana county has a county seat with a population of 1,893 at the 2010 census?", "answer": "Stillwater County, Montana", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Mouni Roy was a contestant on the Indian version of what show?", "answer": "Strictly Come Dancing", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which town is served by Greenbank railway station and lies in the heart of the Cheshire Plain?", "answer": "Northwich", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "The Red River Showdown and the State Fair Classic football games are both played in what stadium during the State Fair of Texas in October?", "answer": "Cotton Bowl", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "When was Charlie Sheen's brother who plays alongside him in the film Cadence born?", "answer": "August 7, 1963", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Numenera is an award-winning science fantasy tabletop role-playing game (RPG) set in the far distant future, written by Monte Cook, an American professional table-top role-playing game designer and writer, best known for his work on what?", "answer": "Dungeons & Dragons", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which English A&R executive and producer has worked with The Scottish/Irish folk rock band The Waterboys?", "answer": "John Owen Williams", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What religion is the university Tae Hyun-sil studied in based in?", "answer": "Buddhism", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Who has had a greater variety of careers, David Butler or Erin Wiedner?", "answer": "David Butler", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Jack and Jill and The Believer, are distributed how often?", "answer": "bi-monthly", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Who is older, Lee Sung-min or Ray Wilson?", "answer": "Raymond Wilson", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "When was the Italian composer died who is Marcel Maas repertoire except Bach to the moderns?", "answer": "23 July 1757", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What rish veterinary surgeon heads the television series The Supervet?", "answer": "Noel Fitzpatrick", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "How many constituencies did this British statesman, army officer, and writer represent who authorized the covert organization British Security Co-ordination in New York?", "answer": "five constituencies", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Saint Mark Methodist Church is one of the few remaining Gothic Revival granite churches in Atlanta, Georgia, the architecture is notable for its use of which quartz monzonite dome monadnock and the site of Stone Mountain Park in Stone Mountain, Georgia?", "answer": "Stone Mountain", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What award did Barathea win at Churchill Downs in 1994?", "answer": "Breeders' Cup Mile", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Who s the cheif executive officer of the company that is the largest provider of mutual funds and the second-largest provider of exchange-traded funds (ETFs) in the world?", "answer": "Mortimer J. \"Tim\" Buckley", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Extralarge stars what American actor whose most famous role is Ricardo Tubbs in Miami Vice?", "answer": "Philip Michael Thomas", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Simon Finnigan was born in what county?", "answer": "Cheshire", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Fritz Lang was an Austrian film director, producer and screenwriter, Lang's final film work was an acting role as himself in which 1963 French drama film written and directed by Jean-Luc Godard, based on the Italian novel \"Il disprezzo\" (\"A Ghost at Noon\")?", "answer": "Contempt", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "When was the Swiss football administrator born who was the President of FIFA.before Gianni Infantino ?", "answer": "10 March 1936", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Kim Eui-sung is an actor who appears in the TV series \"W\", a 2016 South Korean television series that airs on what network?", "answer": "MBC", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "The soldier who received the Medal of Honor for valor demonstrated at the age of 19 for single-handedly holding off an entire company of German soldiers for an hour at the Colmar Pocket in France starred in what 1957 Western film?", "answer": "Night Passage", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What American author was the writer of \"the Gate Thief\"?", "answer": "Orson Scott Card", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "The thirteenth episode of \"The Simpsons\"' seventh season features a president who was Vice President of the US during what years?", "answer": "1981 to 1989", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which was decided first, Selective Draft Law Cases or Katzenbach v. McClung?", "answer": "Selective Draft Law Cases", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "What is does Ulrik Cold have to do with L'incoronazione di Poppea?", "answer": "he made his professional opera debut", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "K\u0161y\u0161tof Lavrinovi\u010d and his twin brother Darju\u0161 Lavrinovi\u010d both play for which team?", "answer": "Lietkabelis Panev\u0117\u017eys", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "The Legislative Assembly of Assiniboia was set up under the provisional government led by a Canadian politician and founder of what province?", "answer": "Manitoba", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Are both Porcelaine and Grand Anglo-Fran\u00e7ais Tricolore scenthounds crossed with Foxhounds?", "answer": "no", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Marchesa, is a brand specializing in high end womenswear, established in what year, by co-founder, Georgina Rose Chapman, an English fashion designer and actress? ", "answer": "2004", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which symbiotic characters were introduced in the two-part episode of Spider-Man? ", "answer": "Venom and Carnage", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Geeks & Greeks is a semi-autobiographical graphic novel written by humorist Steve Altes, it has been described as \"Good Will Hunting\" meets what?", "answer": "Animal House", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "IN 2005 WHAT AUSTRALIAN - AMERICAN LYRIC SOPRANO PERFOMED IN GIULIO CESARE?", "answer": "Danielle de Niese", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which dog breed, the Catahoula Cur or the Flat-Coated Retriever, is a gundog breed originating from the United Kingdom?", "answer": "Flat-Coated Retriever", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "When was the american footballer coach who served the second and final season of his first stint as Stanford's head coach born? ", "answer": "November 30, 1931", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "How old was the boy that William S. Bowdern performed an exorcism on?", "answer": "14-year-old", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "When was the 2004 Intercontinental Cup man of the match born?", "answer": "11 November 1977", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Good Morning Britain was TV-am's flagship breakfast television show, broadcast on weekdays from February 1983 until the franchise ended in 1992, it had many different presenters throughout its run but the most enduring pairing was Anne Diamond and Nick Owen, an English television presenter and newsreader, best known for presenting the breakfast television programme \"TV-am\" and the BBC's local news show \"Midlands Today\" since what year?", "answer": "1997", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Are Kristoffer Rygg and Stevie Ray Vaughan both producers?", "answer": "yes", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "What date was the ninth studio album by Brian Wayne Transeau released?", "answer": "Aug