r was the South Korean film starring Moon Char-Won and an actor who made his debut in 2003's \"Oldboy\" made?", "answer": "2016", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What action-adventure survival video game published by the indie studio Hello Games was combined with \"Super Mario Brothers\" to create the fangame \"No Mario's Sky\"?", "answer": "No Man's Sky", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What UK running race featured T12/13 event winner El Amin Chentouf?", "answer": "London Marathon", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "\"Picture to Burn\" is a song recorded by American singer-songwriter Taylor Swift, was released on February 3, 2008 by which organization, as the fourth single, from her eponymous studio album,\"Taylor Swift\" (2006)?", "answer": "Big Machine Records", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which was the first World Series where games were played outside the United States?", "answer": "1992 World Series", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Who played first base for the American League team in what ESPN selected as the \"Greatest of All Time\" in their \"World Series 100th Anniversary\" countdown?", "answer": "Paul Anthony Sorrento", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which American rock singer of Puerto Rican descent marked his first live performance as a solo artist at Live at the Gods Festival 2002? ", "answer": "Jeff Scott Soto", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Are the cities of Huludao and Qian'an, Hebei both located in China?", "answer": "yes", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Who replaced the chairman of the AFL Commission who started in 2007?", "answer": "Richard Goyder", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which Nordic Bronze Age artifact from the 2nd millennium BC was discovered in Denmark?", "answer": "Trundholm sun chariot", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Did Albert Camus and Ram\u00f3n del Valle-Incl\u00e1n both write?", "answer": "yes", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Which tower was planned to be higher of 590 Madison Avenue and 80 South 