iversity did one of Josiah Cotton's relatives have an honorary doctorate from?", "answer": "University of Glasgow", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Jan Mikulicz-Radecki was a professor in which town that is currently known as Kaliningrad, Russia? ", "answer": "K\u00f6nigsberg", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which is a type of grass, Pleurothallis or Lamarckia?", "answer": "Lamarckia", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Margaret Trudeau had a son who died in an avalanche in what year?", "answer": "1998", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Jagdgeschwader 54 was piloted by the fighter ace of what nationality during World War II?", "answer": "Austria", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Hong Kong based company produces a productt whose canonese name is Lap ceung what is the english translation?", "answer": "Chinese sausage", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What is the birthyear of the quarterback drafted by the NFL team in the 1999 draft that plays in the University of Phoenix Stadium?", "answer": "1976", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which game has more cards, Rummoli or Glasnost The Game ?", "answer": "Rummoli", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Which company owned by British Film producer Kevin Loader and his partner Roger Michell produced the 2017 film My Cousin Rachel?", "answer": "Free Range Films", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What melody from the French opera \"Genevi\u00e8ve de Brabant\" is used by Western Illinois University before all of it's football games and the United States Marine Corps as it's military hymn?", "answer": "\"Potpourri-Fantasie\"", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Charles Halford played Francis \"Chas\" Chandler in a tv series that stars what actor in the title role?", "answer": "Matt Ryan", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Operation \"Panchai Palang, or Panther's Claw\" was part of the war with the public goal to dismantle what organization? ", "answer": "al-Qaeda", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Jack G. Real was an aerospace pioneer and a confidant of an american business man who passed away in what year ?", "answer": "1976", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "The band that created the album Live at Bell's comes from what city and state?", "answer": "Kalamazoo, Michigan", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "USS \"Elrod\" (FFG-55), an \"Oliver Hazard Perry\"-class frigate, is a ship of the United States Navy named after Captain Henry T. Elrod (1905\u20131941), a Marine aviator who was posthumously awarded the Medal of Honor in World War II, for his heroism in the defense of which coral atoll in the western Pacific Ocean in the northeastern area of the Micronesia subregion, 1,501 mi east of Guam, 2,298 mi west of Honolulu and 1,991 mi southeast of Tokyo?", "answer": "Wake Island", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "In what city was Ryan Richards drafted by the Spurs?", "answer": "New York City", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What were Diamond and Shogun?", "answer": "board game", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Are Allium and Mimulus both genuses?", "answer": "yes", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Between Shades of Gray is the debut novel by a writer whose work in published in how many languages?", "answer": "thirty", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "The Prodigy who sampled \"Funky Man\" in a song \"Smack My Bitch Up\" belongs to which nationality? ", "answer": "British", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Who is the only constant member of the band behind \"Epitome of Turture\"?", "answer": "Tom Angelripper", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Krista Detor has been featured on the BBC with a singer sometimes known by what nickname?", "answer": "'The Rochdale Cowboy'", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Some Things I Know is the second album from a singer born in what year?", "answer": "1966", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What film did Alan Baumgarten edit in which the principal photography on the film began on March 8, 2013, in Boston and Worcester, Massachusetts, and New York City?", "answer": "American Hustle", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which of these programs has already launched, Astron or James Webb Space Telescope?", "answer": "Astron", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Which canal was completed first, Dundee Canal or Cascade Locks and Canal?", "answer": "Dundee Canal", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "When was the the ship launched ,that along with the Tripitz and the L\u00fctzow was a target for  Operation Source ?", "answer": "3 October 1936.", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What Painkiller Jane heroine also appeared with Michael Caine and Robert Duvall in \"Secondhand Lions\"?", "answer": "Emmanuelle Vaugier", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "William Duane's co-worker was the first female professor at which university?", "answer": "University of Paris", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What is the real first name of the DJ who compiled the album FabricLive.24?", "answer": "Thomas", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Yale is an unincorporated community in a county that had how many inhabitants in 2010 ?", "answer": "39,134", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What album, that was the follow-up to Speak Now, was released before the album 1989?", "answer": "Red", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Are Kamet and Kongur Tagh both mountains?", "answer": "yes", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "What do Down Beat and Better Homes and Gardens have in common?", "answer": "magazine", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "What were this group of people referred to as (\"Not Ready For what?) that Jon Lovitz was a member of from 1985 to 1990?", "answer": "Prime Time Players", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Who was a United States Secretary of State who had a fashion designed by Herv\u00e9 Pierre Braillard?", "answer": "Hillary Clinton", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What does Bandar-log mean in the second story of \"The Jungle Book\"?", "answer": "monkeys of the Seeonee jungle", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "In what year did 