ed to prevent end?", "answer": "January 23, 1827", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "The Commissioner of Police heads up the largest disciplined service under the Security Bureau of Hong Kong, and reports to whom?", "answer": "Secretary for Security", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Who was the father of the Danish king involved in the Battle of Marton?", "answer": "Ragnar Lodbrok", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which rock band has more members, Muse or The Pretty Reckless?", "answer": "The Pretty Reckless", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Which is a drink named celebrating a train which ran between New York City and Chicago: Sundowner or 20th Century?", "answer": "20th Century", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "What is the name of the culture cultivated in the area of Duncan Farm and Golden Eagle?", "answer": "Hopewell tradition", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Cleophers Hatcher was the first football coach at what member school of the Thurgood Marshall College Fund?", "answer": "Mississippi Valley State University", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Jeff Bauman was the subject of a drama film directed by whom?", "answer": "David Gordon Green", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What \"Pennies From Heaven\" star also appeared in \"Greystoke: The Legend of Tarzan, Lord of the Apes\"?", "answer": "Cheryl Campbell", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "The 2012\u201313 FC Sion season saw the signing of which now-manager of AC Milan Primavera?", "answer": "Gennaro Ivan \"Rino\" Gattuso", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Where is Zambia located?", "answer": "south central Africa", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Done Fullmer and Gene Fullmer were both what type of athlete?", "answer": "boxer", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "In particle physics, the Yukawa interaction was named after which Japanese theoretical physicist?", "answer": "Hideki Yukawa", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Where did the 2008 film starring Grayson \"The Professor\" Boucher premiere?", "