hed in the US?", "answer": "no", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "What are some of the characteristics of Champale because it is a Malt liquor?", "answer": "high alcohol content", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "In what way is Pierre Morel different than Harry Lachman", "answer": "French film director and cinematographer", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Who was born on November 12th, 1944 and is a commentator on Madden NFL 2003?", "answer": "Al Michaels", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What is the nickname of the Premier League match where a Manchester player was awarded a penalty after tumbling over a central defender's outstretched leg?", "answer": "Battle of the Buffet", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Are Nate Ruess and Miles Hunt in the same band?", "answer": "no", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "The McCarran Airport Connector serves what airport named after late U.S. Senator Pat McCarran?", "answer": "McCarran International Airport", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which filmmaker, Hobart Henley or Budd Boetticher, is most famous for the series of low-budget Westerns he made in the late 1950s starring Randolph Scott?", "answer": "Budd Boetticher", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Are Peperomia and Anaphalis both types of plants?", "answer": "yes", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "What character, ranked by Wizard as the 24th Greatest Villain of All Time, once led Titans East?", "answer": "Deathstroke", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What football team is featured in the first episode of the eighteenth season of South Park?", "answer": "Washington Redskins", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which English indie rock band was remixed by Alex Metric?", "answer": "Bloc Party", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Ted Sundquist was promoted to GM of the Denver Broncos in 2001 by the family who purchased the team from which former owner in 1984?", "answer": "Edgar Kaiser", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which low-bypass afterburning turbofa