i Daei", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What actor sold 25 million records as of 2003 and starred in Bullet for Hire? ", "answer": "Jacky Cheung", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Are Watertown International Airport and Alexandria International Airport both airports in the same state ?", "answer": "no", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "The 2002 MAC Championship Game was played in the West Virginia city that is in what two counties?", "answer": "Cabell County and Wayne County", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Where does the English football club based onin which Ian Arnold had a loan spell?", "answer": "Stalybridge, Greater Manchester", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "The Royal Bank of Scotland \u00a320 note is a banknote of the pound sterling, the current cotton note, first issued in which year, bears an image of Lord Ilay, one of the founders of the bank, on the obverse and a vignette on the reverse of Brodick Castle, a castle situated outside the port of Brodick on the Isle of Arran, an island in the Firth of Clyde, Scotland?", "answer": "1987", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What is the name of Glitz's parent that has a headquarters location across the interstate from the Headquarters of Adult Swim?", "answer": "Turner Broadcasting System", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Jennifer Aniston is the daughter of an actor best known for his role on what daytime drama series?", "answer": "\"Days of Our Lives\"", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Baby Jay is part of which athletic teams that represent the University of Kansas?", "answer": "Kansas Jayhawks", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What is the American guitar manufacturer headquartered in Maryland founded in 1985 that endorsed Rian Adkinson?", "answer": "PRS Guitars", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which typical dish of the Faroe Islands is eaten in many parts of the world?", "answer": "Grind og spik", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Loud was an album recorded during the time in which Rihanna was fil