en?", "answer": "Enrique Carreras", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "What alternative rock band, formed in Seattle in 1988 release the compilation album Superfuzz Bigmuff Plus Early Singles in October 1990?", "answer": "Mudhoney", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Who is best known for their work on \"One Life to Live\", Michael Malone or Susan Straight?", "answer": "Michael Malone", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "What type of site are both Cahokia and Emerald Mound and Village Site?", "answer": "pre-Columbian", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Chillicothe Correctional Institution has housed the serial killer known by what nickname?", "answer": "Cleveland Strangler", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "William \"Bill\" MacDonald, was a Scottish heavyweight wrestling champion, and was the father of actor Kenneth MacDonald, who was most famous for playing the role of Mike Fisher in the British sitcom \"Only Fools and Horses\", a British television sitcom created and written by John Sullivan, with sixteen sporadic Christmas specials aired, until the end of the show in which year?", "answer": "2003", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which Swedish movie, which centers on a middle-aged intellectual who attempts to bargain with God, was presented with the award for Best film in 1987?", "answer": "The Sacrifice", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "In what region of England did an independent school established in 1896 merge with King Edward VII and Queen Mary School? ", "answer": "the Fylde", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Bob Mould was the songwriter for the rock band formed in what city in 1979?", "answer": "Saint Paul, Minnesota", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "\"Infinite Dreams\" is a live single released by a band formed in which year ?", "answer": "1975", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Do the bands, Gumball and Kings of Convenience, come from two different countries?", "answer": "yes", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "What is the bowling average of the leading wicket-taker in the 1956\u201357 Quaid-e-Azam Trophy competition?", "answer": "24.70", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What team did Jarrett Brown play for that was a member of the National Collegiate Athletic Association Division?", "answer": "West Virginia Mountaineers", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Taedonggang beer is the leading brand produced by a state-owned brewery in which Asian city?", "answer": "Pyongyang", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What do Chalk FarM and Haim have in common?", "answer": "rock band", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Which ski and snowboard resort has its base 3,441 meters to the north of the highest mountain in both the Spring Mountains and Clark County, Nevada?", "answer": "Lee Canyon", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "In which city was the birthplace of Alessandro Rinaldi?", "answer": "Cremona", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What is a publication that the host of Reid Report politically comments in?", "answer": "The Daily Beast", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Do Welcome to Durham, USA and The Sorrow and the Pity examine the same topic ?", "answer": "no", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Kwon Hyuk's single released in 2016 features what instrument? ", "answer": "synthesizers", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which movie came first Miracle of the White Stallions or Bedknobs and Broomsticks?", "answer": "Miracle of the White Stallions", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Did both Ormindo and Doktor Faust perform at the Teatro San Cassiano opera house?", "answer": "no", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Which singer, Lee Gi-kwang or Kenny Greene, originally debuted as solo singer with the stage name AJ?", "answer": "Lee Gi-kwang", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Which  South Korean boy band has Chase Vincent Malone worked with ", "answer": "U-KISS", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Nancy Langston is a professor at the college located in what Michigan city?", "answer": "Houghton", "type": "bridge"},