l satellite that launched into orbit in what year?", "answer": "1998", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "The Day of the Roses was based on which event, which took place just outside Sydney, Australia?", "answer": "Granville rail disaster", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Was Blink-182 or The Verve Pipe formed further east?", "answer": "The Verve Pipe", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Who was the only actor to appear in leading roles in both The Hunt for Red October (rebooted in 2002 as The Sum of All Fears) and its sequel?", "answer": "James Earl Jones", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What actress, born on August 14th, 1963 won best supporting actress in 1986 for her role in the film \"Manon des Sources\"?", "answer": "Emmanuelle B\u00e9art", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "which band was formed first, Dubstar or Concrete Blonde?", "answer": "Concrete Blonde", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "The first female member of the Australian children's music group formed in Sydney, New South Wales, in 1991 was born in what year?", "answer": "1989", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "How many number-one US jazz albums did this American artist who released Blue Light, Red Light release?", "answer": "ten", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Who started earlier, Ghinzu or Charlotte Gainsbourg?", "answer": "Charlotte Lucy Gainsbourg", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Which correspondent of Frederick Goddard Tuckerman was an American essayist, lecturer, and poet who led the transcendentalist movement of the mid-19th century?", "answer": "Ralph Waldo Emerson", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Down Twisted starred an American actress and former model who was born on February 11th of what year?", "answer": "1961", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which genus of flowering plants contains eight species all from the western Cape Province of South Africa, Calycanthus or Coleonema?", "answer": "Coleonema", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Who managed cinematography for th