ce the the 1965 Atlantic hurricane season was the first to use the modern-day bounds for an Atlantic hurricane season, which are June 1 to 30 of ?", "answer": "November", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Who was the older brother of the man who promoted a beer by a brewing company based in Louisville, Kentucky?", "answer": "Jimmy", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Where was the director of a 2003 Christmas-themed romantic comedy film born?", "answer": "New Zealand", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What Canadian actor acted with Catherine O'hara in \"Waiting for Guffman\"?", "answer": "Eugene Levy", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Stoke Newington Central is a ward in the London Borough of Hackney, it corresponds roughly to Stoke Newington in London, UK and forms part of the Hackney North and Stoke Newington constituency of which British Labour Party politician, who was appointed Shadow Home Secretary, in October 2016?", "answer": "Diane Julie Abbott", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "The American actress and singer Cristin Milioti appeared in which 2013 American film directed by Martin Scorsese?", "answer": "The Wolf of Wall Street", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Manual of The Mother Church was written by which founder of Christian Science?", "answer": "Mary Baker Eddy", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "\u00dcberjam Deux is a studio album that features an American jazz keyboards player who is listed as what?", "answer": "a Steinway Artist", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Who produce 80 to 90 percent of the text to the opera at which Timothy Meyers has a role of Bertolt Brecht's? ", "answer": "Hauptmann", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "\"Come and take it\" was a historic slogan used in the first military engagement of which revolution?", "answer": "the Texas Revolution", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "The Christmas Album is the twentieth studio album by Neil Diamond, and his first to feature Christmas music, it features orchestral and choir arrangements, by