ark that the Beast's Castle themed resturant at Walt Disney World Resort is located in?", "answer": "WED Enterprises", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Situational analysis was coined in a book by Karl Popper in what year?", "answer": "1957", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Who directed the film that won 6 out 10 of its nominations at the 37th C\u00e9sar Awards?", "answer": "Michel Hazanavicius", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Legoland Billund Resort, which includes the theme park ride Lost Kingdom, is located in what country?", "answer": "Denmark", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Where was the the pageant held where Sabrina Herft represented her country in?", "answer": "The AXIS, Las Vegas, Nevada, United States", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What is the nationality of one of the men for whom the Schumann\u2013Runge bands are named?", "answer": "German", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What was the nationality of the actress that played opposite Pat Healy in Take Me?", "answer": "American", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "The Amplifetes have, on their own, worked with which American singer and businesswoman?", "answer": "Madonna Louise Ciccone", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Le Juge is a comic whose story is inspired by a man who called himself what?", "answer": "\"The Law West of the Pecos\"", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Queensbury, New York is named in honor of a Queen who was married to King George III in which year ?", "answer": "1761", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Canadian professional basketball player Jordan Ashley Adams has a brother Kyle Wiltjer who plays for which NBA team?", "answer": "Houston Rockets", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Who wrote the series where Una Palliser  is the singer on the end credits?", "answer": "Barry Devlin", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Where is the company Super Deluxe website of Penelope princess of pets located?  Downtown Los Angeles", "answer": "downtown Los Angeles.", "type": "bridge"}, {"questi