r of a collection of short stories originally published in 1952 as The Apple Tree, which was made into a 1963 American horror-thriller film directed by Alfred Hitchcock ?", "answer": "Daphne du Maurier", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What's the name of the actress who grew up in Gold Coast, Queensland that stars in the episode Power Hungry from the television series Fringe?", "answer": "Anna Torv", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "John McAleese led an SAS team that stormed an embassy in what location?", "answer": "South Kensington, London", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "When was the American government official which took over from Thomas A. Shannon Jr. after he was confirmed born? ", "answer": "March 23, 1952", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Are The Barefoot Executive and Casey Connor both regarding lacrosse?", "answer": "no", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "The Silverdome refers to the stadium that opened in what year?", "answer": "1975", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What American singer-songwriter described as \"rock and roll's first great wild man\" signed with Sun Records?", "answer": "Jerry Lee Lewis", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "In 2005, Armonico Consort produced Henry Purcell's adaptation of \"A Midsummer Night's Dream\"?", "answer": "Henry Purcell\u2019s The Fairy-Queen", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "How many liters of beer did the company, that now makes a beer that became well-known among American GIs during the war in Vietnam in the 1960s and 1970s, produce in 2011?", "answer": "1.2 billion", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Welshly Arms is influenced by the Motown Records R&B group form 1960's and 1970's who still travel with one remaining original member, who is that member?", "answer": "Otis Williams", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "The father of the founder of the Kushner Companies came to the US from Belarus in what year?", "answer": "1949", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What co-educational liberal arts college in the 