olitics?", "answer": "University of Essex", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Zhang Lanxin played a role in which film co-produced, written, directed by, and starring Jackie Chan?", "answer": "CZ12", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which breed is larger in size, the Braque Saint-Germain or the Jack Russell Terrier?", "answer": "Braque Saint-Germain", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Which peak is in the Saltoro Mountains, Broad Peak or Saltoro Kangri?", "answer": "Saltoro Kangri", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "What chancellor of a private university in Phnom Penh graduated from a university with campuses at Lismore and Coffs Harbour in northern New South Wales?", "answer": "Mr. Ich Seng", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "A Streetcar named Desire is a 1995 television drama film, starring what actress who received two Academy awards, one tony award, three emmy awards, five golden Globe awards, and how many screen actors guild awards?", "answer": "one", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Who created the American television sitcom in which Ed O'Neill plays the role of Al Bundy?", "answer": "Michael G. Moye and Ron Leavitt", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Choctaw mythology is related to Choctaws, a Native American tribe, originally from the Southeastern United States (Mississippi, Alabama, and Louisiana), today the Choctaws have four tribes, what is the group name, is one of three federally recognized tribes of Choctaw Native Americans, and is the only federally recognized Native American tribe in the state?", "answer": "Mississippi Band of Choctaw Indians", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "MedStar Washington Hospital Center and Howard University Hospital are both located in what city?", "answer": "Washington, D.C.,", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "E. J. Whitten Medal is named after an Australian rules footballer born on which day ?", "answer": "27 July 1933", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "They Shall Have Music was a musical that starred which support