es, California and was previously called Kara's Flowers?", "answer": "Maroon 5", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "The great-great-grandfather of current head of the House of Hohenzollern held what official title?", "answer": "Kaiser", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "On October 4 Gowell hit a double on a 3\u20132 count, hitting a fastball by a pitcher nicknamed what?", "answer": "Gentleman Jim", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "The Imperial Arcade opened in 1891 on the site now occupied by a shopping centre operated by what company?", "answer": "Scentre Group", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "24 Minutes of \"The Simpsons\" was co-written by which American television writer and producer born in 1959?", "answer": "Ian Maxtone-Graham", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Springfield, Missouri is known as the \"birthplace\" of which original highway in the US Highway System?", "answer": "U.S. Route 66", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which Russian Composer is the Pyotr Ilyich Tchaikovsky symphonic poem Francesca da Rimini, dedicated to? ", "answer": "Sergei Taneyev", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Scream consists of rides of this type in which  the track turns riders upside-down and then returns them to an upright position that has early forms dating back to what year", "answer": "1848", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which tennis player also became a coach, S\u00e9bastien Lareau or Martina Navratilova?", "answer": "Martina Navratilova", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Which movie was released direct to video, The Super Snail Adventure or Barbie and the Three Musketeers?", "answer": "Barbie and the Three Musketeers", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Which film is more suitable with watching with your children, 4 or Bangkok Girl?", "answer": "4", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Which 17th century tower house is in  Dalcross Highland", "answer": "Dalcross Castle", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "In what year was the person who wrote the lyrics for \"Chaar Kadam\" born?", "answer": "1970", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Did Peter Hooton and Floor Jansen found the band The Farm together?", "answer": "no", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "What nationality are both Graziano Delrio and Matteo Renzi?", "answer": "Italian", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Who is the CEO of an airline with its head office in Tremblay-en-France, France?", "answer": "Frantz Yvelin", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What movie is Mark Herman well known for creating?", "answer": "The Boy in the Striped Pyjamas", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What is MV \"Sygna\" located north of the Hunter river in New South Wales, australia?", "answer": "MV \"Sygna\" was a 53,000 tonne Norwegian bulk carrier and now shipwreck", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Fash FC was a weekly UK television programme: a reality/documentary show following ex-professional footballer John Fashanu, an English television presenter and former professional footballer of Nigerian (paternal) and Guyanese (maternal) descent, in his former career, he was a centre-forward from 1978 until 1995, most notably in an eight-year spell at which organization?", "answer": "Wimbledon F.C.", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Peter Hugh Pocklington is an advocate of an economic system that is free from intervention by which party ?", "answer": "government", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which American home magazine was published by Meredith Corporation and written by Gladys Bagg Taber? ", "answer": "Family Circle", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Who was born first, Aaron Katz or Jim Sharman?", "answer": "James David Sharman", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Is At the Drive-In or Black Stone Cherry from further north?", "answer": "Black Stone Cherry", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Which is a band, Tove Lo or P.O.D.?", "answer": "P.O.D.", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "\"War Song\" is a 1971 song by Graham Nash and what former member of Buffalo Springfield?", "answ