 "who wrote hello, goodbye and i am the walrus?", "answer": "written by Paul McCartney", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What was the codename for the battle where the 9th Amphibian Tractor Battalion supported the 6th Marine Division?", "answer": "Operation Iceberg", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What annual Austrian society event which takes place in the building of Vienna State Opera in Vienna was featured in the made-for-TV movie Opernball?", "answer": "The Vienna Opera Ball", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "With little outside influence, the Pashtun culture is used mostly in what type of areas?", "answer": "rural tribal", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "WHich actor from Sweet Hereafter previously won a Tony Award for their performance in \"The Homecoming\"", "answer": "Ian Holm", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Jeremy Stacey is a british drummer who has played with an English singer who is known for his gritty voice and what type of body movement?", "answer": "spasmodic", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What date did an ABC network television film starring Calvin Jung air?", "answer": "November 20, 1983", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "The show \"O\" at the Bellagio is located in what city?", "answer": "Las Vegas", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which Brazilian actress starred in the independent film directed by Eric Eason, Journey to the End of the Night?", "answer": "Alice Braga", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which act is from Japan, L'Arc-en-Ciel or Lorde?", "answer": "L'Arc-en-Ciel (\"The Rainbow\" in French, stylized as L'Arc~en~Ciel) is a Japanese rock band", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "What regular guest of \"7 Day Sunday\" also worked extensively with John Oliver on \"Political Animal\", \"The Department\", and \"The Bugle\"?", "answer": "Andy Zaltzman", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "who is older Gregg Brandon or Urban Meyer ?", "answer": "Gregg Brandon", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Are both Dodecatheon and Bloomeria native to North America?", "answer": "yes", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Invincible is based on the story of which Philadelphia Eagles player?", "answer": "Vincent Papale", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "When did the city located on the north bank of the river running through North Yorkshire and Lancashire gain city status?", "answer": "2002", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What kind of group does Vertical Horizon and Against the Current have in common?", "answer": "rock band", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Based on these paragraphs, which band has more members, Empire Circus, or Maroon 5?", "answer": "Maroon 5", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Dean Hood is the former head football coach at a university that is a regional comprehensive institution located in what city in Kentucky?", "answer": "Richmond", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "An American football player and coach who compiled a record of 116-119-7, served as head coach of a private four-year Christian-based college founded in what year?", "answer": "1886", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Michael Sragow edited film essays for the journalist whose autobiographical novel won what posthumous award?", "answer": "1958 Pulitzer Prize", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "How many member countries does the organization for which Paul Gustafsson held the position Representation in Paris in 1976 ? ", "answer": "35", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Alan Schechter is Professor at Wellesley College and supervised what 92-page paper for a former student?", "answer": "There Is Only the Fight . . . : An Analysis of the Alinsky Model", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Richard George Van Gelder, was a prominent mammalogist who served as the Curator of Mammalogy for which organization, located on the Upper West Side of Manhattan, New York City, is one of the largest museums in the world, abbreviated as AMNH?", "answer": "American Museum of Natural History", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which convicted car thief was murdered one week before Lewis Moran?", "answer": "Andrew Veniamin", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "The Danske Bank Premiership was founded by whom? ", "answer": "John McCredy McAlery", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What occupation did George Gershwin and Jacques Offenbach share?", "answer": "composer", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Which battle took place first Operation Diadem or Battle of the Wilderness ?", "answer": "Battle of the Wilderness", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Where did the story in which India Eisley took a role in its  2016 television film takes place?", "answer": "Southeastern United States", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which documentary provides a more in depth look at a specific moment in time, That's Dancing! or The Reflektor Tapes?", "answer": "The Reflektor Tapes", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "What character played by Gary Dubin in a 1978 American thriller film directed by Jeannot Szwarc?", "answer": "Eddie Marchand", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "In between Mellow Mushroom and Gatti's Pizza which one has corporate offices are in Austin, Texas?", "answer": "Gatti's Pizza", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Were The Dangerous Summer and Archers of Loaf both founded in the same State ?", "answer": "no", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "What is a monthly women's interest magazine launched by Time Inc. in 2000, Real Simple or Gospel Advocate?", "answer": "Real Simple", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "The 3rd IAAF World Athletics Final was held at a stadium that serves primarily as the home stadium of which teams ?", "answer": "AS Monaco and the Monaco national football team", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Where was the man who attempted to assassinate Adolph Botnick from?", "answer": "Greenwood, Mississippi", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "The performing arts center where The Hudson Museum is located in has been operating since what year?", "answer": "1986", "type": "bridge"}, {"ques