illed My Mother", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Where was the leader of the resistance group referred to as FPO active during World War II?", "answer": "Vilnius", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What was the name of the lead guitarist of the band that released the album Illusion of Progress in 2008?", "answer": "Mike Mushok", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "When was the American professional poker player who starred in Extraction born?", "answer": "December 7, 1980", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What Irish rock band from Dublin formed in 1976 also participated in Folkways: The Original Vision in 1989 as a way to raise funds?", "answer": "U2", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Where did the Washington Redskins quarterback who suffered concussion during  the second 2015 preseason game play his college football ?", "answer": "Baylor", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What county is the school that Keiki Kawai\u02bbae\u02bba received a BA in Hawaiian Studies from in?", "answer": "Honolulu County", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which Nassau County hamlet is home to the sister school of Singwango Secondary School?", "answer": "Carle Place, New York", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What profession does Lita and Shim Eun-jin have in common?", "answer": "singer", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "When was the American professional baseball pitcher which The Pittsburgh Pirates selectedut of the University of California born", "answer": "September 8, 1990", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "The Slashdot effect, also known as slashdotting, occurs when a popular website links to a smaller website, causing a massive increase in traffic, the effect has been associated with other websites or metablogs such as Fark, a community website created by who, that allows members to comment on a daily batch of news articles, and other items from various website?", "answer": "Drew Curtis", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What American film director and producer introduced the special on Doug Henning's World of Magic where Lori Lieberman was the musical guest?", "answer": "Gene Kelly", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What is the capital of the country in which Marja-Liisa Olthuis resides?", "answer": "Amsterdam", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "When did Lawrence Durrell\u2019s youngest brother write their debut book?", "answer": "1953", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which documentary aired first, Frida, en trotj\u00e4narinna or Saigon, U.S.A.?", "answer": "Frida, en trotj\u00e4narinna", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Don Balfour was a member of which upper house of the Georgia General Assembly?", "answer": "Georgia State Senate", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "The designer of the Bucksbaum Center for the Arts claims what national heritage?", "answer": "an Argentine American architect", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which player is second in line behind the keeper who plays for FC Barcelona and the Netherlands national team?", "answer": "Diederik Boer", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Robert Frederick Chew, best known for portraying drug kingpin Proposition Joe, a fictional character on what HBO drama?", "answer": "\"The Wire\"", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What were the dates of the Pan American Games in which Roman Gastaldi competed two years prior to competing in the World Championships in Moscow?", "answer": "October 23 to October 30", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Who was the film director for the 2009 film directed by Todd Phillips?", "answer": "Jonathan Lucas", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What soccer player has played for both Sampdoria and Pescara?", "answer": "Hugo Campagnaro", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Greg Cumbel is a broadcaster on NFL for CBS alongside which former American football quarterback?", "answer": "Trent Green", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "California Institute of Technology and University of Tennessee system, are in which country?", "answer": "United States", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "what is the real name of Alex Andreas's potrayal on satge of The Big Bopper?", "answer": "Perry \"J. P.\" Richardson Jr.", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Who was the actor in the 1979 film Firepower, who was known to often co-star with his wife Anne Jackson ?", "answer": "Eli Wallach", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What country does Monte Carlo Millions and Monte Carlo Casino have in common?", "answer": "Monaco", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "The album on which \"We'll Be Fine\" is in leaked how many days before its scheduled release?", "answer": "nine", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Were Harry Wayne Casey and Marie Currie both record producers?", "answer": "no", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": " Larry Wilson is an American film producer and screenwriter, best known for his screenwriting work on the films  \"The Addams Family\" and \"Beetlejuice\", a 1988 American comedy-fantasy film directed by who?", "answer": "Tim Burton", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "In between Le roi malgr\u00e9 lui and Manon, which one was first performed at the Op\u00e9ra-Comique in Paris on 19 January 1884? ", "answer": "Manon", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Gawain and Otello are both what type of performance?", "answer": "opera", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "What multimedia news agency operates in the United Kingdom and Ireland and once employed David Allan Chipp?", "answer": "The Press Association", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Among others, what type of  2-seater sports car does Datuk Wira Lee Chong Wei own with quattro permanent all-wheel drive system?", "answer": "Audi R8", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which film was produced first, Frozen or The Great Locomotive Chase?", "answer": "The Great Locomotive Chase", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "What does the name of Motoi Oyama's company stand for?", "answer": "anima sana in corpore sano", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which American professional soccer team based in F