a Andreyevna Tolokonnikova?", "answer": "Pussy Riot", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What is the name of the American mixed martial artist competing in the UFC, born in 1984, and winning the Middleweight Championship against Chris Weidman?", "answer": "Luke Rockhold", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Famous American actor Robert Rist portrayed popular children's characters, including Michelangelo in \"Teenage Mutant Ninja Turtles,\" Cousin Oliver in \"The Brady Bunch\" and a stuffed dragon in which Disney Channel animated series?", "answer": "Doc McStuffins", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Who owns the retired Grand National-winning National Hunt racehorse trained by Donald McCain, Jr. in a civil parish north east of Malpas and west of Nantwich?", "answer": "Trevor Hemmings", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Burkhard von Weisbriach was an ecclesiastical principality whose capital was the former city of what?", "answer": "Iuvavum", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What team in the National Football Conference, South division did Bruce Hill play for?", "answer": "Tampa Bay Buccaneers", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Are Curtis Bernhardt and Herbert Brenon both German film directors?", "answer": "no", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Linnar Viik is a member of an Advisory Board of a bank headquartered in what country?", "answer": "Finland", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Does Lucio Silla or Pell\u00e9as et M\u00e9lisande have more acts?", "answer": "Pell\u00e9as et M\u00e9lisande", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "What dance in the World Latin Dance Championship is a dance style that originated in the U.S. from African-Americans in the early 1930s?", "answer": "jive", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Tahir Shah was a maker of?", "answer": "Afghan refugees", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "The species Dolomedes briangreenei is named after a physicist that is a professor at what University?", "answer": "Columbia University", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Who was born first, Amir Naderi or Guillermo del Toro?", "answer": "Amir Naderi", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Are both Bangor International Airport and MidAmerica St. Louis Airport located in the United States?", "answer": "yes", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "What is the sponsership name of the irish football league in which Jamie Mulgrew plays", "answer": "Danske Bank Premiership", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "A small portion of Terra Mar belonged to a city in Broward County just north of what?", "answer": "Fort Lauderdale", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What is the capital and administrative centre of the new district that was formerly part of the Akatsi District?", "answer": "Ave Dakpa", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": " Hitmaker starred which member of the band Super Junior?", "answer": "Kim Young-woon", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What two jobs do both Lucky McKee and William Shatner have in common?", "answer": "actor, author", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "What is the second oldest arena in continuous operation in the US also known as?", "answer": "The Expo", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Denzel Curry was born in a suburb of what larger Florida city?", "answer": "Miami Gardens, Florida", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "How big is the state park located in Grafton County, New Hampshire?", "answer": "5655 acre", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Howard Morgan Griffith is a member of the Republican Party and which congressional caucus consisting of conservative and libertarian Republican members of the United States House of Representatives?", "answer": "Freedom Caucus", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "The music video for Welcome to Atlanta features an American former professional boxer born October 19, 1962 who competed during what years?", "answer": "from 1984 to 2011", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which University was founded first, Mahidol University or University of the Philippines?", "answer": "Mahidol University", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "What year was the group who released the album Vigil formed?", "answer": "1964", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "The Manson Family, led by Charles Manson, murdered actress Sharon and four others in what part of the Beverly Crest, north of Beverly Hills, Los Angeles, California?", "answer": "Benedict Canyon", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which People's Republic of China city is at a higher level of government, Dehui or Karamay?", "answer": "Karamay", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "What Dutch footballer has a rap feature in \"Wij zijn Ajax\"?", "answer": "Ryan Babel", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "As a film editor, Jim Clark worked on the British biographical drama film, The Killing Fields, that was released when?", "answer": "1984", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Sands at the Sands was recorded at a historic hotel and casino on the Las Vegas Strip that operated from 1952 to what year?", "answer": "1996", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "In which county is Tupelo Buffalo Park and Zoo located?", "answer": "Lee County", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What year was the World Cup won by the team captained by one of the five footballers to have reached over 100 caps for England?", "answer": "1966", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "During the winter of 1776-1777, Simonds' Regiment of Militia was at a fort located in which US state ?", "answer": "New York", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "The University of Montana Western (UMW) is a public university located in Dillon, a city in and the county seat of Beaverhead County, Montana, in which country?", "answer": "United States", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which annual skateboarding competition was founded by a family who is of Lebanese descent?", "answer": "Maloof Money Cup", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Who founded this women's professional baseball league that existed until 1954 in which Berith Melin played an outfielder?", "answer": "Philip K. Wrigley", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "The Japanese military officer Kenji Hatanaka conspired to prevent the broadcast of the surrender of this emperor who passed away a few decades later and was succeeded by whom?", "answer": "Akihito", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "\"Practice Date\" is the fourth episode of which American political comedy television sitcom starring Amy Poehler?", "answer": "Parks and Recreation", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which singer on the single \"Pictures in the Dark\" was born 29 December 1970?", "answer": "Aled Jones", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Rocky Hinds was the starting quarterback for the college football program that is part of what conference?", "answer": "Mountain West Conference", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "When did the league Ottawa Fury FC moved to in 2017 begin its inaugural season?", "answer": "2011", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "The 2017 Senior League World Series took place from July 29\u2013August 5 in Easley, South Carolina, guadulce, Panama defeated Coral Springs, Florida in the championship game, which is a city in Broward County, Florida, United States, approximately 20 mi northwest of which city?", "answer": "Fort Lauderdale", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": " the Royal Society was unable to meet its promise to finance the publication of Newton's \"Philosophiae Naturalis Principia Mathematica\" and let this to the clerk of the society who was best known for computing what?", "answer": "the orbit of Halley's Comet", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which drug store chain with approximately 40 stores in Hawaii is located in Lahaina Cannery Mall? ", "answer": "Longs Drugs", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Non-brewed condiment is a vinegar substitute created with water, acetic acid, flavourings and often caramel colour, it is sometimes used in fish and chip shops, is a hot dish of which nationality origin, consisting of fried battered fish and hot potato chips?", "answer": "English", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Trey Parker and Edgar Reitz, are Americans?", "answer": "no", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Many Chinese newspapers headlined a  scandal story during the Chinese new year known as what?", "answer": "Spring Festival", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "How many miles away is the Polipoli Spring State Recreation Area from the volcano that forms more than 75% of the Hawaiian Island of Maui?", "answer": "ten miles", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "This town with a population of 2,833 at the 2010 census is home to liberal arts college whose curriculum is based on the study of what?", "answer": "the Great Books", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Deliver Us from Evil stars Eric Bana, Sean Harris, Olivia Munn, Joel McHale and a Venezuelan actor born in what year?", "answer": "1977", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Who released a 1945 animated film starring an anthropomorphic white duck?", "answer": "RKO Radio Pictures", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which one of the two conferences of the National Football League (NFL) does champion Washington Redskins play for?", "answer": "The National Football Conference", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "William Alexander Watson Sheldon (18 January 1907 \u2013 1 November 1999) was an Irish politician and farmer, he was re-elected as an independent or nonpartisan politician starting in which year? ", "answer": "1944", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Are both Flight of the Navigator and Popeye considered films?", "answer": "yes", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "How many votes did Halina Olendzka get from the PiS?", "answer": "5386", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Who wrote the book used as the lead text formalised as the Seven Military Classics?", "answer": "Sun Tzu", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What  ABC-affiliated television station licensed to Poland Spring, Maine, United States and has a larger tower than WBLM?", "answer": "WMTW", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What is the year of the person who was born first, Simone Cipriani, or Stella McCartney?", "answer": "1964", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Suzanna Catharina de Graaff's claim of being the fifth daughter of Tsar Nicholas II and Tsarina Alexandra, was accepted by one of several imposters who clamed to be who?", "answer": "Grand Duchess Anastasia of Russia", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "In what borough of Hertfordshire is the Garston Ladies FC located?", "answer": "Hertsmere borough", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Gopaler Ma in her later years was close to a Scots-Irish social worker and who else?", "answer": "Swami Vivekananda", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Are Vladimir Arnold and Anatoly Fomenko both Soviet mathematicians?", "answer": "yes", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Which nature reserve is located in the province of Ulster in Ireland?", "answer": "Murlough Nature Reserve", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What body of water is near the towns of both Gaiman, Chubut and Trelew?", "answer": "Chubut River", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What year was the film Turn Up the Music was performed for released?", "answer": "2011", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Sources from what headquarters of the United States Department of Defense, claim the missile profile of the Sejil closely matches those of the Ashura (Ghadr-110) and the Samen?", "answer": "The Pentagon", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "\"Hard Rock Bottom of Your Heart\" is recorded by which American country music singer born on May 4, 1959?", "answer": "Randy Travis", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which original member of the Iveys was granted two Novello Awards for \"Without You\" in 1973?", "answer": "Pete Ham", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which was released first, Born Rich or Werner Herzog Eats His Shoe?", "answer": "Werner Herzog Eats His Shoe", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Which mountain is taller, Tirich Mir or Shishapangma?", "answer": "Tirich Mir", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Which central defender spent 20 years of his career at Arsenal F.C. Academy?", "answer": "David O'Leary", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which American author is best known for his work of a third-generation event-driven programming language and integrated development environment (IDE) from Microsoft?", "answer": "Dan Rahmel", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "which one of the three patriarchs of the Israelites was offered in Jehovah-jireh?", "answer": "Isaac", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "In what year was the Holy Roman Emperor whose name day the opera \"La corona\" was intended to celebrate born?", "answer": "1708", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "The Deutsche Gesellschaft f\u00fcr Sch\u00e4dlingsbek\u00e4mpfung mbH (translation: German Corporation for Pest control), in short Degesch, is a German chemical corporation, Degesch had the patent of the infamous Zyklon B, was the trade name of a cyanide-based pesticide invented in which country in the early 1920s?", "answer": "Germany", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Where did Martha Maria Twisleton-Wykeham-Fiennes's brother first achieve success?", "answer": "Royal National Theatre", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "in 2014-15 Sevilla competed in a league that began on which day ?", "answer": "on 23 August 2014", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "When was the arena which hosted the 2015 NCAA Division I Men's Ice Hockey Tournament final opened ?", "answer": "1995", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Christoph Heinrich Kniep was known for accompanying which writer and statesman on a journey to Naples?", "answer": "Johann Wolfgang von Goethe", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "One of the stars of the film Nabi also appeared in what Korean War comedy?", "answer": "Welcome to Dongmakgol", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which writer, P. J. O'Rourke or Wole Soyinka, was awarded the 1986 Nobel Prize in Literature?", "answer": "Akinwande Oluwole \"Wole\" Babatunde Soyinka", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "What is the home country of the studios located at Clarendon Road in Borehamwood?", "answer": "United Kingdom", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Issa Cissokho is of descent from a nation that is landlocked where?", "answer": "West Africa", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What year did the Southern Pacific class AC-9 begin running between Alturas, CA and Nevada's fifth most populous city?", "answer": "1952", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Who directed \"In Cold Blood\", a film based on the non-fiction novel by Truman Capote in addition to the film \"Fever Pitch\"?", "answer": "Richard Brooks", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What was the birth name of the emperor under whom Naevius Sutorius Macro served as prefect of the Praetorian Guard?", "answer": "Gaius Julius Caesar Germanicus", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What member of The Beatles has worked with Ray Cooper?", "answer": "George Harrison", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What are both Borassodendron and Chelidonium?", "answer": "plant", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "What Anglican, day and boarding school predominantly for boys did Richard Pearman Minifie attend?", "answer": "Melbourne Grammar School", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "In the 2010's, Mark Wahlberg starred alongside Will Ferrell in \"The Other Guys\" and which other film?", "answer": "Daddy's Home", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "David Johnston was replaced as Minister for Defence by which Liberal Party member?", "answer": "Kevin James Andrews", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Lenora Isabella Crichlow starred as Annie Sawyer in a British supernatural comedy-drama series that was created and written by Toby Whithouse for broadcast on what channel?", "answer": "BBC Three", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What Minnesota Wild draftee was named top defencemen in the 2008 IIHF World Championship rosters?", "answer": "Brent Burns", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "A New Stereophonic Sound Spectacular is the first album by the Belgian band Hooverphonic when the