ith a college that  provided undergraduate and postgraduate courses in the arts, humanities, business studies, teacher training, health and social care?", "answer": "The University of Cumbria", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which of the following cities is situated at the confluence of the Tuo River and the Yangtze River: Luzhou or Xianning?", "answer": "Luzhou", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "When was \"The Artist of Work\" published?", "answer": "1957", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What former member of the Danish parliament is serving as the Commissioner for Competition?", "answer": "Margrethe Vestager", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What sport is represented by Zuffa founded in 2001 by Frank Fertitta III and Lorenzo Fertitta?", "answer": "mixed martial arts", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What is another name for the Mediterranean Theater of Operations, United States Army invasion of French North Africa during World War II?", "answer": "Operation Gymnast", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which actor in \"Derek and Simon\" was also in \"The Big Bang Theory\"?", "answer": "Simon Helberg", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Of \"Porgy and Bess\" and \"Norma\", which was produced first?", "answer": "Norma", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Matty Dixon plays for the league that is which tier of the English football league system?", "answer": "sixth overall tier", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Who was born in 1948 and featured in a flim written by Nora Ephron?", "answer": "Billy Crystal", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Of the genuses Clitoria and Impatiens, which has a wider geographical distribution?", "answer": "Impatiens", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Adam Clayton Powell Jr. represented a large neighborhood in the US House of Representatives that was formally organized in what year?", "answer": "1658", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which monument must have its history inferred form its location, style, and dedicatory inscriptio