e": "bridge"}, {"question": "What is the population of the country which has Ellen Johnson Sirlea as the 24th president? ", "answer": "4,503,000", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What ranking does the man who Jonathan Brookins defeated on December 4, 2010 have in UFC lightweight rankings?", "answer": "#9", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which brother of Francisco Rodr\u00edguez Araya is known for his ability to deliver pinpoint crosses?", "answer": "Roberto Rodr\u00edguez", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which tennis player played for more countries, Martina Navratilova or Melanie Oudin?", "answer": "Martina Navratilova", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "What year was the album a prequel to '97 Bonnie & Clyde appeared on released?", "answer": "2000", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "The national teams of Spain, Italy, Albania, Israel, Macedonia, and Liechtenstein are members of what football association?", "answer": "Union of European Football Associations", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "For which ballet was this Soviet ballet dancer and choreographer, who portrayed the main character in the film Valentino, a director?", "answer": "Paris Opera Ballet", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": " Timothy B is the second studio solo album by Timothy B. Schmit, the bass guitarist and co-lead vocalist for the Eagles, an American rock band formed where in 1971", "answer": "Los Angeles", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which had more acts/ scenes, The Snow Maiden or Sadko?", "answer": "Sadko", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Big Four are countries that are part of the nations that provide what organization with funds to lend?", "answer": "International Monetary Fund", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Gioachino Rossini and Alessandro Scarlatti are both what?", "answer": "Italian composer", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "The company which formerly owned Southern Comfort and Tuaca manufactures what burbon that was the first to be sold exclusively in sealed bottles?", "answer": "Old Forester", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which District was the niece of Martin Luther King Jr. the representative for?", "answer": "28th", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which was the TV series in which Sada Thompson, an American stage, film and television actress starred along with Gary Frank?", "answer": "\"Family\"", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which rock band perform in an indoor sports arena located in the Near West Side neighborhood of Chicago, Illinois in 2005?", "answer": "Irish rock band U2", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What job did both Ilse Rosenthal-Schneider and Max Planck have in common?", "answer": "physicist", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which Sag Harbor Villiage District building is the best example of Egyptian Revival Style in the US today?", "answer": "the First Presbyterian Church", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What inventions are credited to the person who has a street named after him that runs East and West through the city of Richmond, Virginia?", "answer": "lightning rod, bifocals, and the Franklin stove, among other inventions", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Starship Entertainment, is a South Korean record label established in 2008 by Kim Shi Dae, and formerly home to girl group Sistar, it currently manages artists such as which South Korean-Chinese girl group formed by Starship Entertainment and Yuehua Entertainment which debuted in 2016, also known as WJSN?", "answer": "Cosmic Girls", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which of the writers of \"Let's Stop Talkin\" About It was an American country music singer, songwriter, author, and actress?", "answer": "Deborah Allen", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "In Dutch and Belgian cuisine, rijstevlaai, is a pie with a filling based on rice pudding, if French it's called what?", "answer": "tarte au riz", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which is native to farther east, Punch or Chimay\u00f3 Cocktail?", "answer": "Punch", "type": "comparison"}, {"ques