er was known for the important roles she created in the works of which choreographer who co-founded the New York City Ballet?", "answer": "George Balanchine", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "An English rock band formed in London in 1971 that has achieved eight gold records is signed to a record label founded by who?", "answer": "Albert Grossman", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Ike Turner worked with which famous American Chicago blues and electric blues pianist and organist? ", "answer": "Johnny \"Big Moose\" Walker", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "A betting pool, sports lottery, sweep, or office pool if done at work, is a form of gambling, specifically a variant of parimutuel betting influenced by lotteries, where gamblers pay a fixed price into a \"pool\" (from which taxes and a house \"take\" or \"vig\" are removed), and then make a selection on an outcome, usually related to sport, the vig is also known as juice, under-juice, the cut or the take, is the amount charged by a bookmaker, or \"bookie\", for taking a bet from a gambler?", "answer": "Vigorish", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Are Suggs and Jack Evans both American musicians?", "answer": "no", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "William Corcoran Eustis (July 20, 1862 - November 24, 1921) was a captain in the United States Army and the personal assistant to which General of the Armies during World War I, who was was a senior United States Army officer, that had a nickname of \"Black Jack\"?", "answer": "John Joseph \"Black Jack\" Pershing", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Who was born first, Tom Gullikson or Cara Black?", "answer": "Tom Gullikson", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Hitomi Soga married someone formerly what?", "answer": "United States Army soldier", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What number Secretary of the Air Force resigned as a result of Charles L. Bartlett's reporting?", "answer": "third", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "In the 1999 teen sex comedy film American Pie, the protagonist is caught masturbating with a pie after being told the sport-related euphemisms that became widely used after what worldly event?", "answer": "World War II", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Are Jingdezhen and Ya'an both prefecture-level cities in China?", "answer": "yes", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "exposure to what caused the town that is now Route 66 State Park to be evacuated?", "answer": "dioxin", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "FUN! Online Games features articles on games such as a massively multiplayer online game that as of July 2013 had over 200 million what?", "answer": "registered user accounts", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What type of collection does Etarcomol and Medb have in common?", "answer": "Ulster Cycle", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "A Steady Rain has a charcter that loosly portrays Jeffery Dahmer, who is it?", "answer": "a cannibalistic serial killer", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "how old is the actress that played Honey Ryder in the 1962 James Bond film \"Dr. No\"", "answer": "(born 19 March 1936)", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Guggenheim Abu Dhabi is being designed by an architect who lives in what city?", "answer": "Los Angeles", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Are both Indigofera and Kadsura plant genera?", "answer": "yes", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "The American film director, writer and producer known for  \"Kiss Me Deadly\" (1955), \"The Big Knife\" (1955), etc. produced this 1964 American psychological thriller stars whom in her final film role?", "answer": "Mary Astor", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What 2011 film was Lone Scherifig play in?", "answer": "One Day", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What was the man whom Daniel Goodenow studied law under noted for his involvement in?", "answer": "Treaty of Ghent", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Who's debut album, \"Start Here\", was released on August 28, 2015 and includes the single \"Girl in a Country Song\", who's songs have been 