type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Ed Mangano defeated whom?", "answer": "defeated incumbent Thomas R. Suozzi", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Glamour and The Ladder, are which type of media?", "answer": "publication", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "The John Downing Jr. House is a historic house in downtown Middleport, a village located on the banks of the Ohio River in the southeastern part of the U.S. state of Ohio, notably, his work with the young Samuel Clemens led to a literary appearance years later: writing under the name of \"Mark Twain\", Clemens portrayed him in which book, released in 1883, is a memoir by Mark Twain of his days as a steamboat pilot on the Mississippi River before the American Civil War, and also a travel book, recounting his trip along the Mississippi River from St. Louis to New Orleans many years after the War?", "answer": "Life on the Mississippi", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What is the abbreviation for the franchise responsible for a 2010 animated short film by DreamWorks Animation?", "answer": "HTTYD", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "The Battle of Nanning was fought between the invading Yunnan Army, allied to which faction of Chinese statesman, political and military leader who served as the leader of the Republic of China?", "answer": "Chiang Kai-shek", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "The 1991 Chicago Bears season ended with a playoff loss for their coach, who was inducted into the Pro Football Hall of Fame in what year?", "answer": "1988", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Stephen Hopkins and Bertrand Blier, have which mutual occupation?", "answer": "film director", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "What award was given to the Indian politician belonging to the Indian broad based political party founded in 1885?", "answer": "Padma Vibhushan", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Who produced the 2002 Hong Kong legal drama show starring the Miss Asia 1990?", "answer": "TVB", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Who created the animated television series which was part of the brand belonging to Spin Master?", "answer": "Keith Chapman", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "In what valley is the national park located that is ajacent to Dungog Shire?", "answer": "Hunter Valley", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "The identity of the author of The Intimate Adventures of a London Call Girl was revealed in what year?", "answer": "2009", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What was the name of the album that American rapper Hoodie Allen's song \"All About It\" was featured on?", "answer": "\"People Keep Talking\"", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which band was founded first, Talking Heads or Alkaline Trio?", "answer": "Talking Heads", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "What was the last Audio Adrenaline album on which lead singer Mark Stuart performed?", "answer": "Adios: The Greatest Hits", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Who is the Enlglish film director and producer that was born in 1937 that is working on turning John Pearson's novel into a film? ", "answer": "Ridley Scott", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "More than likely, what type of people were held captive for slave labor at the Ducros Plantation?", "answer": "Africans", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Milan Sachs conducted the premiere of the play Jen\u016ffa by the composer who was inspired by what types of music?", "answer": "Moravian and other Slavic folk music", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "How long was the musician who conceived The Lifehouse Method with his band?", "answer": "over 50 years", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Eveline Cruickshanks is a historian of what historical political movement in Great Britain and Ireland?", "answer": "Eveline Cruickshanks is an historian of seventeenth- and eighteenth-century British political history, specialising in Jacobitism and Toryism", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What is the person who called Tazio Nuvolari \"the greatest driver of the past, the present, and the future\" best known for?", "answer": "for creating the first gasoline-electric hybrid vehicle (Lohner-Porsche), the Volkswagen Beetle, the Mercedes-Benz SS/SSK, several other important developments and Porsche automobiles", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Noal Zaher Shah is the daughter of the seventh child of which king of Afghanistan?", "answer": "Mohammed Zahir Shah", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which song written by Max Martin and Shellback has been compared to the song \"Yodel It!\"?", "answer": "\"Shake It Off\"", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What did Nirvana do differently with \"In Utero\" that caused a documentary to be made about recording the album?", "answer": "hired engineer Steve Albini", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What was the total population of the city at which Air Post was bases? ", "answer": "1,614,300", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Of what state was New England Art Union board member Edward Everett governor?", "answer": "Massachusetts", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "How many people lived in the county seat of the county in Montana named after Abraham Lincoln?", "answer": "2,628", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which band was formed first, Jesus Jones of TV on the Radio?", "answer": "Jesus Jones", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Which musician signed to Sire Records in 1987 was featured on the 1990 soundtrack album for the film Dick Tracy?", "answer": "Ice-T", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What show starring Vanessa Bell Calloway is a remake of a British series of the same name, set in Chicago and airs on Showtime?", "answer": "Shameless", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What late 1800's single issue periodical published by John Francis Bloxam contained the notorious poem \"Two Loves\" used in the imprisonment of Oscar Wilde?", "answer": "the Chameleon: a Bazaar of Dangerous and Smiling Chances", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Kepler is a novel by an Irish novelist who was born in what year?", "answer": "1945", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Who was an operatic tenor, Anita Vogel or Armand Tokatyan ?", "answer": "Armand Tokatyan", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "U.S. Route 75 passes over the Nebraska state line near a city that had how many inhabitants in 2010 ?", "answer": "2,571", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What company was in charge of US distribution for a film starring an actress who also starred in \"Doctor Who\"?", "answer": "Millennium Entertainment", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Sedan is sponsored by whom?", "answer": "Invicta France", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which  2003 animated comedy film written and directed by Sylvain Chomet won the award for Best Film in  9th Lumi\u00e8res Awards", "answer": "The Triplets of Belleville", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "During the Climate Change Conference of 2009, what was the culminating document that came out of it at the conclusion in December 2009.", "answer": "The Copenhagen Agreement", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Director Wim Wenders, Richard Reitinger, and Peter Handke co-wrote what film that features an invisible angle becoming human?", "answer": "Wings of Desire", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which spanish poet, and playwright, supported El Concurso del Cante Jondo?", "answer": "Federico Garc\u00eda Lorca", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What college in New Hampshire along the Connecticut River held the conference that founded The Academic Council of the United Nations System?", "answer": "American Dartmouth College", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "In what Australian state was Cortinarius sublargus first described?", "answer": "South Australia", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which former outfielder born in 1975 hosted Game 1 of the 2014 National League Championship Series?", "answer": "Gabe Kapler", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "The coach who succeeded Dave Smith as coach of the Southern Methodist University's football team was born in which year ?", "answer": "1941", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Sagas of the Demonspawn is a four issue gamebook series written by J. H. Brennan, and who illustrated the latter two, by which British fantasy and science fiction illustrator and modeler known for his work for Games Workshop's White Dwarf magazine, Warhammer Fantasy Battle, Warhammer Fantasy Roleplay and Warhammer 40,000 games?", "answer": "John Blanche", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "The 2010 FA Community Shield was the 88th FA Community Shield, an annual football match contested by the winners of the previous season's Premier League and FA Cup competitions, Manchester United won the match 3\u20131 with goals from Javier Hern\u00e1ndez Balc\u00e1zar, a Mexican professional footballer who plays as a striker for which English club and the Mexico national team?", "answer": "West Ham United", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Of the two Walt Disney films, The Jungle Book or One Little Indian, which introduces Neel Sethi as Mowgli?", "answer": "The Jungle Book", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "How old was Rose Hartwick Thorpe when she wrote the poem she would be largely remembered for writing? ", "answer": "16 years old", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What documentary about the Gilgo Beach Killer debuted on November, 2016 on A&E?", "answer": "The Killing Season", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Paul Dini wrote for which animated comedy series created by Amblin Entertainment?", "answer": "Tiny Toon Adventures", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Grace Nail Johnson's husband began working for the NAACP in what year?", "answer": "1917", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which dog breed, Tyrolean Hound or Braque Francais, are from a very old type of gun dog used for pointing the location of game birds for a hunter?", "answer": "The Braques fran\u00e7ais", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "What is the name of the Scottish actor who has played the part of 'Doctor Who', and who played the part of Daniel in a British radio sitcom as part of a childless couple?", "answer": "David Tennant", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What country does Anjulie and Starbucks have in common?", "answer": "United States", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Jon Kortajarena has modeled for the fashion designer who launched his luxury brand in what year?", "answer": "2006", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What do Daniel Nestor and Jana Novotn\u00e1 have in common?", "answer": "professional tennis player", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "In what year was Google\u2019s Santa Tracker rival founded?", "answer": "1955", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Jason Schwartzman starred in a film starring who as Scott Pilgrim?", "answer": "Michael Cera", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What type of porch leading to the entrance of a building was used in an ancient structure in Rome?", "answer": "Portico", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which county in Washington is VAQ-130 located in?", "answer": "Island County", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What job do both Ingeborg Bachmann and Jean Toomer have?", "answer": "poet", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Which community center for the City & County of Honolulu was the 1991 NCAA Men's Volleyball Tournament played at?", "answer": "Neal S. Blaisdell", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What Japanese weekly magazine published by Shueisha since 1966 also known as Sh\u016bpure,serialized  a manga written by Kazuo Koike?", "answer": "Weekly Playboy", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What census-desingated place on the east shore of Lake Tahoe also features a park and ride location for the South Tahoe Area Transit Authority?", "answer": "Stateline", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What year was H.P. Lovecraft's novella \"At the Mountains of Madness\" published and was the first appearance of The Elder Things?", "answer": "1936", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What actress who stared in An Elephant's tale also won a best actress comedy award at the american anime awards for her work in zatch?",