or of the movie the The talented Mr Ripley that William Horberg produced?", "answer": "Anthony Minghella", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What states have schools that compete in the same conference as Anna Maria College?", "answer": "Connecticut, Maine, Massachusetts, New Hampshire, Rhode Island, and Vermont", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "\"Fifteen\" is the fourth single from the second studio album which was released on what date??", "answer": "November 11, 2008", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Adams of Eagle Lake is an American hour-long police series that starred an actor best known for playing in what legal drama?", "answer": "Matlock", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "This co-presenter of \"Trainspotting Live\" on BBC was born in 1959.", "answer": "Richard Francis \"Dick\" Strawbridge", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Renaissance: Sequential Vol is what by an Argentinian house DJ?", "answer": "second release", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Stoke Newington Central, a ward in the London Borough of Hackney, forms part of the Hackney North and Stoke Newington constituency of a politician from what political party?", "answer": "British Labour Party", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "\"On Air with Ryan Seacrest\" is operated by what company? ", "answer": "Clear Channel Radio", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "WMHT-FM is the callsign of a classical music and NPR radio station licensed to Schenectady, New York, it is sister station to WMHT, a member of which organization?", "answer": "PBS", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Who does Sigourney Weaver play in the movie for which Anna Hamilton Phelan was nominated for an Oscar?", "answer": "Dian Fossey", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What is the name of this Irish film and television actor from the film \"A Hard Day's Night\", who also acted in \"Never Say Die\"?", "answer": "Henry Wilfrid Brambell", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What is the release date of the fourth mixtape by American rapper Joyner Lucas?", "answer": "June 16, 2017", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Hj\u00f6rdis Gunborg Schymberg was what type of operatic soprano voice that specializes in music that is distinguished by agile runs, leaps and trills?", "answer": "coloratura", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Aleksandr Lyapunov and Israel Gelfand, share which mutual occupation?", "answer": "mathematician", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Which professional tennis player is older, Stan Smith or Elena Likhovtseva?", "answer": "Stanley Roger Smith (born December 14, 1946 in Pasadena, California)", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Are Richard Benjamin and Len Wiseman both film directors?", "answer": "yes", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "From 1981 to 1983 Stuart H. Singer was a law clerk for a US Supreme Court justice that died in what year?", "answer": "2002", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": " In 2003, when Marques Batista de Abreu was playing for Nagoya Grampus Eight he was ranked 2nd highest assists in J1 League, the top division of the  Professional Football League of what country?", "answer": "Japan", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What is the Italian translation of the fifth studio album by the Hong Kong-based rock duo formed by Julio Acconci and Dino Acconci? ", "answer": "\"I sing\"", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "The 2012\u201313 FC Bayern Munich season was the 114th season in the club's history and the 48th consecutive season in the top flight of German football, the what in German , since the promotion of the team from the Regionalliga S\u00fcd in 1965, before the start of the season, Bayern signed Dante Bonfim Costa Santos (born 18 October 1983), commonly known as Dante, is a Brazilian professional footballer who plays for French Ligue 1 club Nice?", "answer": "Bundesliga", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Due to concern in regards to the visual appearance of a sacred mountain to Native Hawaiians, the Thirty Meter Telescope has been considered to be built in which alternative site in Spain?", "answer": "Roque de los Muchachos Observatory", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "The ambassador unveiled in 2016 of the Golden Movie Awards has received two nominations for what?", "answer": "Best Actress in a Leading Role", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which opera has more acts, Tha\u00efs or La boh\u00e8me?", "answer": "La boh\u00e8me", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "who died first Giuseppe Verdi or Paul Hindemith?", "answer": "Giuseppe Fortunino Francesco Verdi", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "What type of media technique does Feed the Kitty and Marc Antony and Pussyfoot have in common?", "answer": "animation", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What  Academy Award nominee starred in Miracle of the White Stallions?", "answer": "Edward Albert Heimberger", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Were Gunner Palace and Night Mail releasded in the same year?", "answer": "no", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "In what month was the Rihanna song that Mikky Ekko is best known for being featured on released?", "answer": "January", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Are Il re pastore and Giasone both operas?", "answer": "yes", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "The 1966 BRDC International Trophy race was won by a man born in what year?", "answer": "1926", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which island is located 240km to the south od Australia and is the birth place of Maxwell Arthur Burr?", "answer": "Tasmania", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What fable are both Chicken little films based on", "answer": "Henny Penny", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What is the lifetime professional coaching record of the Hall of Fame coach that coached Tad Boyle in 2015?", "answer": "1,275-965", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What is the full name of the rapper whose second studio album was titled \"Blue Cheese & Coney Island\"?", "answer": "Rufus Arthur Johnson", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What country do Acera and Umbria have in common?", "answer": "Italy", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Are Basil Bunting and Jack Kerouac both writers?", "answer": "yes", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "When does the president died who's advisor was Edward Mandell House?", "answer": "February 3, 1924", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Between The White Stripes and U2, which band was formed earlier?", "answer": "U2", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Freak was a song inspired by the historical drama film about whom?", "answer": "Joseph Merrick", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Do U2 3D and The Tree That Remembers include political statements or stances?", "answer": "yes", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Who was the seven-time World and Olympic medalist killed by John Eleuthere du Pont in January 1996?", "answer": "David Leslie \"Dave\" Schultz", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What nationality is the namesake of HC Andersen?", "answer": "Danish", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which album by singer Viktor Lazlo consists of French chansons by one of France's greatest international stars widely regarded as France's national chanteuse?", "answer": "Loin de Paname", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Where was the ice hockey player  born, whose record of goal by a rookie in one game, Don Murdoch equalled on October 12 1976 ?", "answer": "Kitchener, Ontario", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Where are the headquarters of the bank Linnar Viik serves on the board of?", "answer": "Helsinki, Finland", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "When was the actor born who played a role on \"The Beast\" with Johnny Kastl and was a teen idol and sex symbol?", "answer": "August 18, 1952", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "The Gravedigger's Song was a solo single from a member of which band?", "answer": "Screaming Trees", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Steve Bannon is the executive chairman of a website founded by who ?", "answer": "Andrew Breitbart", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What network broadcast the show featuring the