estion": "What is the date the episode of South Park that showed Randy and Sharon Marsh's address premiered?", "answer": "March 14, 2012", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Are Taylor Hawkins and Tomoko Kawase both actors?", "answer": "no", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Ignite Your Faith and Reunions magazine, are which type of media?", "answer": "magazine", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Leicester City Football Club is an English football club based in Leicester, Leicestershire, the club was founded in which year, the 2016\u201317 UEFA Champions League was their fourth appearance in Europe?", "answer": "1884", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which American plant species, Liquidambar or Claytonia, is also native to northeastern Asia?", "answer": "Claytonia", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Which civil rights activist was killed my the Ku Klux Klan?", "answer": "Michael Schwerner", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Who founded their band first, Bob Marley or Damian Kulash?", "answer": "Robert Nesta Marley", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "What person does Poshu Khamar and Animal Farm have in common?", "answer": "George Orwell", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "The flag that was popularized in the Easter rising of 1916, has what three colors in it ?", "answer": "green (at the hoist), white and orange", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "which  American singer composed songs in Burl Ives Sings Pearly Shells and Other Favorites", "answer": "Wyatt Merle Kilgore", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "How high above sea level is Bok Tower Gardens located on Iron Mountain?", "answer": "295 ft above sea level", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": " Linda Reisman executive produced an American-German horror film written and directed by who?", "answer": "Victor Salva", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Who was the skating partner of \"The Ice Panel\" member replaced by Ruthie Henshall?", "answer": "Andrei Bukin", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Name the harbor where Squirrel Island in Lincoln Conty Maine is located?", "answer": "Boothbay Harbor", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Who directed a 2015 American sports drama film that was a spin-off and sequel to the \"Rocky\" film series, the film features a British professional boxer who held the WBC cruiserweight title from 2016 to 2017? ", "answer": "Ryan Coogler", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What is the name of this American cuisine which originated in the New England region of the United States, characterized by the use of seafood and dairy products with one popular dish being American chop suey? ", "answer": "New England cuisine", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What league does the Edgware-based team Tony Sorrell played for play in?", "answer": "League Two", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What South Korean global leader in online games for PC and mobile developed Crazy Arcade?", "answer": "Nexon", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "The 1957 film \"Cat Girl\" was an unofficial remake of a 1942 horror film directed by who?", "answer": "Jacques Tourneur", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "\"Wing\" is the third episode in a season that concluded on what date?", "answer": "December 7, 2005", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Hagia Irene is located in the outer courtyard of the edifice located in what Turkish capital?", "answer": "Istanbul", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Fun and Galt Aureus both make what kind of music?", "answer": "rock", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "What television show did the South Korean star of the series that airs on KBS2 every Saturday and Sunday from 7:55 p.m. to 9:15 p.m make her debut on?", "answer": "\"School 2013\"", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which band formed first, Sydney's Hoodoo Gurus or Wire?", "answer": "Wire", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "When did the plane that the Vought XF8U-3 Crusader II was designed to compete against enter service with the U.S. Navy?", "answer": "1960", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "The 