tween Lana Del Rey and Soul Coughing, which has a sound that includes jazz grooves?", "answer": "Soul Coughing", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "What film did the singer of \"I Saw Mommy Kissing Santa Claus\" star in?", "answer": "The Two Little Bears", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Are Wojciech Fibak and Tom Okker both Polish tennis players?", "answer": "no", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Sugoi Japan Award is an event that awards Manga, Anime, Light novel, and Entertainment novels. These entertainment styles was development in what century?", "answer": "19th century", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "When did the series that had an American professional mixed martial arts fighter born on August 13, 1972 as a contestant premiere?", "answer": "April 6, 2006", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "How many check-in counters does the airport that has a subsidiary of Malaysia Airline whose head office is in Petaling Jaya, Selangor as one of the airline", "answer": "9", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Alan James and T. Arthur Cottam, have which occupations in common?", "answer": "film director and screenwriter", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "What is the county in which Sierra-at-Tahoe is located?", "answer": "Douglas County", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "How many World Series championships have been won by the team that Bob Veale pitched for from 1972-1974?", "answer": "eight", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What is the name of this collegiate athletic conference whose schools compete in the NCAA, which includes the VCU Rams?", "answer": "Atlantic 10 Conference", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Marie-Barbe de Boullongne was a philanthropist on what continent?", "answer": "North America", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Blink-182 bassist and drummer also played in a rocker supergroup formed in what city in 2005?", "answer": "Los Angeles, California", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Were Songyuan and Shulan in the same province in China?", "answe