n? ", "answer": "October 11, 1962", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "The drug sung about in Jay-Z\u2019s first single from his tenth studio album get bought from?", "answer": "Golden Triangle", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "When did the father of the principal owner and chairman of the Charlotte Hornets pass away?", "answer": "July 23, 1993", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Did both Mark Rydell and Jacques Feyder direct films?", "answer": "yes", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "A Town Called Panic and The Princess and the Frog are both what?", "answer": "animated", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "what does Partition Sejm and Commission of National Education have in common?", "answer": "Lithuanian", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Vladimir Bure is the father of which hockey right-wing position player?", "answer": "Valeri Vladimirovich \"Val\" Bure", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What is the total land area of the airport at which the Continental Airlines Flight 1404 crash happened?", "answer": "33,531 acres", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which of the following is remembered best for Beau Geste: P. C. Wren or James Emanuel?", "answer": "Percival Christopher Wren", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Where is the headquater of corporation  which  official Columbia color is defined as located ", "answer": "Carlstadt, New Jersey", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Danny Hugh Freeze Jr. coached Michael Oher and which other former American football defensive end born on July 28, 1988?", "answer": "Greg Hardy", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "When was the person who was sampled on Breakn' a Sweat born?", "answer": "December 8, 1943", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "The defunct Naval Air Station Alameda is located in what city and state?", "answer": "Alameda, California", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "who is known for more roles, Rob Minkoff or Bob Clark", "answer": "Benjamin \"Bob\" Clark", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Kingsford Smith Drive, Brisbane was named after the aviator who made the first trans-Pacific flight from the US to Australia in what year?", "answer": "1928", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "In which state does the Mexican American brand of Yum! located?", "answer": "California", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Who directed a 1994 crime-thriller produced by Lawrence Turman?", "answer": "Curtis Hanson", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What is the only roadless pass on the Lewis and Clark National Historic Trail?", "answer": "Lewis and Clark Pass", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "The author of Dangerous is associated with what political movement?", "answer": "the alt-right", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which Disneyland park in Florida features the World Showcase that enables visitors to walk from Moroccan, through French and British to Canadian pavilions in minutes?", "answer": "Epcot at Walt Disney World", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "The MOS Technology 6502 8-bit CPU was manufactured by a corporation whose name is an abbreviation for what?", "answer": "Son of Electronic Printer", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Who was an early ethical egoist alternative to the philosophy also known as Ruism?", "answer": "Yang Zhu", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Heinz Werner Engl, the Austrian mathematician is rector of which public university founded by Duke Rudolph IV in 1365 and one of the oldest universities in the German-speaking world?", "answer": "University of Vienna", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "When was the movement that Edgar Bear Runner parlayed with in the 1970s founded?", "answer": "1968", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What is the year of the event which occured first,the 1972 United States Senate, or Margaret Chase Smith was born?", "answer": "1897", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "In What country was actor Nancy Wu born in?", "answer": "Hong Kong", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "When was the source that defines \"Independent Woman\" as \u201cA woman who pays her own bills, buys her own things, and does not allow a man to affect her stability or self-confidence\" founded?", "answer": "1999", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "How many employees did the company that represents Joshua Seftel have in March 2016?", "answer": "1,800", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Who iss the father of an American singer, songwriter and actor who's album is Interplanetary Class Classics?", "answer": "John Lennon", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "The Final Empire is the first novel in which series of epic fantasy novels written by American author Brandon Sanderson and published by Tor Books?", "answer": "Mistborn", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Who produced the album Recess on March 18,2014 featuring the single Dirty Vibe?", "answer": "Skrillex and Diplo", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Operation Inherent Resolve (OIR) is the U.S. military's operational name for the military intervention against the Islamic State of Iraq and Syria (ISIS, in the vernacular, Daesh), including both the campaign in Iraq and the campaign in Syria, which terminology is used to define the timeline of United States government military operations is based on the Committee on International Relations (now known as the U.S. House Committee on Foreign Affairs)?", "answer": "timeline of United States government military operations", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "This Republic, established in 1581 and the focus of The Secret Treaty of Dover, contained how many provinces?", "answer": "Seven", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "The Nissan S30 was the first generation of this sports car manufactured since 1969?", "answer": "Nissan Z-car", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Parisian Nights was a film that featured which English actor?", "answer": "William Henry Pratt", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What Southern League team, founded in 1881, featured player Tot Farnell?", "answer": "Watford", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What country did both Sanskrit Itihasa and Garikapati Narasimha Rao come from?", "answer": "India", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Albert Lee Ueltschi was once a personal pilot to what Pan American World Airways founder?", "answer": "Juan Trippe", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Charlie Cotton is a character who had a one night stand with the character played by which British actress and singer?", "answer": "Samantha Zoe Womack", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which dog is known as French White and Black Hound, the Grand Griffon Vend\u00e9en or the Chien Fran\u00e7ais Blanc et Noir?", "answer": "Chien Fran\u00e7ais Blanc et Noir", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Which character voiced by Kristen Bell is featured in Disneyland's A Christmas Fantasy Parade?", "answer": "Anna", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "The lead singer for the pop rock band Maroon 5 was a returning coach on the fourth season of an American reality talent show that premied on what date?", "answer": "March 25, 2013", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What is the home of the core group that is part of the core artists of Hot Country and is on the Southern Ground Artist's label?  ", "answer": "Atlanta, Georgia", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Prince of Jutland starred which English actor?", "answer": "Christian Charles Philip Bale", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "The 1991\u201392 NBA season was the Hawks' 43rd season in the National Basketball Association, and 24th season in Atlanta, with a 22\u201320 record in late January, which American retired professional basketball player who primarily played for the Atlanta Hawks, ruptured his achilles tendon and was out for the remainder of the season?", "answer": "Jacques Dominique Wilkins", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Jorge Paulo Agostinho Mendes, better known simply as Jorge Mendes, is a Portuguese football agent, Mendes is among the most influential football agents in the world, with clients including David de Gea, a Spanish professional footballer who plays as a goalkeeper for whi